{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794847625540,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5414fd9001PvvE9BbPrUmLbh","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e5413b3a001XRM9GBa5XaIrwU","type":"tool","id":"call_ce0036afa636451b9b454d8d","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/iterations/iteration-001.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/iterations/iteration-001.md, lines 1-97\n1: # Review Iteration 001\n2: \n3: ## Dispatcher\n4: \n5: - Lineage: `docs-7`, area `docs`.\n6: - Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\n7: - Focus: traceability, with correctness, security and maintainability lenses applied to the same two changed README lines. The pass-seven operator focus is the docs area: this branch's net change to the root `README.md` against `origin/main`, where `/create:skill` was renamed `/create:sk-skill`, so every command name the README gives is checked against `.skilled/commands`. `review/review-brief-7.txt` and `review/review-scope-7.txt` were read first; this iteration covers the area they assign to `docs-7`.\n8: - Diff base: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff origin/main 1c3d62def5a -- README.md`, the command on line 1 of the scope file. It reports two lines changed, 2 insertions and 2 deletions: `README.md:269` and `README.md:603`.\n9: - `steer.md` does not exist in the lineage directory, so no lead ruling applied.\n10: - Recorded limits and the holdout rule were honoured: no prompt corpus was opened, no `git diff`/`show`/`log -p` ran over a path containing one, `score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary` was not run, and no CLI session store was read.\n11: \n12: ## Files Reviewed\n13: \n14: | File | Lines read | What was checked |\n15: |------|-----------|------------------|\n16: | `README.md` | 266-271 | The changed extending-Skilled paragraph: the renamed `/create:sk-skill` and the remaining `/create:*` names, plus the `:auto`/`:confirm` sentence |\n17: | `README.md` | 580-613 | The agent list and the whole commands section: all 44 names, the six group counts, and the changed Create list |\n18: | `README.md` | 640-663 | The Doctor table, to test the `Doctor (17)` count against real files |\n19: | `README.md` | 341 | The runtime goal-command paragraph, to confirm the four runtime-owned goal commands are outside the 44 |\n20: | `.skilled/commands/README.txt` | 1-40 | The command tree's own six-group index and counts |\n21: | `.skilled/commands/create/README.txt` | 50-95, 119-180 | The create group index rows, the command-map tree, and every example invocation of the renamed command |\n22: | `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md` | 1-40 | The renamed router's frontmatter name, description, argument hint and owned assets |\n23: | `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md` | 40-80 | The mode routing and execution targets for `:auto` and `:confirm` |\n24: | `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/README.md` | 60-70, 190-198 | The sk-doc hub's thirteen-command sentence and its how-do-I answer naming `/create:sk-skill` |\n25: \n26: Context evidence (read-only, outside the docs scope path): `.skilled/commands/**` file inventory, `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt:1,28`, `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml:113`, `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml:30,39-40`, `.opencode/commands/create/sk-skill.md`, `.claude/commands/create/sk-skill.md`.\n27: \n28: ## Findings - New\n29: \n30: ### P0 Findings\n31: \n32: None.\n33: \n34: ### P1 Findings\n35: \n36: None.\n37: \n38: ### P2 Findings\n39: \n40: None.\n41: \n42: ## Traceability Checks\n43: \n44: | Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n45: |----------|--------|----------|\n46: | `spec_code` | pass | Both changed lines name a command file that exists: `/create:sk-skill` resolves to `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md` and every other `/group:name` token in `README.md` resolves to `.skilled/commands/<group>/<name>.md` (44 of 44). The two changed lines agree with each other. |\n47: | `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | The review target has no `checklist.md` at the packet root; the pass-seven brief and scope file are the operative checklist and both were read. |\n48: | `skill_agent` | pass | The renamed command's own surfaces agree with the README name: `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md:1-13` routes `/create:sk-skill`, and `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt:1,28` presents the same name. |\n49: | `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | No agent body is in the docs scope; the command mirrors that do exist are recorded under Integration Evidence. |\n50: | `feature_catalog_code` | notApplicable | No feature-catalog claim is touched by the two changed README lines. |\n51: | `playbook_capability` | notApplicable | No manual-testing-playbook claim is touched by the two changed README lines. |\n52: \n53: ## Integration Evidence\n54: \n55: - `.skilled/commands/README.txt:21-35` gives the six-group table: create 13, deep 2, doctor 17, design 3, prompt 1, speckit 8, which sums to the README's `Forty-four commands ship in six groups` at `README.md:599`; `local-skilled-alignment.md` sits at the tree root and is not counted in the six groups.\n56: - `.skilled/commands/create/README.txt:57` names `/create:sk-skill <skill-name> [operation] [type] [--path <dir>] [--chained] [:auto|:confirm]`, and `:88` maps `sk-skill.md` to `/create:sk-skill`; both agree with `README.md:269` and `:603`.\n57: - `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/README.md:67` names the same thirteen `/create:*` commands including `/create:sk-skill`, and `:194` answers the how-do-I question with the same name.\n58: - `.opencode/commands/create/sk-skill.md` and `.claude/commands/create/sk-skill.md` exist under the same name, so the two runtime command trees that mirror this group carry the renamed file rather than a stale `skill.md`.\n59: - `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt:28` restarts the workflow with `@markdown /create:sk-skill ...`, the exact name the README now gives.\n60: \n61: ## Edge Cases\n62: \n63: - Iteration numbering: this is the lineage's first iteration (the state log held only the run-initialized config row), so `iteration-001.md` is correct.\n64: - Diff base direction: the scope file prescribes a two-dot `origin/main..1c3d62def5a` README diff. The branch merged `origin/main` at `2b946c9e842`, so the endpoint diff is the branch's own rename and not main's movement; a merge-base-only diff would have hidden nothing because the file's two endpoints differ only in the rename.\n65: - Pre-existing prose: `README.md:599-611` count and group sentences predate this branch. They are context for the changed Create row, not branch findings; the two changed lines do not alter any count.\n66: - The changed line at `:269` also names eight other create commands. Each was resolved individually, because a rename that repaired one name could still leave a sibling broken in the same sentence.\n67: - `security` lens: the changed text is inert documentation. It adds no shell invocation, no path, no secret and no trust boundary, so the lens produced no candidate; that is a clean result, not skipped coverage.\n68: - `maintainability` lens: the new spelling appears in both places that describe the skill command, and no third README sentence retains the old spelling; a future reader has one name to search.\n69: \n70: ## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n71: \n72: - **Command-name resolution:** all 44 `/group:name` tokens in `README.md` resolve to a Markdown file under `.skilled/commands`; the only README command names outside that tree are the four runtime-owned goal commands at `README.md:341` and `:613`, which are documented as runtime additions.\n73: - **Rename completeness:** the old token `/create:skill` (excluding `/create:skill-parent`) appears nowhere in `README.md`; both occurrences were updated in the same change.\n74: - **Create count:** `Create (13)` lists thirteen names and `.skilled/commands/create` holds thirteen command Markdown files (plus `README.txt` and the `assets/` folder).\n75: - **Mode support:** all thirteen create commands carry `[:auto|:confirm]` in their `argument-hint` and own both an `-auto.yaml` and a `-confirm.yaml` asset, so `README.md:269`'s \"Every one runs with `:auto` or with `:confirm`\" holds for the renamed command and its twelve siblings.\n76: - **Confirm semantics:** the renamed command's confirm workflow sets `approvals: step_by_step` and describes \"approval gates at each checkpoint\" (`create-skill-confirm.yaml:30,39-40`), matching the README's \"pause at each step\".\n77: - **Command behaviour claim:** `README.md:269` says the command \"creates or updates a skill\"; `create-skill-auto.yaml:113` sets `skill_path: .skilled/skills/` and the presentation contract offers `full-create`, `full-update`, `reference-only` and `asset-only`, so the README's scope is the shared skill tree rather than one runtime's copy.\n78: - **Doctor count:** the seventeen table rows at `README.md:646-662` match the seventeen command files in `.skilled/commands/doctor`.\n79: \n80: ## Ruled Out\n81: \n82: - **A stale second `/create:skill` reference in the README:** `grep -n \"create:skill\" README.md` returns only the two renamed lines, both already `/create:sk-skill`.\n83: - **A broken command in the changed sentence:** all nine names in the `:269` sentence and all thirteen names in the `:603` list resolve to existing files.\n84: - **A wrong Create count after the rename:** the heading, the list and the folder each carry thirteen entries; renaming a file did not change the count.\n85: - **A command that exists only in the source tree:** the `.opencode` and `.claude` command mirrors carry `create/sk-skill.md`, so the README name is reachable on the runtime surfaces that mirror the group.\n86: - **A stale instruction inside the renamed command:** the presentation contract, the confirm workflow's completion actions and the group index all use `/create:sk-skill`; no old name remains in the commands tree.\n87: \n88: ## Next Focus\n89: \n90: - Dimension: correctness and maintainability\n91: - Focus area: the two changed lines as claims rather than names, plus the counts and mode sentences they sit in, checked against the files they describe\n92: - Reason: traceability is swept; the remaining risk is a true-looking name attached to a false behaviour, count or mode claim\n93: - Rotation status: traceability complete; correctness, security and maintainability have a first pass and need a second read\n94: - Required evidence: per-claim file:line read with one concrete input per candidate\n95: - Recovery note: none\n96: \n97: Review verdict: PASS","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/iterations/iteration-001.md, lines 1-97\n1: # Review Iteration 001\n2: \n3: ## Dispatcher\n4: \n5: - Lineage: `docs-7`, area `docs`.\n6: - Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\n7: - Focus: traceability, with correctness, security and maintainability lenses applied to the same two changed README lines. The pass-seven operator focus is the docs area: this branch's net change to the root `README.md` against `origin/main`, where `/create:skill` was renamed `/create:sk-skill`, so every command name the README gives is checked against `.skilled/commands`. `review/review-brief-7.txt` and `review/review-scope-7.txt` were read first; this iteration covers the area they assign to `docs-7`.\n8: - Diff base: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff origin/main 1c3d62def5a -- README.md`, the command on line 1 of the scope file. It reports two lines changed, 2 insertions and 2 deletions: `README.md:269` and `README.md:603`.\n9: - `steer.md` does not exist in the lineage directory, so no lead ruling applied.\n10: - Recorded limits and the holdout rule were honoured: no prompt corpus was opened, no `git diff`/`show`/`log -p` ran over a path containing one, `score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary` was not run, and no CLI session store was read.\n11: \n12: ## Files Reviewed\n13: \n14: | File | Lines read | What was checked |\n15: |------|-----------|------------------|\n16: | `README.md` | 266-271 | The changed extending-Skilled paragraph: the renamed `/create:sk-skill` and the remaining `/create:*` names, plus the `:auto`/`:confirm` sentence |\n17: | `README.md` | 580-613 | The agent list and the whole commands section: all 44 names, the six group counts, and the changed Create list |\n18: | `README.md` | 640-663 | The Doctor table, to test the `Doctor (17)` count against real files |\n19: | `README.md` | 341 | The runtime goal-command paragraph, to confirm the four runtime-owned goal commands are outside the 44 |\n20: | `.skilled/commands/README.txt` | 1-40 | The command tree's own six-group index and counts |\n21: | `.skilled/commands/create/README.txt` | 50-95, 119-180 | The create group index rows, the command-map tree, and every example invocation of the renamed command |\n22: | `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md` | 1-40 | The renamed router's frontmatter name, description, argument hint and owned assets |\n23: | `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md` | 40-80 | The mode routing and execution targets for `:auto` and `:confirm` |\n24: | `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/README.md` | 60-70, 190-198 | The sk-doc hub's thirteen-command sentence and its how-do-I answer naming `/create:sk-skill` |\n25: \n26: Context evidence (read-only, outside the docs scope path): `.skilled/commands/**` file inventory, `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt:1,28`, `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml:113`, `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml:30,39-40`, `.opencode/commands/create/sk-skill.md`, `.claude/commands/create/sk-skill.md`.\n27: \n28: ## Findings - New\n29: \n30: ### P0 Findings\n31: \n32: None.\n33: \n34: ### P1 Findings\n35: \n36: None.\n37: \n38: ### P2 Findings\n39: \n40: None.\n41: \n42: ## Traceability Checks\n43: \n44: | Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n45: |----------|--------|----------|\n46: | `spec_code` | pass | Both changed lines name a command file that exists: `/create:sk-skill` resolves to `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md` and every other `/group:name` token in `README.md` resolves to `.skilled/commands/<group>/<name>.md` (44 of 44). The two changed lines agree with each other. |\n47: | `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | The review target has no `checklist.md` at the packet root; the pass-seven brief and scope file are the operative checklist and both were read. |\n48: | `skill_agent` | pass | The renamed command's own surfaces agree with the README name: `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md:1-13` routes `/create:sk-skill`, and `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt:1,28` presents the same name. |\n49: | `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | No agent body is in the docs scope; the command mirrors that do exist are recorded under Integration Evidence. |\n50: | `feature_catalog_code` | notApplicable | No feature-catalog claim is touched by the two changed README lines. |\n51: | `playbook_capability` | notApplicable | No manual-testing-playbook claim is touched by the two changed README lines. |\n52: \n53: ## Integration Evidence\n54: \n55: - `.skilled/commands/README.txt:21-35` gives the six-group table: create 13, deep 2, doctor 17, design 3, prompt 1, speckit 8, which sums to the README's `Forty-four commands ship in six groups` at `README.md:599`; `local-skilled-alignment.md` sits at the tree root and is not counted in the six groups.\n56: - `.skilled/commands/create/README.txt:57` names `/create:sk-skill <skill-name> [operation] [type] [--path <dir>] [--chained] [:auto|:confirm]`, and `:88` maps `sk-skill.md` to `/create:sk-skill`; both agree with `README.md:269` and `:603`.\n57: - `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/README.md:67` names the same thirteen `/create:*` commands including `/create:sk-skill`, and `:194` answers the how-do-I question with the same name.\n58: - `.opencode/commands/create/sk-skill.md` and `.claude/commands/create/sk-skill.md` exist under the same name, so the two runtime command trees that mirror this group carry the renamed file rather than a stale `skill.md`.\n59: - `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt:28` restarts the workflow with `@markdown /create:sk-skill ...`, the exact name the README now gives.\n60: \n61: ## Edge Cases\n62: \n63: - Iteration numbering: this is the lineage's first iteration (the state log held only the run-initialized config row), so `iteration-001.md` is correct.\n64: - Diff base direction: the scope file prescribes a two-dot `origin/main..1c3d62def5a` README diff. The branch merged `origin/main` at `2b946c9e842`, so the endpoint diff is the branch's own rename and not main's movement; a merge-base-only diff would have hidden nothing because the file's two endpoints differ only in the rename.\n65: - Pre-existing prose: `README.md:599-611` count and group sentences predate this branch. They are context for the changed Create row, not branch findings; the two changed lines do not alter any count.\n66: - The changed line at `:269` also names eight other create commands. Each was resolved individually, because a rename that repaired one name could still leave a sibling broken in the same sentence.\n67: - `security` lens: the changed text is inert documentation. It adds no shell invocation, no path, no secret and no trust boundary, so the lens produced no candidate; that is a clean result, not skipped coverage.\n68: - `maintainability` lens: the new spelling appears in both places that describe the skill command, and no third README sentence retains the old spelling; a future reader has one name to search.\n69: \n70: ## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n71: \n72: - **Command-name resolution:** all 44 `/group:name` tokens in `README.md` resolve to a Markdown file under `.skilled/commands`; the only README command names outside that tree are the four runtime-owned goal commands at `README.md:341` and `:613`, which are documented as runtime additions.\n73: - **Rename completeness:** the old token `/create:skill` (excluding `/create:skill-parent`) appears nowhere in `README.md`; both occurrences were updated in the same change.\n74: - **Create count:** `Create (13)` lists thirteen names and `.skilled/commands/create` holds thirteen command Markdown files (plus `README.txt` and the `assets/` folder).\n75: - **Mode support:** all thirteen create commands carry `[:auto|:confirm]` in their `argument-hint` and own both an `-auto.yaml` and a `-confirm.yaml` asset, so `README.md:269`'s \"Every one runs with `:auto` or with `:confirm`\" holds for the renamed command and its twelve siblings.\n76: - **Confirm semantics:** the renamed command's confirm workflow sets `approvals: step_by_step` and describes \"approval gates at each checkpoint\" (`create-skill-confirm.yaml:30,39-40`), matching the README's \"pause at each step\".\n77: - **Command behaviour claim:** `README.md:269` says the command \"creates or updates a skill\"; `create-skill-auto.yaml:113` sets `skill_path: .skilled/skills/` and the presentation contract offers `full-create`, `full-update`, `reference-only` and `asset-only`, so the README's scope is the shared skill tree rather than one runtime's copy.\n78: - **Doctor count:** the seventeen table rows at `README.md:646-662` match the seventeen command files in `.skilled/commands/doctor`.\n79: \n80: ## Ruled Out\n81: \n82: - **A stale second `/create:skill` reference in the README:** `grep -n \"create:skill\" README.md` returns only the two renamed lines, both already `/create:sk-skill`.\n83: - **A broken command in the changed sentence:** all nine names in the `:269` sentence and all thirteen names in the `:603` list resolve to existing files.\n84: - **A wrong Create count after the rename:** the heading, the list and the folder each carry thirteen entries; renaming a file did not change the count.\n85: - **A command that exists only in the source tree:** the `.opencode` and `.claude` command mirrors carry `create/sk-skill.md`, so the README name is reachable on the runtime surfaces that mirror the group.\n86: - **A stale instruction inside the renamed command:** the presentation contract, the confirm workflow's completion actions and the group index all use `/create:sk-skill`; no old name remains in the commands tree.\n87: \n88: ## Next Focus\n89: \n90: - Dimension: correctness and maintainability\n91: - Focus area: the two changed lines as claims rather than names, plus the counts and mode sentences they sit in, checked against the files they describe\n92: - Reason: traceability is swept; the remaining risk is a true-looking name attached to a false behaviour, count or mode claim\n93: - Rotation status: traceability complete; correctness, security and maintainability have a first pass and need a second read\n94: - Required evidence: per-claim file:line read with one concrete input per candidate\n95: - Recovery note: none\n96: \n97: Review verdict: PASS"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/iterations/iteration-001.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794847625177,"end":1794847625540}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794847626968,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"id":"prt_1e54156d8001Pd7PSN7k4xiRwv","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e5413b3a001XRM9GBa5XaIrwU","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"47f4fc96f048c942ef2c3edfa54254851e6bf827","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":1761,"output":191,"reasoning":66,"cache":{"read":41472,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794847630122,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"id":"prt_1e541632a001pDTZv6Z5t1HWli","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e54156dd001wpWJGBQrrdimhp","type":"step-start","snapshot":"47f4fc96f048c942ef2c3edfa54254851e6bf827"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794847631444,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e541673b001cDsy1MCLVSOc6y","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e54156dd001wpWJGBQrrdimhp","type":"tool","id":"call_3562074c18be4c60ae970d39","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md, lines 1-471\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review State Log Records\n3: description: JSONL state-log record schemas (config, iteration, event, lineage) and the Review Depth Schema v2 for the deep review loop.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep review state jsonl\"\n6:   - \"review jsonl record schemas\"\n7:   - \"review depth schema\"\n8:   - \"review traceability checks\"\n9:   - \"review graph events\"\n10: importance_tier: important\n11: contextType: implementation\n12: version: 1.11.4.0\n13: ---\n14: \n15: # Deep Review State Log Records\n16: \n17: Open this when you are writing or auditing `deep-review-state.jsonl`, the append-only source of truth for a review run, and need the record shape the reducer expects.\n18: \n19: ---\n20: \n21: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n22: \n23: ### Purpose\n24: \n25: This reference defines the append-only JSONL records that preserve deep-review run state. It covers config, iteration, event, lineage, graph, verdict, traceability, and Review Depth Schema v2 records so reducers and validators can replay the loop deterministically.\n26: \n27: ### When to Use\n28: \n29: - Validating `deep-review-state.jsonl` shape before changing reducers, dashboards, or workflow emission.\n30: - Debugging malformed state records, blocked-stop events, graph convergence events, or lineage fields.\n31: - Adding or checking Review Depth Schema v2 target selection, search coverage, and ledger fields.\n32: - Confirming which fields are required before writing iteration, synthesis, pause, or recovery events.\n33: \n34: ### Key Sources\n35: \n36: | Source | Purpose |\n37: |--------|---------|\n38: | Config record | Establishes session identity, lineage, thresholds, and spec folder routing. |\n39: | Iteration record | Captures focus, reviewed files, findings, convergence ratios, and graph events. |\n40: | Event records | Persist synthesis, blocked-stop, graph convergence, pause, and stuck-recovery decisions. |\n41: | Review Depth Schema v2 | Adds target selection, search coverage, and ledger proof for deeper review iterations. |\n42: \n43: ---\n44: \n45: ## 2. STATE LOG (DEEP-REVIEW-STATE.JSONL)\n46: \n47: Append-only JSON Lines file. One JSON object per line.\n48: \n49: While the mode's authority record still names the legacy writer (`authority-deep-review.json`, state `legacy_authoritative`), this file is the authoritative target the workflow appends to and no ledger backs it. Once that record moves to `new_authoritative_reversible` or `new_authoritative_final` with `selectedWriter: \"dark\"`, the ledger becomes authoritative and the append gateway refreshes this file as a projection of it. The projection folds only the registered stems, and a refresh that would replace an existing config row while dropping any of its keys is refused with `ATTRIBUTION_COLLAPSE` before any bytes are written. The registered stems, the producer census, and what a refresh can and cannot reproduce are in `state-format.md` section 11.\n50: \n51: ### Line 1: Config Record\n52: \n53: ```json\n54: {\"type\":\"config\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"topic\":\"...\",\"reviewTarget\":\"...\",\"sessionId\":\"rvw-...\",\"parentSessionId\":null,\"lineageMode\":\"new\",\"generation\":1,\"continuedFromRun\":null,\"maxIterations\":7,\"convergenceThreshold\":0.10,\"createdAt\":\"2026-03-24T14:00:00Z\",\"specFolder\":\"...\"}\n55: ```\n56: \n57: The projected variant of this row is thin: only `type`, `topic`, `maxIterations`, `generation`, and `timestamp` come back from a ledger refresh. The remaining keys exist only in the row the workflow writes at init.\n58: \n59: ### Iteration Records\n60: \n61: ```json\n62: {\n63:   \"type\": \"iteration\", \"mode\": \"review\", \"iteration\": 3, \"status\": \"complete\",\n64:   \"focus\": \"D3 Traceability - skill/runtime alignment\",\n65:   \"dimensions\": [\"traceability\", \"maintainability\"],\n66:   \"filesReviewed\": [\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/README.md\"],\n67:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-03T12-00-00Z\",\n68:   \"parentSessionId\": null,\n69:   \"lineageMode\": \"resume\",\n70:   \"generation\": 1,\n71:   \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n72:   \"findingsCount\": 4,\n73:   \"findingsSummary\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 3 },\n74:   \"findingsNew\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 1 },\n75:   \"findingDetails\": [\n76:     {\n77:       \"id\": \"P1-001\",\n78:       \"severity\": \"P1\",\n79:       \"title\": \"Missing consumer update\",\n80:       \"dimension\": \"correctness\",\n81:       \"file\": \"path/to/file.ts:42\",\n82:       \"evidence\": \"Observed consumer still reads the old field.\",\n83:       \"recommendation\": \"Update the consumer and add verification.\",\n84:       \"disposition\": \"active\",\n85:       \"findingClass\": \"cross-consumer\",\n86:       \"scopeProof\": \"rg evidence covering producers and consumers\",\n87:       \"affectedSurfaceHints\": [\"producer/helper\", \"consumer/status\"]\n88:     }\n89:   ],\n90:   \"newFindingsRatio\": 0.32,\n91:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-24T14:30:00Z\", \"durationMs\": 52000\n92: }\n93: ```\n94: \n95: **Required fields:** `type`, `mode`, `iteration`, `status`, `focus`, `dimensions`, `filesReviewed`, `findingsCount`, `findingsSummary`, `findingsNew`, `findingDetails`, `newFindingsRatio`, `sessionId`, `generation`, `lineageMode`, `timestamp`, `durationMs`\n96: \n97: **Legacy field:** `run`, the older name for `iteration`. Readers still accept it and the fan-out stop-policy validator does not; new records write `iteration`. Event records keep their own `run` field.\n98: \n99: **Optional fields:** `parentSessionId`, `continuedFromRun`, `findingsRefined`, `findingRefs`, `traceabilityChecks`, `coverage`, `noveltyJustification`, `ruledOut`, `focusTrack`, `scoreEstimate`, `segment`, `convergenceSignals`, `graphEvents`\n100: \n101: | Required Field | Type | Description |\n102: |---------------|------|-------------|\n103: | mode | `\"review\"` | Session mode discriminator |\n104: | dimensions | string[] | Review dimensions addressed this iteration |\n105: | filesReviewed | string[] | Files examined |\n106: | sessionId | string | Current lineage session identifier |\n107: | generation | number | Lineage generation number |\n108: | lineageMode | string | Lifecycle mode used for this run |\n109: | findingsSummary | object | Total active findings: `{ P0, P1, P2 }` |\n110: | findingsNew | object | Net-new findings this iteration: `{ P0, P1, P2 }` |\n111: | findingDetails | array | Active findings with `id`, `severity`, `title`, `dimension`, `file`, `evidence`, `recommendation`, `disposition`, `findingClass`, `scopeProof`, and `affectedSurfaceHints`, use `[]` when there are no findings |\n112: | newFindingsRatio | number | Severity-weighted new findings ratio (0.0-1.0) |\n113: \n114: ### Convergence Signals\n115: \n116: | Signal | Weight | Description |\n117: |--------|--------|-------------|\n118: | rollingAvg | 0.30 | Rolling average of severity-weighted new findings |\n119: | madScore | 0.25 | Noise-floor test against MAD-derived churn |\n120: | dimensionCoverage | 0.45 | Required dimension + protocol coverage stability |\n121: | compositeStop | -- | Weighted stop score (stop if > 0.60) |\n122: \n123: **Severity math:** `refinementMultiplier: 0.5`, `p0OverrideMinRatio: 0.50`, `noFindingsRatio: 0.0`\n124: \n125: ### Graph Events\n126: \n127: The optional `graphEvents` array records coverage graph mutations emitted by a review iteration. The workflow projects them into graph nodes and edges, and the runtime upsert script (`runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs`) persists them into `deep-loop-graph.sqlite`, where they become the source of truth for graph-assisted convergence, hotspot saturation, and blocked-stop evidence.\n128: \n129: ```json\n130: {\n131:   \"type\": \"iteration\", \"mode\": \"review\", \"iteration\": 4, \"status\": \"complete\",\n132:   \"focus\": \"correctness\",\n133:   \"dimensions\": [\"correctness\"],\n134:   \"filesReviewed\": [\"src/api/session.ts\"],\n135:   \"findingsSummary\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 0 },\n136:   \"findingsNew\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 0 },\n137:   \"newFindingsRatio\": 0.18,\n138:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-03-24T10-00-00Z\",\n139:   \"generation\": 1,\n140:   \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n141:   \"graphEvents\": [\n142:     { \"type\": \"dimension\", \"id\": \"d-correctness\", \"label\": \"correctness\" },\n143:     { \"type\": \"file\", \"id\": \"file-session-ts\", \"label\": \"src/api/session.ts\" },\n144:     { \"type\": \"finding\", \"id\": \"f-001\", \"label\": \"Missing CSRF token check on session POST\" },\n145:     { \"type\": \"evidence\", \"id\": \"ev-001\", \"label\": \"src/api/session.ts:42\" },\n146:     { \"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e-in-dim-f-001\", \"relation\": \"IN_DIMENSION\", \"source\": \"f-001\", \"target\": \"d-correctness\" },\n147:     { \"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e-in-file-f-001\", \"relation\": \"IN_FILE\", \"source\": \"f-001\", \"target\": \"file-session-ts\" },\n148:     { \"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e-evidence-f-001\", \"relation\": \"EVIDENCE_FOR\", \"source\": \"ev-001\", \"target\": \"f-001\" }\n149:   ],\n150:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-24T10:12:00Z\",\n151:   \"durationMs\": 51000\n152: }\n153: ```\n154: \n155: #### Event payload shape\n156: \n157: | Field | Type | Required | Description |\n158: |-------|------|----------|-------------|\n159: | type | `\"dimension\"` \\| `\"file\"` \\| `\"finding\"` \\| `\"evidence\"` \\| `\"remediation\"` \\| `\"edge\"` | Yes | Review-loop node kind or the literal `\"edge\"` for relation rows |\n160: | id | string | Yes | Caller-chosen logical id. Must be unique **within** a single `(specFolder, loopType, sessionId)` namespace, see Namespace Rules below |\n161: | label | string | Yes | Human-readable name/caption (dimension, path, finding title, evidence anchor, etc.) |\n162: | relation | `\"COVERS\"` \\| `\"EVIDENCE_FOR\"` \\| `\"CONTRADICTS\"` \\| `\"RESOLVES\"` \\| `\"CONFIRMS\"` \\| `\"ESCALATES\"` \\| `\"IN_DIMENSION\"` \\| `\"IN_FILE\"` | edges only | Review relation type. Required when `type == \"edge\"` |\n163: | source | string | edges only | `id` of the source node inside the current namespace |\n164: | target | string | edges only | `id` of the target node inside the current namespace. Self-loops are rejected by the upsert handler |\n165: | metadata | object | No | Optional free-form metadata persisted alongside the row (e.g. `{ \"hotspot_score\": 2 }`) |\n166: \n167: #### Namespace Rules (REQ-028, REQ-029)\n168: \n169: `graphEvents` entries are scoped by the session that emits them. The coverage graph DB uses a composite primary key of `(spec_folder, loop_type, session_id, id)`, so two independent review sessions in the same spec folder MAY reuse the same logical `id` without collision, each session gets its own row.\n170: \n171: Concrete obligations for producers:\n172: \n173: 1. **Session-local uniqueness**: within one session, an `id` must resolve to exactly one node (or edge) for its entire lifetime. Re-emitting the same `id` is an upsert against the existing row in that session only.\n174: 2. **No cross-session global uniqueness requirement**: callers MUST NOT prefix ids with the session id or random salt to \"avoid collisions\". The DB layer handles namespace isolation. Salting ids only makes provenance harder to read.\n175: 3. **Edge source/target locality**: `source` and `target` in an edge event must name nodes already present in the same namespace. Cross-session edges are not a supported shape.\n176: 4. **Persistence gate**: the reducer refuses to roll graph events forward when a record is missing `sessionId` on the surrounding iteration record, because the DB cannot route the write.\n177: \n178: The composite key `(spec_folder, loop_type, session_id, id)` in `runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-db.ts` enforces this contract directly: two sessions upsert identical node and edge ids, and both rows survive independently.\n179: \n180: ### Synthesis Event\n181: \n182: ```json\n183: {\n184:   \"type\": \"event\", \"event\": \"synthesis_complete\", \"mode\": \"review\",\n185:   \"totalIterations\": 6, \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n186:   \"activeP0\": 0, \"activeP1\": 0, \"activeP2\": 2,\n187:   \"dimensionCoverage\": 1.0, \"stopReason\": \"composite_converged\",\n188:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-24T15:02:00Z\"\n189: }\n190: ```\n191: \n192: **Required:** `type`, `event`, `mode`, `totalIterations`, `verdict`, `activeP0`, `activeP1`, `activeP2`, `dimensionCoverage`, `stopReason`, `timestamp`\n193: \n194: ### Blocked-Stop Event\n195: \n196: When the review legal-stop decision tree returns `blocked`, append a first-class `blocked_stop` event instead of silently overriding STOP to CONTINUE.\n197: \n198: ```json\n199: {\n200:   \"type\": \"event\",\n201:   \"event\": \"blocked_stop\",\n202:   \"mode\": \"review\",\n203:   \"run\": 4,\n204:   \"blockedBy\": [\"dimensionCoverageGate\", \"p0ResolutionGate\"],\n205:   \"gateResults\": {\n206:     \"convergenceGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"score\": 0.72 },\n207:     \"dimensionCoverageGate\": {\n208:       \"pass\": false,\n209:       \"covered\": [\"correctness\", \"security\"],\n210:       \"missing\": [\"traceability\", \"maintainability\"]\n211:     },\n212:     \"p0ResolutionGate\": { \"pass\": false, \"activeP0\": 1 },\n213:     \"evidenceDensityGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"avgEvidencePerFinding\": 1.5 },\n214:     \"hotspotSaturationGate\": { \"pass\": true },\n215:     \"claimAdjudicationGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"activeP0P1\": 2 },\n216:     \"fixCompletenessReplayGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"securitySensitive\": false, \"requiredRows\": 0, \"passingRows\": 0 },\n217:     \"candidateCoverageGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"searchDebt\": [], \"missing\": [] },\n218:     \"graphlessFallbackGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"mode\": \"graph_available\", \"missing\": [], \"unavailabilityReason\": \"\" }\n219:   },\n220:   \"recoveryStrategy\": \"Cover the missing review dimensions, then resolve the active P0.\",\n221:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-11T09:45:00Z\",\n222:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-11T09-00-00Z\",\n223:   \"generation\": 1\n224: }\n225: ```\n226: \n227: `gateResults` carries the full 9-gate set emitted by `step_emit_blocked_stop` in `deep-review.yaml`: `convergenceGate`, `dimensionCoverageGate`, `p0ResolutionGate`, `evidenceDensityGate`, `hotspotSaturationGate`, `claimAdjudicationGate`, `fixCompletenessReplayGate`, `candidateCoverageGate`, and `graphlessFallbackGate`. The last two are v2-rollout gates that pass trivially when the review-depth-v2 search path is inactive. See `../convergence/convergence.md` §1 for the authoritative shape.\n228: \n229: **Required:** `type`, `event`, `mode`, `run`, `blockedBy`, `gateResults`, `recoveryStrategy`, `timestamp`, `sessionId`, `generation`\n230: \n231: ### Graph Convergence Event\n232: \n233: Before the inline 3-signal review vote is allowed to finalize STOP, the workflow must append a `graph_convergence` event for the current review lineage.\n234: \n235: ```json\n236: {\n237:   \"type\": \"event\",\n238:   \"event\": \"graph_convergence\",\n239:   \"mode\": \"review\",\n240:   \"run\": 4,\n241:   \"decision\": \"STOP_ALLOWED\",\n242:   \"signals\": {\n243:     \"dimensionCoverage\": 1,\n244:     \"findingStability\": 0.88,\n245:     \"p0ResolutionRate\": 1,\n246:     \"evidenceDensity\": 1.4,\n247:     \"hotspotSaturation\": 0.75\n248:   },\n249:   \"blockers\": [],\n250:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-11T09:44:00Z\",\n251:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-11T09-00-00Z\",\n252:   \"generation\": 1\n253: }\n254: ```\n255: \n256: **Required:** `type`, `event`, `mode`, `run`, `decision`, `signals`, `blockers`, `timestamp`, `sessionId`, `generation`\n257: \n258: **Decision enum:** `CONTINUE`, `STOP_ALLOWED`, `STOP_BLOCKED`\n259: \n260: **Combined-stop rule:** Final STOP is legal only when the inline review convergence decision says STOP and the latest `graph_convergence.decision == \"STOP_ALLOWED\"`. If the latest graph decision is `STOP_BLOCKED`, set `stop_blocked=true`, emit `blocked_stop`, and continue recovery instead of stopping. If the latest graph decision is `CONTINUE`, downgrade the inline STOP candidate to CONTINUE.\n261: \n262: ### Normalized Pause and Recovery Events\n263: \n264: Pause and recovery events MUST use the frozen shared stop-reason enum at emission time:\n265: \n266: `converged`, `maxIterationsReached`, `blockedStop`, `stuckRecovery`, `error`, `manualStop`, `userPaused`, `maxDurationReached`\n267: \n268: Raw `paused` and `stuck_recovery` labels are not legal persisted event names in the review JSONL contract. The workflow must rewrite them before appending JSONL rows.\n269: \n270: ```json\n271: {\n272:   \"type\": \"event\",\n273:   \"event\": \"userPaused\",\n274:   \"mode\": \"review\",\n275:   \"stopReason\": \"userPaused\",\n276:   \"reason\": \"sentinel file detected\",\n277:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-11T09:32:00Z\",\n278:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-11T09-00-00Z\",\n279:   \"generation\": 1\n280: }\n281: ```\n282: \n283: ```json\n284: {\n285:   \"type\": \"event\",\n286:   \"event\": \"stuckRecovery\",\n287:   \"mode\": \"review\",\n288:   \"stopReason\": \"stuckRecovery\",\n289:   \"fromIteration\": 5,\n290:   \"strategy\": \"Traceability protocol replay: re-run unresolved core or overlay checks\",\n291:   \"targetDimension\": \"traceability\",\n292:   \"outcome\": \"pending\",\n293:   \"reason\": \"Recovery path activated after repeated no-progress iterations\",\n294:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-11T09:40:00Z\",\n295:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-11T09-00-00Z\",\n296:   \"generation\": 1\n297: }\n298: ```\n299: \n300: **Emission rule:** If runtime logic first identifies a raw `paused` or `stuck_recovery` condition, the workflow MUST normalize it to `userPaused` or `stuckRecovery` before writing the JSONL line. Reducers and dashboards may assume persisted event names are already normalized.\n301: \n302: ### Verdict Rules\n303: \n304: | Verdict | Condition | Next Command |\n305: |---------|-----------|--------------|\n306: | FAIL | `activeP0 > 0` OR quality gate failure | `/speckit:plan` |\n307: | CONDITIONAL | `activeP0 == 0` AND (`activeP1 > 0` OR open search debt) | `/speckit:plan` |\n308: | PASS | `activeP0 == 0` AND `activeP1 == 0` AND no open search debt | `/create:changelog` |\n309: \n310: When `activeP2 > 0` on PASS, set `hasAdvisories: true`.\n311: \n312: ### traceabilityChecks Schema\n313: \n314: ```json\n315: {\n316:   \"traceabilityChecks\": {\n317:     \"summary\": {\n318:       \"required\": 2, \"executed\": 3, \"pass\": 1, \"partial\": 1,\n319:       \"fail\": 1, \"blocked\": 0, \"notApplicable\": 0, \"gatingFailures\": 1\n320:     },\n321:     \"results\": [{\n322:       \"protocolId\": \"spec_code\", \"status\": \"fail\", \"gateClass\": \"hard\",\n323:       \"applicable\": true, \"counts\": { \"pass\": 0, \"partial\": 0, \"fail\": 1 },\n324:       \"evidence\": [\"README.md:48\"], \"findingRefs\": [\"F004\"],\n325:       \"summary\": \"README claimed the old report contract.\"\n326:     }]\n327:   }\n328: }\n329: ```\n330: \n331: | Field | Type | Required | Description |\n332: |-------|------|----------|-------------|\n333: | summary.required / executed / pass / partial / fail / blocked / notApplicable | number | Yes | Protocol execution counts |\n334: | summary.gatingFailures | number | Yes | Hard-gate failures blocking STOP |\n335: | results[].protocolId | string | Yes | Canonical protocol identifier |\n336: | results[].status | string | Yes | `pass`, `partial`, `fail`, `blocked`, `notApplicable` |\n337: | results[].gateClass | string | Yes | `hard` or `advisory` |\n338: | results[].applicable | boolean | Yes | Whether the protocol applied |\n339: | results[].counts | object | Yes | Protocol-local summary counts |\n340: | results[].evidence | string[] | No | Supporting file:line refs |\n341: | results[].findingRefs | string[] | No | Related finding identifiers |\n342: | results[].summary | string | Yes | Human-readable one-line result |\n343: \n344: ### Validation Rules\n345: \n346: - Each line must be valid JSON with a `type` field\n347: - `mode` must be `\"review\"` on all iteration and synthesis records\n348: - `iteration` values must be sequential. `newFindingsRatio` must be 0.0-1.0\n349: - `findingsSummary` and `findingsNew` must each contain `P0`, `P1`, `P2` keys\n350: - `findingDetails` must be an array. Each active item must include `findingClass`, `scopeProof`, and `affectedSurfaceHints`\n351: \n352: ---\n353: \n354: ## 3. REVIEW DEPTH SCHEMA (V2)\n355: \n356: `reviewDepthSchemaVersion: 2` is the discriminator for the v2 search-depth contract. Absent values, `null`, or any value other than `2` mean v1 legacy: readers keep today's behavior, and validator hard enforcement applies only when the discriminator is present.\n357: \n358: Frozen v2 contract:\n359: \n360: Top-level review iteration fields when `reviewDepthSchemaVersion: 2`:\n361: - `reviewDepthSchemaVersion: 2`, discriminator\n362: - `reviewDepthApplicability`, `{ scopeClass: 'trivial'|'standard'|'complex', enforcement: 'strict'|'warn'|'skip', reason: string, evidenceRefs: string[] }`\n363: - `targetSelection`, `{ selectedTargets: string[], selectionReason: string, discoveryMethods: string[], omittedHighRiskTargets: string[], graphStatus: 'available'|'unavailable'|'partial', semanticSearchStatus: 'available'|'unavailable'|'partial', evidenceRefs: string[] }`\n364: - `searchCoverage`, `{ requiredBugClasses: string[], covered: string[], ruledOut: string[], deferred: string[], blocked: string[], graphCoverageMode: 'graph'|'graphless_fallback'|'unavailable_blocked' }`\n365: - `searchLedger[]`, array of ledger rows\n366: \n367: Ledger row fields:\n368: - Required: `id, dimension, targetRefs, bugClass, disposition, rationale`\n369: - `hypothesis` (string) OR `invariant` (string), at least one\n370: - `searchActions[]`, `{ method: string, queryOrPath: string, result: string, evidenceRefs: string[] }`\n371: - Disposition-specific link (exactly one):\n372:   - `finding` → `linkedFindingId` (must reference an id present in `findingDetails[]`)\n373:   - `ruled_out` → `ruledOutReason`\n374:   - `deferred` → `deferredReason`\n375:   - `blocked` → `blockedReason`\n376:   - `not_applicable` → `notApplicableReason`\n377: \n378: Trivial-scope exemption: when `reviewDepthApplicability.scopeClass === 'trivial'` AND `reviewDepthApplicability.enforcement === 'skip'`, ledger may be `[]` with cited scope proof in `reviewDepthApplicability.evidenceRefs`.\n379: \n380: ### Applicability\n381: \n382: | Field | Type | Required | Semantics |\n383: |-------|------|----------|-----------|\n384: | `scopeClass` | `'trivial' \\| 'standard' \\| 'complex'` | Yes | Classifies how much depth proof the review target warrants. |\n385: | `enforcement` | `'strict' \\| 'warn' \\| 'skip'` | Yes | `strict` means v2 validators fail shallow records, `warn` emits advisory rollout feedback, `skip` is valid only for trivial scope with proof. |\n386: | `reason` | string | Yes | Human-readable justification for the chosen scope/enforcement pair. |\n387: | `evidenceRefs` | string[] | Yes | File/path refs proving scope classification, required even for skipped trivial ledgers. |\n388: \n389: ### Target Selection\n390: \n391: | Field | Type | Required | Semantics |\n392: |-------|------|----------|-----------|\n393: | `selectedTargets` | string[] | Yes | Files, folders, specs, or surfaces actually searched this iteration. |\n394: | `selectionReason` | string | Yes | Why these targets were highest-value for the dimension or bug class. |\n395: | `discoveryMethods` | string[] | Yes | Methods such as direct read, exact search, semantic search, graph query, producer trace, consumer trace, or negative-test search. |\n396: | `omittedHighRiskTargets` | string[] | Yes | High-risk targets not searched, use `[]` when none were identified. |\n397: | `graphStatus` | `'available' \\| 'unavailable' \\| 'partial'` | Yes | Code/coverage graph availability for this iteration's target selection. |\n398: | `semanticSearchStatus` | `'available' \\| 'unavailable' \\| 'partial'` | Yes | Semantic/code search availability for this iteration. |\n399: | `evidenceRefs` | string[] | Yes | Evidence for target selection and omitted-target claims. |\n400: \n401: ### Search Coverage\n402: \n403: | Field | Type | Required | Semantics |\n404: |-------|------|----------|-----------|\n405: | `requiredBugClasses` | string[] | Yes | Bug classes or invariant families that should be searched for this scope. |\n406: | `covered` | string[] | Yes | Required classes searched with conclusive finding or clean proof. |\n407: | `ruledOut` | string[] | Yes | Required classes searched and explicitly ruled out. |\n408: | `deferred` | string[] | Yes | Required classes postponed with a reason in ledger rows. |\n409: | `blocked` | string[] | Yes | Required classes blocked by missing access, graph/search outage, ambiguity, or scope conflict. |\n410: | `graphCoverageMode` | `'graph' \\| 'graphless_fallback' \\| 'unavailable_blocked'` | Yes | `graph` uses graph evidence, `graphless_fallback` uses direct text/JSON proof, and `unavailable_blocked` records insufficient fallback proof. |\n411: \n412: ### Search Ledger\n413: \n414: | Field | Type | Required | Semantics |\n415: |-------|------|----------|-----------|\n416: | `id` | string | Yes | Stable ledger-row id unique within the iteration record. |\n417: | `dimension` | string | Yes | Review dimension addressed by this row. |\n418: | `targetRefs` | string[] | Yes | Targets searched, should overlap `targetSelection.selectedTargets`. |\n419: | `bugClass` | string | Yes | Candidate bug class or invariant family. |\n420: | `hypothesis` / `invariant` | string | Conditional | At least one must be present and non-empty. |\n421: | `searchActions` | array | Yes | Each action has `method`, `queryOrPath`, `result`, and `evidenceRefs`. |\n422: | `disposition` | string | Yes | One of `finding`, `ruled_out`, `deferred`, `blocked`, `not_applicable`. |\n423: | `rationale` | string | Yes | Why this disposition follows from the evidence. |\n424: \n425: | Disposition | Required link | Rule |\n426: |-------------|---------------|------|\n427: | `finding` | `linkedFindingId` | Must reference an `id` present in `findingDetails[]`. |\n428: | `ruled_out` | `ruledOutReason` | Must explain the negative evidence. |\n429: | `deferred` | `deferredReason` | Must explain why later search is acceptable. |\n430: | `blocked` | `blockedReason` | Must name the blocker and expected recovery path. |\n431: | `not_applicable` | `notApplicableReason` | Must explain why the bug class does not apply to this target. |\n432: \n433: Representative v2 record:\n434: \n435: ```json\n436: {\n437:   \"type\": \"iteration\",\n438:   \"mode\": \"review\",\n439:   \"iteration\": 3,\n440:   \"run\": 3,\n441:   \"status\": \"complete\",\n442:   \"dimensions\": [\"correctness\"],\n443:   \"filesReviewed\": [\"src/review-target.ts\"],\n444:   \"findingsSummary\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 0, \"P2\": 0 },\n445:   \"findingsNew\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 0, \"P2\": 0 },\n446:   \"findingDetails\": [],\n447:   \"newFindingsRatio\": 0,\n448:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-example\",\n449:   \"generation\": 1,\n450:   \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n451:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-22T00:00:00Z\",\n452:   \"durationMs\": 120000,\n453:   \"reviewDepthSchemaVersion\": 2,\n454:   \"reviewDepthApplicability\": { \"scopeClass\": \"standard\", \"enforcement\": \"strict\", \"reason\": \"non-trivial state transition target\", \"evidenceRefs\": [\"src/review-target.ts:1\"] },\n455:   \"targetSelection\": { \"selectedTargets\": [\"src/review-target.ts\"], \"selectionReason\": \"state mutation path under review\", \"discoveryMethods\": [\"direct_read\", \"exact_search\"], \"omittedHighRiskTargets\": [], \"graphStatus\": \"unavailable\", \"semanticSearchStatus\": \"partial\", \"evidenceRefs\": [\"src/review-target.ts:1\"] },\n456:   \"searchCoverage\": { \"requiredBugClasses\": [\"state_transition\"], \"covered\": [], \"ruledOut\": [\"state_transition\"], \"deferred\": [], \"blocked\": [], \"graphCoverageMode\": \"graphless_fallback\" },\n457:   \"searchLedger\": [{ \"id\": \"SL-001\", \"dimension\": \"correctness\", \"targetRefs\": [\"src/review-target.ts\"], \"bugClass\": \"state_transition\", \"hypothesis\": \"state transition can skip validation\", \"searchActions\": [{ \"method\": \"direct_read\", \"queryOrPath\": \"src/review-target.ts\", \"result\": \"validation guard present on all branches\", \"evidenceRefs\": [\"src/review-target.ts:42\"] }], \"disposition\": \"ruled_out\", \"rationale\": \"all mutation branches call the validator\", \"ruledOutReason\": \"guard verified by direct read\" }]\n458: }\n459: ```\n460: \n461: ### Compatibility and Downstream Obligations\n462: \n463: | Record Shape | Reader Behavior | Validator Behavior |\n464: |--------------|-----------------|--------------------|\n465: | v1 legacy: discriminator absent or not `2` | Parse as today's iteration record. | A validator may warn, but must not hard-fail only because v2 fields are absent. |\n466: | v2 trivial+skip | Parse v2 applicability, `searchLedger: []` allowed with cited scope proof. | Validate `reviewDepthApplicability.evidenceRefs`, skip ledger-depth requirements. |\n467: | v2 standard/complex | Parse v2 fields in addition to v1 required fields. | Enforce v2 shape, ledger linkage, coverage reconciliation, and evidence refs. |\n468: \n469: Reducer, dashboard, and report work must preserve and expose `candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`, `ruledOutCandidates`, `cleanSearchProof`, and `searchCoverage`. Until that work ships, these are contract obligations only. `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `deep-review-dashboard.md`, and `review-report.md` are not expected to persist them.\n470: \n471: ---","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md, lines 1-471\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review State Log Records\n3: description: JSONL state-log record schemas (config, iteration, event, lineage) and the Review Depth Schema v2 for the deep review loop.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep review state jsonl\"\n6:   - \"review jsonl record schemas\"\n7:   - \"review depth schema\"\n8:   - \"review traceability checks\"\n9:   - \"review graph events\"\n10: importance_tier: important\n11: contextType: implementation\n12: version: 1.11.4.0\n13: ---\n14: \n15: # Deep Review State Log Records\n16: \n17: Open this when you are writing or auditing `deep-review-state.jsonl`, the append-only source of truth for a review run, and need the record shape the reducer expects.\n18: \n19: ---\n20: \n21: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n22: \n23: ### Purpose\n24: \n25: This reference defines the append-only JSONL records that preserve deep-review run state. It covers config, iteration, event, lineage, graph, verdict, traceability, and Review Depth Schema v2 records so reducers and validators can replay the loop deterministically.\n26: \n27: ### When to Use\n28: \n29: - Validating `deep-review-state.jsonl` shape before changing reducers, dashboards, or workflow emission.\n30: - Debugging malformed state records, blocked-stop events, graph convergence events, or lineage fields.\n31: - Adding or checking Review Depth Schema v2 target selection, search coverage, and ledger fields.\n32: - Confirming which fields are required before writing iteration, synthesis, pause, or recovery events.\n33: \n34: ### Key Sources\n35: \n36: | Source | Purpose |\n37: |--------|---------|\n38: | Config record | Establishes session identity, lineage, thresholds, and spec folder routing. |\n39: | Iteration record | Captures focus, reviewed files, findings, convergence ratios, and graph events. |\n40: | Event records | Persist synthesis, blocked-stop, graph convergence, pause, and stuck-recovery decisions. |\n41: | Review Depth Schema v2 | Adds target selection, search coverage, and ledger proof for deeper review iterations. |\n42: \n43: ---\n44: \n45: ## 2. STATE LOG (DEEP-REVIEW-STATE.JSONL)\n46: \n47: Append-only JSON Lines file. One JSON object per line.\n48: \n49: While the mode's authority record still names the legacy writer (`authority-deep-review.json`, state `legacy_authoritative`), this file is the authoritative target the workflow appends to and no ledger backs it. Once that record moves to `new_authoritative_reversible` or `new_authoritative_final` with `selectedWriter: \"dark\"`, the ledger becomes authoritative and the append gateway refreshes this file as a projection of it. The projection folds only the registered stems, and a refresh that would replace an existing config row while dropping any of its keys is refused with `ATTRIBUTION_COLLAPSE` before any bytes are written. The registered stems, the producer census, and what a refresh can and cannot reproduce are in `state-format.md` section 11.\n50: \n51: ### Line 1: Config Record\n52: \n53: ```json\n54: {\"type\":\"config\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"topic\":\"...\",\"reviewTarget\":\"...\",\"sessionId\":\"rvw-...\",\"parentSessionId\":null,\"lineageMode\":\"new\",\"generation\":1,\"continuedFromRun\":null,\"maxIterations\":7,\"convergenceThreshold\":0.10,\"createdAt\":\"2026-03-24T14:00:00Z\",\"specFolder\":\"...\"}\n55: ```\n56: \n57: The projected variant of this row is thin: only `type`, `topic`, `maxIterations`, `generation`, and `timestamp` come back from a ledger refresh. The remaining keys exist only in the row the workflow writes at init.\n58: \n59: ### Iteration Records\n60: \n61: ```json\n62: {\n63:   \"type\": \"iteration\", \"mode\": \"review\", \"iteration\": 3, \"status\": \"complete\",\n64:   \"focus\": \"D3 Traceability - skill/runtime alignment\",\n65:   \"dimensions\": [\"traceability\", \"maintainability\"],\n66:   \"filesReviewed\": [\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/README.md\"],\n67:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-03T12-00-00Z\",\n68:   \"parentSessionId\": null,\n69:   \"lineageMode\": \"resume\",\n70:   \"generation\": 1,\n71:   \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n72:   \"findingsCount\": 4,\n73:   \"findingsSummary\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 3 },\n74:   \"findingsNew\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 1 },\n75:   \"findingDetails\": [\n76:     {\n77:       \"id\": \"P1-001\",\n78:       \"severity\": \"P1\",\n79:       \"title\": \"Missing consumer update\",\n80:       \"dimension\": \"correctness\",\n81:       \"file\": \"path/to/file.ts:42\",\n82:       \"evidence\": \"Observed consumer still reads the old field.\",\n83:       \"recommendation\": \"Update the consumer and add verification.\",\n84:       \"disposition\": \"active\",\n85:       \"findingClass\": \"cross-consumer\",\n86:       \"scopeProof\": \"rg evidence covering producers and consumers\",\n87:       \"affectedSurfaceHints\": [\"producer/helper\", \"consumer/status\"]\n88:     }\n89:   ],\n90:   \"newFindingsRatio\": 0.32,\n91:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-24T14:30:00Z\", \"durationMs\": 52000\n92: }\n93: ```\n94: \n95: **Required fields:** `type`, `mode`, `iteration`, `status`, `focus`, `dimensions`, `filesReviewed`, `findingsCount`, `findingsSummary`, `findingsNew`, `findingDetails`, `newFindingsRatio`, `sessionId`, `generation`, `lineageMode`, `timestamp`, `durationMs`\n96: \n97: **Legacy field:** `run`, the older name for `iteration`. Readers still accept it and the fan-out stop-policy validator does not; new records write `iteration`. Event records keep their own `run` field.\n98: \n99: **Optional fields:** `parentSessionId`, `continuedFromRun`, `findingsRefined`, `findingRefs`, `traceabilityChecks`, `coverage`, `noveltyJustification`, `ruledOut`, `focusTrack`, `scoreEstimate`, `segment`, `convergenceSignals`, `graphEvents`\n100: \n101: | Required Field | Type | Description |\n102: |---------------|------|-------------|\n103: | mode | `\"review\"` | Session mode discriminator |\n104: | dimensions | string[] | Review dimensions addressed this iteration |\n105: | filesReviewed | string[] | Files examined |\n106: | sessionId | string | Current lineage session identifier |\n107: | generation | number | Lineage generation number |\n108: | lineageMode | string | Lifecycle mode used for this run |\n109: | findingsSummary | object | Total active findings: `{ P0, P1, P2 }` |\n110: | findingsNew | object | Net-new findings this iteration: `{ P0, P1, P2 }` |\n111: | findingDetails | array | Active findings with `id`, `severity`, `title`, `dimension`, `file`, `evidence`, `recommendation`, `disposition`, `findingClass`, `scopeProof`, and `affectedSurfaceHints`, use `[]` when there are no findings |\n112: | newFindingsRatio | number | Severity-weighted new findings ratio (0.0-1.0) |\n113: \n114: ### Convergence Signals\n115: \n116: | Signal | Weight | Description |\n117: |--------|--------|-------------|\n118: | rollingAvg | 0.30 | Rolling average of severity-weighted new findings |\n119: | madScore | 0.25 | Noise-floor test against MAD-derived churn |\n120: | dimensionCoverage | 0.45 | Required dimension + protocol coverage stability |\n121: | compositeStop | -- | Weighted stop score (stop if > 0.60) |\n122: \n123: **Severity math:** `refinementMultiplier: 0.5`, `p0OverrideMinRatio: 0.50`, `noFindingsRatio: 0.0`\n124: \n125: ### Graph Events\n126: \n127: The optional `graphEvents` array records coverage graph mutations emitted by a review iteration. The workflow projects them into graph nodes and edges, and the runtime upsert script (`runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs`) persists them into `deep-loop-graph.sqlite`, where they become the source of truth for graph-assisted convergence, hotspot saturation, and blocked-stop evidence.\n128: \n129: ```json\n130: {\n131:   \"type\": \"iteration\", \"mode\": \"review\", \"iteration\": 4, \"status\": \"complete\",\n132:   \"focus\": \"correctness\",\n133:   \"dimensions\": [\"correctness\"],\n134:   \"filesReviewed\": [\"src/api/session.ts\"],\n135:   \"findingsSummary\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 0 },\n136:   \"findingsNew\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 0 },\n137:   \"newFindingsRatio\": 0.18,\n138:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-03-24T10-00-00Z\",\n139:   \"generation\": 1,\n140:   \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n141:   \"graphEvents\": [\n142:     { \"type\": \"dimension\", \"id\": \"d-correctness\", \"label\": \"correctness\" },\n143:     { \"type\": \"file\", \"id\": \"file-session-ts\", \"label\": \"src/api/session.ts\" },\n144:     { \"type\": \"finding\", \"id\": \"f-001\", \"label\": \"Missing CSRF token check on session POST\" },\n145:     { \"type\": \"evidence\", \"id\": \"ev-001\", \"label\": \"src/api/session.ts:42\" },\n146:     { \"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e-in-dim-f-001\", \"relation\": \"IN_DIMENSION\", \"source\": \"f-001\", \"target\": \"d-correctness\" },\n147:     { \"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e-in-file-f-001\", \"relation\": \"IN_FILE\", \"source\": \"f-001\", \"target\": \"file-session-ts\" },\n148:     { \"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e-evidence-f-001\", \"relation\": \"EVIDENCE_FOR\", \"source\": \"ev-001\", \"target\": \"f-001\" }\n149:   ],\n150:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-24T10:12:00Z\",\n151:   \"durationMs\": 51000\n152: }\n153: ```\n154: \n155: #### Event payload shape\n156: \n157: | Field | Type | Required | Description |\n158: |-------|------|----------|-------------|\n159: | type | `\"dimension\"` \\| `\"file\"` \\| `\"finding\"` \\| `\"evidence\"` \\| `\"remediation\"` \\| `\"edge\"` | Yes | Review-loop node kind or the literal `\"edge\"` for relation rows |\n160: | id | string | Yes | Caller-chosen logical id. Must be unique **within** a single `(specFolder, loopType, sessionId)` namespace, see Namespace Rules below |\n161: | label | string | Yes | Human-readable name/caption (dimension, path, finding title, evidence anchor, etc.) |\n162: | relation | `\"COVERS\"` \\| `\"EVIDENCE_FOR\"` \\| `\"CONTRADICTS\"` \\| `\"RESOLVES\"` \\| `\"CONFIRMS\"` \\| `\"ESCALATES\"` \\| `\"IN_DIMENSION\"` \\| `\"IN_FILE\"` | edges only | Review relation type. Required when `type == \"edge\"` |\n163: | source | string | edges only | `id` of the source node inside the current namespace |\n164: | target | string | edges only | `id` of the target node inside the current namespace. Self-loops are rejected by the upsert handler |\n165: | metadata | object | No | Optional free-form metadata persisted alongside the row (e.g. `{ \"hotspot_score\": 2 }`) |\n166: \n167: #### Namespace Rules (REQ-028, REQ-029)\n168: \n169: `graphEvents` entries are scoped by the session that emits them. The coverage graph DB uses a composite primary key of `(spec_folder, loop_type, session_id, id)`, so two independent review sessions in the same spec folder MAY reuse the same logical `id` without collision, each session gets its own row.\n170: \n171: Concrete obligations for producers:\n172: \n173: 1. **Session-local uniqueness**: within one session, an `id` must resolve to exactly one node (or edge) for its entire lifetime. Re-emitting the same `id` is an upsert against the existing row in that session only.\n174: 2. **No cross-session global uniqueness requirement**: callers MUST NOT prefix ids with the session id or random salt to \"avoid collisions\". The DB layer handles namespace isolation. Salting ids only makes provenance harder to read.\n175: 3. **Edge source/target locality**: `source` and `target` in an edge event must name nodes already present in the same namespace. Cross-session edges are not a supported shape.\n176: 4. **Persistence gate**: the reducer refuses to roll graph events forward when a record is missing `sessionId` on the surrounding iteration record, because the DB cannot route the write.\n177: \n178: The composite key `(spec_folder, loop_type, session_id, id)` in `runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-db.ts` enforces this contract directly: two sessions upsert identical node and edge ids, and both rows survive independently.\n179: \n180: ### Synthesis Event\n181: \n182: ```json\n183: {\n184:   \"type\": \"event\", \"event\": \"synthesis_complete\", \"mode\": \"review\",\n185:   \"totalIterations\": 6, \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n186:   \"activeP0\": 0, \"activeP1\": 0, \"activeP2\": 2,\n187:   \"dimensionCoverage\": 1.0, \"stopReason\": \"composite_converged\",\n188:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-24T15:02:00Z\"\n189: }\n190: ```\n191: \n192: **Required:** `type`, `event`, `mode`, `totalIterations`, `verdict`, `activeP0`, `activeP1`, `activeP2`, `dimensionCoverage`, `stopReason`, `timestamp`\n193: \n194: ### Blocked-Stop Event\n195: \n196: When the review legal-stop decision tree returns `blocked`, append a first-class `blocked_stop` event instead of silently overriding STOP to CONTINUE.\n197: \n198: ```json\n199: {\n200:   \"type\": \"event\",\n201:   \"event\": \"blocked_stop\",\n202:   \"mode\": \"review\",\n203:   \"run\": 4,\n204:   \"blockedBy\": [\"dimensionCoverageGate\", \"p0ResolutionGate\"],\n205:   \"gateResults\": {\n206:     \"convergenceGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"score\": 0.72 },\n207:     \"dimensionCoverageGate\": {\n208:       \"pass\": false,\n209:       \"covered\": [\"correctness\", \"security\"],\n210:       \"missing\": [\"traceability\", \"maintainability\"]\n211:     },\n212:     \"p0ResolutionGate\": { \"pass\": false, \"activeP0\": 1 },\n213:     \"evidenceDensityGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"avgEvidencePerFinding\": 1.5 },\n214:     \"hotspotSaturationGate\": { \"pass\": true },\n215:     \"claimAdjudicationGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"activeP0P1\": 2 },\n216:     \"fixCompletenessReplayGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"securitySensitive\": false, \"requiredRows\": 0, \"passingRows\": 0 },\n217:     \"candidateCoverageGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"searchDebt\": [], \"missing\": [] },\n218:     \"graphlessFallbackGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"mode\": \"graph_available\", \"missing\": [], \"unavailabilityReason\": \"\" }\n219:   },\n220:   \"recoveryStrategy\": \"Cover the missing review dimensions, then resolve the active P0.\",\n221:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-11T09:45:00Z\",\n222:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-11T09-00-00Z\",\n223:   \"generation\": 1\n224: }\n225: ```\n226: \n227: `gateResults` carries the full 9-gate set emitted by `step_emit_blocked_stop` in `deep-review.yaml`: `convergenceGate`, `dimensionCoverageGate`, `p0ResolutionGate`, `evidenceDensityGate`, `hotspotSaturationGate`, `claimAdjudicationGate`, `fixCompletenessReplayGate`, `candidateCoverageGate`, and `graphlessFallbackGate`. The last two are v2-rollout gates that pass trivially when the review-depth-v2 search path is inactive. See `../convergence/convergence.md` §1 for the authoritative shape.\n228: \n229: **Required:** `type`, `event`, `mode`, `run`, `blockedBy`, `gateResults`, `recoveryStrategy`, `timestamp`, `sessionId`, `generation`\n230: \n231: ### Graph Convergence Event\n232: \n233: Before the inline 3-signal review vote is allowed to finalize STOP, the workflow must append a `graph_convergence` event for the current review lineage.\n234: \n235: ```json\n236: {\n237:   \"type\": \"event\",\n238:   \"event\": \"graph_convergence\",\n239:   \"mode\": \"review\",\n240:   \"run\": 4,\n241:   \"decision\": \"STOP_ALLOWED\",\n242:   \"signals\": {\n243:     \"dimensionCoverage\": 1,\n244:     \"findingStability\": 0.88,\n245:     \"p0ResolutionRate\": 1,\n246:     \"evidenceDensity\": 1.4,\n247:     \"hotspotSaturation\": 0.75\n248:   },\n249:   \"blockers\": [],\n250:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-11T09:44:00Z\",\n251:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-11T09-00-00Z\",\n252:   \"generation\": 1\n253: }\n254: ```\n255: \n256: **Required:** `type`, `event`, `mode`, `run`, `decision`, `signals`, `blockers`, `timestamp`, `sessionId`, `generation`\n257: \n258: **Decision enum:** `CONTINUE`, `STOP_ALLOWED`, `STOP_BLOCKED`\n259: \n260: **Combined-stop rule:** Final STOP is legal only when the inline review convergence decision says STOP and the latest `graph_convergence.decision == \"STOP_ALLOWED\"`. If the latest graph decision is `STOP_BLOCKED`, set `stop_blocked=true`, emit `blocked_stop`, and continue recovery instead of stopping. If the latest graph decision is `CONTINUE`, downgrade the inline STOP candidate to CONTINUE.\n261: \n262: ### Normalized Pause and Recovery Events\n263: \n264: Pause and recovery events MUST use the frozen shared stop-reason enum at emission time:\n265: \n266: `converged`, `maxIterationsReached`, `blockedStop`, `stuckRecovery`, `error`, `manualStop`, `userPaused`, `maxDurationReached`\n267: \n268: Raw `paused` and `stuck_recovery` labels are not legal persisted event names in the review JSONL contract. The workflow must rewrite them before appending JSONL rows.\n269: \n270: ```json\n271: {\n272:   \"type\": \"event\",\n273:   \"event\": \"userPaused\",\n274:   \"mode\": \"review\",\n275:   \"stopReason\": \"userPaused\",\n276:   \"reason\": \"sentinel file detected\",\n277:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-11T09:32:00Z\",\n278:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-11T09-00-00Z\",\n279:   \"generation\": 1\n280: }\n281: ```\n282: \n283: ```json\n284: {\n285:   \"type\": \"event\",\n286:   \"event\": \"stuckRecovery\",\n287:   \"mode\": \"review\",\n288:   \"stopReason\": \"stuckRecovery\",\n289:   \"fromIteration\": 5,\n290:   \"strategy\": \"Traceability protocol replay: re-run unresolved core or overlay checks\",\n291:   \"targetDimension\": \"traceability\",\n292:   \"outcome\": \"pending\",\n293:   \"reason\": \"Recovery path activated after repeated no-progress iterations\",\n294:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-11T09:40:00Z\",\n295:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-11T09-00-00Z\",\n296:   \"generation\": 1\n297: }\n298: ```\n299: \n300: **Emission rule:** If runtime logic first identifies a raw `paused` or `stuck_recovery` condition, the workflow MUST normalize it to `userPaused` or `stuckRecovery` before writing the JSONL line. Reducers and dashboards may assume persisted event names are already normalized.\n301: \n302: ### Verdict Rules\n303: \n304: | Verdict | Condition | Next Command |\n305: |---------|-----------|--------------|\n306: | FAIL | `activeP0 > 0` OR quality gate failure | `/speckit:plan` |\n307: | CONDITIONAL | `activeP0 == 0` AND (`activeP1 > 0` OR open search debt) | `/speckit:plan` |\n308: | PASS | `activeP0 == 0` AND `activeP1 == 0` AND no open search debt | `/create:changelog` |\n309: \n310: When `activeP2 > 0` on PASS, set `hasAdvisories: true`.\n311: \n312: ### traceabilityChecks Schema\n313: \n314: ```json\n315: {\n316:   \"traceabilityChecks\": {\n317:     \"summary\": {\n318:       \"required\": 2, \"executed\": 3, \"pass\": 1, \"partial\": 1,\n319:       \"fail\": 1, \"blocked\": 0, \"notApplicable\": 0, \"gatingFailures\": 1\n320:     },\n321:     \"results\": [{\n322:       \"protocolId\": \"spec_code\", \"status\": \"fail\", \"gateClass\": \"hard\",\n323:       \"applicable\": true, \"counts\": { \"pass\": 0, \"partial\": 0, \"fail\": 1 },\n324:       \"evidence\": [\"README.md:48\"], \"findingRefs\": [\"F004\"],\n325:       \"summary\": \"README claimed the old report contract.\"\n326:     }]\n327:   }\n328: }\n329: ```\n330: \n331: | Field | Type | Required | Description |\n332: |-------|------|----------|-------------|\n333: | summary.required / executed / pass / partial / fail / blocked / notApplicable | number | Yes | Protocol execution counts |\n334: | summary.gatingFailures | number | Yes | Hard-gate failures blocking STOP |\n335: | results[].protocolId | string | Yes | Canonical protocol identifier |\n336: | results[].status | string | Yes | `pass`, `partial`, `fail`, `blocked`, `notApplicable` |\n337: | results[].gateClass | string | Yes | `hard` or `advisory` |\n338: | results[].applicable | boolean | Yes | Whether the protocol applied |\n339: | results[].counts | object | Yes | Protocol-local summary counts |\n340: | results[].evidence | string[] | No | Supporting file:line refs |\n341: | results[].findingRefs | string[] | No | Related finding identifiers |\n342: | results[].summary | string | Yes | Human-readable one-line result |\n343: \n344: ### Validation Rules\n345: \n346: - Each line must be valid JSON with a `type` field\n347: - `mode` must be `\"review\"` on all iteration and synthesis records\n348: - `iteration` values must be sequential. `newFindingsRatio` must be 0.0-1.0\n349: - `findingsSummary` and `findingsNew` must each contain `P0`, `P1`, `P2` keys\n350: - `findingDetails` must be an array. Each active item must include `findingClass`, `scopeProof`, and `affectedSurfaceHints`\n351: \n352: ---\n353: \n354: ## 3. REVIEW DEPTH SCHEMA (V2)\n355: \n356: `reviewDepthSchemaVersion: 2` is the discriminator for the v2 search-depth contract. Absent values, `null`, or any value other than `2` mean v1 legacy: readers keep today's behavior, and validator hard enforcement applies only when the discriminator is present.\n357: \n358: Frozen v2 contract:\n359: \n360: Top-level review iteration fields when `reviewDepthSchemaVersion: 2`:\n361: - `reviewDepthSchemaVersion: 2`, discriminator\n362: - `reviewDepthApplicability`, `{ scopeClass: 'trivial'|'standard'|'complex', enforcement: 'strict'|'warn'|'skip', reason: string, evidenceRefs: string[] }`\n363: - `targetSelection`, `{ selectedTargets: string[], selectionReason: string, discoveryMethods: string[], omittedHighRiskTargets: string[], graphStatus: 'available'|'unavailable'|'partial', semanticSearchStatus: 'available'|'unavailable'|'partial', evidenceRefs: string[] }`\n364: - `searchCoverage`, `{ requiredBugClasses: string[], covered: string[], ruledOut: string[], deferred: string[], blocked: string[], graphCoverageMode: 'graph'|'graphless_fallback'|'unavailable_blocked' }`\n365: - `searchLedger[]`, array of ledger rows\n366: \n367: Ledger row fields:\n368: - Required: `id, dimension, targetRefs, bugClass, disposition, rationale`\n369: - `hypothesis` (string) OR `invariant` (string), at least one\n370: - `searchActions[]`, `{ method: string, queryOrPath: string, result: string, evidenceRefs: string[] }`\n371: - Disposition-specific link (exactly one):\n372:   - `finding` → `linkedFindingId` (must reference an id present in `findingDetails[]`)\n373:   - `ruled_out` → `ruledOutReason`\n374:   - `deferred` → `deferredReason`\n375:   - `blocked` → `blockedReason`\n376:   - `not_applicable` → `notApplicableReason`\n377: \n378: Trivial-scope exemption: when `reviewDepthApplicability.scopeClass === 'trivial'` AND `reviewDepthApplicability.enforcement === 'skip'`, ledger may be `[]` with cited scope proof in `reviewDepthApplicability.evidenceRefs`.\n379: \n380: ### Applicability\n381: \n382: | Field | Type | Required | Semantics |\n383: |-------|------|----------|-----------|\n384: | `scopeClass` | `'trivial' \\| 'standard' \\| 'complex'` | Yes | Classifies how much depth proof the review target warrants. |\n385: | `enforcement` | `'strict' \\| 'warn' \\| 'skip'` | Yes | `strict` means v2 validators fail shallow records, `warn` emits advisory rollout feedback, `skip` is valid only for trivial scope with proof. |\n386: | `reason` | string | Yes | Human-readable justification for the chosen scope/enforcement pair. |\n387: | `evidenceRefs` | string[] | Yes | File/path refs proving scope classification, required even for skipped trivial ledgers. |\n388: \n389: ### Target Selection\n390: \n391: | Field | Type | Required | Semantics |\n392: |-------|------|----------|-----------|\n393: | `selectedTargets` | string[] | Yes | Files, folders, specs, or surfaces actually searched this iteration. |\n394: | `selectionReason` | string | Yes | Why these targets were highest-value for the dimension or bug class. |\n395: | `discoveryMethods` | string[] | Yes | Methods such as direct read, exact search, semantic search, graph query, producer trace, consumer trace, or negative-test search. |\n396: | `omittedHighRiskTargets` | string[] | Yes | High-risk targets not searched, use `[]` when none were identified. |\n397: | `graphStatus` | `'available' \\| 'unavailable' \\| 'partial'` | Yes | Code/coverage graph availability for this iteration's target selection. |\n398: | `semanticSearchStatus` | `'available' \\| 'unavailable' \\| 'partial'` | Yes | Semantic/code search availability for this iteration. |\n399: | `evidenceRefs` | string[] | Yes | Evidence for target selection and omitted-target claims. |\n400: \n401: ### Search Coverage\n402: \n403: | Field | Type | Required | Semantics |\n404: |-------|------|----------|-----------|\n405: | `requiredBugClasses` | string[] | Yes | Bug classes or invariant families that should be searched for this scope. |\n406: | `covered` | string[] | Yes | Required classes searched with conclusive finding or clean proof. |\n407: | `ruledOut` | string[] | Yes | Required classes searched and explicitly ruled out. |\n408: | `deferred` | string[] | Yes | Required classes postponed with a reason in ledger rows. |\n409: | `blocked` | string[] | Yes | Required classes blocked by missing access, graph/search outage, ambiguity, or scope conflict. |\n410: | `graphCoverageMode` | `'graph' \\| 'graphless_fallback' \\| 'unavailable_blocked'` | Yes | `graph` uses graph evidence, `graphless_fallback` uses direct text/JSON proof, and `unavailable_blocked` records insufficient fallback proof. |\n411: \n412: ### Search Ledger\n413: \n414: | Field | Type | Required | Semantics |\n415: |-------|------|----------|-----------|\n416: | `id` | string | Yes | Stable ledger-row id unique within the iteration record. |\n417: | `dimension` | string | Yes | Review dimension addressed by this row. |\n418: | `targetRefs` | string[] | Yes | Targets searched, should overlap `targetSelection.selectedTargets`. |\n419: | `bugClass` | string | Yes | Candidate bug class or invariant family. |\n420: | `hypothesis` / `invariant` | string | Conditional | At least one must be present and non-empty. |\n421: | `searchActions` | array | Yes | Each action has `method`, `queryOrPath`, `result`, and `evidenceRefs`. |\n422: | `disposition` | string | Yes | One of `finding`, `ruled_out`, `deferred`, `blocked`, `not_applicable`. |\n423: | `rationale` | string | Yes | Why this disposition follows from the evidence. |\n424: \n425: | Disposition | Required link | Rule |\n426: |-------------|---------------|------|\n427: | `finding` | `linkedFindingId` | Must reference an `id` present in `findingDetails[]`. |\n428: | `ruled_out` | `ruledOutReason` | Must explain the negative evidence. |\n429: | `deferred` | `deferredReason` | Must explain why later search is acceptable. |\n430: | `blocked` | `blockedReason` | Must name the blocker and expected recovery path. |\n431: | `not_applicable` | `notApplicableReason` | Must explain why the bug class does not apply to this target. |\n432: \n433: Representative v2 record:\n434: \n435: ```json\n436: {\n437:   \"type\": \"iteration\",\n438:   \"mode\": \"review\",\n439:   \"iteration\": 3,\n440:   \"run\": 3,\n441:   \"status\": \"complete\",\n442:   \"dimensions\": [\"correctness\"],\n443:   \"filesReviewed\": [\"src/review-target.ts\"],\n444:   \"findingsSummary\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 0, \"P2\": 0 },\n445:   \"findingsNew\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 0, \"P2\": 0 },\n446:   \"findingDetails\": [],\n447:   \"newFindingsRatio\": 0,\n448:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-example\",\n449:   \"generation\": 1,\n450:   \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n451:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-22T00:00:00Z\",\n452:   \"durationMs\": 120000,\n453:   \"reviewDepthSchemaVersion\": 2,\n454:   \"reviewDepthApplicability\": { \"scopeClass\": \"standard\", \"enforcement\": \"strict\", \"reason\": \"non-trivial state transition target\", \"evidenceRefs\": [\"src/review-target.ts:1\"] },\n455:   \"targetSelection\": { \"selectedTargets\": [\"src/review-target.ts\"], \"selectionReason\": \"state mutation path under review\", \"discoveryMethods\": [\"direct_read\", \"exact_search\"], \"omittedHighRiskTargets\": [], \"graphStatus\": \"unavailable\", \"semanticSearchStatus\": \"partial\", \"evidenceRefs\": [\"src/review-target.ts:1\"] },\n456:   \"searchCoverage\": { \"requiredBugClasses\": [\"state_transition\"], \"covered\": [], \"ruledOut\": [\"state_transition\"], \"deferred\": [], \"blocked\": [], \"graphCoverageMode\": \"graphless_fallback\" },\n457:   \"searchLedger\": [{ \"id\": \"SL-001\", \"dimension\": \"correctness\", \"targetRefs\": [\"src/review-target.ts\"], \"bugClass\": \"state_transition\", \"hypothesis\": \"state transition can skip validation\", \"searchActions\": [{ \"method\": \"direct_read\", \"queryOrPath\": \"src/review-target.ts\", \"result\": \"validation guard present on all branches\", \"evidenceRefs\": [\"src/review-target.ts:42\"] }], \"disposition\": \"ruled_out\", \"rationale\": \"all mutation branches call the validator\", \"ruledOutReason\": \"guard verified by direct read\" }]\n458: }\n459: ```\n460: \n461: ### Compatibility and Downstream Obligations\n462: \n463: | Record Shape | Reader Behavior | Validator Behavior |\n464: |--------------|-----------------|--------------------|\n465: | v1 legacy: discriminator absent or not `2` | Parse as today's iteration record. | A validator may warn, but must not hard-fail only because v2 fields are absent. |\n466: | v2 trivial+skip | Parse v2 applicability, `searchLedger: []` allowed with cited scope proof. | Validate `reviewDepthApplicability.evidenceRefs`, skip ledger-depth requirements. |\n467: | v2 standard/complex | Parse v2 fields in addition to v1 required fields. | Enforce v2 shape, ledger linkage, coverage reconciliation, and evidence refs. |\n468: \n469: Reducer, dashboard, and report work must preserve and expose `candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`, `ruledOutCandidates`, `cleanSearchProof`, and `searchCoverage`. Until that work ships, these are contract obligations only. `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `deep-review-dashboard.md`, and `review-report.md` are not expected to persist them.\n470: \n471: ---"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794847631163,"end":1794847631444}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794847631478,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e54164450023KVTyseHFcwUC2","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e54156dd001wpWJGBQrrdimhp","type":"tool","id":"call_ec94497af87e4146a61ec88c","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"wc -l .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml; grep -n \"step_init\\|step_create_state_log\\|step_reduce_state\\|phase_init\\|phase_main_loop\\|phase_synthesis\\|step_resolve_artifact_root\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml | head -60"},"output":"    2340 .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\n102:  trigger: \"At workflow START, before phase_init\"\n181:  # step_resolve_artifact_root plus the shared resolver, so root specs keep\n219:  step_resolve_artifact_root:\n305:    description: \"Spawn fan-out lineages; skip and proceed to phase_init normally when single-executor\"\n311:      This step runs before phase_init, so pass the raw review_focus. fanout-run.cjs\n323:      After all lineages complete, jump directly to phase_synthesis — skip phase_init and\n324:      phase_main_loop entirely (those are the single-executor path). The merge step in\n325:      phase_synthesis will consolidate results across all lineages.\n349:  phase_init:\n556:          open_run: \"Run step_create_state_log.command unchanged. With the hand-written log set aside, it opens the run from the moved config.\"\n587:          skip_to: phase_synthesis\n720:      step_create_state_log:\n833:      step_init_complete:\n954:          skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1138:            when: \"Run once, immediately before control jumps to phase_synthesis: in if_existing_terminal_path, in the divergent pivot's if_failed and on_error branches, and in every confirm-mode manualStop exit (on_C) into phase_synthesis: both divergent pivot gates, gate_pre_iteration and the post-iteration gate. The auto three-errors stop (reason error) reaches it through if_existing_terminal_path. The duration stop in step_check_max_duration runs it, once, before its jump to phase_synthesis. Never run it when the pivot continues the loop.\"\n1257:                      skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1301:                      skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1304:                  skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1308:              skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1312:            skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1415:        on_C: { set: { reason: \"manualStop\" }, run_first: record_terminal_gates, proceed_to: phase_synthesis }\n1800:        on_C: { set: { reason: \"manualStop\" }, run_first: record_terminal_gates, proceed_to: phase_synthesis }\n1816:  phase_synthesis:\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"    2340 .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\n102:  trigger: \"At workflow START, before phase_init\"\n181:  # step_resolve_artifact_root plus the shared resolver, so root specs keep\n219:  step_resolve_artifact_root:\n305:    description: \"Spawn fan-out lineages; skip and proceed to phase_init normally when single-executor\"\n311:      This step runs before phase_init, so pass the raw review_focus. fanout-run.cjs\n323:      After all lineages complete, jump directly to phase_synthesis — skip phase_init and\n324:      phase_main_loop entirely (those are the single-executor path). The merge step in\n325:      phase_synthesis will consolidate results across all lineages.\n349:  phase_init:\n556:          open_run: \"Run step_create_state_log.command unchanged. With the hand-written log set aside, it opens the run from the moved config.\"\n587:          skip_to: phase_synthesis\n720:      step_create_state_log:\n833:      step_init_complete:\n954:          skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1138:            when: \"Run once, immediately before control jumps to phase_synthesis: in if_existing_terminal_path, in the divergent pivot's if_failed and on_error branches, and in every confirm-mode manualStop exit (on_C) into phase_synthesis: both divergent pivot gates, gate_pre_iteration and the post-iteration gate. The auto three-errors stop (reason error) reaches it through if_existing_terminal_path. The duration stop in step_check_max_duration runs it, once, before its jump to phase_synthesis. Never run it when the pivot continues the loop.\"\n1257:                      skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1301:                      skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1304:                  skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1308:              skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1312:            skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1415:        on_C: { set: { reason: \"manualStop\" }, run_first: record_terminal_gates, proceed_to: phase_synthesis }\n1800:        on_C: { set: { reason: \"manualStop\" }, run_first: record_terminal_gates, proceed_to: phase_synthesis }\n1816:  phase_synthesis:\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"wc -l .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml; grep -n \\\"step_init\\\\|step_create_state_log\\\\|step_reduce_state\\\\|phase_init\\\\|phase_main_loop\\\\|phase_synthesis\\\\|step_resolve_artifact_root\\\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml | head -60\"}"},"time":{"start":1794847630405,"end":1794847631478}}}}
