{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794847691446,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5424f55001L1EWflgON3JZRb","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e54243a9001muqnsdhufcHgDh","type":"tool","id":"call_bd187aa6a1424d42a8ff15c2","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 05f776202e0 5b2b062baef -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md .env.example"},"output":"diff --git a/.env.example b/.env.example\nindex eed1600be87..ad163e8a646 100644\n--- a/.env.example\n+++ b/.env.example\n@@ -408,6 +408,7 @@ webflow_WEBFLOW_TOKEN=\n # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_THRESHOLD_CONFIDENCE=0.8 # Advisor recommend confidence threshold\n # SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=                  # Enable debug output in the skill_advisor.py CLI\n # SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLE_BUILTIN_SEMANTIC= # Disable built-in semantic matching in the advisor script\n+# SKILL_ADVISOR_FRESH_PROMPTS_PATH=    # Test-only path of the fresh behaviour rows the command transcript scorer labels (default: its own behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl)\n # (Aliases that route to the SYSTEM_* names above: SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED,\n #  SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED, SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_TRUSTED,\n #  SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_DEV_ALLOW_STALE.)\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md\nindex fcb2da4831d..ee4e2e67497 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md\n@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n   - \"advisor_recommend\"\n   - \"which skill should handle this\"\n   - \"route this request\"\n-version: 0.12.21.0\n+version: 0.12.22.0\n ---\n \n # system-skill-advisor\n@@ -173,7 +173,7 @@ A scan follows a top-level `local-*` link only when the link's real path resolve\n \n The `semantic_shadow` lane runs against the pluggable embedder layer in `@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/`, which the advisor owns. The registry holds text-tuned embedding models and defaults through a local-first cascade to a local model when no embedder is explicitly set. For the full model registry, the cascade tier table and the swap workflow, see `INSTALL-GUIDE.md` §12.\n \n-Command rows use the same embedder. The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 46 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves, and `skill_graph_scan` embeds it into its own `vec_cmd_<dim>` table beside the skill vectors. The scan skips a row whose text has not changed and prunes a row that is no longer generated. A command row normally passes only on one of its own phrases or its slash string. It can also pass on meaning: the prompt's real embedding has to reach a cosine of 0.72 against the row and lead the next command row by 0.02. A command that passed this way ranks first only when it leads the top passing skill by the same 0.02. A prompt that asks for no change, such as \"no edits\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only question lets only a command whose route only reads pass on meaning. Without the local embedder (Ollama serving `nomic-embed-text`) no cosine exists, so command rows pass on their phrases alone.\n+Command rows use the same embedder. The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 47 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves, and `skill_graph_scan` embeds it into its own `vec_cmd_<dim>` table beside the skill vectors. The scan skips a row whose text has not changed and prunes a row that is no longer generated. A command row normally passes only on one of its own phrases or its slash string. It can also pass on meaning: the prompt's real embedding has to reach a cosine of 0.72 against the row and lead the next command row by 0.02. A command that passed this way ranks first only when it leads the top passing skill by the same 0.02. A prompt that asks for no change, such as \"no edits\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only question lets only a command whose route only reads pass on meaning. Without the local embedder (Ollama serving `nomic-embed-text`) no cosine exists, so command rows pass on their phrases alone.\n \n ### The Nine Commands\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md\nindex fc0f57e7050..b98f209227d 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md\n@@ -105,7 +105,7 @@ Exit codes:\n - Reference and asset doc frontmatter `trigger_phrases` feed routing only when `SPECKIT_ADVISOR_DOC_TRIGGERS=true`.\n - Skill authors change routing vocabulary in `graph-metadata.json`.\n \n-`advisor_status` reports `indexStaleness` on every successful call and, with `includeEmbeddingsHealth`, an opt-in `embeddingsHealth` covering provider resolution and the local model server.\n+`advisor_status` reports `indexStaleness` on every successful call and, with `includeEmbeddingsHealth`, an opt-in `embeddingsHealth` covering provider resolution and the local model server. It adds `hookHealth` once a prompt hook has written a health record for the workspace.\n \n The advisor implementation, skill-graph library and package-local database live under this skill package, while memory remains focused on memory tools.\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md\nindex b3b90611adf..cc991de66d8 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md\n@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@ This release also stops offering a command where none fits the request. It adds\n - **The top hub keeps its command in the hook.** A row the brief never shows can no longer take it. <!-- section: Brief Commands -->\n - **A tool that does not show up reaches the doctor helper.** The brief names `/doctor:helper` beside the skills. <!-- section: Brief Commands -->\n - **A bare problem word can now lead with a doctor command.** It needs a skill that matched on shared words only. <!-- section: Brief Commands -->\n-- **A no-edit prompt gets no command on any path.** More wordings now count as no-edit. <!-- section: No-Edit Prompts -->\n+- **A no-edit prompt gets no command it did not type.** More wordings now count as no-edit. <!-- section: No-Edit Prompts -->\n - **A refusal or a question is not a request.** A command the prompt refuses or asks about is not offered. A command named with no such lead is, when its owner and route gates pass. <!-- section: Command Fit -->\n - **A refusal covers a whole or-list.** `no need to run` counts, and a question mark ends the sentence before it. <!-- section: Command Fit -->\n - **Every runtime leads with the same head.** The head row keeps its command under every request shape. <!-- section: One Head on Every Runtime -->\n@@ -56,7 +56,7 @@ This release also stops offering a command where none fits the request. It adds\n \n #### A Record on Every Prompt\n \n-The Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi and DSH hooks share one handler. That handler now appends a health record on every prompt. Before, it wrote one only with `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` set. A record holds the runtime, the status, the freshness, the duration and the cache hit. A disabled hook writes one too:\n+The Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi, DSH and Vibe hooks share one handler. That handler now appends a health record on every prompt. Before, it wrote one only with `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` set. A record holds the runtime, the status, the freshness, the duration and the cache hit. A disabled hook writes one too:\n \n ```json\n {\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-13T20:30:20.999Z\",\"runtime\":\"claude\",\"status\":\"skipped\",\"freshness\":\"unavailable\",\"durationMs\":1,\"cacheHit\":false}\n@@ -119,7 +119,7 @@ A passing skill used to block the doctor hand-off unless the prompt carried a st\n \n #### No Command When You Rule Out a Change\n \n-The scorer already held back commands on a no-edit prompt. The hub route did not. A hub could offer a writing command to \"just list\" or \"no edits\". Now one shared check covers the hub route, both scorer gates and the read-only check.\n+The scorer already held back commands on a no-edit prompt. The hub route did not. A hub could offer a writing command to \"just list\" or \"no edits\". Now one shared check covers the hub route, both scorer gates and the read-only check. A command you typed yourself stays, because what you typed outranks the wording around it.\n \n #### More Wordings Count as No-Edit\n \n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"diff --git a/.env.example b/.env.example\nindex eed1600be87..ad163e8a646 100644\n--- a/.env.example\n+++ b/.env.example\n@@ -408,6 +408,7 @@ webflow_WEBFLOW_TOKEN=\n # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_THRESHOLD_CONFIDENCE=0.8 # Advisor recommend confidence threshold\n # SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=                  # Enable debug output in the skill_advisor.py CLI\n # SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLE_BUILTIN_SEMANTIC= # Disable built-in semantic matching in the advisor script\n+# SKILL_ADVISOR_FRESH_PROMPTS_PATH=    # Test-only path of the fresh behaviour rows the command transcript scorer labels (default: its own behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl)\n # (Aliases that route to the SYSTEM_* names above: SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED,\n #  SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED, SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_TRUSTED,\n #  SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_DEV_ALLOW_STALE.)\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md\nindex fcb2da4831d..ee4e2e67497 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md\n@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n   - \"advisor_recommend\"\n   - \"which skill should handle this\"\n   - \"route this request\"\n-version: 0.12.21.0\n+version: 0.12.22.0\n ---\n \n # system-skill-advisor\n@@ -173,7 +173,7 @@ A scan follows a top-level `local-*` link only when the link's real path resolve\n \n The `semantic_shadow` lane runs against the pluggable embedder layer in `@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/`, which the advisor owns. The registry holds text-tuned embedding models and defaults through a local-first cascade to a local model when no embedder is explicitly set. For the full model registry, the cascade tier table and the swap workflow, see `INSTALL-GUIDE.md` §12.\n \n-Command rows use the same embedder. The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 46 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves, and `skill_graph_scan` embeds it into its own `vec_cmd_<dim>` table beside the skill vectors. The scan skips a row whose text has not changed and prunes a row that is no longer generated. A command row normally passes only on one of its own phrases or its slash string. It can also pass on meaning: the prompt's real embedding has to reach a cosine of 0.72 against the row and lead the next command row by 0.02. A command that passed this way ranks first only when it leads the top passing skill by the same 0.02. A prompt that asks for no change, such as \"no edits\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only question lets only a command whose route only reads pass on meaning. Without the local embedder (Ollama serving `nomic-embed-text`) no cosine exists, so command rows pass on their phrases alone.\n+Command rows use the same embedder. The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 47 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves, and `skill_graph_scan` embeds it into its own `vec_cmd_<dim>` table beside the skill vectors. The scan skips a row whose text has not changed and prunes a row that is no longer generated. A command row normally passes only on one of its own phrases or its slash string. It can also pass on meaning: the prompt's real embedding has to reach a cosine of 0.72 against the row and lead the next command row by 0.02. A command that passed this way ranks first only when it leads the top passing skill by the same 0.02. A prompt that asks for no change, such as \"no edits\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only question lets only a command whose route only reads pass on meaning. Without the local embedder (Ollama serving `nomic-embed-text`) no cosine exists, so command rows pass on their phrases alone.\n \n ### The Nine Commands\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md\nindex fc0f57e7050..b98f209227d 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md\n@@ -105,7 +105,7 @@ Exit codes:\n - Reference and asset doc frontmatter `trigger_phrases` feed routing only when `SPECKIT_ADVISOR_DOC_TRIGGERS=true`.\n - Skill authors change routing vocabulary in `graph-metadata.json`.\n \n-`advisor_status` reports `indexStaleness` on every successful call and, with `includeEmbeddingsHealth`, an opt-in `embeddingsHealth` covering provider resolution and the local model server.\n+`advisor_status` reports `indexStaleness` on every successful call and, with `includeEmbeddingsHealth`, an opt-in `embeddingsHealth` covering provider resolution and the local model server. It adds `hookHealth` once a prompt hook has written a health record for the workspace.\n \n The advisor implementation, skill-graph library and package-local database live under this skill package, while memory remains focused on memory tools.\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md\nindex b3b90611adf..cc991de66d8 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md\n@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@ This release also stops offering a command where none fits the request. It adds\n - **The top hub keeps its command in the hook.** A row the brief never shows can no longer take it. <!-- section: Brief Commands -->\n - **A tool that does not show up reaches the doctor helper.** The brief names `/doctor:helper` beside the skills. <!-- section: Brief Commands -->\n - **A bare problem word can now lead with a doctor command.** It needs a skill that matched on shared words only. <!-- section: Brief Commands -->\n-- **A no-edit prompt gets no command on any path.** More wordings now count as no-edit. <!-- section: No-Edit Prompts -->\n+- **A no-edit prompt gets no command it did not type.** More wordings now count as no-edit. <!-- section: No-Edit Prompts -->\n - **A refusal or a question is not a request.** A command the prompt refuses or asks about is not offered. A command named with no such lead is, when its owner and route gates pass. <!-- section: Command Fit -->\n - **A refusal covers a whole or-list.** `no need to run` counts, and a question mark ends the sentence before it. <!-- section: Command Fit -->\n - **Every runtime leads with the same head.** The head row keeps its command under every request shape. <!-- section: One Head on Every Runtime -->\n@@ -56,7 +56,7 @@ This release also stops offering a command where none fits the request. It adds\n \n #### A Record on Every Prompt\n \n-The Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi and DSH hooks share one handler. That handler now appends a health record on every prompt. Before, it wrote one only with `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` set. A record holds the runtime, the status, the freshness, the duration and the cache hit. A disabled hook writes one too:\n+The Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi, DSH and Vibe hooks share one handler. That handler now appends a health record on every prompt. Before, it wrote one only with `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` set. A record holds the runtime, the status, the freshness, the duration and the cache hit. A disabled hook writes one too:\n \n ```json\n {\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-13T20:30:20.999Z\",\"runtime\":\"claude\",\"status\":\"skipped\",\"freshness\":\"unavailable\",\"durationMs\":1,\"cacheHit\":false}\n@@ -119,7 +119,7 @@ A passing skill used to block the doctor hand-off unless the prompt carried a st\n \n #### No Command When You Rule Out a Change\n \n-The scorer already held back commands on a no-edit prompt. The hub route did not. A hub could offer a writing command to \"just list\" or \"no edits\". Now one shared check covers the hub route, both scorer gates and the read-only check.\n+The scorer already held back commands on a no-edit prompt. The hub route did not. A hub could offer a writing command to \"just list\" or \"no edits\". Now one shared check covers the hub route, both scorer gates and the read-only check. A command you typed yourself stays, because what you typed outranks the wording around it.\n \n #### More Wordings Count as No-Edit\n \n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 05f776202e0 5b2b062baef -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md .env.example\"}"},"time":{"start":1794847690581,"end":1794847691446}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794847692594,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"id":"prt_1e542573200133ouqNvqGuN0nn","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e54243a9001muqnsdhufcHgDh","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"26cfc423d20d77f7d5abdd8d2721af79157b89b4","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":1344,"output":141,"reasoning":38,"cache":{"read":84864,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794847695978,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"id":"prt_1e542646a00141guh0rX4CRd4S","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e5425736001J0t7MlpHTKEwo9","type":"step-start","snapshot":"26cfc423d20d77f7d5abdd8d2721af79157b89b4"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794847697046,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e54264bf001YSoIDGDHJNHYVM","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e5425736001J0t7MlpHTKEwo9","type":"tool","id":"call_09afce73376748ae9700aca7","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff e91faf28b8c^2 e91faf28b8c -- .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt .skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md"},"output":"diff --git a/.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md b/.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md\nindex 50649d6a020..3f37fdbad2b 100644\n--- a/.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md\n+++ b/.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md\n@@ -43,8 +43,8 @@ Other gaps cost your agent time. A recommendation said `sk-doc` when you asked f\n - **Install a patched Node.js first.** Node 20, 23 and 25 are no longer accepted. <!-- section: Node.js -->\n - **An agent can no longer read or write `.env`.** It gets key names, parse errors and fingerprints instead, on all eight runtimes. <!-- section: Dotenv Guard -->\n - **A hub skill names the command to type.** The brief also says whether to run it, start it or ask first. <!-- section: Skill Advisor -->\n-- **A typed slash command always reaches the model.** It arrives with its policy and the skill that owns it. <!-- section: Skill Advisor -->\n-- **Doctor checks show whether the brief arrives.** `/doctor:setup` gains an embedder leg and a delivery leg. <!-- section: Skill Advisor -->\n+- **A typed slash command always reaches the model.** It arrives with its policy and the skill that owns it. **Breaking:** `/create:skill` is now `/create:sk-skill`, with no alias. <!-- section: Skill Advisor -->\n+- **Doctor checks show whether the brief arrives.** `/doctor:setup` gains an embedder leg and a delivery leg. Hook health shows with no debug flag. <!-- section: Skill Advisor -->\n - **Claude Code hands over by default.** A hop keeps the running command, the goal, the session's name and its mode. The other runtimes stay off until you turn them on. <!-- section: Session Handover -->\n - **The shell shim runs only a wrapper it trusts.** A cloned repository can no longer supply the script your shell runs. <!-- section: Session Handover -->\n - **One main name now covers the whole feature.** The hook folder, the switches, the seed and the docs say session handover. The in-session spelling still works for the on and off switches. <!-- section: Session Handover -->\n@@ -104,28 +104,28 @@ Claude Code, Devin and Cursor also carry their own deny list for dotenv files. S\n \n #### A Hub Skill Names the Command to Type\n \n-The advisor used to say `sk-doc` for \"create a readme\". You then had to find `/create:readme` yourself. Now a hub recommendation carries the command for the mode it picked. A brief head reads `use system-spec-kit → /speckit:plan (start)`. A hub that cannot pick one mode says so, as `sk-doc (needs a mode)`. A deep-loop command is offered only when the prompt asks for depth.\n+The advisor used to say `sk-doc` for \"create a readme\". You then had to find `/create:readme` yourself. Now a hub recommendation carries the command for the mode it picked. A brief head reads `use system-spec-kit → /speckit:plan (start)`. A hub that cannot pick one mode says so, as `sk-doc (needs a mode)`. It says so only when your prompt names that hub. In the prompt hook, the top hub keeps its command even when a lower row carries the same one. A deep-loop command is offered only when the prompt asks for depth or types that command. A mention of `/deep:review` no longer offers `/deep:research`.\n \n #### Every Command Has a Run, Start or Ask Policy\n \n Each of the 44 tracked commands records what it writes and what it must ask first. The generator turns that record into one policy. `run` means the agent may run it now. `start` means it starts without `:auto`, so its setup asks. `ask` means it offers the command and waits. Gate 2 in `AGENTS.md` now tells the agent how to follow each one. A typed command or a direct instruction outranks the policy.\n \n-A typed slash command now reaches the model on every tracked row, with its policy and owner skill. Plain requests reach their command more often too. Paraphrases the tuning never saw still mostly miss.\n+A typed slash command now reaches the model on every tracked row, with its policy and owner skill. Plain requests reach their command more often too. Paraphrases the tuning never saw still mostly miss. A file name such as `/create:sk-skill.md` is not read as a typed command. A mode suffix such as `/deep:review:auto` still counts. **Breaking:** `/create:skill` is now `/create:sk-skill` on every runtime. A command file named `skill.md` made Claude Code read its folder as one skill. That hid 12 of the 44 commands. No command file answers to the old name. There is no alias. The advisor reads a typed `/create:skill` as `/create:sk-skill`. So that prompt gets `sk-doc` with `/create:sk-skill (start)`. Scripts and saved prompts still need the new name. The runtime mirror check now fails any command file named `skill.md`.\n \n #### Meaning Matching Has Its Own Doctor Route\n \n-A command can also pass on meaning when the local embedder runs. Each scored command row carries its own vector. A prompt needs a close match and a clear lead over the next command. A prompt that asks for no change gets no command this way. `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` checks the embedder and plans each missing step. It asks before it pulls a model or starts a server. It never installs Ollama itself. The prompt embedding gives up after 750 ms.\n+A command can also pass on meaning when the local embedder runs. Each scored command row carries its own vector. A prompt needs a close match and a clear lead over the next command. A prompt that asks for no change gets no command this way or from a hub route. A command you type still comes through. \"make no changes\" and \"don't make any changes\" both count. `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` checks the embedder and plans each missing step. It asks before it pulls a model or starts a server. It never installs Ollama itself. The prompt embedding gives up after 750 ms.\n \n #### Doctor Checks Show Whether the Brief Arrives\n \n-`/doctor:setup` gains two read-only legs. The embedder leg reads DEGRADED when meaning matching is off. The delivery leg reads DEGRADED when a prompt hook is missing or not approved. On Codex, no brief arrives until you approve the project hooks. A default `embed` now leaves Claude Code a one-line `CLAUDE.md` pointer to `AGENTS.md`.\n+`/doctor:setup` gains two read-only legs. The embedder leg reads DEGRADED when meaning matching is off. The delivery leg reads DEGRADED when a prompt hook is missing or not approved. On Codex, no brief arrives until you approve the project hooks. A default `embed` now leaves Claude Code a one-line `CLAUDE.md` pointer to `AGENTS.md`. Hook health no longer needs `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG`. Every prompt hook run writes a health record, even a disabled one. It holds the runtime, status, freshness, duration and cache hit. It holds no prompt text. The OpenCode plugin writes none. `advisor_status` then shows a `hookHealth` section. It adds the share of answers from the local scorer and the time of the newest record. The setup advisor leg shows both. The hook-wiring check now reads the command a shell would run. A hook that only names the advisor script reads as missing. The Codex check names the fix for a missing entry.\n \n #### Smaller Fixes\n \n - **A question about the trigger index reaches spec-kit.** It used to end at the doctor helper. A question about index drift still goes to the doctor.\n - **The doctor hand-off names the matched command.** It used to name only `/doctor:helper`, even when the exact command was known.\n - **A prompt that names a `system-`, `cli-` or `mcp-` skill is read.** The prompt policy used to read only `sk-` names.\n-- **An OpenCode brief names the command and its policy.** The plugin used to drop both.\n+- **An OpenCode brief names the command and its policy.** The plugin used to drop both. It also drops a second route line that printed `targets=none`.\n - **Three plain spec requests now reach spec-kit.** The advisor used to miss them.\n - **A read-only question about git history reaches sk-git.** `show the git log` used to return no skill. The question must name git, a commit or one of the branches main, master and develop.\n - **The advisor starts on the Node.js its native module was built for.** An install now records that Node.js. A session on another major version used to fail its first call with `daemon launcher exited with code 1`.\n@@ -574,7 +574,7 @@ The lookup budget is 200 ms at p95. A lookup with no hits takes 89 to 102 ms aga\n - **If an agent needs a `.env` value:** it now asks you. Paste the value yourself or compare fingerprints. For fingerprints, run `openssl rand -base64 32` and export the result as `ENV_SECRET_GUARD_PEPPER` in your shell profile. Never put it in a file inside a repository.\n - **If you embed the shipped `AGENTS.md`:** run `/doctor:agents-md` to take the new Gate 2 and Gate 6 wording. Remove any link of your own to the three retired reply rules.\n - **If you run the skill advisor from a built copy:** run `npm run build` in `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime` once.\n-- **If you match on an advisor command id:** `memory:save` and `command-memory-save` are now `command-speckit-save`. `command-spec-kit` is now one id per command, such as `command-speckit-plan`. `command-prompt-improver` is now `command-prompt-improve`.\n+- **If you type `/create:skill` or match on an advisor command id:** type `/create:sk-skill` instead. Change any script or saved prompt that names the old command. `memory:save` and `command-memory-save` are now `command-speckit-save`. `command-spec-kit` is now one id per command, such as `command-speckit-plan`. `command-prompt-improver` is now `command-prompt-improve`. `command-create-skill` is now `command-create-sk-skill`.\n - **On Codex:** approve the project hooks in `/hooks`, including the new `SessionStart` row. Until then the advisor brief never arrives. The compaction pointer does not run either. To turn on meaning matching anywhere, run `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder`.\n - **If Skilled is installed in your project:** run `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-hook-registrations.cjs` from the project root. It rewrites `.claude/settings.json` and `.codex/hooks.json`. Add `--check` to check for drift without writing.\n - **If a script or setting names a hook folder:** use the new name. `dispatch/` is `cli-dispatch/`, `task-dispatch/` is `subagent-dispatch-guard/` and `completion/` is `completion-evidence/`. `codex-watchdog/` and `hook-install/` are now `codex-global-hooks-check/`.\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md b/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\nindex 741500591d9..89fc19ec009 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\n@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\n name: sk-doc\n description: \"Documentation & component authoring hub: skills, agents, commands, READMEs, catalogs, playbooks, changelogs, goals, frontmatter.\"\n allowed-tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob]\n-version: 2.9.16.0\n+version: 2.10.0.0\n metadata:\n   family: sk-util\n ---\n@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@ Use this skill for documentation and OpenCode-component authoring, and for docum\n \n | Mode | Use it for | Packet | Command |\n |------|------------|--------|---------|\n-| **sk-create-skill** | Scaffold an OpenCode skill (and, via `sk-create-skill-parent`, a parent hub with nested mode packets) | `sk-create-skill/` | `/create:skill`, `/create:skill-parent` |\n+| **sk-create-skill** | Scaffold an OpenCode skill (and, via `sk-create-skill-parent`, a parent hub with nested mode packets) | `sk-create-skill/` | `/create:sk-skill`, `/create:skill-parent` |\n | **sk-create-readme** | Author a folder, code-folder or skill README, a repository front page and its install, contributing and security guides | `sk-create-readme/` | `/create:readme` |\n | **sk-create-agent** | Scaffold an OpenCode agent (permission/authority frontmatter) | `sk-create-agent/` | `/create:agent` |\n | **sk-create-command** | Scaffold an OpenCode slash command (argument-hint + allowed-tools + router/presentation split) | `sk-create-command/` | `/create:command` |\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md b/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md\nindex 914dd24d94f..f7a7ed60a92 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md\n@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n   - \"sk-create-skill routing\"\n importance_tier: normal\n contextType: general\n-version: 1.0.4.0\n+version: 1.0.5.0\n router_state: active\n skill_pointer: SKILL.md\n ---\n@@ -24,13 +24,13 @@ The router answers one question: given a request, which skill-local resources lo\n what happens when nothing matches. Every path below stays inside this skill folder, and no resource other than `DEFAULT_RESOURCE`\n loads before an intent selects it.\n \n-Requests reach this packet when they ask to create or rebuild an OpenCode skill under `.skilled/skills/`, to run `/create:skill` for a standalone skill or `/create:skill-parent` for a parent hub, to author or repair a skill package's `SKILL.md`, `README.md`, `references/`, `assets/`, `scripts/` or `changelog/`, or to validate and package a skill with `scripts/package_skill.py`. Its vocabulary is `create skill`, `new skill`, `skill scaffold`, `SKILL.md scaffold`, `OpenCode skill`, `parent hub`, `mode packet`, `nested workflow packet` and `package skill`. It routes to two resource families: the `references/shared/` doctrine and its root-metadata contract, which both modes load first, and the mode's own `references/<key>/` plus `assets/<key>/` trees, where `create-skill` resolves the `skill` key and `create-skill-parent` resolves `parent-skill`.\n+Requests reach this packet when they ask to create or rebuild an OpenCode skill under `.skilled/skills/`, to run `/create:sk-skill` for a standalone skill or `/create:skill-parent` for a parent hub, to author or repair a skill package's `SKILL.md`, `README.md`, `references/`, `assets/`, `scripts/` or `changelog/`, or to validate and package a skill with `scripts/package_skill.py`. Its vocabulary is `create skill`, `new skill`, `skill scaffold`, `SKILL.md scaffold`, `OpenCode skill`, `parent hub`, `mode packet`, `nested workflow packet` and `package skill`. It routes to two resource families: the `references/shared/` doctrine and its root-metadata contract, which both modes load first, and the mode's own `references/<key>/` plus `assets/<key>/` trees, where `create-skill` resolves the `skill` key and `create-skill-parent` resolves `parent-skill`.\n \n ---\n \n ## 2. INTENT MODEL\n \n-- **`SKILL_PACKAGE`** fires on `create skill`, `/create:skill`, `new skill`, `skill scaffold`, `SKILL.md scaffold`, `OpenCode skill`, `sk-skill`, `create sk-`, `reusable capability`, `reusable helper`, `starter reference docs`, `package skill`, `doc rewrite guard`, `doc-rewrite-guard.py`, `render ledger`, `render-known-debt.json`, `exempt from the render checks`, `render exempt map`, `kept every claim` and `kept every original claim` at weight 4. It loads the five shared docs — `references/shared/overview.md`, `references/shared/common-pitfalls.md`, `references/shared/validation-and-packaging.md`, `references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md`, `references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md` — then `references/skill/creation-workflow.md`, `references/skill/examples-and-maintenance.md`, `references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md`, and the eight `assets/skill/` templates: `assets/skill/skill-md-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-asset-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-procedure-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-scaffold-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-smart-router.md`, `assets/skill/skill-router-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-sync-manifest-template.md`. The skill README template is not in this set: the `sk-create-readme` mode owns it and writes the README step.\n+- **`SKILL_PACKAGE`** fires on `create skill`, `/create:sk-skill`, `new skill`, `skill scaffold`, `SKILL.md scaffold`, `OpenCode skill`, `sk-skill`, `create sk-`, `reusable capability`, `reusable helper`, `starter reference docs`, `package skill`, `doc rewrite guard`, `doc-rewrite-guard.py`, `render ledger`, `render-known-debt.json`, `exempt from the render checks`, `render exempt map`, `kept every claim` and `kept every original claim` at weight 4. It loads the five shared docs — `references/shared/overview.md`, `references/shared/common-pitfalls.md`, `references/shared/validation-and-packaging.md`, `references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md`, `references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md` — then `references/skill/creation-workflow.md`, `references/skill/examples-and-maintenance.md`, `references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md`, and the eight `assets/skill/` templates: `assets/skill/skill-md-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-asset-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-procedure-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-scaffold-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-smart-router.md`, `assets/skill/skill-router-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-sync-manifest-template.md`. The skill README template is not in this set: the `sk-create-readme` mode owns it and writes the README step.\n - **`PARENT_HUB`** fires on `/create:skill-parent`, `parent skill`, `parent hub`, `mode packet`, `nested workflow packet`, `mode-registry.json` and `hub-router.json` at weight 4. It loads the same five shared docs, then `references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md`, `references/parent-skill/parent-hub-router-schema.md`, `references/parent-skill/compiled-routing-architecture.md`, and the five `assets/parent-skill/` templates: `assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-template.md`, `assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-readme-template.md`, `assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-root-router-template.md`, `assets/parent-skill/scaffold/hub-skill-scaffold.md`, `assets/parent-skill/scaffold/packet-skill-scaffold.md`.\n \n ---\n@@ -94,7 +94,7 @@ RESOURCE_KEY_BY_MODE = {\n }\n \n INTENT_MODEL = {\n-    \"SKILL_PACKAGE\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create skill\", \"/create:skill\", \"new skill\", \"skill scaffold\", \"skill.md scaffold\", \"opencode skill\", \"sk-skill\", \"create sk-\", \"reusable capability\", \"reusable helper\", \"starter reference docs\", \"package skill\", \"doc rewrite guard\", \"doc-rewrite-guard.py\", \"render ledger\", \"render-known-debt.json\", \"exempt from the render checks\", \"render exempt map\", \"kept every claim\", \"kept every original claim\"]},\n+    \"SKILL_PACKAGE\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create skill\", \"/create:sk-skill\", \"new skill\", \"skill scaffold\", \"skill.md scaffold\", \"opencode skill\", \"sk-skill\", \"create sk-\", \"reusable capability\", \"reusable helper\", \"starter reference docs\", \"package skill\", \"doc rewrite guard\", \"doc-rewrite-guard.py\", \"render ledger\", \"render-known-debt.json\", \"exempt from the render checks\", \"render exempt map\", \"kept every claim\", \"kept every original claim\"]},\n     \"PARENT_HUB\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"/create:skill-parent\", \"parent skill\", \"parent hub\", \"mode packet\", \"nested workflow packet\", \"mode-registry.json\", \"hub-router.json\"]},\n }\n \n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"diff --git a/.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md b/.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md\nindex 50649d6a020..3f37fdbad2b 100644\n--- a/.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md\n+++ b/.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md\n@@ -43,8 +43,8 @@ Other gaps cost your agent time. A recommendation said `sk-doc` when you asked f\n - **Install a patched Node.js first.** Node 20, 23 and 25 are no longer accepted. <!-- section: Node.js -->\n - **An agent can no longer read or write `.env`.** It gets key names, parse errors and fingerprints instead, on all eight runtimes. <!-- section: Dotenv Guard -->\n - **A hub skill names the command to type.** The brief also says whether to run it, start it or ask first. <!-- section: Skill Advisor -->\n-- **A typed slash command always reaches the model.** It arrives with its policy and the skill that owns it. <!-- section: Skill Advisor -->\n-- **Doctor checks show whether the brief arrives.** `/doctor:setup` gains an embedder leg and a delivery leg. <!-- section: Skill Advisor -->\n+- **A typed slash command always reaches the model.** It arrives with its policy and the skill that owns it. **Breaking:** `/create:skill` is now `/create:sk-skill`, with no alias. <!-- section: Skill Advisor -->\n+- **Doctor checks show whether the brief arrives.** `/doctor:setup` gains an embedder leg and a delivery leg. Hook health shows with no debug flag. <!-- section: Skill Advisor -->\n - **Claude Code hands over by default.** A hop keeps the running command, the goal, the session's name and its mode. The other runtimes stay off until you turn them on. <!-- section: Session Handover -->\n - **The shell shim runs only a wrapper it trusts.** A cloned repository can no longer supply the script your shell runs. <!-- section: Session Handover -->\n - **One main name now covers the whole feature.** The hook folder, the switches, the seed and the docs say session handover. The in-session spelling still works for the on and off switches. <!-- section: Session Handover -->\n@@ -104,28 +104,28 @@ Claude Code, Devin and Cursor also carry their own deny list for dotenv files. S\n \n #### A Hub Skill Names the Command to Type\n \n-The advisor used to say `sk-doc` for \"create a readme\". You then had to find `/create:readme` yourself. Now a hub recommendation carries the command for the mode it picked. A brief head reads `use system-spec-kit → /speckit:plan (start)`. A hub that cannot pick one mode says so, as `sk-doc (needs a mode)`. A deep-loop command is offered only when the prompt asks for depth.\n+The advisor used to say `sk-doc` for \"create a readme\". You then had to find `/create:readme` yourself. Now a hub recommendation carries the command for the mode it picked. A brief head reads `use system-spec-kit → /speckit:plan (start)`. A hub that cannot pick one mode says so, as `sk-doc (needs a mode)`. It says so only when your prompt names that hub. In the prompt hook, the top hub keeps its command even when a lower row carries the same one. A deep-loop command is offered only when the prompt asks for depth or types that command. A mention of `/deep:review` no longer offers `/deep:research`.\n \n #### Every Command Has a Run, Start or Ask Policy\n \n Each of the 44 tracked commands records what it writes and what it must ask first. The generator turns that record into one policy. `run` means the agent may run it now. `start` means it starts without `:auto`, so its setup asks. `ask` means it offers the command and waits. Gate 2 in `AGENTS.md` now tells the agent how to follow each one. A typed command or a direct instruction outranks the policy.\n \n-A typed slash command now reaches the model on every tracked row, with its policy and owner skill. Plain requests reach their command more often too. Paraphrases the tuning never saw still mostly miss.\n+A typed slash command now reaches the model on every tracked row, with its policy and owner skill. Plain requests reach their command more often too. Paraphrases the tuning never saw still mostly miss. A file name such as `/create:sk-skill.md` is not read as a typed command. A mode suffix such as `/deep:review:auto` still counts. **Breaking:** `/create:skill` is now `/create:sk-skill` on every runtime. A command file named `skill.md` made Claude Code read its folder as one skill. That hid 12 of the 44 commands. No command file answers to the old name. There is no alias. The advisor reads a typed `/create:skill` as `/create:sk-skill`. So that prompt gets `sk-doc` with `/create:sk-skill (start)`. Scripts and saved prompts still need the new name. The runtime mirror check now fails any command file named `skill.md`.\n \n #### Meaning Matching Has Its Own Doctor Route\n \n-A command can also pass on meaning when the local embedder runs. Each scored command row carries its own vector. A prompt needs a close match and a clear lead over the next command. A prompt that asks for no change gets no command this way. `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` checks the embedder and plans each missing step. It asks before it pulls a model or starts a server. It never installs Ollama itself. The prompt embedding gives up after 750 ms.\n+A command can also pass on meaning when the local embedder runs. Each scored command row carries its own vector. A prompt needs a close match and a clear lead over the next command. A prompt that asks for no change gets no command this way or from a hub route. A command you type still comes through. \"make no changes\" and \"don't make any changes\" both count. `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` checks the embedder and plans each missing step. It asks before it pulls a model or starts a server. It never installs Ollama itself. The prompt embedding gives up after 750 ms.\n \n #### Doctor Checks Show Whether the Brief Arrives\n \n-`/doctor:setup` gains two read-only legs. The embedder leg reads DEGRADED when meaning matching is off. The delivery leg reads DEGRADED when a prompt hook is missing or not approved. On Codex, no brief arrives until you approve the project hooks. A default `embed` now leaves Claude Code a one-line `CLAUDE.md` pointer to `AGENTS.md`.\n+`/doctor:setup` gains two read-only legs. The embedder leg reads DEGRADED when meaning matching is off. The delivery leg reads DEGRADED when a prompt hook is missing or not approved. On Codex, no brief arrives until you approve the project hooks. A default `embed` now leaves Claude Code a one-line `CLAUDE.md` pointer to `AGENTS.md`. Hook health no longer needs `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG`. Every prompt hook run writes a health record, even a disabled one. It holds the runtime, status, freshness, duration and cache hit. It holds no prompt text. The OpenCode plugin writes none. `advisor_status` then shows a `hookHealth` section. It adds the share of answers from the local scorer and the time of the newest record. The setup advisor leg shows both. The hook-wiring check now reads the command a shell would run. A hook that only names the advisor script reads as missing. The Codex check names the fix for a missing entry.\n \n #### Smaller Fixes\n \n - **A question about the trigger index reaches spec-kit.** It used to end at the doctor helper. A question about index drift still goes to the doctor.\n - **The doctor hand-off names the matched command.** It used to name only `/doctor:helper`, even when the exact command was known.\n - **A prompt that names a `system-`, `cli-` or `mcp-` skill is read.** The prompt policy used to read only `sk-` names.\n-- **An OpenCode brief names the command and its policy.** The plugin used to drop both.\n+- **An OpenCode brief names the command and its policy.** The plugin used to drop both. It also drops a second route line that printed `targets=none`.\n - **Three plain spec requests now reach spec-kit.** The advisor used to miss them.\n - **A read-only question about git history reaches sk-git.** `show the git log` used to return no skill. The question must name git, a commit or one of the branches main, master and develop.\n - **The advisor starts on the Node.js its native module was built for.** An install now records that Node.js. A session on another major version used to fail its first call with `daemon launcher exited with code 1`.\n@@ -574,7 +574,7 @@ The lookup budget is 200 ms at p95. A lookup with no hits takes 89 to 102 ms aga\n - **If an agent needs a `.env` value:** it now asks you. Paste the value yourself or compare fingerprints. For fingerprints, run `openssl rand -base64 32` and export the result as `ENV_SECRET_GUARD_PEPPER` in your shell profile. Never put it in a file inside a repository.\n - **If you embed the shipped `AGENTS.md`:** run `/doctor:agents-md` to take the new Gate 2 and Gate 6 wording. Remove any link of your own to the three retired reply rules.\n - **If you run the skill advisor from a built copy:** run `npm run build` in `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime` once.\n-- **If you match on an advisor command id:** `memory:save` and `command-memory-save` are now `command-speckit-save`. `command-spec-kit` is now one id per command, such as `command-speckit-plan`. `command-prompt-improver` is now `command-prompt-improve`.\n+- **If you type `/create:skill` or match on an advisor command id:** type `/create:sk-skill` instead. Change any script or saved prompt that names the old command. `memory:save` and `command-memory-save` are now `command-speckit-save`. `command-spec-kit` is now one id per command, such as `command-speckit-plan`. `command-prompt-improver` is now `command-prompt-improve`. `command-create-skill` is now `command-create-sk-skill`.\n - **On Codex:** approve the project hooks in `/hooks`, including the new `SessionStart` row. Until then the advisor brief never arrives. The compaction pointer does not run either. To turn on meaning matching anywhere, run `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder`.\n - **If Skilled is installed in your project:** run `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-hook-registrations.cjs` from the project root. It rewrites `.claude/settings.json` and `.codex/hooks.json`. Add `--check` to check for drift without writing.\n - **If a script or setting names a hook folder:** use the new name. `dispatch/` is `cli-dispatch/`, `task-dispatch/` is `subagent-dispatch-guard/` and `completion/` is `completion-evidence/`. `codex-watchdog/` and `hook-install/` are now `codex-global-hooks-check/`.\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md b/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\nindex 741500591d9..89fc19ec009 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\n@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\n name: sk-doc\n description: \"Documentation & component authoring hub: skills, agents, commands, READMEs, catalogs, playbooks, changelogs, goals, frontmatter.\"\n allowed-tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob]\n-version: 2.9.16.0\n+version: 2.10.0.0\n metadata:\n   family: sk-util\n ---\n@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@ Use this skill for documentation and OpenCode-component authoring, and for docum\n \n | Mode | Use it for | Packet | Command |\n |------|------------|--------|---------|\n-| **sk-create-skill** | Scaffold an OpenCode skill (and, via `sk-create-skill-parent`, a parent hub with nested mode packets) | `sk-create-skill/` | `/create:skill`, `/create:skill-parent` |\n+| **sk-create-skill** | Scaffold an OpenCode skill (and, via `sk-create-skill-parent`, a parent hub with nested mode packets) | `sk-create-skill/` | `/create:sk-skill`, `/create:skill-parent` |\n | **sk-create-readme** | Author a folder, code-folder or skill README, a repository front page and its install, contributing and security guides | `sk-create-readme/` | `/create:readme` |\n | **sk-create-agent** | Scaffold an OpenCode agent (permission/authority frontmatter) | `sk-create-agent/` | `/create:agent` |\n | **sk-create-command** | Scaffold an OpenCode slash command (argument-hint + allowed-tools + router/presentation split) | `sk-create-command/` | `/create:command` |\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md b/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md\nindex 914dd24d94f..f7a7ed60a92 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md\n@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n   - \"sk-create-skill routing\"\n importance_tier: normal\n contextType: general\n-version: 1.0.4.0\n+version: 1.0.5.0\n router_state: active\n skill_pointer: SKILL.md\n ---\n@@ -24,13 +24,13 @@ The router answers one question: given a request, which skill-local resources lo\n what happens when nothing matches. Every path below stays inside this skill folder, and no resource other than `DEFAULT_RESOURCE`\n loads before an intent selects it.\n \n-Requests reach this packet when they ask to create or rebuild an OpenCode skill under `.skilled/skills/`, to run `/create:skill` for a standalone skill or `/create:skill-parent` for a parent hub, to author or repair a skill package's `SKILL.md`, `README.md`, `references/`, `assets/`, `scripts/` or `changelog/`, or to validate and package a skill with `scripts/package_skill.py`. Its vocabulary is `create skill`, `new skill`, `skill scaffold`, `SKILL.md scaffold`, `OpenCode skill`, `parent hub`, `mode packet`, `nested workflow packet` and `package skill`. It routes to two resource families: the `references/shared/` doctrine and its root-metadata contract, which both modes load first, and the mode's own `references/<key>/` plus `assets/<key>/` trees, where `create-skill` resolves the `skill` key and `create-skill-parent` resolves `parent-skill`.\n+Requests reach this packet when they ask to create or rebuild an OpenCode skill under `.skilled/skills/`, to run `/create:sk-skill` for a standalone skill or `/create:skill-parent` for a parent hub, to author or repair a skill package's `SKILL.md`, `README.md`, `references/`, `assets/`, `scripts/` or `changelog/`, or to validate and package a skill with `scripts/package_skill.py`. Its vocabulary is `create skill`, `new skill`, `skill scaffold`, `SKILL.md scaffold`, `OpenCode skill`, `parent hub`, `mode packet`, `nested workflow packet` and `package skill`. It routes to two resource families: the `references/shared/` doctrine and its root-metadata contract, which both modes load first, and the mode's own `references/<key>/` plus `assets/<key>/` trees, where `create-skill` resolves the `skill` key and `create-skill-parent` resolves `parent-skill`.\n \n ---\n \n ## 2. INTENT MODEL\n \n-- **`SKILL_PACKAGE`** fires on `create skill`, `/create:skill`, `new skill`, `skill scaffold`, `SKILL.md scaffold`, `OpenCode skill`, `sk-skill`, `create sk-`, `reusable capability`, `reusable helper`, `starter reference docs`, `package skill`, `doc rewrite guard`, `doc-rewrite-guard.py`, `render ledger`, `render-known-debt.json`, `exempt from the render checks`, `render exempt map`, `kept every claim` and `kept every original claim` at weight 4. It loads the five shared docs — `references/shared/overview.md`, `references/shared/common-pitfalls.md`, `references/shared/validation-and-packaging.md`, `references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md`, `references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md` — then `references/skill/creation-workflow.md`, `references/skill/examples-and-maintenance.md`, `references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md`, and the eight `assets/skill/` templates: `assets/skill/skill-md-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-asset-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-procedure-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-scaffold-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-smart-router.md`, `assets/skill/skill-router-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-sync-manifest-template.md`. The skill README template is not in this set: the `sk-create-readme` mode owns it and writes the README step.\n+- **`SKILL_PACKAGE`** fires on `create skill`, `/create:sk-skill`, `new skill`, `skill scaffold`, `SKILL.md scaffold`, `OpenCode skill`, `sk-skill`, `create sk-`, `reusable capability`, `reusable helper`, `starter reference docs`, `package skill`, `doc rewrite guard`, `doc-rewrite-guard.py`, `render ledger`, `render-known-debt.json`, `exempt from the render checks`, `render exempt map`, `kept every claim` and `kept every original claim` at weight 4. It loads the five shared docs — `references/shared/overview.md`, `references/shared/common-pitfalls.md`, `references/shared/validation-and-packaging.md`, `references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md`, `references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md` — then `references/skill/creation-workflow.md`, `references/skill/examples-and-maintenance.md`, `references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md`, and the eight `assets/skill/` templates: `assets/skill/skill-md-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-asset-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-procedure-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-scaffold-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-smart-router.md`, `assets/skill/skill-router-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-sync-manifest-template.md`. The skill README template is not in this set: the `sk-create-readme` mode owns it and writes the README step.\n - **`PARENT_HUB`** fires on `/create:skill-parent`, `parent skill`, `parent hub`, `mode packet`, `nested workflow packet`, `mode-registry.json` and `hub-router.json` at weight 4. It loads the same five shared docs, then `references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md`, `references/parent-skill/parent-hub-router-schema.md`, `references/parent-skill/compiled-routing-architecture.md`, and the five `assets/parent-skill/` templates: `assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-template.md`, `assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-readme-template.md`, `assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-root-router-template.md`, `assets/parent-skill/scaffold/hub-skill-scaffold.md`, `assets/parent-skill/scaffold/packet-skill-scaffold.md`.\n \n ---\n@@ -94,7 +94,7 @@ RESOURCE_KEY_BY_MODE = {\n }\n \n INTENT_MODEL = {\n-    \"SKILL_PACKAGE\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create skill\", \"/create:skill\", \"new skill\", \"skill scaffold\", \"skill.md scaffold\", \"opencode skill\", \"sk-skill\", \"create sk-\", \"reusable capability\", \"reusable helper\", \"starter reference docs\", \"package skill\", \"doc rewrite guard\", \"doc-rewrite-guard.py\", \"render ledger\", \"render-known-debt.json\", \"exempt from the render checks\", \"render exempt map\", \"kept every claim\", \"kept every original claim\"]},\n+    \"SKILL_PACKAGE\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create skill\", \"/create:sk-skill\", \"new skill\", \"skill scaffold\", \"skill.md scaffold\", \"opencode skill\", \"sk-skill\", \"create sk-\", \"reusable capability\", \"reusable helper\", \"starter reference docs\", \"package skill\", \"doc rewrite guard\", \"doc-rewrite-guard.py\", \"render ledger\", \"render-known-debt.json\", \"exempt from the render checks\", \"render exempt map\", \"kept every claim\", \"kept every original claim\"]},\n     \"PARENT_HUB\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"/create:skill-parent\", \"parent skill\", \"parent hub\", \"mode packet\", \"nested workflow packet\", \"mode-registry.json\", \"hub-router.json\"]},\n }\n \n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff e91faf28b8c^2 e91faf28b8c -- .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt .skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794847696063,"end":1794847697046}}}}
