{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794847731817,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e542e968001zC00KjB8k8JrsZ","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e542b8f2001i38ypbrmG3HCPL","type":"tool","id":"call_d69fbe1764ef493d992d8011","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"47\\b\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md | head; echo \"=== command row counts in code ===\"; grep -rn \"command rows\\|commandRows\\|COMMAND_ROWS\\|command_rows\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime --include=*.ts --include=*.mjs --include=*.json -l | head -20"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:176:Command rows use the same embedder. The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 47 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves, and `skill_graph_scan` embeds it into its own `vec_cmd_<dim>` table beside the skill vectors. The scan skips a row whose text has not changed and prunes a row that is no longer generated. A command row normally passes only on one of its own phrases or its slash string. It can also pass on meaning: the prompt's real embedding has to reach a cosine of 0.72 against the row and lead the next command row by 0.02. A command that passed this way ranks first only when it leads the top passing skill by the same 0.02. A prompt that asks for no change, such as \"no edits\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only question lets only a command whose route only reads pass on meaning. Without the local embedder (Ollama serving `nomic-embed-text`) no cosine exists, so command rows pass on their phrases alone.\n=== command row counts in code ===\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-head-length.vitest.ts\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-command-bridges.vitest.ts\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.ts\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:176:Command rows use the same embedder. The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 47 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves, and `skill_graph_scan` embeds it into its own `vec_cmd_<dim>` table beside the skill vectors. The scan skips a row whose text has not changed and prunes a row that is no longer generated. A command row normally passes only on one of its own phrases or its slash string. It can also pass on meaning: the prompt's real embedding has to reach a cosine of 0.72 against the row and lead the next command row by 0.02. A command that passed this way ranks first only when it leads the top passing skill by the same 0.02. A prompt that asks for no change, such as \"no edits\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only question lets only a command whose route only reads pass on meaning. Without the local embedder (Ollama serving `nomic-embed-text`) no cosine exists, so command rows pass on their phrases alone.\n=== command row counts in code ===\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-head-length.vitest.ts\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-command-bridges.vitest.ts\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.ts\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \\\"47\\\\b\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md | head; echo \\\"=== command row counts in code ===\\\"; grep -rn \\\"command rows\\\\|commandRows\\\\|COMMAND_ROWS\\\\|command_rows\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime --include=*.ts --include=*.mjs --include=*.json -l | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794847730024,"end":1794847731817}}}}
