{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794847877400,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e54523e5001AgMLOuF0hKCJQg","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e544f25d001ajqVZGZ16DFEKc","type":"tool","id":"call_0fa5049caa3245929c862d65","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 5b2b062baef e91faf28b8c -- .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt; echo \"=== full branch->merge for presentation (word diff) ===\"; git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --word-diff=porcelain 5b2b062baef e91faf28b8c -- .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt | head -40"},"output":"diff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt\nindex bbc8c02f918..948bbb4e2d4 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt\n@@ -55,7 +55,7 @@ Ask every answer that is still missing in one prompt, then wait. This follows th\n Where should Skilled go? Answer any or all in one reply, for example \"/Users/me/code/my-app, claude and codex, auto, embed\".\n \n 1) Target repo: the absolute path, for example /Users/me/code/my-app\n-2) Runtimes: claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin, pi, or \"the ones already there\"\n+2) Runtimes: claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin, pi, vibe, dsh, or \"the ones already there\"\n 3) Link shape: auto / whole / merge   (auto unless a real folder already sits where a link would go)\n 4) Instruction file: embed / link   (embed keeps the repo's own AGENTS.md; link points AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and REPO RULES.md at the checkout's copies)\n ```\n@@ -75,9 +75,7 @@ The example carries all four answers so the shape of a full reply is visible. Ne\n | `embed` | step 2 stays | The repo keeps its own `AGENTS.md` and the shipped sections are refreshed into it |\n | `link` | step 1 gains `--link-instructions`, step 2 is dropped | `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `REPO RULES.md` become links into the checkout |\n \n-A runtime name outside claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin and pi or the ones already there, a shape outside the three, or an instruction word outside the two is not guessed. Ask that one question again with the accepted values. When the engine refuses a root, show its `ERROR:` line as it printed and ask question 1 again.\n-\n-DSH is not offered, because the link manifest has no DSH row.\n+A runtime name outside the nine, a shape outside the three, or an instruction word outside the two is not guessed. Ask that one question again with the accepted values. When the engine refuses a root, show its `ERROR:` line as it printed and ask question 1 again.\n \n ## 5. The Symlink Check\n \n=== full branch->merge for presentation (word diff) ===\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt\nindex bbc8c02f918..948bbb4e2d4 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt\n@@ -55,7 +55,7 @@ Ask every answer that is still missing in one prompt, then wait. This follows th\n Where should Skilled go? Answer any or all in one reply, for example \"/Users/me/code/my-app, claude and codex, auto, embed\".\n~\n \n~\n 1) Target repo: the absolute path, for example /Users/me/code/my-app\n~\n 2) Runtimes: claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin, pi, \n+vibe, dsh,\n  or \"the ones already there\"\n~\n 3) Link shape: auto / whole / merge   (auto unless a real folder already sits where a link would go)\n~\n 4) Instruction file: embed / link   (embed keeps the repo's own AGENTS.md; link points AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and REPO RULES.md at the checkout's copies)\n~\n ```\n~\n@@ 