 `package skill`, `doc rewrite guard`, `doc-rewrite-guard.py`, `render ledger`, `render-known-debt.json`, `exempt from the render checks`, `render exempt map`, `kept every claim` and `kept every original claim` at weight 4. It loads the five shared docs — `references/shared/overview.md`, `references/shared/common-pitfalls.md`, `references/shared/validation-and-packaging.md`, `references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md`, `references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md` — then `references/skill/creation-workflow.md`, `references/skill/examples-and-maintenance.md`, `references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md`, and the eight `assets/skill/` templates: `assets/skill/skill-md-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-asset-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-procedure-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-scaffold-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-smart-router.md`, `assets/skill/skill-router-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-sync-manifest-template.md`. The skill README template is not in this set: the `sk-create-readme` mode owns it and writes the README step.\n - **`PARENT_HUB`** fires on `/create:skill-parent`, `parent skill`, `parent hub`, `mode packet`, `nested workflow packet`, `mode-registry.json` and `hub-router.json` at weight 4. It loads the same five shared docs, then `references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md`, `references/parent-skill/parent-hub-router-schema.md`, `references/parent-skill/compiled-routing-architecture.md`, and the five `assets/parent-skill/` templates: `assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-template.md`, `assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-readme-template.md`, `assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-root-router-template.md`, `assets/parent-skill/scaffold/hub-skill-scaffold.md`, `assets/parent-skill/scaffold/packet-skill-scaffold.md`.\n \n ---\n@@ -50,7 +50,7 @@ SKILL AUTHORING REQUEST\n     +- Standalone skill -> workflowMode: sk-create-skill\n     |   +- scripts/init_skill.py\n     |   +- assets/skill/sk