{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794847903817,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5458e5c001sVa0d5lOjnHCvw","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e5457b84001ajhj6McguZEKmH","type":"tool","id":"call_cf85945d0fea4d12a3416718","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts","offset":1,"limit":60},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts, lines 1-60\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: Command Routing Slice\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: \n5: // Ratchets live command routing against the committed capture. An aggregate can\n6: // hold still while one row is gained and another lost, so the rows are compared\n7: // one by one and the corpus hash pins the prompts the capture was measured\n8: // against: a scoring change, a bridge-metadata change or a corpus edit has to\n9: // surface here instead of drifting in silently.\n10: \n11: import { existsSync, mkdtempSync, readFileSync, rmSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n12: import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\n13: import { dirname, join, resolve } from 'node:path';\n14: import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n15: \n16: import { afterEach, beforeAll, beforeEach, describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\n17: import {\n18:   assertFitRowsUnique as captureAssertFitRowsUnique,\n19:   scoreCommandCorpus as captureCommandCorpus,\n20: } from '../scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs';\n21: \n22: const HERE = dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\n23: const ROUTING = resolve(HERE, '../scripts/routing-accuracy');\n24: const CORPUS_PATH = join(ROUTING, 'command-prompts.jsonl');\n25: const BASELINE_PATH = join(ROUTING, 'command-routing-baseline.json');\n26: \n27: // A host with its own hub vocabulary routes some rows differently from upstream.\n28: // It keeps its own capture in a `.host.json` file beside the upstream one, and\n29: // the ratchet reads that file whenever it exists. Every row stays guarded on the\n30: // host, including the rows its vocabulary moved.\n31: function capturePath(upstreamPath: string): string {\n32:   const hostPath = upstreamPath.replace(/\\.json$/, '.host.json');\n33:   return existsSync(hostPath) ? hostPath : upstreamPath;\n34: }\n35: \n36: const BASELINE_READ_PATH = capturePath(BASELINE_PATH);\n37: // The capture prints its JSON to stdout, so a host writes its own file by\n38: // redirecting that output rather than through `--write`, which targets upstream.\n39: const RECAPTURE = BASELINE_READ_PATH === BASELINE_PATH\n40:   ? 'node scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs --write'\n41:   : 'node scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs > scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.host.json';\n42: \n43: // The capture projects these nine names to score reproducibly. A harness imports\n44: // the module and scores in process, so the projection has to be undone before\n45: // the call returns or it silently changes how every later test scores.\n46: const PROJECTED_ENV = [\n47:   'SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR',\n48:   'SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLE_BUILTIN_SEMANTIC',\n49:   'VITEST',\n50:   'SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL',\n51:   'PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE',\n52:   'SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_WEIGHTS_JSON',\n53:   'SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_SHADOW_WEIGHTS_JSON',\n54:   'SPECKIT_ADVISOR_BM25_LEXICAL_SHADOW',\n55:   'SPECKIT_PRIVATE_SKILL_ROOTS',\n56: ] as const;\n57: \n58: type ProjectedEnv = Readonly<Record<(typeof PROJECTED_ENV)[number], string | undefined>>;\n59: \n60: function readProjectedEnv(): ProjectedEnv {\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 61]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts, lines 1-60\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: Command Routing Slice\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: \n5: // Ratchets live command routing against the committed capture. An aggregate can\n6: // hold still while one row is gained and another lost, so the rows are compared\n7: // one by one and the corpus hash pins the prompts the capture was measured\n8: // against: a scoring change, a bridge-metadata change or a corpus edit has to\n9: // surface here instead of drifting in silently.\n10: \n11: import { existsSync, mkdtempSync, readFileSync, rmSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n12: import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\n13: import { dirname, join, resolve } from 'node:path';\n14: import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n15: \n16: import { afterEach, beforeAll, beforeEach, describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\n17: import {\n18:   assertFitRowsUnique as captureAssertFitRowsUnique,\n19:   scoreCommandCorpus as captureCommandCorpus,\n20: } from '../scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs';\n21: \n22: const HERE = dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\n23: const ROUTING = resolve(HERE, '../scripts/routing-accuracy');\n24: const CORPUS_PATH = join(ROUTING, 'command-prompts.jsonl');\n25: const BASELINE_PATH = join(ROUTING, 'command-routing-baseline.json');\n26: \n27: // A host with its own hub vocabulary routes some rows differently from upstream.\n28: // It keeps its own capture in a `.host.json` file beside the upstream one, and\n29: // the ratchet reads that file whenever it exists. Every row stays guarded on the\n30: // host, including the rows its vocabulary moved.\n31: function capturePath(upstreamPath: string): string {\n32:   const hostPath = upstreamPath.replace(/\\.json$/, '.host.json');\n33:   return existsSync(hostPath) ? hostPath : upstreamPath;\n34: }\n35: \n36: const BASELINE_READ_PATH = capturePath(BASELINE_PATH);\n37: // The capture prints its JSON to stdout, so a host writes its own file by\n38: // redirecting that output rather than through `--write`, which targets upstream.\n39: const RECAPTURE = BASELINE_READ_PATH === BASELINE_PATH\n40:   ? 'node scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs --write'\n41:   : 'node scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs > scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.host.json';\n42: \n43: // The capture projects these nine names to score reproducibly. A harness imports\n44: // the module and scores in process, so the projection has to be undone before\n45: // the call returns or it silently changes how every later test scores.\n46: const PROJECTED_ENV = [\n47:   'SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR',\n48:   'SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLE_BUILTIN_SEMANTIC',\n49:   'VITEST',\n50:   'SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL',\n51:   'PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE',\n52:   'SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_WEIGHTS_JSON',\n53:   'SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_SHADOW_WEIGHTS_JSON',\n54:   'SPECKIT_ADVISOR_BM25_LEXICAL_SHADOW',\n55:   'SPECKIT_PRIVATE_SKILL_ROOTS',\n56: ] as const;\n57: \n58: type ProjectedEnv = Readonly<Record<(typeof PROJECTED_ENV)[number], string | undefined>>;\n59: \n60: function readProjectedEnv(): ProjectedEnv {\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 61]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":60}"},"time":{"start":1794847903324,"end":1794847903817}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794847903850,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5458965001kmVhEHIWEEYHT0","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e5457b84001ajhj6McguZEKmH","type":"tool","id":"call_fb0d767db1804cc5a31903ec","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '1,30p' .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md; echo \"=== router grep ===\"; grep -n \"skill-readme-template\\|/create:sk-skill\\|/create:skill\\b\" .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md | head -20; echo \"=== file exists? ===\"; ls .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/ | head -20"},"output":"---\nname: sk-doc\ndescription: \"Documentation & component authoring hub: skills, agents, commands, READMEs, catalogs, playbooks, changelogs, goals, frontmatter.\"\nallowed-tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob]\nversion: 2.10.0.0\nmetadata:\n  family: sk-util\n---\n\n<!-- Keywords: sk-doc, documentation, markdown, authoring, parent-hub, mode-registry, hub-router, workflowmode, packetkind, sk-create-skill, sk-create-readme, sk-create-agent, sk-create-command, sk-create-feature-catalog, sk-create-manual-testing-playbook, sk-create-benchmark, sk-create-changelog, sk-create-diff, sk-create-repo-rule, sk-create-frontmatter, sk-create-goal, sk-create-with-human-voice, sk-create-quality-control, human-voice-rules, hvr, shared-backbone, create-quality-control-pipeline -->\n\n# Documentation Authoring Hub (sk-doc)\n\nOne advisor identity, fifteen workflow modes across fourteen packets, one shared sk-create-quality-control backbone.\n`sk-doc` is the parent hub for documentation and OpenCode-component authoring.\nIt holds NO per-packet logic: it routes by `workflowMode` through `mode-registry.json`, and each packet keeps its own contract in its nested folder.\nThe cross-cutting sk-create-quality-control pipeline (validators, global standards, frontmatter/llms/template assets) lives once in `shared/` and is consumed by every packet.\n\n**Version authority.** This file's `version` frontmatter is the hub's release version and matches the newest entry under `changelog/`; `description.json`, `mode-registry.json` and `hub-router.json` carry the same value, so every hub-root JSON routing file states the same release; `ROUTER.md` keeps its own document version.\n\n---\n\n## 1. WHEN TO USE\n\nUse this skill for documentation and OpenCode-component authoring, and for document-quality work. The hub classifies the request, resolves a `workflowMode`, and loads the matching nested packet.\n\n| Mode | Use it for | Packet | Command |\n|------|------------|--------|---------|\n| **sk-create-skill** | Scaffold an OpenCode skill (and, via `sk-create-skill-parent`, a parent hub with nested mode packets) | `sk-create-skill/` | `/create:sk-skill`, `/create:skill-parent` |\n| **sk-create-readme** | Author a folder, code-folder or skill README, a repository front page and its install, contributing and security guides | `sk-create-readme/` | `/create:readme` |\n=== router grep ===\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md:27:Requests reach this packet when they ask to create or rebuild an OpenCode skill under `.skilled/skills/`, to run `/create:sk-skill` for a standalone skill or `/create:skill-parent` for a parent hub, to author or repair a skill package's `SKILL.md`, `README.md`, `references/`, `assets/`, `scripts/` or `changelog/`, or to validate and package a skill with `scripts/package_skill.py`. Its vocabulary is `create skill`, `new skill`, `skill scaffold`, `SKILL.md scaffold`, `OpenCode skill`, `parent hub`, `mode packet`, `nested workflow packet` and `package skill`. It routes to two resource families: the `references/shared/` doctrine and its root-metadata contract, which both modes load first, and the mode's own `references/<key>/` plus `assets/<key>/` trees, where `create-skill` resolves the `skill` key and `create-skill-parent` resolves `parent-skill`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md:33:- **`SKILL_PACKAGE`** fires on `create skill`, `/create:sk-skill`, `new skill`, `skill scaffold`, `SKILL.md scaffold`, `OpenCode skill`, `sk-skill`, `create sk-`, `reusable capability`, `reusable helper`, `starter reference docs`, `package skill`, `doc rewrite guard`, `doc-rewrite-guard.py`, `render ledger`, `render-known-debt.json`, `exempt from the render checks`, `render exempt map`, `kept every claim` and `kept every original claim` at weight 4. It loads the five shared docs — `references/shared/overview.md`, `references/shared/common-pitfalls.md`, `references/shared/validation-and-packaging.md`, `references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md`, `references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md` — then `references/skill/creation-workflow.md`, `references/skill/examples-and-maintenance.md`, `references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md`, and the eight `assets/skill/` templates: `assets/skill/skill-md-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-asset-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-procedure-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-scaffold-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-smart-router.md`, `assets/skill/skill-router-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-sync-manifest-template.md`. The skill README template is not in this set: the `sk-create-readme` mode owns it and writes the README step.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md:34:- **`PARENT_HUB`** fires on `/create:skill-parent`, `parent skill`, `parent hub`, `mode packet`, `nested workflow packet`, `mode-registry.json` and `hub-router.json` at weight 4. It loads the same five shared docs, then `references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md`, `references/parent-skill/parent-hub-router-schema.md`, `references/parent-skill/compiled-routing-architecture.md`, and the five `assets/parent-skill/` templates: `assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-template.md`, `assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-readme-template.md`, `assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-root-router-template.md`, `assets/parent-skill/scaffold/hub-skill-scaffold.md`, `assets/parent-skill/scaffold/packet-skill-scaffold.md`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md:97:    \"SKILL_PACKAGE\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create skill\", \"/create:sk-skill\", \"new skill\", \"skill scaffold\", \"skill.md scaffold\", \"opencode skill\", \"sk-skill\", \"create sk-\", \"reusable capability\", \"reusable helper\", \"starter reference docs\", \"package skill\", \"doc rewrite guard\", \"doc-rewrite-guard.py\", \"render ledger\", \"render-known-debt.json\", \"exempt from the render checks\", \"render exempt map\", \"kept every claim\", \"kept every original claim\"]},\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md:98:    \"PARENT_HUB\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"/create:skill-parent\", \"parent skill\", \"parent hub\", \"mode packet\", \"nested workflow packet\", \"mode-registry.json\", \"hub-router.json\"]},\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md:134:        \"assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-readme-template.md\",\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md:29:| **sk-create-skill** | Scaffold an OpenCode skill (and, via `sk-create-skill-parent`, a parent hub with nested mode packets) | `sk-create-skill/` | `/create:sk-skill`, `/create:skill-parent` |\n=== file exists? ===\nskill-asset-template.md\nskill-graph-metadata-template.json\nskill-leaf-manifest-config-template.json\nskill-md-template.md\nskill-procedure-template.md\nskill-reference-template.md\nskill-router-template.md\nskill-scaffold-template.md\nskill-smart-router.md\nskill-sync-manifest-template.md\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: sk-doc\ndescription: \"Documentation & component authoring hub: skills, agents, commands, READMEs, catalogs, playbooks, changelogs, goals, frontmatter.\"\nallowed-tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob]\nversion: 2.10.0.0\nmetadata:\n  family: sk-util\n---\n\n<!-- Keywords: sk-doc, documentation, markdown, authoring, parent-hub, mode-registry, hub-router, workflowmode, packetkind, sk-create-skill, sk-create-readme, sk-create-agent, sk-create-command, sk-create-feature-catalog, sk-create-manual-testing-playbook, sk-create-benchmark, sk-create-changelog, sk-create-diff, sk-create-repo-rule, sk-create-frontmatter, sk-create-goal, sk-create-with-human-voice, sk-create-quality-control, human-voice-rules, hvr, shared-backbone, create-quality-control-pipeline -->\n\n# Documentation Authoring Hub (sk-doc)\n\nOne advisor identity, fifteen workflow modes across fourteen packets, one shared sk-create-quality-control backbone.\n`sk-doc` is the parent hub for documentation and OpenCode-component authoring.\nIt holds NO per-packet logic: it routes by `workflowMode` through `mode-registry.json`, and each packet keeps its own contract in its nested folder.\nThe cross-cutting sk-create-quality-control pipeline (validators, global standards, frontmatter/llms/template assets) lives once in `shared/` and is consumed by every packet.\n\n**Version authority.** This file's `version` frontmatter is the hub's release version and matches the newest entry under `changelog/`; `description.json`, `mode-registry.json` and `hub-router.json` carry the same value, so every hub-root JSON routing file states the same release; `ROUTER.md` keeps its own document version.\n\n---\n\n## 1. WHEN TO USE\n\nUse this skill for documentation and OpenCode-component authoring, and for document-quality work. The hub classifies the request, resolves a `workflowMode`, and loads the matching nested packet.\n\n| Mode | Use it for | Packet | Command |\n|------|------------|--------|---------|\n| **sk-create-skill** | Scaffold an OpenCode skill (and, via `sk-create-skill-parent`, a parent hub with nested mode packets) | `sk-create-skill/` | `/create:sk-skill`, `/create:skill-parent` |\n| **sk-create-readme** | Author a folder, code-folder or skill README, a repository front page and its install, contributing and security guides | `sk-create-readme/` | `/create:readme` |\n=== router grep ===\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md:27:Requests reach this packet when they ask to create or rebuild an OpenCode skill under `.skilled/skills/`, to run `/create:sk-skill` for a standalone skill or `/create:skill-parent` for a parent hub, to author or repair a skill package's `SKILL.md`, `README.md`, `references/`, `assets/`, `scripts/` or `changelog/`, or to validate and package a skill with `scripts/package_skill.py`. Its vocabulary is `create skill`, `new skill`, `skill scaffold`, `SKILL.md scaffold`, `OpenCode skill`, `parent hub`, `mode packet`, `nested workflow packet` and `package skill`. It routes to two resource families: the `references/shared/` doctrine and its root-metadata contract, which both modes load first, and the mode's own `references/<key>/` plus `assets/<key>/` trees, where `create-skill` resolves the `skill` key and `create-skill-parent` resolves `parent-skill`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md:33:- **`SKILL_PACKAGE`** fires on `create skill`, `/create:sk-skill`, `new skill`, `skill scaffold`, `SKILL.md scaffold`, `OpenCode skill`, `sk-skill`, `create sk-`, `reusable capability`, `reusable helper`, `starter reference docs`, `package skill`, `doc rewrite guard`, `doc-rewrite-guard.py`, `render ledger`, `render-known-debt.json`, `exempt from the render checks`, `render exempt map`, `kept every claim` and `kept every original claim` at weight 4. It loads the five shared docs — `references/shared/overview.md`, `references/shared/common-pitfalls.md`, `references/shared/validation-and-packaging.md`, `references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md`, `references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md` — then `references/skill/creation-workflow.md`, `references/skill/examples-and-maintenance.md`, `references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md`, and the eight `assets/skill/` templates: `assets/skill/skill-md-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-asset-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-procedure-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-scaffold-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-smart-router.md`, `assets/skill/skill-router-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-sync-manifest-template.md`. The skill README template is not in this set: the `sk-create-readme` mode owns it and writes the README step.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md:34:- **`PARENT_HUB`** fires on `/create:skill-parent`, `parent skill`, `parent hub`, `mode packet`, `nested workflow packet`, `mode-registry.json` and `hub-router.json` at weight 4. It loads the same five shared docs, then `references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md`, `references/parent-skill/parent-hub-router-schema.md`, `references/parent-skill/compiled-routing-architecture.md`, and the five `assets/parent-skill/` templates: `assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-template.md`, `assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-readme-template.md`, `assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-root-router-template.md`, `assets/parent-skill/scaffold/hub-skill-scaffold.md`, `assets/parent-skill/scaffold/packet-skill-scaffold.md`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md:97:    \"SKILL_PACKAGE\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create skill\", \"/create:sk-skill\", \"new skill\", \"skill scaffold\", \"skill.md scaffold\", \"opencode skill\", \"sk-skill\", \"create sk-\", \"reusable capability\", \"reusable helper\", \"starter reference docs\", \"package skill\", \"doc rewrite guard\", \"doc-rewrite-guard.py\", \"render ledger\", \"render-known-debt.json\", \"exempt from the render checks\", \"render exempt map\", \"kept every claim\", \"kept every original claim\"]},\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md:98:    \"PARENT_HUB\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"/create:skill-parent\", \"parent skill\", \"parent hub\", \"mode packet\", \"nested workflow packet\", \"mode-registry.json\", \"hub-router.json\"]},\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md:134:        \"assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-readme-template.md\",\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md:29:| **sk-create-skill** | Scaffold an OpenCode skill (and, via `sk-create-skill-parent`, a parent hub with nested mode packets) | `sk-create-skill/` | `/create:sk-skill`, `/create:skill-parent` |\n=== file exists? ===\nskill-asset-template.md\nskill-graph-metadata-template.json\nskill-leaf-manifest-config-template.json\nskill-md-template.md\nskill-procedure-template.md\nskill-reference-template.md\nskill-router-template.md\nskill-scaffold-template.md\nskill-smart-router.md\nskill-sync-manifest-template.md\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '1,30p' .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md; echo \\\"=== router grep ===\\\"; grep -n \\\"skill-readme-template\\\\|/create:sk-skill\\\\|/create:skill\\\\b\\\" .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md | head -20; echo \\\"=== file exists? ===\\\"; ls .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/ | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794847902053,"end":1794847903850}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794847905342,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"id":"prt_1e545963e001rrrVfersv2H0re","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e5457b84001ajhj6McguZEKmH","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"092426e4f81bb6b2eecf8b0057528ac081747188","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":1498,"output":270,"reasoning":220,"cache":{"read":139136,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794847907629,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"id":"prt_1e5459f2d0019cm5d6LAe5gIR2","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e54596460012wP0DCiEjzrj2V","type":"step-start","snapshot":"092426e4f81bb6b2eecf8b0057528ac081747188"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794847915215,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e545b77a00263qQXoM0OSe0JZ","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e54596460012wP0DCiEjzrj2V","type":"tool","id":"call_97dbb9b1d4e240c18ece05f1","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '1,80p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs"},"output":"// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// MODULE: Vibe Prompt Advisor Part\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// The turn-start composer's advisor part. Vibe runs a fresh hook process for\n// every turn, so the receipts that keep a brief from repeating have to survive\n// the process: the shared handler's own file-backed store drops the constant\n// directive block once it is proven delivered, and a per-session head receipt\n// drops the routing head while the route has not changed. A child session, a\n// subagent and a blank prompt get nothing. Every failure contributes no text,\n// so a slow or broken advisor never blocks the turn.\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 1. IMPORTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nimport { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\nimport { existsSync, mkdirSync, readFileSync, readdirSync, statSync, unlinkSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\nimport { dirname, join, resolve } from 'node:path';\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n\nimport { isHookEnabled } from '../../../../hooks/shared/hook-flags.mjs';\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 2. CONSTANTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n// A Vibe session runs in a throwaway folder, so the checkout is located from\n// this file instead: vibe -> hooks -> system-skill-advisor -> skills -> .skilled -> root.\nconst REPO_ROOT = resolve(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '../../../../..');\n\nconst ADVISOR_MODULE_URL = new URL(\n  '../../runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js',\n  import.meta.url,\n).href;\n\n// Mirrors the advisor renderer's directive label. A brief that drifts past it is\n// never split, so it is always delivered whole.\nconst DIRECTIVE_SEPARATOR = '\\nDirectives:';\nconst CHILD_SESSION_ENV = 'AI_SESSION_CHILD';\n// The directive store's own base directory, so one switch isolates both receipts\n// in a test or a scratch run.\nconst STATE_DIR_ENV = 'SPECKIT_DIRECTIVE_LIFECYCLE_STATE_DIR';\nconst HEAD_RECEIPT_SUBDIR = 'vibe-turn-start';\nconst MAX_HEAD_RECEIPTS = 64;\n// Vibe has no command loader and its prompt stubs name the dash form, so a head\n// that names a command is the one place a model learns which document to read.\nconst COMMAND_DOCUMENT_LABEL = 'Command documents (read in full before taking one): ';\nconst COMMAND_TOKEN_PATTERN = /(?:^|[\\s(])\\/([a-z][a-z0-9-]*)(?::([a-z][a-z0-9-]*))?/g;\n\nexport const ERROR_POLICY = 'fail-open';\n// The advisor keys its metrics and outcome records by runtime and drops a label it does not list.\nexport const ADVISOR_RUNTIME = 'vibe';\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 3. HELPERS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n// A dispatched child inherits AI_SESSION_CHILD=1, and a subagent Vibe spawned\n// itself carries a parent session id. Either marks a session whose prompt is a\n// fixed task, where a route suggestion is noise.\nfunction isChildSession(payload, env) {\n  if (String(env[CHILD_SESSION_ENV] ?? '').trim() === '1') return true;\n  const parent = payload?.parent_session_id;\n  return typeof parent === 'string' && parent.trim() !== '';\n}\n\nfunction headReceiptDir(env = process.env) {\n  const configured = env[STATE_DIR_ENV]?.trim();\n  const base = configured ? resolve(configured) : join(tmpdir(), 'speckit-advisor');\n  return join(base, HEAD_RECEIPT_SUBDIR);\n}\n\nfunction headReceiptPath(sessionId, env = process.env) {\n  const digest = createHash('sha256').update(sessionId).digest('hex').slice(0, 16);\n  return join(headReceiptDir(env), `${digest}.head`);\n}\n\nfunction readHeadReceipt(sessionId, env = process.env) {\n  try {\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// MODULE: Vibe Prompt Advisor Part\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// The turn-start composer's advisor part. Vibe runs a fresh hook process for\n// every turn, so the receipts that keep a brief from repeating have to survive\n// the process: the shared handler's own file-backed store drops the constant\n// directive block once it is proven delivered, and a per-session head receipt\n// drops the routing head while the route has not changed. A child session, a\n// subagent and a blank prompt get nothing. Every failure contributes no text,\n// so a slow or broken advisor never blocks the turn.\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 1. IMPORTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nimport { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\nimport { existsSync, mkdirSync, readFileSync, readdirSync, statSync, unlinkSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\nimport { dirname, join, resolve } from 'node:path';\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n\nimport { isHookEnabled } from '../../../../hooks/shared/hook-flags.mjs';\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 2. CONSTANTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n// A Vibe session runs in a throwaway folder, so the checkout is located from\n// this file instead: vibe -> hooks -> system-skill-advisor -> skills -> .skilled -> root.\nconst REPO_ROOT = resolve(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '../../../../..');\n\nconst ADVISOR_MODULE_URL = new URL(\n  '../../runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js',\n  import.meta.url,\n).href;\n\n// Mirrors the advisor renderer's directive label. A brief that drifts past it is\n// never split, so it is always delivered whole.\nconst DIRECTIVE_SEPARATOR = '\\nDirectives:';\nconst CHILD_SESSION_ENV = 'AI_SESSION_CHILD';\n// The directive store's own base directory, so one switch isolates both receipts\n// in a test or a scratch run.\nconst STATE_DIR_ENV = 'SPECKIT_DIRECTIVE_LIFECYCLE_STATE_DIR';\nconst HEAD_RECEIPT_SUBDIR = 'vibe-turn-start';\nconst MAX_HEAD_RECEIPTS = 64;\n// Vibe has no command loader and its prompt stubs name the dash form, so a head\n// that names a command is the one place a model learns which document to read.\nconst COMMAND_DOCUMENT_LABEL = 'Command documents (read in full before taking one): ';\nconst COMMAND_TOKEN_PATTERN = /(?:^|[\\s(])\\/([a-z][a-z0-9-]*)(?::([a-z][a-z0-9-]*))?/g;\n\nexport const ERROR_POLICY = 'fail-open';\n// The advisor keys its metrics and outcome records by runtime and drops a label it does not list.\nexport const ADVISOR_RUNTIME = 'vibe';\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 3. HELPERS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n// A dispatched child inherits AI_SESSION_CHILD=1, and a subagent Vibe spawned\n// itself carries a parent session id. Either marks a session whose prompt is a\n// fixed task, where a route suggestion is noise.\nfunction isChildSession(payload, env) {\n  if (String(env[CHILD_SESSION_ENV] ?? '').trim() === '1') return true;\n  const parent = payload?.parent_session_id;\n  return typeof parent === 'string' && parent.trim() !== '';\n}\n\nfunction headReceiptDir(env = process.env) {\n  const configured = env[STATE_DIR_ENV]?.trim();\n  const base = configured ? resolve(configured) : join(tmpdir(), 'speckit-advisor');\n  return join(base, HEAD_RECEIPT_SUBDIR);\n}\n\nfunction headReceiptPath(sessionId, env = process.env) {\n  const digest = createHash('sha256').update(sessionId).digest('hex').slice(0, 16);\n  return join(headReceiptDir(env), `${digest}.head`);\n}\n\nfunction readHeadReceipt(sessionId, env = process.env) {\n  try {\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '1,80p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs\"}"},"time":{"start":1794847913850,"end":1794847915215}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794847915382,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e545b9830015aqcxjmv7gdDmJ","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e54596460012wP0DCiEjzrj2V","type":"tool","id":"call_4642fc9b1ed44230b508969d","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"prompt-advisor\\|recordAdvisorHookDiagnostic\\|persistAdvisorHook\" .skilled/hooks .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks 2>/dev/null | grep -v node_modules | head -25"},"output":".skilled/hooks/directive-lifecycle/README.md:81:| Pi | None registered | None | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts` | Nothing, on a proven same-content repeat. |\n.skilled/hooks/directive-lifecycle/README.md:82:| DSH | None registered | None | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs` | The routing head only, while the same block is still in context. |\n.skilled/hooks/directive-lifecycle/README.md:92:Pi uses its own in-memory check in `prompt-advisor.ts`. It drops its whole contribution on a proven same-content repeat. `SPECKIT_PI_DIRECTIVE_DEDUP` toggles that in-memory check, which is on by default.\n.skilled/hooks/cli-dispatch/pi/dispatch-preflight-lint.test.ts:11:import promptAdvisor from '../../../skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor';\n.skilled/hooks/cli-dispatch/pi/README.md:59:- [`../../../skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts`](../../../skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts): the advisor whose directive dedup the second suite covers.\n.skilled/hooks/cli-dispatch/pi/directive-dedup.test.ts:16:} from '../../../skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor';\n.skilled/hooks/session-lifecycle/vibe/turn-start.test.mjs:23:import { ADVISOR_RUNTIME, buildAdvisorPart } from '../../../skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs';\n.skilled/hooks/session-lifecycle/vibe/README.md:29:The advisor brief is built by `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs` under the `vibe` runtime label. A blank prompt, a dispatched child (`AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`) and a subagent (`parent_session_id` set) get no brief. The shared handler's file-backed directive store sends the constant `Directives:` block once. A per-session head receipt sends the routing head only when it changed.\n.skilled/hooks/session-lifecycle/vibe/README.md:116:- [`../../../skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs`](../../../skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs): the advisor part the composer calls.\n.skilled/hooks/session-lifecycle/vibe/turn-start.mjs:27:import { buildAdvisorPart } from '../../../skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs';\n.skilled/hooks/coverage-rationale.md:71:Per the module: *\"host lifecycle hooks advance durable policy state independently of prompt payloads.\"* Elsewhere the de-dup lives in `prompt-advisor.ts` (Pi), `prompt-advisor.mjs` (DSH), `system-skill-advisor` state (OpenCode), the shared `user-prompt-submit` (Codex/Cursor/Devin). The DSH adapter sends the full directive block once per session start or completed compaction and the `Advisor:` head alone while the block is unchanged, and the `directive-lifecycle` switch restores the full brief every turn.\n.skilled/hooks/injection-contract.md:68:- **Channel per runtime:** Claude Code `[SYS]` (`user-prompt-submit.js` -> `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`). Cursor/Devin `[SYS]` (same shim, re-wrapped into each CLI's own envelope). Codex `[SYS]` (mirror of the Claude shim). OpenCode `[SYS]` (`system-skill-advisor.js` via `experimental.chat.system.transform`). Pi `[MSG]` (`prompt-advisor.ts` forwards the shared context onto the visible prompt via the `input` event's `{action:\"transform\"}`). DSH `[SYS]` (`agent/pre-step`, interactive only, as an appended `repo-guards` message).\n.skilled/hooks/README.md:391:| `directive-lifecycle` | ✓ covered | by-design: embedded in the shared `user-prompt-submit` lifecycle | by-design: embedded in the shared `user-prompt-submit` lifecycle | by-design: embedded in the shared `user-prompt-submit` lifecycle | by-design: embedded in `system-skill-advisor` lifecycle state | by-design: embedded in `prompt-advisor.ts` directive de-dup | by-design: embedded in `prompt-advisor.mjs` directive de-dup | by-design: embedded in the Vibe turn-start advisor part |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/pi/README.md:48:| `lib/claude-hook-adapter.ts` | (library) | `spawnSync` proxy into this skill's compiled Claude hook outputs plus the JSON-envelope parser. It is imported by the session bridges and the advisor's `prompt-advisor.ts`. |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/hooks/directive-lifecycle/README.md:81:| Pi | None registered | None | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts` | Nothing, on a proven same-content repeat. |\n.skilled/hooks/directive-lifecycle/README.md:82:| DSH | None registered | None | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs` | The routing head only, while the same block is still in context. |\n.skilled/hooks/directive-lifecycle/README.md:92:Pi uses its own in-memory check in `prompt-advisor.ts`. It drops its whole contribution on a proven same-content repeat. `SPECKIT_PI_DIRECTIVE_DEDUP` toggles that in-memory check, which is on by default.\n.skilled/hooks/cli-dispatch/pi/dispatch-preflight-lint.test.ts:11:import promptAdvisor from '../../../skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor';\n.skilled/hooks/cli-dispatch/pi/README.md:59:- [`../../../skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts`](../../../skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts): the advisor whose directive dedup the second suite covers.\n.skilled/hooks/cli-dispatch/pi/directive-dedup.test.ts:16:} from '../../../skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor';\n.skilled/hooks/session-lifecycle/vibe/turn-start.test.mjs:23:import { ADVISOR_RUNTIME, buildAdvisorPart } from '../../../skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs';\n.skilled/hooks/session-lifecycle/vibe/README.md:29:The advisor brief is built by `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs` under the `vibe` runtime label. A blank prompt, a dispatched child (`AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`) and a subagent (`parent_session_id` set) get no brief. The shared handler's file-backed directive store sends the constant `Directives:` block once. A per-session head receipt sends the routing head only when it changed.\n.skilled/hooks/session-lifecycle/vibe/README.md:116:- [`../../../skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs`](../../../skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs): the advisor part the composer calls.\n.skilled/hooks/session-lifecycle/vibe/turn-start.mjs:27:import { buildAdvisorPart } from '../../../skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs';\n.skilled/hooks/coverage-rationale.md:71:Per the module: *\"host lifecycle hooks advance durable policy state independently of prompt payloads.\"* Elsewhere the de-dup lives in `prompt-advisor.ts` (Pi), `prompt-advisor.mjs` (DSH), `system-skill-advisor` state (OpenCode), the shared `user-prompt-submit` (Codex/Cursor/Devin). The DSH adapter sends the full directive block once per session start or completed compaction and the `Advisor:` head alone while the block is unchanged, and the `directive-lifecycle` switch restores the full brief every turn.\n.skilled/hooks/injection-contract.md:68:- **Channel per runtime:** Claude Code `[SYS]` (`user-prompt-submit.js` -> `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`). Cursor/Devin `[SYS]` (same shim, re-wrapped into each CLI's own envelope). Codex `[SYS]` (mirror of the Claude shim). OpenCode `[SYS]` (`system-skill-advisor.js` via `experimental.chat.system.transform`). Pi `[MSG]` (`prompt-advisor.ts` forwards the shared context onto the visible prompt via the `input` event's `{action:\"transform\"}`). DSH `[SYS]` (`agent/pre-step`, interactive only, as an appended `repo-guards` message).\n.skilled/hooks/README.md:391:| `directive-lifecycle` | ✓ covered | by-design: embedded in the shared `user-prompt-submit` lifecycle | by-design: embedded in the shared `user-prompt-submit` lifecycle | by-design: embedded in the shared `user-prompt-submit` lifecycle | by-design: embedded in `system-skill-advisor` lifecycle state | by-design: embedded in `prompt-advisor.ts` directive de-dup | by-design: embedded in `prompt-advisor.mjs` directive de-dup | by-design: embedded in the Vibe turn-start advisor part |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/pi/README.md:48:| `lib/claude-hook-adapter.ts` | (library) | `spawnSync` proxy into this skill's compiled Claude hook outputs plus the JSON-envelope parser. It is imported by the session bridges and the advisor's `prompt-advisor.ts`. |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \\\"prompt-advisor\\\\|recordAdvisorHookDiagnostic\\\\|persistAdvisorHook\\\" .skilled/hooks .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks 2>/dev/null | grep -v node_modules | head -25\"}"},"time":{"start":1794847914371,"end":1794847915382}}}}
