{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794847991008,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e546e1c3001E8WY3lcxFmQ1Hn","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e546c17c001BBzbwgjKtxtYte","type":"tool","id":"call_8fb522a51528483abc29d2ea","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 5b2b062baef e91faf28b8c -- .skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md | sed -n '1,140p'"},"output":"diff --git a/.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md b/.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md\nindex 502afa0800f..3f37fdbad2b 100644\n--- a/.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md\n+++ b/.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md\n@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n   - \"goal carried across a hop\"\n   - \"lookup reports total candidates\"\n   - \"strict overlay writes\"\n+  - \"mistral vibe runtime hooks\"\n importance_tier: \"normal\"\n contextType: \"general\"\n ---\n@@ -19,11 +20,13 @@ This release changes what you install, what an agent may read and what it is tol\n \n Long sessions hand over more cleanly, and Claude Code now does it by default. Pi and OpenCode now finish a hop too, and so does Mistral Vibe. The feature now has one main name, session handover. A hop to a fresh session carries the running command, the goal and the session's name and mode. The shell shim trusts only your own checkout. Search answers now say how much they left out. A new spec document is found before the index catches up. The spec commands now save the continuity they report.\n \n-Projects that vendor Skilled get stricter overlay checks and an engine that cleans up after itself. Pi 1.5.2 loads every hook adapter again. A plain frontend request now reaches the code skill's frontend guidance. Skilled's own checks and tests also run faster.\n+Mistral Vibe joins as the eighth runtime. Its sessions run Skilled's guards, the advisor brief, the goal and decision capture through hooks. Claude Code can also keep your own copy of Skilled's hooks in step.\n+\n+Projects that vendor Skilled get stricter overlay checks and an engine that cleans up after itself. Pi 1.5.2 loads every hook adapter again. Hook folders now carry names that say what they guard. The dispatch audit log hides a password written inside a URL. A plain frontend request now reaches the code skill's frontend guidance. Skilled's own checks and tests also run faster.\n \n Deep loops now stop on a decision a script computes. Each deep command runs from one workflow file. The AI Council leaves Deep Loop and becomes its own agent. A deep review now fails while a required check still fails at its stop. Scripts now compute those checks and the verdict. The agent files now ask only for steps their own tools can take.\n \n-> Spec folders: `specs/system-speckit/repo-operations/004-node-security-patch-update`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/hook-injection-pipeline/007-env-secret-guard`, `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/036-review-remediation`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/037-relaunch-test-speed`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/038-goal-and-workflow-resume`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/039-hop-dialog-goal-title`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/040-claude-default-on-release-notes`, `specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/006-purpose-retention-across-handovers`, `specs/cli-external-orchestration/opencode-platform/004-self-invocation-guard-api-key`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/retrieval-integrations/001-sweet-search-integration`, `specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/005-goldfish-cold-read-plan-review`, `specs/agents-md/repo-rule-operations/005-reply-rule-pruning`, `specs/system-skilled-doctor/001-skill-and-overlay-build/008-overlay-first-write-checks`, `specs/system-skilled-doctor/001-skill-and-overlay-build/009-overlay-write-checks-follow-up`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/hook-platform/006-file-relative-adapter-imports`, `specs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/006-test-cycle-speed`, `specs/system-speckit/repo-operations/005-main-ci-red-checks` and `specs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/002-named-subtracks-and-host-repos`, `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/009-git-history-lift`, `specs/sk-doc/doc-validation-tooling/005-router-empty-block-capture`, `specs/sk-doc/hub-routing-and-surfaces/006-compiled-route-rule-growth`, `specs/system-skill-advisor/runtime-lifecycle/006-advisor-native-node-resolution`, `specs/sk-doc/hub-routing-and-surfaces/007-host-spec-tree-readers`, `specs/sk-code/verification-guards/005-surface-intent-fold-declaration`, `specs/sk-git/commit-standards/008-doctor-host-hook-acceptance`, `specs/sk-code/hub-architecture/006-sk-code-audit-remediation`, `specs/sk-code/hub-architecture/007-ci-vocabulary-single-source`, `specs/sk-doc/document-standards/003-changelog-system/006-remove-release-size-limit`, `specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/007-speckit-command-gates-step-order-drift`, `specs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/005-subtrack-proposal-and-archive-reach`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/041-cross-runtime-handover-parity`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/042-handover-gap-closure`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/043-vibe-handover-flag-and-live-hop`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/044-in-session-handover-rename`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/045-vibe-automatic-handover`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/046-vibe-history-locator`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/047-vibe-handover-hardening`, `specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/004-workflow-logic-hardening`, `specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation` and `specs/agents/007-agent-alignment-follow-ups`\n+> Spec folders: `specs/system-speckit/repo-operations/004-node-security-patch-update`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/hook-injection-pipeline/007-env-secret-guard`, `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/036-review-remediation`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/037-relaunch-test-speed`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/038-goal-and-workflow-resume`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/039-hop-dialog-goal-title`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/040-claude-default-on-release-notes`, `specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/006-purpose-retention-across-handovers`, `specs/cli-external-orchestration/opencode-platform/004-self-invocation-guard-api-key`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/retrieval-integrations/001-sweet-search-integration`, `specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/005-goldfish-cold-read-plan-review`, `specs/agents-md/repo-rule-operations/005-reply-rule-pruning`, `specs/system-skilled-doctor/001-skill-and-overlay-build/008-overlay-first-write-checks`, `specs/system-skilled-doctor/001-skill-and-overlay-build/009-overlay-write-checks-follow-up`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/hook-platform/006-file-relative-adapter-imports`, `specs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/006-test-cycle-speed`, `specs/system-speckit/repo-operations/005-main-ci-red-checks` and `specs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/002-named-subtracks-and-host-repos`, `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/009-git-history-lift`, `specs/sk-doc/doc-validation-tooling/005-router-empty-block-capture`, `specs/sk-doc/hub-routing-and-surfaces/006-compiled-route-rule-growth`, `specs/system-skill-advisor/runtime-lifecycle/006-advisor-native-node-resolution`, `specs/sk-doc/hub-routing-and-surfaces/007-host-spec-tree-readers`, `specs/sk-code/verification-guards/005-surface-intent-fold-declaration`, `specs/sk-git/commit-standards/008-doctor-host-hook-acceptance`, `specs/sk-code/hub-architecture/006-sk-code-audit-remediation`, `specs/sk-code/hub-architecture/007-ci-vocabulary-single-source`, `specs/sk-doc/document-standards/003-changelog-system/006-remove-release-size-limit`, `specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/007-speckit-command-gates-step-order-drift`, `specs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/005-subtrack-proposal-and-archive-reach`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/041-cross-runtime-handover-parity`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/042-handover-gap-closure`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/043-vibe-handover-flag-and-live-hop`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/044-in-session-handover-rename`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/045-vibe-automatic-handover`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/046-vibe-history-locator`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/047-vibe-handover-hardening`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/048-cross-runtime-handover-parity-fixes`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/049-handover-doc-alignment`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/050-handover-doc-alignment-2`, `specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/004-workflow-logic-hardening`, `specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation`, `specs/agents/007-agent-alignment-follow-ups`, `specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/hook-platform/009-claude-user-hook-sync`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/051-handover-doc-alignment-3`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/decision-capture/001-decision-capture/012-session-scoped-sweep-and-consume`, `specs/system-skilled-doctor/004-symlink-vibe-and-dsh-runtimes`, `specs/system-skilled-doctor/001-skill-and-overlay-build/011-restore-pinned-value-when-json-entry-set-leaves-overlay`, `specs/system-skilled-doctor/001-skill-and-overlay-build/012-fix-barter-022-handover-items-for-doctor-scripts`, `specs/sk-code/hub-architecture/008-host-surface-hint-and-score-window`, `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/010-baseline-capture-after-graph-scan` and `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/hook-platform/008-hook-library-cleanup-and-readme-rewrite`\n \n &nbsp;\n \n@@ -31,7 +34,7 @@ Deep loops now stop on a decision a script computes. Each deep command runs from\n \n Some gaps put your project at risk. A security notice in October patched Node.js. Skilled still accepted Node 20. Any agent could read `.env` and send every secret in it to the model.\n \n-Other gaps cost your agent time. A recommendation said `sk-doc` when you asked for a README. The agent then had to find `/create:readme` on its own. A search cut at its limit never said what it hid. A session that hopped mid-command came back as a plain chat and lost its place. And handover shipped off everywhere, so most Claude Code users never had it. Pi and OpenCode did not finish a hop in a live test either. The switches still said relaunch, while the docs said handover. A spec command reported a save that never wrote a line. A deep loop left its stop call to the model running it. Two runs on the same state could stop differently. A deep review could pass while a required check failed. The model running it judged those checks. The coverage check could not read what reviews recorded. Several agent files asked for steps their own tools could not take.\n+Other gaps cost your agent time. A recommendation said `sk-doc` when you asked for a README. The agent then had to find `/create:readme` on its own. A search cut at its limit never said what it hid. A session that hopped mid-command came back as a plain chat and lost its place. And handover shipped off everywhere, so most Claude Code users never had it. Pi and OpenCode did not finish a hop in a live test either. The switches still said relaunch, while the docs said handover. A spec command reported a save that never wrote a line. A deep loop left its stop call to the model running it. Two runs on the same state could stop differently. A deep review could pass while a required check failed. The model running it judged those checks. The coverage check could not read what reviews recorded. Several agent files asked for steps their own tools could not take. Mistral Vibe was not a runtime Skilled could guard. A copy of Skilled's hooks in your own Claude settings went stale and failed outside Skilled. Hook folders named `dispatch` and `completion` did not say what they guarded. The dispatch audit log kept any password written inside a URL.\n \n &nbsp;\n \n@@ -48,6 +51,7 @@ Other gaps cost your agent time. A recommendation said `sk-doc` when you asked f\n - **Old switch names are no longer read.** Rename each one. Move any open handoff note to the new folder. <!-- section: Session Handover -->\n - **Pi and OpenCode now finish a hop.** Both complete the same hop as Claude Code, with no input from you. <!-- section: Session Handover -->\n - **Mistral Vibe hands over on its own.** Turn on its switch and a Vibe session near its compaction point starts a fresh one, like Claude Code. <!-- section: Session Handover -->\n+- **Mistral Vibe is the eighth runtime.** Its sessions run Skilled's guards, advisor brief, goal and decision capture through 18 hook entries. <!-- section: Mistral Vibe -->\n - **A search says what it left out.** Lookups report their total. Free-text search shows one row per file. <!-- section: Search -->\n - **A new spec document is found at once.** A lookup with no hits reads the documents the index does not list yet. <!-- section: Search -->\n - **Agents reread your request before they say done.** The restraint check now runs when a spec adds scope. <!-- section: Spec Workflow -->\n@@ -58,7 +62,10 @@ Other gaps cost your agent time. A recommendation said `sk-doc` when you asked f\n - **Agents ask only for what their tools can do.** The orchestrator sends deep work to its command. Each agent has a way to finish that it can take. <!-- section: Agents -->\n - **A plain frontend request reaches the code skill's frontend mode.** The code skill's keyword copies and documents now agree with its router. <!-- section: Code Skill -->\n - **A vendored tree can refuse writes no overlay owns.** The overlay engine also clears its own leftovers. <!-- section: Installs and Overlays -->\n+- **Claude Code can keep your own hook copy in step.** One switch copies Skilled's hooks into `~/.claude/settings.json` at each session start. <!-- section: Installs and Overlays -->\n - **Pi 1.5.2 loads every hook adapter again.** Before, no Pi session on that version ran with its guards. <!-- section: Installs and Overlays -->\n+- **Hook folders say what they guard.** `dispatch/` is now `cli-dispatch/`, and the unused standalone pre-commit is gone. <!-- section: Hook Library -->\n+- **The dispatch audit log hides URL passwords.** A new log is readable by its owner only. <!-- section: Hook Library -->\n - **Skilled's own CI and tests run faster.** This changes nothing in your project. <!-- section: Skilled's Own Repository -->\n \n &nbsp;\n@@ -125,6 +132,7 @@ A command can also pass on meaning when the local embedder runs. Each scored com\n - **A deep review request reaches Deep Loop.** \"deep review this branch\" now gets `/deep:review`. A question about the AI council gets `/speckit:ai-council`.\n - **A hub with many modes routes fast.** The compiled route built one rule for every subset of a hub's modes on every call. A hub with 18 modes built 262,125 rules and timed out. A rule now covers at most four modes.\n - **A typed session handover names `/speckit:handoff`.** The advisor named no command for `session handover`, `in session handover` or `session-handover`. It now names the handoff command for all three.\n+- **A README request for a hook, plugin or runtime folder gets its own template.** sk-doc gained three README templates for those folders. \"README for the session-handover hook\" now reaches the hook template.\n \n &nbsp;\n \n@@ -168,7 +176,7 @@ A Vibe sender used to be told that nothing would end its session. In one live ho\n \n #### A Claimed Note Offers the Sender's History\n \n-A session that took over used to know only what the note said. In a live test, six of six receivers answered `UNKNOWN` when asked for a detail the note left out. Now `claim` prints a `## History Lookup` section after the note body. It holds one read-only command that searches and loads the sender's earlier turns for 30 minutes after the claim. With it, three of three receivers looked the detail up and answered correctly. Claude Code, Codex and Mistral Vibe senders get the section. It is left out when the sender ran in another checkout or the runtime is not built.\n+A session that took over used to know only what the note said. In a live test, six of six receivers answered `UNKNOWN` when asked for a detail the note left out. Now `claim` prints a `## History Lookup` section after the note body. It holds one read-only command that searches and loads the sender's earlier turns for 30 minutes after the claim. With it, three of three receivers looked the detail up and answered correctly. Claude Code, Codex, Mistral Vibe, Pi and OpenCode senders get the section. Each browsed turn shows the tool call it made, such as `bash {\"command\":\"wc -l README.md\"}`. The section is left out when the sender ran in another checkout or the runtime is not built.\n \n **Breaking:** The lookup is no longer offered after a compaction, on any runtime. The OpenCode plugin `session-history-lookup.js` is gone. Compaction summaries and the `/speckit:resume` pointer are unchanged.\n \n@@ -177,6 +185,8 @@ The lookup also refused any Claude Code session that ran two tools in one messag\n #### Smaller Fixes\n \n - **A waiting hop never stalls in silence.** On Claude Code only the Stop hook arms a hop, and a question dialog after `prepare` kept the turn open. That dialog is now refused while the hop can still arm, on Claude Code, Pi and OpenCode. A hop waiting on background tasks says so at each Stop. A Stop that cannot arm names the cause. Your next prompt calls a waiting hop off. Pi and OpenCode also tell the model when a new prompt withdraws a hop.\n+- **A hop that cannot arm is called off.** On Codex, Pi and OpenCode, a turn end that failed to arm left its record waiting. A later turn could then hop from a stale note. The record is now marked deferred, and your next prompt withdraws it.\n+- **A nudge arrives once.** Two hooks running at once could deliver the same nudge twice, 16 ms apart. Claude Code, Codex and Vibe now deliver it once.\n - **A compacted Codex session finds its note.** After a compaction, Codex is pointed at the open note, the way Claude Code already was. If the note is stale, Codex is told so instead.\n - **A Pi receiver keeps its claim instructions.** Other extensions add blocks to the seed. The receiver asked for a spec folder again. Pi now reads the seed from its first block.\n - **The claim output names the closing step.** Codex claimed its note and never closed it. `claim` now prints the `complete` command after the note body, on every runtime.\n@@ -190,6 +200,32 @@ The lookup also refused any Claude Code session that ran two tools in one messag\n - **One waiter reclaims a stale lock.** Several waiters could each remove an old lock and all enter at once.\n - **A provider key no longer blocks an OpenCode dispatch.** The cli-opencode guard now ignores `OPENCODE_API_KEY`. Every other `OPENCODE_` variable still trips it.\n - **The cli-opencode docs name the OpenCode 2.3.0 commands.** Credentials are under `opencode auth list`. Agents are listed by `opencode debug agents`.\n+- **The handover docs name what the code does.** Cursor's handoff command is `/speckit-handoff`, and a linking repository needs `.vibe` too. The env reference now lists every variable the wrapper exports.\n+\n+&nbsp;\n+\n+## Mistral Vibe\n+\n+#### Vibe Joins as a Runtime Mode\n+\n+Mistral Vibe is Mistral's coding CLI. It is now the eighth runtime, as the `cli-mistral-vibe` mode. A dispatch runs headless as `vibe -p`. It may pick only two models, `deepseek-flash` and `glm-flash`. Both run at maximum thinking. Seven rules refuse an unsafe dispatch. One requires `--output-dir`, because only `export.json` says whether a run finished. Another requires Skilled's guards in the run's own Vibe home. Deep loops can run a Vibe lineage beside another executor. The `.vibe/` folder ships generated copies of the agents, skills and commands.\n+\n+#### Vibe Sessions Run Skilled's Hooks\n+\n+`.vibe/hooks.toml` registers 18 hook entries. Start Vibe with `--trust` in your checkout, so it loads them. At session start, the model gets its goal and the session context. Each prompt then gets the skill advisor brief. Before a tool runs, five guards judge it. They are the spec gate, the dotenv guard, the dispatch check, the commit message gate and the deep-loop guard. A refusal reads like this: `env-secret-guard: .env is a dotenv file and its values must not reach the model.`\n+\n+An edit that leaves a build behind its sources gets a `STALE DIST WARNING` with the tool result. An answer you give through Vibe's question tool lands in the decision queue for `/speckit:save`. A turn that ends on an option menu written in prose is sent back once. The model is told to ask with the question tool instead. After a compaction, the goal, the history lookup offer and any open handoff note come back once.\n+\n+Two gaps remain, because Vibe sets them. Vibe removes its question tool from a headless run, so answers are captured only in the terminal app. A turn-end refusal becomes a retry, and Vibe accepts the turn after three.\n+\n+#### Smaller Fixes\n+\n+- **A background command no longer slips past the guards.** Vibe names that tool `process.start`, and the guards knew only `process_start`. So a background read of `.env` ran unjudged. Every shell guard now judges it.\n+- **Text typed into a running shell is judged too.** A model could start `bash -i` and type `cat .env` into it. The shell guards now read typed text as a command.\n+- **A kill switch in `hook-flags.env` turns a Vibe part off.** The advisor, question-menu and completion parts ignored the file and kept running. Now a switch there stops them.\n+- **Hooks run from a checkout reached through a link.** Started through a symlinked path, the Vibe hooks printed nothing. Now they print what they print from the real path.\n+- **A slow startup guard no longer silences the rest.** The startup check gave its guards less time than one guard may need. Then every guard's warning was lost. It now waits 9 s.\n+- **A dispatch that changes folder first is still checked.** The rule that gives each run its own Vibe home ignored a `cd` before the run.\n \n &nbsp;\n \n@@ -262,6 +298,7 @@ Gate 6 named five rule files to load around a reply. Three mostly repeated the o\n - **The spec workflows share one copy of common parts.** Check rules, checkpoint choices, goal prompts, documentation levels and phase splitting now live in `speckit-lifecycle-shared.yaml`. Every path the workflows name now exists. Steps and timers that nothing used are gone.\n - **Release notes have no size ceilings.** The shape check no longer counts lines, H4 items or glance bullets. Its sentence gates stay.\n - **One spec-kit build is enough.** `npm run build` in `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit` used to leave a build the validator called stale.\n+- **A save records only its own session's answers.** With two sessions open, a save was offered the other session's answers. From a linked worktree it found none. Now it reads its own session's transcript. A worktree also shares the main checkout's answer queue, so an answer saved there stops showing as pending.\n \n &nbsp;\n \n@@ -373,6 +410,7 @@ The code skill kept its routing keywords in several copies. Its CI keywords sat\n - **An implementation request loads the implement doctrine.** The hub router never loaded `workflow-implement.md` before.\n - **The code skill's router check fails without its registry.** A missing `mode-registry.json` used to pass with nothing checked. A one-line re-export file no longer needs a module header.\n - **A `lite` code review skips nothing by default.** It skips small diffs only when `SK_CODE_REVIEW_MIN_CHANGED_LINES` is set.\n+- **A surface hint joins a scored route.** `--surface-hint FRONTEND` on `review this function for bugs` now adds the frontend surface to the route. A hinted prompt that scores nothing routes to the hinted surface.\n \n &nbsp;\n \n@@ -390,9 +428,15 @@ A project that moved onto the engine reported three bugs and three gaps. All are\n \n Pi 1.5.1 changed how it loads a linked extension. On Pi 1.5.2, 16 adapters then failed to load and `pi -p` exited 1. Each entry in `.pi/extensions/` is now a one-line file that re-exports its adapter. Pi 1.5.0 and Pi 1.5.2 both load all 22 entries.\n \n+#### Claude Code Keeps Your Hook Copy in Step\n+\n+Some users copy Skilled's hooks into `~/.claude/settings.json`. That copy went stale when a hook folder was renamed. A stale copy ran hooks twice inside Skilled. Outside Skilled it failed with `mk claude hook could not resolve`. Now each hook command first checks for `.skilled/hooks` and exits quietly without it. A folder that holds only Skilled data, such as `~/.skilled`, does not count. Claude Code runs a command found in both files once.\n+\n+Set `SYSTEM_CLAUDE_USER_HOOK_SYNC_ENABLED=1` to keep the copy current. Each session start in your Skilled checkout then copies the project's hooks into your user settings. It keeps your other settings and your own hooks. It writes only when something changed. The first write keeps a backup at `~/.claude/settings.json.pre-skilled-hook-sync`. A linked worktree never writes. `node .skilled/bin/sync-claude-user-hooks.mjs --check` prints `sync-claude-user-hooks: OK` when the copy matches. Turning the switch off leaves the last copy in place.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"diff --git a/.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md b/.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md\nindex 502afa0800f..3f37fdbad2b 100644\n--- a/.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md\n+++ b/.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md\n@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n   - \"goal carried across a hop\"\n   - \"lookup reports total candidates\"\n   - \"strict overlay writes\"\n+  - \"mistral vibe runtime hooks\"\n importance_tier: \"normal\"\n contextType: \"general\"\n ---\n@@ -19,11 +20,13 @@ This release changes what you install, what an agent may read and what it is tol\n \n Long sessions hand over more cleanly, and Claude Code now does it by default. Pi and OpenCode now finish a hop too, and so does Mistral Vibe. The feature now has one main name, session handover. A hop to a fresh session carries the running command, the goal and the session's name and mode. The shell shim trusts only your own checkout. Search answers now say how much they left out. A new spec document is found before the index catches up. The spec commands now save the continuity they report.\n \n-Projects that vendor Skilled get stricter overlay checks and an engine that cleans up after itself. Pi 1.5.2 loads every hook adapter again. A plain frontend request now reaches the code skill's frontend guidance. Skilled's own checks and tests also run faster.\n+Mistral Vibe joins as the eighth runtime. Its sessions run Skilled's guards, the advisor brief, the goal and decision capture through hooks. Claude Code can also keep your own copy of Skilled's hooks in step.\n+\n+Projects that vendor Skilled get stricter overlay checks and an engine that cleans up after itself. Pi 1.5.2 loads every hook adapter again. Hook folders now carry names that say what they guard. The dispatch audit log hides a password written inside a URL. A plain frontend request now reaches the code skill's frontend guidance. Skilled's own checks and tests also run faster.\n \n Deep loops now stop on a decision a script computes. Each deep command runs from one workflow file. The AI Council leaves Deep Loop and becomes its own agent. A deep review now fails while a required check still fails at its stop. Scripts now compute those checks and the verdict. The agent files now ask only for steps their own tools can take.\n \n-> Spec folders: `specs/system-speckit/repo-operations/004-node-security-patch-update`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/hook-injection-pipeline/007-env-secret-guard`, `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/036-review-remediation`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/037-relaunch-test-speed`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/038-goal-and-workflow-resume`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/039-hop-dialog-goal-title`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/040-claude-default-on-release-notes`, `specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/006-purpose-retention-across-handovers`, `specs/cli-external-orchestration/opencode-platform/004-self-invocation-guard-api-key`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/retrieval-integrations/001-sweet-search-integration`, `specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/005-goldfish-cold-read-plan-review`, `specs/agents-md/repo-rule-operations/005-reply-rule-pruning`, `specs/system-skilled-doctor/001-skill-and-overlay-build/008-overlay-first-write-checks`, `specs/system-skilled-doctor/001-skill-and-overlay-build/009-overlay-write-checks-follow-up`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/hook-platform/006-file-relative-adapter-imports`, `specs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/006-test-cycle-speed`, `specs/system-speckit/repo-operations/005-main-ci-red-checks` and `specs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/002-named-subtracks-and-host-repos`, `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/009-git-history-lift`, `specs/sk-doc/doc-validation-tooling/005-router-empty-block-capture`, `specs/sk-doc/hub-routing-and-surfaces/006-compiled-route-rule-growth`, `specs/system-skill-advisor/runtime-lifecycle/006-advisor-native-node-resolution`, `specs/sk-doc/hub-routing-and-surfaces/007-host-spec-tree-readers`, `specs/sk-code/verification-guards/005-surface-intent-fold-declaration`, `specs/sk-git/commit-standards/008-doctor-host-hook-acceptance`, `specs/sk-code/hub-architecture/006-sk-code-audit-remediation`, `specs/sk-code/hub-architecture/007-ci-vocabulary-single-source`, `specs/sk-doc/document-standards/003-changelog-system/006-remove-release-size-limit`, `specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/007-speckit-command-gates-step-order-drift`, `specs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/005-subtrack-proposal-and-archive-reach`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/041-cross-runtime-handover-parity`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/042-handover-gap-closure`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/043-vibe-handover-flag-and-live-hop`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/044-in-session-handover-rename`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/045-vibe-automatic-handover`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/046-vibe-history-locator`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/047-vibe-handover-hardening`, `specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/004-workflow-logic-hardening`, `specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation` and `specs/agents/007-agent-alignment-follow-ups`\n+> Spec folders: `specs/system-speckit/repo-operations/004-node-security-patch-update`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/hook-injection-pipeline/007-env-secret-guard`, `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/036-review-remediation`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/037-relaunch-test-speed`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/038-goal-and-workflow-resume`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/039-hop-dialog-goal-title`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/040-claude-default-on-release-notes`, `specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/006-purpose-retention-across-handovers`, `specs/cli-external-orchestration/opencode-platform/004-self-invocation-guard-api-key`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/retrieval-integrations/001-sweet-search-integration`, `specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/005-goldfish-cold-read-plan-review`, `specs/agents-md/repo-rule-operations/005-reply-rule-pruning`, `specs/system-skilled-doctor/001-skill-and-overlay-build/008-overlay-first-write-checks`, `specs/system-skilled-doctor/001-skill-and-overlay-build/009-overlay-write-checks-follow-up`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/hook-platform/006-file-relative-adapter-imports`, `specs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/006-test-cycle-speed`, `specs/system-speckit/repo-operations/005-main-ci-red-checks` and `specs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/002-named-subtracks-and-host-repos`, `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/009-git-history-lift`, `specs/sk-doc/doc-validation-tooling/005-router-empty-block-capture`, `specs/sk-doc/hub-routing-and-surfaces/006-compiled-route-rule-growth`, `specs/system-skill-advisor/runtime-lifecycle/006-advisor-native-node-resolution`, `specs/sk-doc/hub-routing-and-surfaces/007-host-spec-tree-readers`, `specs/sk-code/verification-guards/005-surface-intent-fold-declaration`, `specs/sk-git/commit-standards/008-doctor-host-hook-acceptance`, `specs/sk-code/hub-architecture/006-sk-code-audit-remediation`, `specs/sk-code/hub-architecture/007-ci-vocabulary-single-source`, `specs/sk-doc/document-standards/003-changelog-system/006-remove-release-size-limit`, `specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/007-speckit-command-gates-step-order-drift`, `specs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/005-subtrack-proposal-and-archive-reach`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/041-cross-runtime-handover-parity`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/042-handover-gap-closure`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/043-vibe-handover-flag-and-live-hop`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/044-in-session-handover-rename`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/045-vibe-automatic-handover`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/046-vibe-history-locator`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/047-vibe-handover-hardening`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/048-cross-runtime-handover-parity-fixes`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/049-handover-doc-alignment`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/050-handover-doc-alignment-2`, `specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/004-workflow-logic-hardening`, `specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation`, `specs/agents/007-agent-alignment-follow-ups`, `specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/hook-platform/009-claude-user-hook-sync`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/002-session-handover-loop/051-handover-doc-alignment-3`, `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/decision-capture/001-decision-capture/012-session-scoped-sweep-and-consume`, `specs/system-skilled-doctor/004-symlink-vibe-and-dsh-runtimes`, `specs/system-skilled-doctor/001-skill-and-overlay-build/011-restore-pinned-value-when-json-entry-set-leaves-overlay`, `specs/system-skilled-doctor/001-skill-and-overlay-build/012-fix-barter-022-handover-items-for-doctor-scripts`, `specs/sk-code/hub-architecture/008-host-surface-hint-and-score-window`, `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/010-baseline-capture-after-graph-scan` and `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/hook-platform/008-hook-library-cleanup-and-readme-rewrite`\n \n &nbsp;\n \n@@ -31,7 +34,7 @@ Deep loops now stop on a decision a script computes. Each deep command runs from\n \n Some gaps put your project at risk. A security notice in October patched Node.js. Skilled still accepted Node 20. Any agent could read `.env` and send every secret in it to the model.\n \n-Other gaps cost your agent time. A recommendation said `sk-doc` when you asked for a README. The agent then had to find `/create:readme` on its own. A search cut at its limit never said what it hid. A session that hopped mid-command came back as a plain chat and lost its place. And handover shipped off everywhere, so most Claude Code users never had it. Pi and OpenCode did not finish a hop in a live test either. The switches still said relaunch, while the docs said handover. A spec command reported a save that never wrote a line. A deep loop left its stop call to the model running it. Two runs on the same state could stop differently. A deep review could pass while a required check failed. The model running it judged those checks. The coverage check could not read what reviews recorded. Several agent files asked for steps their own tools could not take.\n+Other gaps cost your agent time. A recommendation said `sk-doc` when you asked for a README. The agent then had to find `/create:readme` on its own. A search cut at its limit never said what it hid. A session that hopped mid-command came back as a plain chat and lost its place. And handover shipped off everywhere, so most Claude Code users never had it. Pi and OpenCode did not finish a hop in a live test either. The switches still said relaunch, while the docs said handover. A spec command reported a save that never wrote a line. A deep loop left its stop call to the model running it. Two runs on the same state could stop differently. A deep review could pass while a required check failed. The model running it judged those checks. The coverage check could not read what reviews recorded. Several agent files asked for steps their own tools could not take. Mistral Vibe was not a runtime Skilled could guard. A copy of Skilled's hooks in your own Claude settings went stale and failed outside Skilled. Hook folders named `dispatch` and `completion` did not say what they guarded. The dispatch audit log kept any password written inside a URL.\n \n &nbsp;\n \n@@ -48,6 +51,7 @@ Other gaps cost your agent time. A recommendation said `sk-doc` when you asked f\n - **Old switch names are no longer read.** Rename each one. Move any open handoff note to the new folder. <!-- section: Session Handover -->\n - **Pi and OpenCode now finish a hop.** Both complete the same hop as Claude Code, with no input from you. <!-- section: Session Handover -->\n - **Mistral Vibe hands over on its own.** Turn on its switch and a Vibe session near its compaction point starts a fresh one, like Claude Code. <!-- section: Session Handover -->\n+- **Mistral Vibe is the eighth runtime.** Its sessions run Skilled's guards, advisor brief, goal and decision capture through 18 hook entries. <!-- section: Mistral Vibe -->\n - **A search says what it left out.** Lookups report their total. Free-text search shows one row per file. <!-- section: Search -->\n - **A new spec document is found at once.** A lookup with no hits reads the documents the index does not list yet. <!-- section: Search -->\n - **Agents reread your request before they say done.** The restraint check now runs when a spec adds scope. <!-- section: Spec Workflow -->\n@@ -58,7 +62,10 @@ Other gaps cost your agent time. A recommendation said `sk-doc` when you asked f\n - **Agents ask only for what their tools can do.** The orchestrator sends deep work to its command. Each agent has a way to finish that it can take. <!-- section: Agents -->\n - **A plain frontend request reaches the code skill's frontend mode.** The code skill's keyword copies and documents now agree with its router. <!-- section: Code Skill -->\n - **A vendored tree can refuse writes no overlay owns.** The overlay engine also clears its own leftovers. <!-- section: Installs and Overlays -->\n+- **Claude Code can keep your own hook copy in step.** One switch copies Skilled's hooks into `~/.claude/settings.json` at each session start. <!-- section: Installs and Overlays -->\n - **Pi 1.5.2 loads every hook adapter again.** Before, no Pi session on that version ran with its guards. <!-- section: Installs and Overlays -->\n+- **Hook folders say what they guard.** `dispatch/` is now `cli-dispatch/`, and the unused standalone pre-commit is gone. <!-- section: Hook Library -->\n+- **The dispatch audit log hides URL passwords.** A new log is readable by its owner only. <!-- section: Hook Library -->\n - **Skilled's own CI and tests run faster.** This changes nothing in your project. <!-- section: Skilled's Own Repository -->\n \n &nbsp;\n@@ -125,6 +132,7 @@ A command can also pass on meaning when the local embedder runs. Each scored com\n - **A deep review request reaches Deep Loop.** \"deep review this branch\" now gets `/deep:review`. A question about the AI council gets `/speckit:ai-council`.\n - **A hub with many modes routes fast.** The compiled route built one rule for every subset of a hub's modes on every call. A hub with 18 modes built 262,125 rules and timed out. A rule now covers at most four modes.\n - **A typed session handover names `/speckit:handoff`.** The advisor named no command for `session handover`, `in session handover` or `session-handover`. It now names the handoff command for all three.\n+- **A README request for a hook, plugin or runtime folder gets its own template.** sk-doc gained three README templates for those folders. \"README for the session-handover hook\" now reaches the hook template.\n \n &nbsp;\n \n@@ -168,7 +176,7 @@ A Vibe sender used to be told that nothing would end its session. In one live ho\n \n #### A Claimed Note Offers the Sender's History\n \n-A session that took over used to know only what the note said. In a live test, six of six receivers answered `UNKNOWN` when asked for a detail the note left out. Now `claim` prints a `## History Lookup` section after the note body. It holds one read-only command that searches and loads the sender's earlier turns for 30 minutes after the claim. With it, three of three receivers looked the detail up and answered correctly. Claude Code, Codex and Mistral Vibe senders get the section. It is left out when the sender ran in another checkout or the runtime is not built.\n+A session that took over used to know only what the note said. In a live test, six of six receivers answered `UNKNOWN` when asked for a detail the note left out. Now `claim` prints a `## History Lookup` section after the note body. It holds one read-only command that searches and loads the sender's earlier turns for 30 minutes after the claim. With it, three of three receivers looked the detail up and answered correctly. Claude Code, Codex, Mistral Vibe, Pi and OpenCode senders get the section. Each browsed turn shows the tool call it made, such as `bash {\"command\":\"wc -l README.md\"}`. The section is left out when the sender ran in another checkout or the runtime is not built.\n \n **Breaking:** The lookup is no longer offered after a compaction, on any runtime. The OpenCode plugin `session-history-lookup.js` is gone. Compaction summaries and the `/speckit:resume` pointer are unchanged.\n \n@@ -177,6 +185,8 @@ The lookup also refused any Claude Code session that ran two tools in one messag\n #### Smaller Fixes\n \n - **A waiting hop never stalls in silence.** On Claude Code only the Stop hook arms a hop, and a question dialog after `prepare` kept the turn open. That dialog is now refused while the hop can still arm, on Claude Code, Pi and OpenCode. A hop waiting on background tasks says so at each Stop. A Stop that cannot arm names the cause. Your next prompt calls a waiting hop off. Pi and OpenCode also tell the model when a new prompt withdraws a hop.\n+- **A hop that cannot arm is called off.** On Codex, Pi and OpenCode, a turn end that failed to arm left its record waiting. A later turn could then hop from a stale note. The record is now marked deferred, and your next prompt withdraws it.\n+- **A nudge arrives once.** Two hooks running at once could deliver the same nudge twice, 16 ms apart. Claude Code, Codex and Vibe now deliver it once.\n - **A compacted Codex session finds its note.** After a compaction, Codex is pointed at the open note, the way Claude Code already was. If the note is stale, Codex is told so instead.\n - **A Pi receiver keeps its claim instructions.** Other extensions add blocks to the seed. The receiver asked for a spec folder again. Pi now reads the seed from its first block.\n - **The claim output names the closing step.** Codex claimed its note and never closed it. `claim` now prints the `complete` command after the note body, on every runtime.\n@@ -190,6 +200,32 @@ The lookup also refused any Claude Code session that ran two tools in one messag\n - **One waiter reclaims a stale lock.** Several waiters could each remove an old lock and all enter at once.\n - **A provider key no longer blocks an OpenCode dispatch.** The cli-opencode guard now ignores `OPENCODE_API_KEY`. Every other `OPENCODE_` variable still trips it.\n - **The cli-opencode docs name the OpenCode 2.3.0 commands.** Credentials are under `opencode auth list`. Agents are listed by `opencode debug agents`.\n+- **The handover docs name what the code does.** Cursor's handoff command is `/speckit-handoff`, and a linking repository needs `.vibe` too. The env reference now lists every variable the wrapper exports.\n+\n+&nbsp;\n+\n+## Mistral Vibe\n+\n+#### Vibe Joins as a Runtime Mode\n+\n+Mistral Vibe is Mistral's coding CLI. It is now the eighth runtime, as the `cli-mistral-vibe` mode. A dispatch runs headless as `vibe -p`. It may pick only two models, `deepseek-flash` and `glm-flash`. Both run at maximum thinking. Seven rules refuse an unsafe dispatch. One requires `--output-dir`, because only `export.json` says whether a run finished. Another requires Skilled's guards in the run's own Vibe home. Deep loops can run a Vibe lineage beside another executor. The `.vibe/` folder ships generated copies of the agents, skills and commands.\n+\n+#### Vibe Sessions Run Skilled's Hooks\n+\n+`.vibe/hooks.toml` registers 18 hook entries. Start Vibe with `--trust` in your checkout, so it loads them. At session start, the model gets its goal and the session context. Each prompt then gets the skill advisor brief. Before a tool runs, five guards judge it. They are the spec gate, the dotenv guard, the dispatch check, the commit message gate and the deep-loop guard. A refusal reads like this: `env-secret-guard: .env is a dotenv file and its values must not reach the model.`\n+\n+An edit that leaves a build behind its sources gets a `STALE DIST WARNING` with the tool result. An answer you give through Vibe's question tool lands in the decision queue for `/speckit:save`. A turn that ends on an option menu written in prose is sent back once. The model is told to ask with the question tool instead. After a compaction, the goal, the history lookup offer and any open handoff note come back once.\n+\n+Two gaps remain, because Vibe sets them. Vibe removes its question tool from a headless run, so answers are captured only in the terminal app. A turn-end refusal becomes a retry, and Vibe accepts the turn after three.\n+\n+#### Smaller Fixes\n+\n+- **A background command no longer slips past the guards.** Vibe names that tool `process.start`, and the guards knew only `process_start`. So a background read of `.env` ran unjudged. Every shell guard now judges it.\n+- **Text typed into a running shell is judged too.** A model could start `bash -i` and type `cat .env` into it. The shell guards now read typed text as a command.\n+- **A kill switch in `hook-flags.env` turns a Vibe part off.** The advisor, question-menu and completion parts ignored the file and kept running. Now a switch there stops them.\n+- **Hooks run from a checkout reached through a link.** Started through a symlinked path, the Vibe hooks printed nothing. Now they print what they print from the real path.\n+- **A slow startup guard no longer silences the rest.** The startup check gave its guards less time than one guard may need. Then every guard's warning was lost. It now waits 9 s.\n+- **A dispatch that changes folder first is still checked.** The rule that gives each run its own Vibe home ignored a `cd` before the run.\n \n &nbsp;\n \n@@ -262,6 +298,7 @@ Gate 6 named five rule files to load around a reply. Three mostly repeated the o\n - **The spec workflows share one copy of common parts.** Check rules, checkpoint choices, goal prompts, documentation levels and phase splitting now live in `speckit-lifecycle-shared.yaml`. Every path the workflows name now exists. Steps and timers that nothing used are gone.\n - **Release notes have no size ceilings.** The shape check no longer counts lines, H4 items or glance bullets. Its sentence gates stay.\n - **One spec-kit build is enough.** `npm run build` in `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit` used to leave a build the validator called stale.\n+- **A save records only its own session's answers.** With two sessions open, a save was offered the other session's answers. From a linked worktree it found none. Now it reads its own session's transcript. A worktree also shares the main checkout's answer queue, so an answer saved there stops showing as pending.\n \n &nbsp;\n \n@@ -373,6 +410,7 @@ The code skill kept its routing keywords in several copies. Its CI keywords sat\n - **An implementation request loads the implement doctrine.** The hub router never loaded `workflow-implement.md` before.\n - **The code skill's router check fails without its registry.** A missing `mode-registry.json` used to pass with nothing checked. A one-line re-export file no longer needs a module header.\n - **A `lite` code review skips nothing by default.** It skips small diffs only when `SK_CODE_REVIEW_MIN_CHANGED_LINES` is set.\n+- **A surface hint joins a scored route.** `--surface-hint FRONTEND` on `review this function for bugs` now adds the frontend surface to the route. A hinted prompt that scores nothing routes to the hinted surface.\n \n &nbsp;\n \n@@ -390,9 +428,15 @@ A project that moved onto the engine reported three bugs and three gaps. All are\n \n Pi 1.5.1 changed how it loads a linked extension. On Pi 1.5.2, 16 adapters then failed to load and `pi -p` exited 1. Each entry in `.pi/extensions/` is now a one-line file that re-exports its adapter. Pi 1.5.0 and Pi 1.5.2 both load all 22 entries.\n \n+#### Claude Code Keeps Your Hook Copy in Step\n+\n+Some users copy Skilled's hooks into `~/.claude/settings.json`. That copy went stale when a hook folder was renamed. A stale copy ran hooks twice inside Skilled. Outside Skilled it failed with `mk claude hook could not resolve`. Now each hook command first checks for `.skilled/hooks` and exits quietly without it. A folder that holds only Skilled data, such as `~/.skilled`, does not count. Claude Code runs a command found in both files once.\n+\n+Set `SYSTEM_CLAUDE_USER_HOOK_SYNC_ENABLED=1` to keep the copy current. Each session start in your Skilled checkout then copies the project's hooks into your user settings. It keeps your other settings and your own hooks. It writes only when something changed. The first write keeps a backup at `~/.claude/settings.json.pre-skilled-hook-sync`. A linked worktree never writes. `node .skilled/bin/sync-claude-user-hooks.mjs --check` prints `sync-claude-user-hooks: OK` when the copy matches. Turning the switch off leaves the last copy in place.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 5b2b062baef e91faf28b8c -- .skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md | sed -n '1,140p'\"}"},"time":{"start":1794847990211,"end":1794847991008}}}}
