{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794848113407,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e548c03200294zb7JqjBN63Tp","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e548aabc001JbR25feBHVFbQT","type":"tool","id":"call_24aadf2a888e438f9bc5fd10","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '425,450p' .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs; echo \"=== presentation 50-82 ===\"; sed -n '50,82p' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt"},"output":" * @returns {Array<object>}\n */\nfunction selectEntries(manifest, root, options) {\n  const requestedRuntimes = csvValues(options.runtimes);\n  const runtimes = options.runtimes === null || options.runtimes === undefined\n    ? Object.keys(manifest.runtimes).filter((name) => {\n      const first = manifest.runtimes[name][0];\n      return first && lstatOrNull(rootPathFor(first, root));\n    })\n    : requestedRuntimes;\n  for (const runtime of runtimes) {\n    if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(manifest.runtimes, runtime)) {\n      throw new UsageError('unknown runtime: ' + runtime);\n    }\n  }\n  const extras = csvValues(options.include);\n  for (const extra of extras) {\n    if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(manifest.extras, extra)) {\n      throw new UsageError('unknown extra: ' + extra);\n    }\n  }\n\n  const selected = [];\n  for (const entry of manifest.core) selected.push({ entry, group: 'core' });\n  for (const runtime of runtimes) {\n    for (const entry of manifest.runtimes[runtime]) selected.push({ entry, group: runtime });\n=== presentation 50-82 ===\n## 3. The Install Prompt\n\nAsk every answer that is still missing in one prompt, then wait. This follows the consolidated question protocol. Questions 1 and 2 are dropped when `--root` and `--runtimes` were passed. The link shape and the instruction choice have no flag, so they are always in the prompt.\n\n```text\nWhere should Skilled go? Answer any or all in one reply, for example \"/Users/me/code/my-app, claude and codex, auto, embed\".\n\n1) Target repo: the absolute path, for example /Users/me/code/my-app\n2) Runtimes: claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin, pi, vibe, dsh, or \"the ones already there\"\n3) Link shape: auto / whole / merge   (auto unless a real folder already sits where a link would go)\n4) Instruction file: embed / link   (embed keeps the repo's own AGENTS.md; link points AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and REPO RULES.md at the checkout's copies)\n```\n\nThe example carries all four answers so the shape of a full reply is visible. Never print a question the flags already answered.\n\n## 4. Accepted Answers\n\n| Answer | Binds | Meaning |\n|--------|-------|---------|\n| An absolute path | `--root <dir>` | The project repo that receives the links. The path must exist and be a directory; the engine exits 2 and names it otherwise |\n| `claude`, `claude and codex`, `claude,opencode` | `--runtimes <list>` | The runtime folders to link, as a comma list |\n| `the ones already there`, empty, `any` | no `--runtimes` | The engine keeps the runtimes its own detection finds in the root, and always links `.skilled` |\n| `auto` | `--mode auto` | Whole link where the path is free, merge where a real folder is in the way. The one to pick |\n| `whole` | `--mode whole` | One link per entry, refused where a real folder exists |\n| `merge` | `--mode merge` | A real folder whose children are links. A local file already in the folder is kept and reported, never overwritten |\n| `embed` | step 2 stays | The repo keeps its own `AGENTS.md` and the shipped sections are refreshed into it |\n| `link` | step 1 gains `--link-instructions`, step 2 is dropped | `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `REPO RULES.md` become links into the checkout |\n\nA runtime name outside the nine, a shape outside the three, or an instruction word outside the two is not guessed. Ask that one question again with the accepted values. When the engine refuses a root, show its `ERROR:` line as it printed and ask question 1 again.\n\n## 5. The Symlink Check\n\nRun `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root <dir> [--runtimes <list>] [--link-instructions]` once, in place and read-only, then render its entry lines as they print:\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":" * @returns {Array<object>}\n */\nfunction selectEntries(manifest, root, options) {\n  const requestedRuntimes = csvValues(options.runtimes);\n  const runtimes = options.runtimes === null || options.runtimes === undefined\n    ? Object.keys(manifest.runtimes).filter((name) => {\n      const first = manifest.runtimes[name][0];\n      return first && lstatOrNull(rootPathFor(first, root));\n    })\n    : requestedRuntimes;\n  for (const runtime of runtimes) {\n    if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(manifest.runtimes, runtime)) {\n      throw new UsageError('unknown runtime: ' + runtime);\n    }\n  }\n  const extras = csvValues(options.include);\n  for (const extra of extras) {\n    if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(manifest.extras, extra)) {\n      throw new UsageError('unknown extra: ' + extra);\n    }\n  }\n\n  const selected = [];\n  for (const entry of manifest.core) selected.push({ entry, group: 'core' });\n  for (const runtime of runtimes) {\n    for (const entry of manifest.runtimes[runtime]) selected.push({ entry, group: runtime });\n=== presentation 50-82 ===\n## 3. The Install Prompt\n\nAsk every answer that is still missing in one prompt, then wait. This follows the consolidated question protocol. Questions 1 and 2 are dropped when `--root` and `--runtimes` were passed. The link shape and the instruction choice have no flag, so they are always in the prompt.\n\n```text\nWhere should Skilled go? Answer any or all in one reply, for example \"/Users/me/code/my-app, claude and codex, auto, embed\".\n\n1) Target repo: the absolute path, for example /Users/me/code/my-app\n2) Runtimes: claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin, pi, vibe, dsh, or \"the ones already there\"\n3) Link shape: auto / whole / merge   (auto unless a real folder already sits where a link would go)\n4) Instruction file: embed / link   (embed keeps the repo's own AGENTS.md; link points AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and REPO RULES.md at the checkout's copies)\n```\n\nThe example carries all four answers so the shape of a full reply is visible. Never print a question the flags already answered.\n\n## 4. Accepted Answers\n\n| Answer | Binds | Meaning |\n|--------|-------|---------|\n| An absolute path | `--root <dir>` | The project repo that receives the links. The path must exist and be a directory; the engine exits 2 and names it otherwise |\n| `claude`, `claude and codex`, `claude,opencode` | `--runtimes <list>` | The runtime folders to link, as a comma list |\n| `the ones already there`, empty, `any` | no `--runtimes` | The engine keeps the runtimes its own detection finds in the root, and always links `.skilled` |\n| `auto` | `--mode auto` | Whole link where the path is free, merge where a real folder is in the way. The one to pick |\n| `whole` | `--mode whole` | One link per entry, refused where a real folder exists |\n| `merge` | `--mode merge` | A real folder whose children are links. A local file already in the folder is kept and reported, never overwritten |\n| `embed` | step 2 stays | The repo keeps its own `AGENTS.md` and the shipped sections are refreshed into it |\n| `link` | step 1 gains `--link-instructions`, step 2 is dropped | `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `REPO RULES.md` become links into the checkout |\n\nA runtime name outside the nine, a shape outside the three, or an instruction word outside the two is not guessed. Ask that one question again with the accepted values. When the engine refuses a root, show its `ERROR:` line as it printed and ask question 1 again.\n\n## 5. The Symlink Check\n\nRun `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root <dir> [--runtimes <list>] [--link-instructions]` once, in place and read-only, then render its entry lines as they print:\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '425,450p' .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs; echo \\\"=== presentation 50-82 ===\\\"; sed -n '50,82p' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794848112690,"end":1794848113407}}}}
