{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794848339041,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e54c328a001ySd2YKpn57prBo","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e54c0de7001YutKnTnGrw6MO2","type":"tool","id":"call_54f0cc7f22b046e7805f7dd8","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md","offset":30,"limit":130},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md, lines 30-153\n30: | **sk-create-readme** | Author a folder, code-folder or skill README, a repository front page and its install, contributing and security guides | `sk-create-readme/` | `/create:readme` |\n31: | **sk-create-agent** | Scaffold an OpenCode agent (permission/authority frontmatter) | `sk-create-agent/` | `/create:agent` |\n32: | **sk-create-command** | Scaffold an OpenCode slash command (argument-hint + allowed-tools + router/presentation split) | `sk-create-command/` | `/create:command` |\n33: | **sk-create-feature-catalog** | Author a feature-catalog inventory package | `sk-create-feature-catalog/` | `/create:feature-catalog` |\n34: | **sk-create-manual-testing-playbook** | Author a manual-testing-playbook package | `sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/` | `/create:manual-testing-playbook` |\n35: | **sk-create-benchmark** | Author MCP-promotion and behavior packages or inputs | `sk-create-benchmark/` | `/create:benchmark` |\n36: | **sk-create-changelog** | Author a global component changelog entry (version bump + topology-aware placement). Packet-local changelogs are deprecated | `sk-create-changelog/` | `/create:changelog` |\n37: | **sk-create-diff** | Produce a local, Git-free before/after review of an edited document (text/Markdown/HTML/DOCX/text-PDF) as a self-contained HTML report | `sk-create-diff/` | `/create:diff` |\n38: | **sk-create-repo-rule** | Create, revise or retire a repo-local rule under `repo-rules/` and wire it into `REPO RULES.md` (four decision tests refuse most requests) | `sk-create-repo-rule/` | `/create:repo-rule` |\n39: | **sk-create-with-human-voice** | Apply the Human Voice Rules to prose, or score prose against them, with a scope gate and a re-scan | `sk-create-with-human-voice/` | `/create:with-human-voice` |\n40: | **sk-create-frontmatter** | Own the YAML frontmatter contract: per-class field rules, the description budget, and the 4-part `version` derivation | `sk-create-frontmatter/` | — (routes via aliases) |\n41: | **sk-create-goal** | Author or revise a packet `goal.md`: the durable directive, three to seven self-contained completion criteria, and the phase-parent binding table (session-goal setting stays with the goal hooks) | `sk-create-goal/` | `/create:goal` |\n42: | **sk-create-quality-control** | Validate / score / optimize an EXISTING document (extract → DQI → HVR → validate) | `sk-create-quality-control/` | (routes via aliases) |\n43: \n44: ### When NOT to Use\n45: - Code implementation, tests, or debugging — use `sk-code`.\n46: - Git worktree, branch, commit, PR, or release work — use `sk-git`.\n47: - Spec-folder workflow / memory / save context — use `system-spec-kit`.\n48: - A measured Style Reference (design tokens extracted from a live source) — use `sk-design-md-generator`.\n49: - The `shared/` backbone is consumed by the packets, not invoked as a user workflow.\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## 2. SMART ROUTING\n54: \n55: Routing is **registry-driven at runtime and authored in `hub-router.json`** in two stages.\n56: Stage 1 (hub → mode) selects a mode: `hub-router.json` `vocabularyClasses` is the one authored routing vocabulary.\n57: The `mode-registry.json` aliases, each packet's `Keyword triggers:` line and the root `ROUTER.md` intents are checked against it.\n58: `sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-hub-vocabulary-source.cjs` fails on the `alias`, `stage-two`, `triggers` and `packets` legs; its `stage-two-reverse` leg only reports.\n59: Stage 2 (mode → leaves) lives in the root [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md), which maps the request's authoring intent to the packet-local leaf resources that mode loads.\n60: The two layers stay separate: the hub never emits leaf paths, and the surface router never re-decides the mode.\n61: The advisor routes every documentation and authoring query to the single identity `sk-doc`.\n62: Resolve the mode with `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-doc --prompt \"<task>\"`.\n63: Act on the decision: `route` loads its `targets`, `clarify` and `defer` ask, `reject` refuses.\n64: Compiled routing is the default.\n65: An unclear documentation intent asks for disambiguation, because `routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `null`.\n66: Run the compiled-routing directive in [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) before selecting hub resources.\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: ## 3. HOW IT WORKS\n71: \n72: ### Terms\n73: \n74: - **`workflowMode`**: the public packet key a request resolves to, such as `sk-create-skill`.\n75: - **`packetKind`**: `workflow` for every sk-doc packet, because this hub has no surface axis.\n76: - **`backendKind`**: `template-scaffold` for the create-* generators and `sk-create-quality-control` for the quality-control mode.\n77: - **packet**: a nested `sk-create-*` folder that keeps its own authoring contract, references, assets and scripts.\n78: - **`mode-registry.json`**: the registry that owns each packet's discriminator, aliases, command and `advisorRouting`.\n79: - **`hub-router.json`**: stage one's signals, vocabulary classes, default fallback resource and bundle rules.\n80: - **`vocabularyClasses`**: the one authored routing vocabulary that the registry aliases, the `Keyword triggers:` lines and the `ROUTER.md` intents are checked against.\n81: - **`ROUTER.md`**: stage two's `INTENT_SIGNALS` and `RESOURCE_MAP`, which map an authoring intent to the packet-local leaf resources its mode loads.\n82: - **leaf**: a canonical `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair from `leaf-manifest.json` that a `RESOURCE_MAP` path converts to.\n83: - **`defer`**: the outcome that asks for disambiguation, which this hub reaches because `routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `null`.\n84: - **shared backbone**: the `shared/` copy of the sk-create-quality-control pipeline that every packet consumes.\n85: - **`graph-metadata.json`**: the one advisor identity for the whole skill, which no packet or `shared/` directory carries.\n86: \n87: ### Layout\n88: ```\n89: sk-doc/\n90:   SKILL.md               # this routing hub (no per-packet logic)\n91:   ROUTER.md              # stage-two surface router (authoring intent -> leaf sets)\n92:   mode-registry.json     # the fifteen-mode discriminator + advisorRouting (single source of truth)\n93:   hub-router.json        # router signals + vocabulary classes\n94:   description.json       # hub advisor descriptor\n95:   graph-metadata.json    # the ONE advisor identity for the whole skill\n96:   changelog/  manual-testing-playbook/  benchmark/  feature-catalog/\n97:   sk-create-skill/  sk-create-readme/  sk-create-agent/  sk-create-command/\n98:   sk-create-feature-catalog/  sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/\n99:   sk-create-benchmark/  sk-create-changelog/  sk-create-diff/\n100:   sk-create-repo-rule/  sk-create-frontmatter/  sk-create-goal/\n101:   sk-create-with-human-voice/  sk-create-quality-control/    # nested workflow packets\n102:   scripts/               # facade symlinks -> shared/ + owning packets (tool paths only)\n103:   shared/                # sk-create-quality-control backbone: validators, global standards, shared assets\n104: ```\n105: \n106: Each packet is self-contained (its own `SKILL.md`, `README.md`, `changelog/`, and moved `references/`/`assets/`/`scripts/`) and carries **no** `graph-metadata.json`, so the advisor discovers exactly one `sk-doc` identity.\n107: \n108: ### Shared backbone\n109: `shared/` holds the universal sk-create-quality-control pipeline consumed by every packet:\n110: - Generic validator scripts in `shared/scripts/`.\n111: - Cross-cutting standards and vocabulary in `shared/references/`.\n112: - Shared templates in `shared/assets/`.\n113: \n114: The generic validator `shared/scripts/cite-drift-scan.mjs` counts and resolves the `<path>.<ext>:<line>` citations in every tracked skill doc.\n115: It makes zero model calls by default.\n116: `--jev` runs the backend and needs `--out <dir>`, so every call is recorded, and the Jev arm and the advisory live in the sibling `shared/scripts/classifier-cite-drift-scan.mjs`.\n117: `validate_document.py` runs the same check as a non-blocking advisory on the document it validates.\n118: It prints `cite-drift advisory:` lines only when a Jev credential is stored, never changes the exit code, and `JEV_FEATURE_CITE_DRIFT=0` (older name: `SKDOC_CITE_DRIFT_CHECK=0`) skips it.\n119: The `sk-doc/scripts/` root directory keeps facade symlinks pointing inward to `shared/` and the owning packets so tool paths resolve.\n120: There are no hub-root `assets/` or `references/` aggregation directories: consumers reference each packet's own `assets/`/`references/` or the `shared/` backbone directly.\n121: \n122: ---\n123: \n124: ## 4. RULES\n125: \n126: ### ✅ ALWAYS\n127: - **ALWAYS** resolve a packet through `mode-registry.json`; never hardcode a router mapping in the hub.\n128: - **ALWAYS** keep authoring contracts in the packets; the hub stays routing-only.\n129: - **ALWAYS** keep exactly one `graph-metadata.json` (this hub's) so the advisor sees one identity.\n130: - **ALWAYS** keep the root `ROUTER.md` `RESOURCE_MAP` in sync with `leaf-manifest.json` and `leaf-aliases.json` — the leaf sets dual-read to canonical typed pairs at the one contract boundary.\n131: - **ALWAYS** keep the sk-create-quality-control pipeline as one shared source under `shared/`, consumed by the packets.\n132: - **ALWAYS** keep changelogs as real files at the hub and in each packet — never symlinked.\n133: \n134: ### ⛔ NEVER\n135: - **NEVER** add a `graph-metadata.json` inside a packet or `shared/`.\n136: - **NEVER** put per-packet authoring logic in the hub.\n137: - **NEVER** add a surface axis or a `surfaceBundle` outcome — sk-doc is workflow-only.\n138: \n139: ### ⚠️ ESCALATE IF\n140: - A new documentation workflow is needed — extend `mode-registry.json` and open a packet; do not bolt logic onto the hub.\n141: - A packet would become a near-empty shell (generic doctrine, no type-specific behavior) — fold it into `shared/` instead.\n142: \n143: ---\n144: \n145: ## 5. REFERENCES\n146: \n147: - Registry: `mode-registry.json` (fifteen modes across fourteen packets, `packetKind: workflow`).\n148: - Hub router: `hub-router.json` (signals + vocabulary classes).\n149: - Surface router: `ROUTER.md` (authoring intent to packet-local leaf sets).\n150: - Advisor descriptor: `description.json`; skill-graph identity: `graph-metadata.json`.\n151: - Packets: `sk-create-skill/`, `sk-create-readme/`, `sk-create-agent/`, `sk-create-command/`, `sk-create-feature-catalog/`, `sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/`, `sk-create-benchmark/`, `sk-create-changelog/`, `sk-create-diff/`, `sk-create-repo-rule/`, `sk-create-frontmatter/`, `sk-create-goal/`, `sk-create-with-human-voice/`, `sk-create-quality-control/`.\n152: - Shared backbone: `shared/scripts/`, `shared/references/`, `shared/assets/`.\n153: - Parent-skill pattern: `sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md`.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md, lines 30-153\n30: | **sk-create-readme** | Author a folder, code-folder or skill README, a repository front page and its install, contributing and security guides | `sk-create-readme/` | `/create:readme` |\n31: | **sk-create-agent** | Scaffold an OpenCode agent (permission/authority frontmatter) | `sk-create-agent/` | `/create:agent` |\n32: | **sk-create-command** | Scaffold an OpenCode slash command (argument-hint + allowed-tools + router/presentation split) | `sk-create-command/` | `/create:command` |\n33: | **sk-create-feature-catalog** | Author a feature-catalog inventory package | `sk-create-feature-catalog/` | `/create:feature-catalog` |\n34: | **sk-create-manual-testing-playbook** | Author a manual-testing-playbook package | `sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/` | `/create:manual-testing-playbook` |\n35: | **sk-create-benchmark** | Author MCP-promotion and behavior packages or inputs | `sk-create-benchmark/` | `/create:benchmark` |\n36: | **sk-create-changelog** | Author a global component changelog entry (version bump + topology-aware placement). Packet-local changelogs are deprecated | `sk-create-changelog/` | `/create:changelog` |\n37: | **sk-create-diff** | Produce a local, Git-free before/after review of an edited document (text/Markdown/HTML/DOCX/text-PDF) as a self-contained HTML report | `sk-create-diff/` | `/create:diff` |\n38: | **sk-create-repo-rule** | Create, revise or retire a repo-local rule under `repo-rules/` and wire it into `REPO RULES.md` (four decision tests refuse most requests) | `sk-create-repo-rule/` | `/create:repo-rule` |\n39: | **sk-create-with-human-voice** | Apply the Human Voice Rules to prose, or score prose against them, with a scope gate and a re-scan | `sk-create-with-human-voice/` | `/create:with-human-voice` |\n40: | **sk-create-frontmatter** | Own the YAML frontmatter contract: per-class field rules, the description budget, and the 4-part `version` derivation | `sk-create-frontmatter/` | — (routes via aliases) |\n41: | **sk-create-goal** | Author or revise a packet `goal.md`: the durable directive, three to seven self-contained completion criteria, and the phase-parent binding table (session-goal setting stays with the goal hooks) | `sk-create-goal/` | `/create:goal` |\n42: | **sk-create-quality-control** | Validate / score / optimize an EXISTING document (extract → DQI → HVR → validate) | `sk-create-quality-control/` | (routes via aliases) |\n43: \n44: ### When NOT to Use\n45: - Code implementation, tests, or debugging — use `sk-code`.\n46: - Git worktree, branch, commit, PR, or release work — use `sk-git`.\n47: - Spec-folder workflow / memory / save context — use `system-spec-kit`.\n48: - A measured Style Reference (design tokens extracted from a live source) — use `sk-design-md-generator`.\n49: - The `shared/` backbone is consumed by the packets, not invoked as a user workflow.\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## 2. SMART ROUTING\n54: \n55: Routing is **registry-driven at runtime and authored in `hub-router.json`** in two stages.\n56: Stage 1 (hub → mode) selects a mode: `hub-router.json` `vocabularyClasses` is the one authored routing vocabulary.\n57: The `mode-registry.json` aliases, each packet's `Keyword triggers:` line and the root `ROUTER.md` intents are checked against it.\n58: `sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-hub-vocabulary-source.cjs` fails on the `alias`, `stage-two`, `triggers` and `packets` legs; its `stage-two-reverse` leg only reports.\n59: Stage 2 (mode → leaves) lives in the root [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md), which maps the request's authoring intent to the packet-local leaf resources that mode loads.\n60: The two layers stay separate: the hub never emits leaf paths, and the surface router never re-decides the mode.\n61: The advisor routes every documentation and authoring query to the single identity `sk-doc`.\n62: Resolve the mode with `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-doc --prompt \"<task>\"`.\n63: Act on the decision: `route` loads its `targets`, `clarify` and `defer` ask, `reject` refuses.\n64: Compiled routing is the default.\n65: An unclear documentation intent asks for disambiguation, because `routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `null`.\n66: Run the compiled-routing directive in [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) before selecting hub resources.\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: ## 3. HOW IT WORKS\n71: \n72: ### Terms\n73: \n74: - **`workflowMode`**: the public packet key a request resolves to, such as `sk-create-skill`.\n75: - **`packetKind`**: `workflow` for every sk-doc packet, because this hub has no surface axis.\n76: - **`backendKind`**: `template-scaffold` for the create-* generators and `sk-create-quality-control` for the quality-control mode.\n77: - **packet**: a nested `sk-create-*` folder that keeps its own authoring contract, references, assets and scripts.\n78: - **`mode-registry.json`**: the registry that owns each packet's discriminator, aliases, command and `advisorRouting`.\n79: - **`hub-router.json`**: stage one's signals, vocabulary classes, default fallback resource and bundle rules.\n80: - **`vocabularyClasses`**: the one authored routing vocabulary that the registry aliases, the `Keyword triggers:` lines and the `ROUTER.md` intents are checked against.\n81: - **`ROUTER.md`**: stage two's `INTENT_SIGNALS` and `RESOURCE_MAP`, which map an authoring intent to the packet-local leaf resources its mode loads.\n82: - **leaf**: a canonical `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair from `leaf-manifest.json` that a `RESOURCE_MAP` path converts to.\n83: - **`defer`**: the outcome that asks for disambiguation, which this hub reaches because `routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `null`.\n84: - **shared backbone**: the `shared/` copy of the sk-create-quality-control pipeline that every packet consumes.\n85: - **`graph-metadata.json`**: the one advisor identity for the whole skill, which no packet or `shared/` directory carries.\n86: \n87: ### Layout\n88: ```\n89: sk-doc/\n90:   SKILL.md               # this routing hub (no per-packet logic)\n91:   ROUTER.md              # stage-two surface router (authoring intent -> leaf sets)\n92:   mode-registry.json     # the fifteen-mode discriminator + advisorRouting (single source of truth)\n93:   hub-router.json        # router signals + vocabulary classes\n94:   description.json       # hub advisor descriptor\n95:   graph-metadata.json    # the ONE advisor identity for the whole skill\n96:   changelog/  manual-testing-playbook/  benchmark/  feature-catalog/\n97:   sk-create-skill/  sk-create-readme/  sk-create-agent/  sk-create-command/\n98:   sk-create-feature-catalog/  sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/\n99:   sk-create-benchmark/  sk-create-changelog/  sk-create-diff/\n100:   sk-create-repo-rule/  sk-create-frontmatter/  sk-create-goal/\n101:   sk-create-with-human-voice/  sk-create-quality-control/    # nested workflow packets\n102:   scripts/               # facade symlinks -> shared/ + owning packets (tool paths only)\n103:   shared/                # sk-create-quality-control backbone: validators, global standards, shared assets\n104: ```\n105: \n106: Each packet is self-contained (its own `SKILL.md`, `README.md`, `changelog/`, and moved `references/`/`assets/`/`scripts/`) and carries **no** `graph-metadata.json`, so the advisor discovers exactly one `sk-doc` identity.\n107: \n108: ### Shared backbone\n109: `shared/` holds the universal sk-create-quality-control pipeline consumed by every packet:\n110: - Generic validator scripts in `shared/scripts/`.\n111: - Cross-cutting standards and vocabulary in `shared/references/`.\n112: - Shared templates in `shared/assets/`.\n113: \n114: The generic validator `shared/scripts/cite-drift-scan.mjs` counts and resolves the `<path>.<ext>:<line>` citations in every tracked skill doc.\n115: It makes zero model calls by default.\n116: `--jev` runs the backend and needs `--out <dir>`, so every call is recorded, and the Jev arm and the advisory live in the sibling `shared/scripts/classifier-cite-drift-scan.mjs`.\n117: `validate_document.py` runs the same check as a non-blocking advisory on the document it validates.\n118: It prints `cite-drift advisory:` lines only when a Jev credential is stored, never changes the exit code, and `JEV_FEATURE_CITE_DRIFT=0` (older name: `SKDOC_CITE_DRIFT_CHECK=0`) skips it.\n119: The `sk-doc/scripts/` root directory keeps facade symlinks pointing inward to `shared/` and the owning packets so tool paths resolve.\n120: There are no hub-root `assets/` or `references/` aggregation directories: consumers reference each packet's own `assets/`/`references/` or the `shared/` backbone directly.\n121: \n122: ---\n123: \n124: ## 4. RULES\n125: \n126: ### ✅ ALWAYS\n127: - **ALWAYS** resolve a packet through `mode-registry.json`; never hardcode a router mapping in the hub.\n128: - **ALWAYS** keep authoring contracts in the packets; the hub stays routing-only.\n129: - **ALWAYS** keep exactly one `graph-metadata.json` (this hub's) so the advisor sees one identity.\n130: - **ALWAYS** keep the root `ROUTER.md` `RESOURCE_MAP` in sync with `leaf-manifest.json` and `leaf-aliases.json` — the leaf sets dual-read to canonical typed pairs at the one contract boundary.\n131: - **ALWAYS** keep the sk-create-quality-control pipeline as one shared source under `shared/`, consumed by the packets.\n132: - **ALWAYS** keep changelogs as real files at the hub and in each packet — never symlinked.\n133: \n134: ### ⛔ NEVER\n135: - **NEVER** add a `graph-metadata.json` inside a packet or `shared/`.\n136: - **NEVER** put per-packet authoring logic in the hub.\n137: - **NEVER** add a surface axis or a `surfaceBundle` outcome — sk-doc is workflow-only.\n138: \n139: ### ⚠️ ESCALATE IF\n140: - A new documentation workflow is needed — extend `mode-registry.json` and open a packet; do not bolt logic onto the hub.\n141: - A packet would become a near-empty shell (generic doctrine, no type-specific behavior) — fold it into `shared/` instead.\n142: \n143: ---\n144: \n145: ## 5. REFERENCES\n146: \n147: - Registry: `mode-registry.json` (fifteen modes across fourteen packets, `packetKind: workflow`).\n148: - Hub router: `hub-router.json` (signals + vocabulary classes).\n149: - Surface router: `ROUTER.md` (authoring intent to packet-local leaf sets).\n150: - Advisor descriptor: `description.json`; skill-graph identity: `graph-metadata.json`.\n151: - Packets: `sk-create-skill/`, `sk-create-readme/`, `sk-create-agent/`, `sk-create-command/`, `sk-create-feature-catalog/`, `sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/`, `sk-create-benchmark/`, `sk-create-changelog/`, `sk-create-diff/`, `sk-create-repo-rule/`, `sk-create-frontmatter/`, `sk-create-goal/`, `sk-create-with-human-voice/`, `sk-create-quality-control/`.\n152: - Shared backbone: `shared/scripts/`, `shared/references/`, `shared/assets/`.\n153: - Parent-skill pattern: `sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md`."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\",\"offset\":30,\"limit\":130}"},"time":{"start":1794848338570,"end":1794848339041}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794848339047,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e54c31e3001TT6X3pHxd6vZBu","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e54c0de7001YutKnTnGrw6MO2","type":"tool","id":"call_e952b647bf104add9b2aeeec","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".env.example"},"output":"Read file .env.example, lines 1-643\n1: # =============================================================================\n2: # .env.example  —  Environment variable template\n3: # =============================================================================\n4: #\n5: # CONVENTIONS\n6: #   - Every variable here is OPTIONAL except the Code Mode provider secrets in\n7: #     Section 1. The system runs on sensible defaults when nothing is set.\n8: #   - Non-secret lines are COMMENTED and show the DEFAULT value. Uncomment the\n9: #     line and change the value to override that default.\n10: #   - Flag semantics:\n11: #       Graduated ON  = enabled by default; set  false  to DISABLE.\n12: #       Opt-in OFF    = disabled by default; set  true   to ENABLE.\n13: #   - A default shown as empty means \"unset by default\":  # VAR=    # ...\n14: #   - Booleans accept  1/true/yes/on  (and their negatives) unless noted.\n15: #\n16: # WHERE THESE ARE READ\n17: #   Code Mode loads a filled-in .env for its provider secrets (Section 1), and\n18: #   nothing else in this repository loads it. Hooks, validators and git hooks\n19: #   read the process environment. The validation off switches in Section 5, the\n20: #   hook kill-switches in Section 8 and the Jev feature switches in Section 17\n21: #   also read .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env, where a saved switch stays on until\n22: #   a set environment value overrides it. A switch written only in .env counts\n23: #   where your shell or runtime exports it.\n24: #\n25: # SETTING ONE LOCALLY\n26: #   This file is a template: no reader loads its values. Copy a line to where its\n27: #   reader looks, uncomment it and change the value:\n28: #     - export NAME=value in ~/.zshrc or ~/.bashrc works for every setting and wins\n29: #       over hook-flags.env\n30: #     - .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env (copy hook-flags.env.example) for the hook,\n31: #       validation and Jev switches, SESSION_HANDOVER_NOTIFY_HOPS and SESSION_HANDOVER_GOAL\n32: #     - .claude/settings.local.json, env block, for Claude Code sessions only\n33: #     - .env (copy this file) only for the Code Mode keys in Section 1\n34: #   ENV_SECRET_GUARD_PEPPER (Section 8) is the exception: export it in your shell\n35: #   profile only, never in any of the files above.\n36: #   All four are gitignored. /doctor:env list shows every setting and where it is\n37: #   set, by name only; /doctor:env NAME saves one after showing the exact line.\n38: #\n39: # EXHAUSTIVE REFERENCE\n40: #   The full, source-generated SPECKIT_* feature-flag reference (types, read\n41: #   sites, rollout notes) lives in:\n42: #     .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md\n43: #   This file is a practical template; that document is authoritative.\n44: #\n45: # =============================================================================\n46: \n47: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n48: # 1. CODE MODE — MCP PROVIDER SECRETS  (fill these in)\n49: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n50: \n51: # These are the ONLY required values. Leave blank to disable a provider.\n52: # Code Mode resolves a manual's bare ${VAR} reference as {manual_name}_{VAR},\n53: # and DOUBLES every underscore in the manual name: a manual called\n54: # my_manual looking up ${API_KEY} needs my__manual_API_KEY.\n55: # A key under any other spelling is simply not found, and the manual fails to\n56: # register at server startup with no runtime symptom beyond a shorter tool list.\n57: # Never commit a filled-in .env — keep secrets out of version control.\n58: \n59: # GitHub  (github_GITHUB_TOKEN is an accepted alias)\n60: github_GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN=\n61: \n62: # ClickUp needs no key here: the clickup_official manual signs in with OAuth on first launch\n63: \n64: # Notion MCP\n65: notion_NOTION_TOKEN=\n66: \n67: # Obsidian  (Local REST API plugin: key + base URL + SSL verify toggle)\n68: obsidian_OBSIDIAN_API_KEY=\n69: obsidian_OBSIDIAN_VERIFY_SSL=\n70: obsidian_OBSIDIAN_BASE_URL=\n71: \n72: # Figma\n73: figma_FIGMA_API_KEY=\n74: \n75: # Webflow\n76: webflow_WEBFLOW_TOKEN=\n77: \n78: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n79: # 2. SPEC KIT ENGINE — PATHS, IPC & PREFLIGHT\n80: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n81: \n82: # Paths, shared IPC, lease and preflight controls for the spec-kit engine and the shared launchers.\n83: #\n84: # OWNERSHIP MARKERS\n85: #   Rows here and in Section 7 carry an ownership marker naming their owner: the HF model\n86: #   server and the skill advisor share the launcher, IPC and embedding rows. A marker governs\n87: #   the contiguous run of rows beneath it, up to the next blank line. An UNMARKED row belongs\n88: #   to the spec-kit engine itself.\n89: \n90: # --- Database & workspace paths ---\n91: # SPECKIT_SPECS_DIR=         # Override the specs root (auto-detected)\n92: # SPEC_KIT_SPECS_DIR=        # Alias for the specs root override\n93: # SPECKIT_TEMPLATES_BASE=    # Override the spec-doc templates directory (bundled default)\n94: # SPECKIT_RG_BIN=            # Path to the ripgrep binary for retrieval (default: rg on PATH)\n95: # SPEC_KIT_DB_DIR=           # Spec-kit database directory (alias SPECKIT_DB_DIR; auto)\n96: # MEMORY_DB_PATH=            # Explicit database file path; wins over the directory\n97: # MEMORY_BASE_PATH=          # Base path spec-kit resolves workspace files against (current directory)\n98: \n99: # --- Launcher, daemon & IPC ---\n100: # shared: owned by the HF model server and the skill advisor\n101: # SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_BRIDGE_DISABLED=false # Force legacy strict-single-writer (no IPC bridge)\n102: # SPECKIT_MAX_SECONDARY_CLIENTS=64      # Max concurrent secondary stdio clients on the IPC socket\n103: # SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MIN=30  # Idle self-exit timeout (min); 0 disables the monitor\n104: # SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR=               # Override daemon IPC socket dir (REQUIRED short path on macOS)\n105: # SPECKIT_PROXY_COLD_START_ATTEMPTS=30  # Connect attempts while a cold launcher backend comes up\n106: # SPECKIT_PS_PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS=2000      # Timeout for the process-table probe that checks daemons\n107: \n108: # shared: owned by the HF model server and the skill advisor\n109: # SPECKIT_LEASE_PROBE_RETRIES=1         # Consecutive failed liveness probes before reaping the lease owner\n110: # SPECKIT_LEASE_PROBE_RETRY_TIMEOUT_MS=1500 # Per-attempt timeout for each lease retry probe\n111: # SPECKIT_LEASE_PROBE_RETRY_BACKOFF_MS=250  # Backoff between lease liveness-probe attempts\n112: \n113: # SPECKIT_STOP_HOOK_ORPHAN_SWEEP=off    # Stop-hook orphan sweep: off / dry-run / live\n114: \n115: # --- Boot, validation & preflight ---\n116: # SPECKIT_FRONTMATTER_ALLOWLIST=        # Override path to the frontmatter grandfather allowlist JSON\n117: # SPECKIT_VERBOSE_RESOLVER=false        # Log the cause when the level-contract resolver falls back\n118: # SPECKIT_PYTHON_BIN=                   # Python interpreter for spec-kit scripts (auto)\n119: # SPEC_KIT_PLUGIN_NODE_BINARY=          # Node binary for the spec-kit plugin (auto)\n120: \n121: # shared: owned by the HF model server and the skill advisor\n122: # SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_SCOPE=             # IPC socket scope selector (internal default)\n123: # SPECKIT_BRIDGE_RESPAWN_DISABLED=      # Disable launcher IPC-bridge respawn (set 1)\n124: \n125: # --- Launcher RSS watchdog & crash loop ---\n126: # shared: owned by the HF model server and the skill advisor\n127: # SPECKIT_CONTEXT_SERVER_MAX_RSS_MB=    # RSS ceiling (MB) for the default launcher watchdog (unset=off)\n128: # SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_RSS_SELF_EXIT=       # Recycle on an RSS breach (set 1, with a MAX_RSS_MB value)\n129: # SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_RSS_WATCHDOG_INTERVAL_MS=15000 # How often the watchdog samples RSS\n130: # SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_RSS_CONSECUTIVE_BREACHES=3 # Breaching samples in a row before a recycle\n131: # SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_RSS_GRACE_MS=7000    # Wait before a recycled process is force-killed\n132: # SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_CRASH_LOOP_MAX_DEATHS=3 # Deaths within the window before the launcher gives up\n133: # SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_CRASH_LOOP_WINDOW_MS=60000 # Window the crash-loop guard counts deaths in\n134: # SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_CRASH_LOOP_INITIAL_BACKOFF_MS=250 # First restart backoff after a death\n135: # SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_CRASH_LOOP_MAX_BACKOFF_MS=5000 # Restart backoff ceiling\n136: \n137: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n138: # 3. SHARED RANKING ALGORITHMS\n139: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n140: # Read by shared/algorithms/rrf-fusion.ts, whose only live consumer is the skill\n141: # advisor's fusion scorer. Spec-kit retrieval is lexical and reads none of these.\n142: \n143: # SPECKIT_RRF=true                      # Master switch for Reciprocal Rank Fusion (graduated ON)\n144: # SPECKIT_RRF_K=40                      # RRF smoothing constant k (>0; lower = more top-heavy)\n145: # SPECKIT_RETRIEVAL_PROFILE_WEIGHTS=    # Override per-profile retrieval weights (JSON)\n146: \n147: # SPECKIT_SCORE_NORMALIZATION=true      # Composite score normalization (graduated ON)\n148: # SPECKIT_CALIBRATED_OVERLAP_BONUS=true # Overlap bonus for multi-channel convergence (graduated ON)\n149: \n150: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n151: # 4. SPEC KIT ENGINE — DISCOVERY & COMPILED ROUTING\n152: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n153: \n154: # SPECKIT_FOLDER_DISCOVERY_TOKEN_THRESHOLD=0.45 # Per-token similarity threshold for folder-name matching\n155: # SPECKIT_DESCRIPTION_REPAIR_MERGE_SAFE=true # Merge-safe description repair during discovery (graduated ON)\n156: \n157: # --- Compiled routing ---\n158: # SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING=             # Serve compiled per-hub router: unset=default cohort, 1=force, 0=kill\n159: # SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING_DEBUG=       # Emit stderr breadcrumbs when a compiled route falls back to legacy\n160: \n161: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n162: # 5. SPEC KIT ENGINE — VALIDATION, SPEC GATE & GENERATED METADATA\n163: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n164: \n165: # --- Validation off switches (1/true/yes/on; also read from .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env, a set env var wins) ---\n166: # SPECKIT_SKIP_VALIDATION=              # Switch spec folder validation (validate.sh) off. CI never sets it\n167: # SKDOC_SKIP_VALIDATION=                # Switch every sk-doc format validator off. CI never sets it\n168: \n169: # SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE=true              # Advisory acceptance-criteria coverage scan (graduated ON)\n170: # SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE_FLOOR=0.9         # Min covered acceptance-criteria ratio for the advisory scan\n171: # SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE_ENFORCE=false     # Fail the rule instead of advising when coverage is under the floor (opt-in)\n172: # SPECKIT_AUTHORED_CONTINUITY_SNAPSHOT=false # Compact-hook authored continuity snapshot path (opt-in)\n173: # SPECKIT_COMPLETION_FRESHNESS=false    # Strict-only completion-freshness validation rule (opt-in)\n174: # SPECKIT_COMPLETION_FRESHNESS_ENFORCE=false # Promote stale freshness findings from warning to error\n175: # SPECKIT_ENTITY_CONFIG_PATH=           # Override path to the entity-extraction rules JSON (built-in default)\n176: \n177: # --- validate.sh options and rule cutoffs ---\n178: # SPECKIT_STRICT=                       # true = same as --strict\n179: # SPECKIT_VERBOSE=                      # true = same as --verbose\n180: # SPECKIT_JSON=                         # true = same as --json\n181: # SPECKIT_QUIET=                        # true = same as --quiet\n182: # SPECKIT_RULES=                        # Comma-separated subset of rules to run\n183: # SPECKIT_DRAFT_AUTO_REPAIR=true        # Graduated ON: a strict full-rule validate on a Draft packet repairs derived metadata once; 0/false/off keeps it read-only\n184: # SPECKIT_VALIDATION=                   # false switches validate.sh off (older form of SPECKIT_SKIP_VALIDATION)\n185: # SPECKIT_POST_VALIDATE=                # 1 = create.sh validates a folder right after scaffolding it\n186: # SKIP_TEMPLATE_CHECK=                  # 1 = the frontmatter rule skips its template-source check\n187: # SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE=true               # Acceptance-criteria closure rule (graduated ON)\n188: # SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE_CUTOFF=2026-08-30  # Packets created before this date stay advisory for closure\n189: # SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE_CUTOFF=2026-08-30 # Packets created before this date stay advisory for coverage\n190: # SPECKIT_SOURCE_TAG_CUTOFF=2026-10-04  # Packets created on or before this date skip SOURCE_TAGS\n191: # SPECKIT_CANONICAL_SAVE_CUTOFF=2026-05-01T00:00:00Z # Packets older than this skip canonical-save checks\n192: # SPECKIT_CANONICAL_SAVE_FRESHNESS_SLACK_MS=600000 # Slack between description and graph freshness\n193: \n194: # --- Spec Gate (Gate-3) + child dispatch ---\n195: # SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_ENFORCE=             # Opt-in deny mode for a mutation with no resolved spec folder\n196: # SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED=            # Fail-open no-op: no question, no denial, no state writes\n197: # SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_3_DELIVERY_SUPPRESSION= # Suppression is default-on; set 0/false/no/off to re-ask at every in-gate mutation\n198: # AI_SESSION_CHILD=                     # Mark a dispatched sub-session (1) so Gate-3 is a no-op\n199: # SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER=                   # Bind the session's spec folder up front so Gate-3 is answered\n200: # SPECIFY_FEATURE=                      # Name the target packet for the spec scripts directly\n201: # AUTO_SAVE_MODE=                       # true = spec-folder detection never prompts\n202: # SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_ACTIVE_RETENTION_DAYS=2 # Age before an untouched spec-gate state file is swept\n203: # SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_ARCHIVE_RETENTION_DAYS=90 # Retention before an archived spec-gate file is pruned\n204: # SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_SWEEP_INTERVAL_MS=3600000 # Min interval between spec-gate state sweeps\n205: # SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_WARNING_LOG_MAX_BYTES=262144 # Size at which the spec-gate warning log rotates\n206: \n207: # --- Generated-metadata integrity & data quality ---\n208: # SPECKIT_GENERATOR_HARDENING=true      # Fingerprint + phase-parent + telemetry hardening (graduated ON)\n209: # SPECKIT_GENERATED_METADATA_GRANDFATHER=false # Report mode for the metadata-integrity rule (default enforces)\n210: # SPECKIT_STATUS_COMPLETION_CONSISTENCY_GATE=false # Cross-check derived complete status (report mode)\n211: # SPECKIT_IDENTITY_MERGE_SAFETY=true    # Shared identity resolver + lineage-merge guard (graduated ON)\n212: # SPECKIT_GENERATED_METADATA_DRIFT_GATE=true # Synopsis drift gate + shared-extractor routing (graduated ON)\n213: # SPECKIT_GENERATED_METADATA_Z_EXCLUSION=true # Exclude z-future staging dirs from folder discovery; z_archive stays in (graduated ON)\n214: # SPECKIT_IDEMPOTENT_DESCRIPTION_WRITES=true # Content-gated description.json / cache writes (graduated ON)\n215: # SPECKIT_METADATA_DISK_CONSISTENCY_ENFORCE=true # Fail strict on metadata/on-disk path mismatch (enforcing)\n216: # SPECKIT_STATUS_CROSS_DOC_ENFORCE=true # Fail strict on spec.md vs implementation-summary status drift (enforcing)\n217: # SPECKIT_CHILD_DRIFT_ENFORCE=true      # Fail strict on phase-parent children_ids drift (enforcing)\n218: # SPECKIT_VALIDATE_SCRIPT=              # Override the validate.sh path the freshness sweep invokes\n219: \n220: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n221: # 6. SPEC KIT ENGINE — TELEMETRY & INDEXING\n222: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n223: \n224: # SPECKIT_METRICS_ENABLED=              # Enable advisor/metrics emission (set true)\n225: \n226: # SPECKIT_INDEX_SPEC_DOCS=true          # Spec-document discovery for metadata and the spec-root registry (set false to return no documents)\n227: \n228: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n229: # 7. EMBEDDING + LOCAL HF MODEL SERVER\n230: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n231: \n232: # Provider cascade (local-first): Ollama -> hf-local -> OpenAI -> Voyage.\n233: \n234: # --- Provider selection ---\n235: # shared: owned by the HF model server and the skill advisor\n236: # EMBEDDINGS_PROVIDER=auto              # Provider: auto (cascade) or force a specific provider\n237: # OLLAMA_EMBEDDINGS_MODEL=nomic-embed-text-v1.5 # Ollama embedding model (local default)\n238: # HF_EMBEDDINGS_MODEL=nomic-ai/nomic-embed-text-v1.5 # Local HF model (single resident model)\n239: # HF_EMBEDDINGS_DTYPE=                  # HF model dtype override (e.g. q8/fp16)\n240: # OPENAI_API_KEY=                       # Enables OpenAI text-embedding-3-small in the cascade\n241: # VOYAGE_API_KEY=                       # Enables Voyage voyage-code-3 in the cascade\n242: # EMBEDDING_DIM=                        # Explicit embedding-dimension override (derived by default)\n243: # HF_EMBEDDINGS_PREFIX_QUERY=           # Override the local HF query prefix (registry default)\n244: # HF_EMBEDDINGS_PREFIX_DOC=             # Override the local HF document prefix (registry default)\n245: # OLLAMA_BASE_URL=                      # Ollama origin (local daemon by default)\n246: # OLLAMA_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=            # Pin every Ollama request to one deadline (adaptive by default)\n247: # OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1 # OpenAI-compatible endpoint for embeddings\n248: # OPENAI_EMBEDDINGS_MODEL=              # OpenAI embedding model (text-embedding-3-small)\n249: # VOYAGE_BASE_URL=                      # Voyage endpoint override\n250: # VOYAGE_EMBEDDINGS_MODEL=              # Voyage embedding model (voyage-code-3)\n251: \n252: # --- Local HF model server ---\n253: # shared: owned by the HF model server and the skill advisor\n254: # HF_EMBED_SERVER_URL=                  # Model-server endpoint (unix path / unix:// / tcp://; default socket)\n255: # HF_EMBED_SERVER_READY_TIMEOUT_MS=45000 # Initial readiness budget waiting for the model server\n256: # SPECKIT_HF_MODEL_SERVER_MAX_RSS_MB=   # RSS ceiling (MB) for the supervised model-server tree (unset=off)\n257: # SPECKIT_HF_MODEL_SERVER_RSS_SELF_EXIT= # Recycle model server on an RSS breach (set 1, with MAX_RSS_MB)\n258: # SPECKIT_HF_MODEL_SERVER_LOADING_MAX_MS=150000 # Max age for one model-server load attempt\n259: # SPECKIT_HF_MODEL_SERVER_GIVEUP_COOLDOWN_MS=60000 # Cooldown after crash-loop give-up\n260: # SPECKIT_HF_MODEL_SERVER_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MIN=10 # Evict idle resident model server after N min (0=keep warm)\n261: # SPECKIT_HF_MODEL_SERVER_ORPHAN_REAP=0 # Disable orphan reap when another init system owns the shared socket\n262: # SPECKIT_HF_READY_LATCH_TTL_MS=30000   # How long a successful readiness check is trusted (max 120000)\n263: # HF_EMBED_ALLOW_REMOTE_BIND=           # 1 = allow a TCP bind beyond localhost (needs HF_EMBED_AUTH_TOKEN)\n264: # HF_EMBED_AUTH_TOKEN=                  # Token a remote client must send to the model server\n265: \n266: # shared: owned by the HF model server and the skill advisor\n267: # SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_MODEL_SERVER_ENABLED= # Skill-advisor arms the shared model-server spawn by default; set 0 to turn it off\n268: \n269: # --- Cascade probe timing ---\n270: # shared: owned by the HF model server and the skill advisor\n271: # SPECKIT_CASCADE_PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS=2500 # Per-provider HTTP probe timeout for auto-select\n272: # SPECKIT_CASCADE_LOCK_STALE_MS=30000   # Staleness threshold for the auto-select advisory lock\n273: # SPECKIT_CASCADE_SLEEP_MS=25           # Polling sleep while waiting for the auto-select lock\n274: \n275: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n276: # 8. HOOK KILL-SWITCHES  (default enabled, session handover only on Claude Code, user-hook sync off, set truthy to DISABLE)\n277: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n278: \n279: # May also be set in .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env (a real env var wins).\n280: \n281: # HOOK_FLAGS_CONFIG=                    # Override the hook-flags config file path\n282: # SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED=                # Master switch for every hook concern below\n283: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=        # Disable skill-advisor injection\n284: # SYSTEM_COMPLETION_DISABLED=           # Disable completion-evidence warnings\n285: # SYSTEM_DIRECTIVE_LIFECYCLE_DISABLED=  # Disable directive lifecycle boundary handling\n286: # SYSTEM_DISPATCH_DISABLED=             # Disable dispatch preflight and audit hooks\n287: # CLI_DISPATCH_AUDIT_DISABLED=          # Disable the dispatch audit trail only (canonical name)\n288: # SYSTEM_DISPATCH_GUARD_DISABLED=       # Disable the dispatch preflight guard only\n289: # SYSTEM_INJECTION_SCREEN_DISABLED=     # Disable the fetched-web-text injection screen\n290: # SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED=      # Session handover loop on every runtime when 1, off everywhere when 0 (context nudge, stop arm, compact pointer)\n291: # Unset, the loop is on for Claude Code and off on every other runtime.\n292: # Per-runtime overrides: a non-empty value (1 on, 0 off) beats SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED for that\n293: # runtime, and empty or unset falls back to it. DISABLED and SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED still beat every enable flag.\n294: # SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_CLAUDE_ENABLED=    # Claude Code\n295: # SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_CODEX_ENABLED=     # Codex\n296: # SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_PI_ENABLED=        # Pi\n297: # SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_OPENCODE_ENABLED=  # OpenCode\n298: # SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_CURSOR_ENABLED=    # Cursor\n299: # SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_DEVIN_ENABLED=     # Devin\n300: # SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_VIBE_ENABLED=      # Mistral Vibe\n301: # SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_DISABLED=     # Turn the session-handover loop off, wins over every enable flag above\n302: # Claude user-hook sync, off by default: at each Claude Code session start in a primary checkout, copy\n303: # this checkout's Claude hooks into ~/.claude/settings.json, keeping every other key and hook. Set it in\n304: # the hook-flags.env of the checkout that should own the copy; an env var turns it on for every checkout.\n305: # SYSTEM_CLAUDE_USER_HOOK_SYNC_ENABLED=  # Turn the sync on (set 1); a backup is kept as settings.json.pre-skilled-hook-sync\n306: # SYSTEM_CLAUDE_USER_HOOK_SYNC_DISABLED= # Stop the sync, wins over its enable flag\n307: # SYSTEM_TASK_DISPATCH_DISABLED=        # Disable task-dispatch warnings and denials\n308: # SYSTEM_DECISION_CAPTURE_DISABLED=     # Disable decision capture: no answer is queued for the next save\n309: # SYSTEM_ASK_SURFACE_DISABLED=         # Disable the ask-surface guard: a typed option menu is never sent back\n310: # SYSTEM_ENV_SECRET_GUARD_DISABLED=     # Disable the dotenv guard. Read from the shell environment only: a line in hook-flags.env or .env does nothing\n311: # SYSTEM_OVERLAY_GUARD_DISABLED=        # Disable the vendored-overlay edit guard\n312: # SYSTEM_PERMISSION_POLICY_DISABLED=    # Disable Devin permission-policy decisions\n313: # SK_CODE_POST_EDIT_QUALITY_DISABLED=   # Disable post-edit quality warnings\n314: # MCP_ROUTE_GUARD_DISABLED=             # Disable MCP route warnings and audit records\n315: # OPENCODE_GOAL_DISABLED=               # Disable goal injection and tools (alias OPENCODE_GOAL_PLUGIN_DISABLED)\n316: # SK_GIT_PREFLIGHT_DISABLED=            # Disable git-preflight advisories\n317: # CODEX_WATCHDOG_DISABLED=              # Disable Codex hook-drift warnings\n318: # SYSTEM_SESSION_LIFECYCLE_DISABLED=    # Disable session-start/stop/compaction hook handling\n319: # SYSTEM_SESSION_CLEANUP_DISABLED=      # Disable session cleanup and teardown\n320: # SYSTEM_HOOK_INSTALL_DISABLED=         # Disable Codex hook installation and check mode\n321: # SYSTEM_DIST_FRESHNESS_DISABLED=       # Disable dist-freshness checks\n322: # SYSTEM_GIT_WORKTREE_GUARD_DISABLED=   # Disable the worktree warning\n323: # SYSTEM_GIT_HOOKS_CHECK_DISABLED=      # Disable the git-hooks installation warning\n324: # SYSTEM_GIT_COMMIT_HOOKS_DISABLED=     # Emergency-off for the pre-commit chain\n325: \n326: # ── Dotenv guard fingerprint key (unset by default) ──\n327: # The guard compares two dotenv values by an HMAC-SHA256 fingerprint and never shows either one.\n328: # Unset, the fingerprint is refused rather than computed without a key. Generate a key with\n329: # `openssl rand -base64 32` and export it from your shell profile only: never put it in .env, in\n330: # hook-flags.env or in any file inside a repository, because a key the agent can read lets it\n331: # test guesses against a fingerprint.\n332: # ENV_SECRET_GUARD_PEPPER=              # HMAC key for env_secret_fingerprint and `env-secret.cjs fingerprint`\n333: # ENV_SECRET_GUARD_WRITE_CHECK=         # restore (default): undo a dotenv write a shell call made. report: name it and leave it\n334: # ENV_SECRET_GUARD_STATE_DIR=           # Where the guard keeps its record and dotenv backups (default ~/.local/state/env-secret-guard)\n335: \n336: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n337: # 9. HOOK LIFECYCLE\n338: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n339: \n340: # SPECKIT_DIRECTIVE_LIFECYCLE_DEDUP=true # Drop constant policy on a confirmed same-epoch repeat (graduated ON)\n341: # SPECKIT_PI_DIRECTIVE_DEDUP=true       # Pi directive dedup on a proven repeat (graduated ON)\n342: # SPECKIT_DIRECTIVE_LIFECYCLE_STATE_DIR= # Override the directive-lifecycle private state root (temp default)\n343: # SPECKIT_OPENCODE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS=3000 # Timeout for the OpenCode advisor plugin bridge\n344: # SPECKIT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS=       # Timeout for the Claude advisor hook (ms)\n345: # SPECKIT_CLAUDE_CODE_STATE_DIR=        # Override the Claude Code hook state directory\n346: # SPECKIT_OPENCODE_STATE_DIR=           # Override the OpenCode hook state directory\n347: \n348: # --- Session cleanup & orphan sweeper ---\n349: # SESSION_CLEANUP_LOG_PATH=~/.local/share/session-cleanup.log # Session cleanup log (older name CLAUDE_SESSION_CLEANUP_LOG_PATH)\n350: # SESSION_CLEANUP_LOG_MAX_BYTES=10485760 # Size at which the cleanup log rotates (older name CLAUDE_SESSION_CLEANUP_LOG_MAX_BYTES)\n351: # SPECKIT_SESSION_START_ORPHAN_SWEEP=   # Sweep orphaned MCP processes at OpenCode session start (opt-in, set 1)\n352: # SPECKIT_ORPHAN_SWEEPER_BIN=           # Override the orphan sweeper script path\n353: # ORPHAN_AGE_MIN_SEC=300                # Min age before an orphaned MCP helper is swept\n354: # ORPHAN_TMP_AGE_HOURS=24               # Min age before a temporary dispatch artifact is swept\n355: # ORPHAN_TEMP_PROCESS_AGE_HOURS=6       # Min age before a parentless process from a temp or scratch folder is swept\n356: # ORPHAN_SWEEPER_LOG_PATH=~/.local/share/orphan-sweeper.log # Orphan sweeper log\n357: # ORPHAN_SWEEPER_LOG_MAX_BYTES=10485760 # Size at which the sweeper log rotates\n358: \n359: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n360: # 10. SKILL ADVISOR\n361: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n362: \n363: # Threshold / calibration overrides for the 5-lane scorer and prompt-policy.\n364: \n365: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD=0.8 # Confidence threshold for the fusion scorer (0..1)\n366: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_UNCERTAINTY_THRESHOLD=0.35 # Uncertainty ceiling for the fusion scorer (0..1)\n367: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_CALIBRATION_OVERRIDE_JSON= # Partial override for routing calibration bonuses (JSON)\n368: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_PROMPT_POLICY_PATH=   # Override the prompt-policy linguistic-sets JSON (bundled default)\n369: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_PROMPT_POLICY_MIN_VISIBLE_CHARS=15 # Min visible chars for the short-casual skip path\n370: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_PROMPT_POLICY_MEANINGFUL_TOKEN_FLOOR=3 # Min meaningful tokens for the work-intent fire rule\n371: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_PROMPT_POLICY_LENGTH_AND_TOKEN_VISIBLE_CHARS=20 # Visible-char threshold, length+token rule\n372: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_PROMPT_POLICY_LENGTH_AND_TOKEN_MEANINGFUL_FLOOR=4 # Meaningful-token threshold, length+token rule\n373: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_PROMPT_POLICY_LONG_NON_CASUAL_CHARS=50 # Visible-char threshold for the long-prompt fire rule\n374: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_WEIGHTS_JSON=    # Override live-lane weights for the 5-lane scorer (JSON partial)\n375: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_SHADOW_WEIGHTS_JSON= # Override shadow-mode lane weights (JSON partial)\n376: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_DOC_TRIGGERS=         # Opt-in doc-frontmatter trigger harvest (set true)\n377: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_WORKSPACE_ALLOWLIST=  # Extra allowed workspaceRoot prefixes (colon-separated)\n378: # SPECKIT_PRIVATE_SKILL_ROOTS=          # Trusted roots a private local-* skill link may point into (colon-separated absolute paths)\n379: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_RRF_FUSION=false      # Route the scorer through RRF instead of the weighted blend (opt-in)\n380: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_SHADOW_DELTA_ENABLED= # Enable shadow-delta collection (set 1/true)\n381: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_SHADOW_DELTA_PATH=    # Shadow-delta sink path (setting it also enables collection)\n382: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_HOOK_CACHE_HIT_P95_WARN_MS=75 # Warn threshold for advisor cache-hit p95 latency (ms)\n383: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_HOOK_CACHE_HIT_P95_PAGE_MS=150 # Page threshold for advisor cache-hit p95 latency (ms)\n384: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_HOOK_FAILOPEN_WARN_RATE=0.02 # Fail-open rate that raises a warning\n385: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_HOOK_FAILOPEN_PAGE_RATE=0.05 # Fail-open rate that raises a page\n386: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_BM25_LEXICAL_SHADOW=  # Score a BM25 lexical lane in shadow mode (opt-in)\n387: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_FEEDBACK_CALIBRATION_SHADOW= # Record feedback calibration in shadow mode (opt-in)\n388: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_FEEDBACK_CALIBRATION_PATH= # Override the feedback calibration records path\n389: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_ROUTE_EXCLUSIONS_DIR= # Override the route-exclusions directory\n390: # SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_FALLBACK_TIMEOUT_MS=250 # Budget for the hooks' CLI fallback call\n391: # SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL=    # 1 = the Python advisor scores locally instead of calling the native runtime\n392: \n393: # --- OpenCode advisor plugin limits ---\n394: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_BRIDGE_TIMEOUT_MS=2500 # Timeout for one plugin bridge call\n395: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CACHE_TTL_MS=300000 # How long a cached brief is reused\n396: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_CACHE_ENTRIES=1000 # Max cached briefs\n397: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_TOKENS=80    # Token cap for one brief\n398: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_PROMPT_BYTES=65536 # Longest prompt the plugin sends to the advisor\n399: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_BRIEF_CHARS=2048 # Longest brief the plugin injects\n400: \n401: # --- Skill Advisor daemon: disable / trust / debug ---\n402: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=   # Disable the skill-advisor hook (alias of the kill-switch)\n403: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=           # Enable skill-advisor debug logging\n404: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR=          # Override the skill-advisor DB directory (auto)\n405: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_NODE_BINARY=     # Node binary for the skill-advisor daemon (auto)\n406: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_TRUST_DEFAULT=   # Daemon-side trust default (set \"trusted\" for no-_meta clients)\n407: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_STRICT_SINGLE_WRITER= # Strict single-writer enforcement for the advisor DB\n408: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_THRESHOLD_CONFIDENCE=0.8 # Advisor recommend confidence threshold\n409: # SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=                  # Enable debug output in the skill_advisor.py CLI\n410: # SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLE_BUILTIN_SEMANTIC= # Disable built-in semantic matching in the advisor script\n411: # SKILL_ADVISOR_FRESH_PROMPTS_PATH=    # Test-only path of the fresh behaviour rows the command transcript scorer labels (default: its own behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl)\n412: # (Aliases that route to the SYSTEM_* names above: SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED,\n413: #  SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED, SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_TRUSTED,\n414: #  SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_DEV_ALLOW_STALE.)\n415: \n416: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n417: # 11. OPENCODE GOAL PLUGIN\n418: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n419: \n420: # Plugin-level controls (restart OpenCode after changing).\n421: \n422: # OPENCODE_GOAL_DISABLED=               # Disable goal injection and plugin behavior (set 1) — canonical\n423: # OPENCODE_GOAL_PLUGIN_DISABLED=        # Accepted alias for the line above\n424: # OPENCODE_GOAL_AUTONOMY=               # Continuation mode: active / smoke / passive (unset=disabled)\n425: # OPENCODE_GOAL_DEBUG=                  # Write bounded debug events to the goal-events log (set 1)\n426: # OPENCODE_GOAL_VERIFIER=heuristic      # Completion verifier: heuristic (deterministic) or llm\n427: # OPENCODE_GOAL_MAX_OBJECTIVE_CHARS=4000 # Max stored raw objective length\n428: # OPENCODE_GOAL_MAX_GOAL_PROMPT_CHARS=4000 # Max generated goalPrompt length (clamped to 4000)\n429: # OPENCODE_GOAL_MAX_INJECTION_CHARS=4800 # Max [active_goal] injection block length\n430: # OPENCODE_GOAL_MAX_EVIDENCE_CHARS=1200 # Max verifier evidence retained in goal state\n431: # OPENCODE_GOAL_STATE_ARCHIVE_RETENTION_DAYS=90 # Retention before an archived goal-state file is pruned\n432: # OPENCODE_GOAL_STATE_ACTIVE_RETENTION_DAYS=2 # Age before an orphaned active-state file is swept\n433: # OPENCODE_GOAL_STATE_SWEEP_INTERVAL_MS=3600000 # Min interval between orphaned-active-state sweeps\n434: # OPENCODE_GOAL_VERIFIER_TIMEOUT_MS=30000 # Ceiling on one verifier run (ms)\n435: # OPENCODE_GOAL_CONTINUATION_TIMEOUT_MS=30000 # Ceiling on one guarded continuation turn (ms)\n436: # OPENCODE_GOAL_JSONL_MAX_BYTES=5242880 # Size at which a goal event log rotates\n437: # OPENCODE_GOAL_STATE_DIR=              # Override the goal-state directory\n438: # OPENCODE_GOAL_RUNTIME_LABEL=          # Runtime label recorded in goal state\n439: # OPENCODE_SPECS_ROOT=                  # Specs root the goal plugin resolves against\n440: \n441: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n442: # 12. CLI FRONT DOOR (DUAL-STACK)\n443: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n444: \n445: # Warm-only / prompt-time markers for the daemon-backed CLIs. Truthy = warm-only.\n446: \n447: # SPECKIT_CLI_PROMPT_TIME=              # Cross-CLI prompt-time marker (implies warm-only)\n448: # OPENCODE_PROMPT_TIME=                 # Runtime prompt-time marker (implies warm-only)\n449: # CLAUDE_CODE_PROMPT_TIME=              # Runtime prompt-time marker (implies warm-only)\n450: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_WARM_ONLY=   # Default the skill-advisor CLI to warm-only\n451: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_PROMPT_TIME= # Mark the skill-advisor CLI call as prompt-time\n452: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_DEV_ALLOW_STALE= # Dev override for the skill-advisor shim dist-freshness guard\n453: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_TRUSTED=     # Send skill-advisor CLI calls as trusted (needed for mutations)\n454: \n455: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n456: # 13. DEEP-LOOP RUNTIME & GUARD\n457: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n458: \n459: # SPECKIT_FANOUT_NEAR_DUP_DEDUP=false   # Collapse near-duplicate findings in the fan-out merge (opt-in)\n460: # DEEP_LOOP_EVIDENCE_ENFORCEMENT=       # Enforce evidence requirements in the deep loop (opt-in)\n461: # DEEP_LOOP_MIN_OBSERVATIONS=           # Min confirming observations a finding needs before convergence counts it; setting it enables the guard\n462: # SYSTEM_DEEP_LOOP_GUARD_REJECT=        # Hard-block a Deep Route mode-mismatch dispatch (set 1)\n463: # SYSTEM_DEEP_LOOP_GUARD_REJECT_LOOP=   # Hard-block repeated hand-offs to the same loop executor (set 1)\n464: # SYSTEM_DEEP_LOOP_GUARD_ACTIVE_RETENTION_DAYS=2 # Age before an untouched loop-guard state file is swept\n465: # SYSTEM_DEEP_LOOP_GUARD_ARCHIVE_RETENTION_DAYS=90 # Retention before an archived loop-guard file is pruned\n466: # SYSTEM_DEEP_LOOP_GUARD_SWEEP_INTERVAL_MS=3600000 # Min interval between loop-guard state sweeps\n467: \n468: # --- Paths, gates and review enforcement ---\n469: # DEEP_LOOP_REPO_ROOT=                  # Pin the repository root the deep-loop scripts resolve against\n470: # DEEP_LOOP_AUTHORITY_ROOT=             # Override the authority root (relative values resolve against the repo)\n471: # DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR=            # Override the coverage graph database directory\n472: # DEEP_LOOP_LEDGER_BACKING_GATE=        # Set 0 as an emergency off for the ledger-backing gate (on by default)\n473: # DEEP_LOOP_MIN_OBSERVATIONS_GUARD=     # Turn on the min-observations guard at its default count (set 1)\n474: # DEEP_LOOP_VERIFY_GATEWAY_RECEIPT=     # Verify the gateway receipt on each iteration (set 1)\n475: # DEEP_REVIEW_V2_ENFORCEMENT=warn       # Deep-review v2 contract enforcement: warn / strict / off\n476: # SPECKIT_PROVENANCE_CHECK=             # Check executor build provenance (opt-in, set 1)\n477: \n478: # --- Codex dispatch defaults for skill benchmarks ---\n479: # SKILL_BENCH_CODEX_MODEL=gpt-6-luna    # Codex model for benchmark dispatches\n480: # SKILL_BENCH_CODEX_EFFORT=xhigh        # Reasoning effort for benchmark dispatches\n481: # SKILL_BENCH_CODEX_TIER=fast           # Service tier for benchmark dispatches\n482: # SKILL_BENCH_CODEX_SANDBOX=read-only   # Sandbox for benchmark dispatches\n483: # SKILL_BENCH_CODEX_TIMEOUT_MS=480000   # Timeout for one benchmark dispatch\n484: \n485: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n486: # 14. CROSS-AI CLI DISPATCH  (external CLI orchestration)\n487: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n488: \n489: # Overrides for delegating to external coding CLIs. Most CLIs use OAuth; the\n490: # credential vars below are optional headless/API overrides.\n491: # For a dispatched child that must not inherit an enforced spec gate, pair\n492: # SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_ENFORCE=0 with AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 (see Section 5).\n493: \n494: # --- Pi ---\n495: # PI_BIN=pi                             # Pi CLI binary path override\n496: # PI_CACHE_RETENTION=                   # Pi cache retention setting (unset by default)\n497: \n498: # --- Claude Code ---\n499: # CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR=                   # Claude Code project root; Claude Code sets it for hooks, which fall back to the payload cwd\n500: \n501: # --- OpenCode CLI ---\n502: # OPENCODE_BIN=                         # OpenCode CLI binary path override\n503: # OPENCODE_DIR=                         # OpenCode config/project directory override\n504: # OPENCODE_API_KEY=                     # Optional OpenCode headless API key (unset by default)\n505: \n506: # --- Devin CLI ---\n507: # DEVIN_PROJECT_DIR=                    # Devin project root directory override\n508: # DEVIN_API_KEY=                        # Optional Devin headless API key (unset by default)\n509: \n510: # --- Cursor CLI ---\n511: # CURSOR_AUTH_TOKEN=                    # Cursor headless auth token (unset by default)\n512: # CURSOR_API_ENDPOINT=                  # Override the Cursor API endpoint (default api2.cursor.sh)\n513: \n514: # --- Codex CLI ---\n515: # CODEX_PROJECT_DIR=                    # Codex project root directory override\n516: \n517: # --- DeepSeek Harness (dsh) dispatch ---\n518: # LLMGATEWAY_API_KEY=                   # Key the dsh LLM Gateway route patch names (export it, never commit a value)\n519: # DSH_HOME=                             # Set per dispatch to a fresh mktemp -d folder, never shared and never set here\n520: \n521: # --- Mistral Vibe dispatch ---\n522: # MISTRAL_API_KEY=                      # Prefer the Vibe sign-in key from the keychain, which bills the Vibe budget (export it, never commit a value)\n523: # VIBE_HOME=                            # Vibe home override; fan-out lineages set their own, so never set it here\n524: # VIBE_SKILLS_SOURCE_DIR=               # Skills the Vibe skill sync links (.skilled/skills)\n525: # VIBE_SKILLS_OUTPUT_DIR=               # Where the Vibe skill links go (.vibe/skills)\n526: # VIBE_COMMANDS_SOURCE_DIR=             # Commands the Vibe prompt sync reads (.skilled/commands)\n527: # VIBE_PROMPTS_OUTPUT_DIR=              # Where the Vibe prompt stubs go (.vibe/prompts)\n528: # VIBE_AGENTS_SOURCE_DIR=               # Agents the Vibe profile sync reads (.skilled/agents)\n529: # VIBE_AGENTS_OUTPUT_DIR=               # Where the Vibe agent profiles go (.vibe/agents)\n530: \n531: # --- DeepSeek Harness (dsh) mirror sync ---\n532: # DSH_SKILLS_SOURCE_DIR=                # Skills the dsh skill sync links (.skilled/skills)\n533: # DSH_SKILLS_OUTPUT_DIR=                # Where the dsh skill links go (.dsh/skills)\n534: # DSH_COMMANDS_SOURCE_DIR=              # Commands the dsh prompt sync reads (.skilled/commands)\n535: # DSH_PROMPTS_OUTPUT_DIR=               # Where the dsh prompt stubs go (.dsh/prompts)\n536: # DSH_AGENTS_SOURCE_DIR=                # Agents the dsh persona sync reads (.skilled/agents)\n537: # DSH_AGENTS_OUTPUT_DIR=                # Where the dsh persona patches go (.dsh/agents)\n538: \n539: # --- Other skills ---\n540: # SK_CODE_DIR=                          # Override the sk-code skill directory\n541: # SK_DESIGN_STYLE_DB_MODE=              # sk-design style-DB backend mode (e.g. legacy)\n542: \n543: # --- Manual testing playbook conversation runner ---\n544: # CONVERSATION_WATCH=decision-capture   # Comma list of .skilled/skills/.state subfolders the repository snapshot watches\n545: # CONVERSATION_CHECK_TIMEOUT_MS=60000   # Time limit for each turn's check command\n546: # CODEX_HOME=                           # Codex home (~/.codex): the runner's hook-trust step reads and restores its config.toml, and the decision-capture Codex sweep finds session files under its sessions/\n547: # TMUX_TMPDIR=                          # Parent of the tmux-<uid> folder where the runner looks for its private sockets (/tmp)\n548: \n549: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n550: # 16. SK-GIT & LIVE-SYNC\n551: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n552: \n553: # Preflight advisories, git-hook bypasses, and the continuous-integration loop.\n554: \n555: # --- Preflight advisory suppression ---\n556: # SKGIT_ADVISORY=                       # Set 0 to disable all sk-git preflight advisories\n557: # SKGIT_ADVISORY_SKIP=                  # Suppress one rule id, or a family prefix (e.g. commit)\n558: \n559: # --- Git-hook bypasses (use only when a hook is genuinely wrong) ---\n560: # Each one lasts one command and is read from the environment only. Every block\n561: # message names its own. SYSTEM_GIT_COMMIT_HOOKS_DISABLED (Section 8) turns off\n562: # every pre-commit gate, the agent mirror gate included, which has no switch of its own.\n563: # SPECKIT_SKIP_COMMENT_HYGIENE=         # Skip the pre-commit comment-hygiene gate (set 1)\n564: # SPECKIT_SKIP_PHRASE_LINT=             # Skip the pre-commit template phrase lint gate (set 1)\n565: # SPECKIT_SKIP_MIRROR_PARITY=           # Skip the pre-commit mirror-parity gate (set 1)\n566: # SPECKIT_SKIP_CARD_SYNC=               # Skip the pre-commit prompt-card sync gate (set 1)\n567: # SPECKIT_SKIP_MCP_MUTATION_CLASS=      # Skip the pre-commit MCP mutation-class gate (set 1)\n568: # SPECKIT_SKIP_ROUTE_REMINT=            # Skip the pre-commit compiled-routing re-mint (set 1)\n569: # SPECKIT_SKIP_CONTRACT_RECOMPILE=      # Skip the pre-commit deep command contract recompile (set 1)\n570: # SPECKIT_SKIP_SPEC_REMINT=             # Skip the pre-commit spec metadata re-mint (set 1)\n571: # SPECKIT_SKIP_PREPARE_COMMIT_MSG=      # Skip the Commit-Id and Spec: stamper, which never blocks (set 1)\n572: # SPECKIT_COMMIT_SPEC=                  # Packet the stamper writes as the Spec: trailer of a single commit (<track>/<packet>[/<phase>])\n573: # SPECKIT_ALLOW_REMOTE_PUSH=            # Allow ONE push to a non-allowlisted branch (1 updates it, the branch name creates it)\n574: # SPECKIT_SKIP_PREPUSH_SKILL_GATE=      # Skip the pre-push skill-root-metadata gate (set 1)\n575: # SPECKIT_SKIP_PREPUSH_ROUTE_GATE=      # Skip the pre-push compiled-routing gate (set 1)\n576: # SPECKIT_SKIP_PREPUSH_TRACK_GATE=      # Skip the pre-push track-root children_ids gate (set 1)\n577: # SPECKIT_ALLOW_MASS_DELETION=          # Allow a push past the mass-deletion ceiling (set 1)\n578: # SPECKIT_MASS_DELETION_THRESHOLD=100   # Tracked files a push may delete before the ceiling blocks it\n579: \n580: # --- Worktrees ---\n581: # SPECKIT_WORKTREE_BASE=                # Relocate worktrees out of the checkout (default .worktrees)\n582: # SPECKIT_WORKTREE_SHARED_PATHS=        # Extra relative paths symlinked into each wrapper worktree\n583: # SPECKIT_WORKTREE_GUARD=               # Set off to silence the shared-checkout worktree warning\n584: # SPECKIT_GIT_TIMEOUT=20                # Seconds one index-reading git call may take in the git hooks, the launcher and the worktree reaper\n585: # SPECKIT_WORKTREE_ADD_TIMEOUT=60        # Seconds the launcher gives git worktree add before it fails the launch\n586: # SPECKIT_FSMON_REAPER=                 # Override the fsmonitor daemon reaper script path\n587: # SPECKIT_WORKTREE_AUTOREAP=1            # Set 0 to stop the session-start sweep that removes merged, idle numbered worktrees (once per 6 hours)\n588: # SPECKIT_WORKTREE_REAPER=              # Override the worktree reaper script path the session-start sweep runs\n589: # FSMON_PROBE_TIMEOUT=15                # Seconds the reaper waits on one git or lsof call\n590: # FSMON_STOP_TIMEOUT=5                  # Seconds the reaper gives git's own daemon stop\n591: # FSMON_TERM_WAIT=5                     # Seconds the reaper waits after SIGTERM before SIGKILL\n592: # FSMON_KILL_WAIT=3                     # Seconds the reaper waits for a daemon to exit after SIGKILL\n593: # SPECKIT_GIT_HOOKS_GUARD=on            # Git-hooks install warning + self-heal (set off to silence)\n594: \n595: # --- Continuous-integration live sync ---\n596: # SYSTEM_LIVE_SYNC_DISABLED=            # Master switch for the whole live-sync loop\n597: # SYSTEM_PRIMARY_RECONCILE_DISABLED=    # Disable SessionStart reconcile of the primary checkout\n598: # SYSTEM_LIVE_FOLLOW_DISABLED=          # Disable the IDE checkout follower auto-start\n599: # SPECKIT_AUTOSYNC=                     # Per-launch publish opt-out (wrapper sessions export 1)\n600: # SPECKIT_LIVE_BRANCH=                  # The live branch a wrapper session publishes to\n601: # SPECKIT_LIVE_REMOTE=origin            # Remote used by the live-sync scripts\n602: # SPECKIT_SYNC_RETRIES=3                # Push-race retries in the publish loop\n603: # SPECKIT_PRIMARY_RECONCILE_TIMEOUT=12  # Network timeout (s) for the SessionStart reconcile\n604: # SPECKIT_PRIMARY_RECONCILE_LOCK_TTL=45 # Stale-lock TTL (s) for the reconcile single-flight\n605: # SPECKIT_DIST_AUTO_REBUILD=            # Controls dist rebuild after a freshness check (NOT a disable flag)\n606: # LIVE_FOLLOW_MANAGED_LOG=0             # 1 = the IDE follower rotates its own log (the auto-start sets it)\n607: # LIVE_FOLLOW_LOG_MAX_BYTES=262144      # Size at which a managed follower log rotates\n608: # GATE_REGISTRY=                        # Override the git-hook gate registry path\n609: \n610: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n611: # 17. JEV CLASSIFIER FEATURES  (on when a Jev credential is stored)\n612: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n613: \n614: # Each feature below asks Typesafe's Jev classifier one measured question and\n615: # runs on its own once `jev` is on PATH and `jev auth status --provider official`\n616: # passes (store the key once with `jev auth set --provider official`). No key,\n617: # no call: without a credential every path behaves as if these lines were absent.\n618: # Set a switch to 0/false/no/off to turn it off. Read from the environment, then\n619: # from .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env, so a saved switch holds across sessions.\n620: # JEV_FEATURES=                         # Master switch: 0 turns every Jev feature off\n621: # JEV_FEATURE_CITE_DRIFT=               # Citation drift advisory in validate_document.py (older name: SKDOC_CITE_DRIFT_CHECK)\n622: # JEV_FEATURE_INJECTION_SCREEN=         # fetched-text screen for instructions aimed at an AI agent (Claude Code, Devin, OpenCode, Pi)\n623: # JEV_PROVIDER=official                 # Jev provider every feature asks (official or openrouter)\n624: # JEV_TRANSPORT=                        # Set jev to skip Pi's classifier and always use the jev CLI\n625: \n626: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n627: # 18. SESSION HANDOVER  (session handover under skilled-loop)\n628: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n629: \n630: # The threshold and window apply to every session; outside skilled-loop the nudge asks\n631: # only for a note. The hop and age limits apply inside the loop. The loop ships on for Claude Code\n632: # and off on every other runtime. SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED (Section 8, also read from\n633: # hook-flags.env) set to 1 turns it on everywhere and set to 0 turns it off everywhere, and a\n634: # non-empty SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_<RUNTIME>_ENABLED (Section 8) overrides it for one runtime, so\n635: # ENABLED=1 with CLAUDE_ENABLED=0 is on everywhere except Claude Code. SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_DISABLED=1\n636: # turns it off and wins over every enable flag. While it is off, /speckit:handoff refuses and\n637: # auto-compaction stays the fallback. The loop itself sets SKILLED_LOOP_* for each session, so never set those. The one exception is SKILLED_LOOP_TRUSTED_CHECKOUTS below, which only an operator sets.\n638: # SESSION_HANDOVER_THRESHOLD=0.80       # Context fill that triggers the handoff nudge\n639: # SESSION_HANDOVER_WINDOW_TOKENS=       # Context window to measure against (autoCompactWindow, then 1M for a [1m] model, else unknown and no nudge)\n640: # SESSION_HANDOVER_MAX_HOPS=10          # Max hops in one loop before relaunch stops\n641: # SESSION_HANDOVER_MAX_AGE_MIN=10       # Max age of an armed record the wrapper still relaunches\n642: # SESSION_HANDOVER_NOTIFY_HOPS=         # macOS notice on each hand-over (off; also read from hook-flags.env)\n643: # SKILLED_LOOP_TRUSTED_CHECKOUTS=       # Extra checkouts whose wrapper the shell shim may run (colon-separated absolute paths)\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 644]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .env.example, lines 1-643\n1: # =============================================================================\n2: # .env.example  —  Environment variable template\n3: # =============================================================================\n4: #\n5: # CONVENTIONS\n6: #   - Every variable here is OPTIONAL except the Code Mode provider secrets in\n7: #     Section 1. The system runs on sensible defaults when nothing is set.\n8: #   - Non-secret lines are COMMENTED and show the DEFAULT value. Uncomment the\n9: #     line and change the value to override that default.\n10: #   - Flag semantics:\n11: #       Graduated ON  = enabled by default; set  false  to DISABLE.\n12: #       Opt-in OFF    = disabled by default; set  true   to ENABLE.\n13: #   - A default shown as empty means \"unset by default\":  # VAR=    # ...\n14: #   - Booleans accept  1/true/yes/on  (and their negatives) unless noted.\n15: #\n16: # WHERE THESE ARE READ\n17: #   Code Mode loads a filled-in .env for its provider secrets (Section 1), and\n18: #   nothing else in this repository loads it. Hooks, validators and git hooks\n19: #   read the process environment. The validation off switches in Section 5, the\n20: #   hook kill-switches in Section 8 and the Jev feature switches in Section 17\n21: #   also read .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env, where a saved switch stays on until\n22: #   a set environment value overrides it. A switch written only in .env counts\n23: #   where your shell or runtime exports it.\n24: #\n25: # SETTING ONE LOCALLY\n26: #   This file is a template: no reader loads its values. Copy a line to where its\n27: #   reader looks, uncomment it and change the value:\n28: #     - export NAME=value in ~/.zshrc or ~/.bashrc works for every setting and wins\n29: #       over hook-flags.env\n30: #     - .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env (copy hook-flags.env.example) for the hook,\n31: #       validation and Jev switches, SESSION_HANDOVER_NOTIFY_HOPS and SESSION_HANDOVER_GOAL\n32: #     - .claude/settings.local.json, env block, for Claude Code sessions only\n33: #     - .env (copy this file) only for the Code Mode keys in Section 1\n34: #   ENV_SECRET_GUARD_PEPPER (Section 8) is the exception: export it in your shell\n35: #   profile only, never in any of the files above.\n36: #   All four are gitignored. /doctor:env list shows every setting and where it is\n37: #   set, by name only; /doctor:env NAME saves one after showing the exact line.\n38: #\n39: # EXHAUSTIVE REFERENCE\n40: #   The full, source-generated SPECKIT_* feature-flag reference (types, read\n41: #   sites, rollout notes) lives in:\n42: #     .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md\n43: #   This file is a practical template; that document is authoritative.\n44: #\n45: # =============================================================================\n46: \n47: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n48: # 1. CODE MODE — MCP PROVIDER SECRETS  (fill these in)\n49: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n50: \n51: # These are the ONLY required values. Leave blank to disable a provider.\n52: # Code Mode resolves a manual's bare ${VAR} reference as {manual_name}_{VAR},\n53: # and DOUBLES every underscore in the manual name: a manual called\n54: # my_manual looking up ${API_KEY} needs my__manual_API_KEY.\n55: # A key under any other spelling is simply not found, and the manual fails to\n56: # register at server startup with no runtime symptom beyond a shorter tool list.\n57: # Never commit a filled-in .env — keep secrets out of version control.\n58: \n59: # GitHub  (github_GITHUB_TOKEN is an accepted alias)\n60: github_GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN=\n61: \n62: # ClickUp needs no key here: the clickup_official manual signs in with OAuth on first launch\n63: \n64: # Notion MCP\n65: notion_NOTION_TOKEN=\n66: \n67: # Obsidian  (Local REST API plugin: key + base URL + SSL verify toggle)\n68: obsidian_OBSIDIAN_API_KEY=\n69: obsidian_OBSIDIAN_VERIFY_SSL=\n70: obsidian_OBSIDIAN_BASE_URL=\n71: \n72: # Figma\n73: figma_FIGMA_API_KEY=\n74: \n75: # Webflow\n76: webflow_WEBFLOW_TOKEN=\n77: \n78: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n79: # 2. SPEC KIT ENGINE — PATHS, IPC & PREFLIGHT\n80: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n81: \n82: # Paths, shared IPC, lease and preflight controls for the spec-kit engine and the shared launchers.\n83: #\n84: # OWNERSHIP MARKERS\n85: #   Rows here and in Section 7 carry an ownership marker naming their owner: the HF model\n86: #   server and the skill advisor share the launcher, IPC and embedding rows. A marker governs\n87: #   the contiguous run of rows beneath it, up to the next blank line. An UNMARKED row belongs\n88: #   to the spec-kit engine itself.\n89: \n90: # --- Database & workspace paths ---\n91: # SPECKIT_SPECS_DIR=         # Override the specs root (auto-detected)\n92: # SPEC_KIT_SPECS_DIR=        # Alias for the specs root override\n93: # SPECKIT_TEMPLATES_BASE=    # Override the spec-doc templates directory (bundled default)\n94: # SPECKIT_RG_BIN=            # Path to the ripgrep binary for retrieval (default: rg on PATH)\n95: # SPEC_KIT_DB_DIR=           # Spec-kit database directory (alias SPECKIT_DB_DIR; auto)\n96: # MEMORY_DB_PATH=            # Explicit database file path; wins over the directory\n97: # MEMORY_BASE_PATH=          # Base path spec-kit resolves workspace files against (current directory)\n98: \n99: # --- Launcher, daemon & IPC ---\n100: # shared: owned by the HF model server and the skill advisor\n101: # SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_BRIDGE_DISABLED=false # Force legacy strict-single-writer (no IPC bridge)\n102: # SPECKIT_MAX_SECONDARY_CLIENTS=64      # Max concurrent secondary stdio clients on the IPC socket\n103: # SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MIN=30  # Idle self-exit timeout (min); 0 disables the monitor\n104: # SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR=               # Override daemon IPC socket dir (REQUIRED short path on macOS)\n105: # SPECKIT_PROXY_COLD_START_ATTEMPTS=30  # Connect attempts while a cold launcher backend comes up\n106: # SPECKIT_PS_PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS=2000      # Timeout for the process-table probe that checks daemons\n107: \n108: # shared: owned by the HF model server and the skill advisor\n109: # SPECKIT_LEASE_PROBE_RETRIES=1         # Consecutive failed liveness probes before reaping the lease owner\n110: # SPECKIT_LEASE_PROBE_RETRY_TIMEOUT_MS=1500 # Per-attempt timeout for each lease retry probe\n111: # SPECKIT_LEASE_PROBE_RETRY_BACKOFF_MS=250  # Backoff between lease liveness-probe attempts\n112: \n113: # SPECKIT_STOP_HOOK_ORPHAN_SWEEP=off    # Stop-hook orphan sweep: off / dry-run / live\n114: \n115: # --- Boot, validation & preflight ---\n116: # SPECKIT_FRONTMATTER_ALLOWLIST=        # Override path to the frontmatter grandfather allowlist JSON\n117: # SPECKIT_VERBOSE_RESOLVER=false        # Log the cause when the level-contract resolver falls back\n118: # SPECKIT_PYTHON_BIN=                   # Python interpreter for spec-kit scripts (auto)\n119: # SPEC_KIT_PLUGIN_NODE_BINARY=          # Node binary for the spec-kit plugin (auto)\n120: \n121: # shared: owned by the HF model server and the skill advisor\n122: # SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_SCOPE=             # IPC socket scope selector (internal default)\n123: # SPECKIT_BRIDGE_RESPAWN_DISABLED=      # Disable launcher IPC-bridge respawn (set 1)\n124: \n125: # --- Launcher RSS watchdog & crash loop ---\n126: # shared: owned by the HF model server and the skill advisor\n127: # SPECKIT_CONTEXT_SERVER_MAX_RSS_MB=    # RSS ceiling (MB) for the default launcher watchdog (unset=off)\n128: # SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_RSS_SELF_EXIT=       # Recycle on an RSS breach (set 1, with a MAX_RSS_MB value)\n129: # SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_RSS_WATCHDOG_INTERVAL_MS=15000 # How often the watchdog samples RSS\n130: # SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_RSS_CONSECUTIVE_BREACHES=3 # Breaching samples in a row before a recycle\n131: # SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_RSS_GRACE_MS=7000    # Wait before a recycled process is force-killed\n132: # SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_CRASH_LOOP_MAX_DEATHS=3 # Deaths within the window before the launcher gives up\n133: # SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_CRASH_LOOP_WINDOW_MS=60000 # Window the crash-loop guard counts deaths in\n134: # SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_CRASH_LOOP_INITIAL_BACKOFF_MS=250 # First restart backoff after a death\n135: # SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_CRASH_LOOP_MAX_BACKOFF_MS=5000 # Restart backoff ceiling\n136: \n137: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n138: # 3. SHARED RANKING ALGORITHMS\n139: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n140: # Read by shared/algorithms/rrf-fusion.ts, whose only live consumer is the skill\n141: # advisor's fusion scorer. Spec-kit retrieval is lexical and reads none of these.\n142: \n143: # SPECKIT_RRF=true                      # Master switch for Reciprocal Rank Fusion (graduated ON)\n144: # SPECKIT_RRF_K=40                      # RRF smoothing constant k (>0; lower = more top-heavy)\n145: # SPECKIT_RETRIEVAL_PROFILE_WEIGHTS=    # Override per-profile retrieval weights (JSON)\n146: \n147: # SPECKIT_SCORE_NORMALIZATION=true      # Composite score normalization (graduated ON)\n148: # SPECKIT_CALIBRATED_OVERLAP_BONUS=true # Overlap bonus for multi-channel convergence (graduated ON)\n149: \n150: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n151: # 4. SPEC KIT ENGINE — DISCOVERY & COMPILED ROUTING\n152: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n153: \n154: # SPECKIT_FOLDER_DISCOVERY_TOKEN_THRESHOLD=0.45 # Per-token similarity threshold for folder-name matching\n155: # SPECKIT_DESCRIPTION_REPAIR_MERGE_SAFE=true # Merge-safe description repair during discovery (graduated ON)\n156: \n157: # --- Compiled routing ---\n158: # SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING=             # Serve compiled per-hub router: unset=default cohort, 1=force, 0=kill\n159: # SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING_DEBUG=       # Emit stderr breadcrumbs when a compiled route falls back to legacy\n160: \n161: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n162: # 5. SPEC KIT ENGINE — VALIDATION, SPEC GATE & GENERATED METADATA\n163: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n164: \n165: # --- Validation off switches (1/true/yes/on; also read from .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env, a set env var wins) ---\n166: # SPECKIT_SKIP_VALIDATION=              # Switch spec folder validation (validate.sh) off. CI never sets it\n167: # SKDOC_SKIP_VALIDATION=                # Switch every sk-doc format validator off. CI never sets it\n168: \n169: # SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE=true              # Advisory acceptance-criteria coverage scan (graduated ON)\n170: # SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE_FLOOR=0.9         # Min covered acceptance-criteria ratio for the advisory scan\n171: # SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE_ENFORCE=false     # Fail the rule instead of advising when coverage is under the floor (opt-in)\n172: # SPECKIT_AUTHORED_CONTINUITY_SNAPSHOT=false # Compact-hook authored continuity snapshot path (opt-in)\n173: # SPECKIT_COMPLETION_FRESHNESS=false    # Strict-only completion-freshness validation rule (opt-in)\n174: # SPECKIT_COMPLETION_FRESHNESS_ENFORCE=false # Promote stale freshness findings from warning to error\n175: # SPECKIT_ENTITY_CONFIG_PATH=           # Override path to the entity-extraction rules JSON (built-in default)\n176: \n177: # --- validate.sh options and rule cutoffs ---\n178: # SPECKIT_STRICT=                       # true = same as --strict\n179: # SPECKIT_VERBOSE=                      # true = same as --verbose\n180: # SPECKIT_JSON=                         # true = same as --json\n181: # SPECKIT_QUIET=                        # true = same as --quiet\n182: # SPECKIT_RULES=                        # Comma-separated subset of rules to run\n183: # SPECKIT_DRAFT_AUTO_REPAIR=true        # Graduated ON: a strict full-rule validate on a Draft packet repairs derived metadata once; 0/false/off keeps it read-only\n184: # SPECKIT_VALIDATION=                   # false switches validate.sh off (older form of SPECKIT_SKIP_VALIDATION)\n185: # SPECKIT_POST_VALIDATE=                # 1 = create.sh validates a folder right after scaffolding it\n186: # SKIP_TEMPLATE_CHECK=                  # 1 = the frontmatter rule skips its template-source check\n187: # SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE=true               # Acceptance-criteria closure rule (graduated ON)\n188: # SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE_CUTOFF=2026-08-30  # Packets created before this date stay advisory for closure\n189: # SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE_CUTOFF=2026-08-30 # Packets created before this date stay advisory for coverage\n190: # SPECKIT_SOURCE_TAG_CUTOFF=2026-10-04  # Packets created on or before this date skip SOURCE_TAGS\n191: # SPECKIT_CANONICAL_SAVE_CUTOFF=2026-05-01T00:00:00Z # Packets older than this skip canonical-save checks\n192: # SPECKIT_CANONICAL_SAVE_FRESHNESS_SLACK_MS=600000 # Slack between description and graph freshness\n193: \n194: # --- Spec Gate (Gate-3) + child dispatch ---\n195: # SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_ENFORCE=             # Opt-in deny mode for a mutation with no resolved spec folder\n196: # SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED=            # Fail-open no-op: no question, no denial, no state writes\n197: # SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_3_DELIVERY_SUPPRESSION= # Suppression is default-on; set 0/false/no/off to re-ask at every in-gate mutation\n198: # AI_SESSION_CHILD=                     # Mark a dispatched sub-session (1) so Gate-3 is a no-op\n199: # SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER=                   # Bind the session's spec folder up front so Gate-3 is answered\n200: # SPECIFY_FEATURE=                      # Name the target packet for the spec scripts directly\n201: # AUTO_SAVE_MODE=                       # true = spec-folder detection never prompts\n202: # SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_ACTIVE_RETENTION_DAYS=2 # Age before an untouched spec-gate state file is swept\n203: # SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_ARCHIVE_RETENTION_DAYS=90 # Retention before an archived spec-gate file is pruned\n204: # SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_SWEEP_INTERVAL_MS=3600000 # Min interval between spec-gate state sweeps\n205: # SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_WARNING_LOG_MAX_BYTES=262144 # Size at which the spec-gate warning log rotates\n206: \n207: # --- Generated-metadata integrity & data quality ---\n208: # SPECKIT_GENERATOR_HARDENING=true      # Fingerprint + phase-parent + telemetry hardening (graduated ON)\n209: # SPECKIT_GENERATED_METADATA_GRANDFATHER=false # Report mode for the metadata-integrity rule (default enforces)\n210: # SPECKIT_STATUS_COMPLETION_CONSISTENCY_GATE=false # Cross-check derived complete status (report mode)\n211: # SPECKIT_IDENTITY_MERGE_SAFETY=true    # Shared identity resolver + lineage-merge guard (graduated ON)\n212: # SPECKIT_GENERATED_METADATA_DRIFT_GATE=true # Synopsis drift gate + shared-extractor routing (graduated ON)\n213: # SPECKIT_GENERATED_METADATA_Z_EXCLUSION=true # Exclude z-future staging dirs from folder discovery; z_archive stays in (graduated ON)\n214: # SPECKIT_IDEMPOTENT_DESCRIPTION_WRITES=true # Content-gated description.json / cache writes (graduated ON)\n215: # SPECKIT_METADATA_DISK_CONSISTENCY_ENFORCE=true # Fail strict on metadata/on-disk path mismatch (enforcing)\n216: # SPECKIT_STATUS_CROSS_DOC_ENFORCE=true # Fail strict on spec.md vs implementation-summary status drift (enforcing)\n217: # SPECKIT_CHILD_DRIFT_ENFORCE=true      # Fail strict on phase-parent children_ids drift (enforcing)\n218: # SPECKIT_VALIDATE_SCRIPT=              # Override the validate.sh path the freshness sweep invokes\n219: \n220: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n221: # 6. SPEC KIT ENGINE — TELEMETRY & INDEXING\n222: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n223: \n224: # SPECKIT_METRICS_ENABLED=              # Enable advisor/metrics emission (set true)\n225: \n226: # SPECKIT_INDEX_SPEC_DOCS=true          # Spec-document discovery for metadata and the spec-root registry (set false to return no documents)\n227: \n228: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n229: # 7. EMBEDDING + LOCAL HF MODEL SERVER\n230: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n231: \n232: # Provider cascade (local-first): Ollama -> hf-local -> OpenAI -> Voyage.\n233: \n234: # --- Provider selection ---\n235: # shared: owned by the HF model server and the skill advisor\n236: # EMBEDDINGS_PROVIDER=auto              # Provider: auto (cascade) or force a specific provider\n237: # OLLAMA_EMBEDDINGS_MODEL=nomic-embed-text-v1.5 # Ollama embedding model (local default)\n238: # HF_EMBEDDINGS_MODEL=nomic-ai/nomic-embed-text-v1.5 # Local HF model (single resident model)\n239: # HF_EMBEDDINGS_DTYPE=                  # HF model dtype override (e.g. q8/fp16)\n240: # OPENAI_API_KEY=                       # Enables OpenAI text-embedding-3-small in the cascade\n241: # VOYAGE_API_KEY=                       # Enables Voyage voyage-code-3 in the cascade\n242: # EMBEDDING_DIM=                        # Explicit embedding-dimension override (derived by default)\n243: # HF_EMBEDDINGS_PREFIX_QUERY=           # Override the local HF query prefix (registry default)\n244: # HF_EMBEDDINGS_PREFIX_DOC=             # Override the local HF document prefix (registry default)\n245: # OLLAMA_BASE_URL=                      # Ollama origin (local daemon by default)\n246: # OLLAMA_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=            # Pin every Ollama request to one deadline (adaptive by default)\n247: # OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1 # OpenAI-compatible endpoint for embeddings\n248: # OPENAI_EMBEDDINGS_MODEL=              # OpenAI embedding model (text-embedding-3-small)\n249: # VOYAGE_BASE_URL=                      # Voyage endpoint override\n250: # VOYAGE_EMBEDDINGS_MODEL=              # Voyage embedding model (voyage-code-3)\n251: \n252: # --- Local HF model server ---\n253: # shared: owned by the HF model server and the skill advisor\n254: # HF_EMBED_SERVER_URL=                  # Model-server endpoint (unix path / unix:// / tcp://; default socket)\n255: # HF_EMBED_SERVER_READY_TIMEOUT_MS=45000 # Initial readiness budget waiting for the model server\n256: # SPECKIT_HF_MODEL_SERVER_MAX_RSS_MB=   # RSS ceiling (MB) for the supervised model-server tree (unset=off)\n257: # SPECKIT_HF_MODEL_SERVER_RSS_SELF_EXIT= # Recycle model server on an RSS breach (set 1, with MAX_RSS_MB)\n258: # SPECKIT_HF_MODEL_SERVER_LOADING_MAX_MS=150000 # Max age for one model-server load attempt\n259: # SPECKIT_HF_MODEL_SERVER_GIVEUP_COOLDOWN_MS=60000 # Cooldown after crash-loop give-up\n260: # SPECKIT_HF_MODEL_SERVER_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MIN=10 # Evict idle resident model server after N min (0=keep warm)\n261: # SPECKIT_HF_MODEL_SERVER_ORPHAN_REAP=0 # Disable orphan reap when another init system owns the shared socket\n262: # SPECKIT_HF_READY_LATCH_TTL_MS=30000   # How long a successful readiness check is trusted (max 120000)\n263: # HF_EMBED_ALLOW_REMOTE_BIND=           # 1 = allow a TCP bind beyond localhost (needs HF_EMBED_AUTH_TOKEN)\n264: # HF_EMBED_AUTH_TOKEN=                  # Token a remote client must send to the model server\n265: \n266: # shared: owned by the HF model server and the skill advisor\n267: # SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_MODEL_SERVER_ENABLED= # Skill-advisor arms the shared model-server spawn by default; set 0 to turn it off\n268: \n269: # --- Cascade probe timing ---\n270: # shared: owned by the HF model server and the skill advisor\n271: # SPECKIT_CASCADE_PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS=2500 # Per-provider HTTP probe timeout for auto-select\n272: # SPECKIT_CASCADE_LOCK_STALE_MS=30000   # Staleness threshold for the auto-select advisory lock\n273: # SPECKIT_CASCADE_SLEEP_MS=25           # Polling sleep while waiting for the auto-select lock\n274: \n275: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n276: # 8. HOOK KILL-SWITCHES  (default enabled, session handover only on Claude Code, user-hook sync off, set truthy to DISABLE)\n277: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n278: \n279: # May also be set in .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env (a real env var wins).\n280: \n281: # HOOK_FLAGS_CONFIG=                    # Override the hook-flags config file path\n282: # SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED=                # Master switch for every hook concern below\n283: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=        # Disable skill-advisor injection\n284: # SYSTEM_COMPLETION_DISABLED=           # Disable completion-evidence warnings\n285: # SYSTEM_DIRECTIVE_LIFECYCLE_DISABLED=  # Disable directive lifecycle boundary handling\n286: # SYSTEM_DISPATCH_DISABLED=             # Disable dispatch preflight and audit hooks\n287: # CLI_DISPATCH_AUDIT_DISABLED=          # Disable the dispatch audit trail only (canonical name)\n288: # SYSTEM_DISPATCH_GUARD_DISABLED=       # Disable the dispatch preflight guard only\n289: # SYSTEM_INJECTION_SCREEN_DISABLED=     # Disable the fetched-web-text injection screen\n290: # SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED=      # Session handover loop on every runtime when 1, off everywhere when 0 (context nudge, stop arm, compact pointer)\n291: # Unset, the loop is on for Claude Code and off on every other runtime.\n292: # Per-runtime overrides: a non-empty value (1 on, 0 off) beats SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED for that\n293: # runtime, and empty or unset falls back to it. DISABLED and SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED still beat every enable flag.\n294: # SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_CLAUDE_ENABLED=    # Claude Code\n295: # SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_CODEX_ENABLED=     # Codex\n296: # SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_PI_ENABLED=        # Pi\n297: # SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_OPENCODE_ENABLED=  # OpenCode\n298: # SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_CURSOR_ENABLED=    # Cursor\n299: # SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_DEVIN_ENABLED=     # Devin\n300: # SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_VIBE_ENABLED=      # Mistral Vibe\n301: # SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_DISABLED=     # Turn the session-handover loop off, wins over every enable flag above\n302: # Claude user-hook sync, off by default: at each Claude Code session start in a primary checkout, copy\n303: # this checkout's Claude hooks into ~/.claude/settings.json, keeping every other key and hook. Set it in\n304: # the hook-flags.env of the checkout that should own the copy; an env var turns it on for every checkout.\n305: # SYSTEM_CLAUDE_USER_HOOK_SYNC_ENABLED=  # Turn the sync on (set 1); a backup is kept as settings.json.pre-skilled-hook-sync\n306: # SYSTEM_CLAUDE_USER_HOOK_SYNC_DISABLED= # Stop the sync, wins over its enable flag\n307: # SYSTEM_TASK_DISPATCH_DISABLED=        # Disable task-dispatch warnings and denials\n308: # SYSTEM_DECISION_CAPTURE_DISABLED=     # Disable decision capture: no answer is queued for the next save\n309: # SYSTEM_ASK_SURFACE_DISABLED=         # Disable the ask-surface guard: a typed option menu is never sent back\n310: # SYSTEM_ENV_SECRET_GUARD_DISABLED=     # Disable the dotenv guard. Read from the shell environment only: a line in hook-flags.env or .env does nothing\n311: # SYSTEM_OVERLAY_GUARD_DISABLED=        # Disable the vendored-overlay edit guard\n312: # SYSTEM_PERMISSION_POLICY_DISABLED=    # Disable Devin permission-policy decisions\n313: # SK_CODE_POST_EDIT_QUALITY_DISABLED=   # Disable post-edit quality warnings\n314: # MCP_ROUTE_GUARD_DISABLED=             # Disable MCP route warnings and audit records\n315: # OPENCODE_GOAL_DISABLED=               # Disable goal injection and tools (alias OPENCODE_GOAL_PLUGIN_DISABLED)\n316: # SK_GIT_PREFLIGHT_DISABLED=            # Disable git-preflight advisories\n317: # CODEX_WATCHDOG_DISABLED=              # Disable Codex hook-drift warnings\n318: # SYSTEM_SESSION_LIFECYCLE_DISABLED=    # Disable session-start/stop/compaction hook handling\n319: # SYSTEM_SESSION_CLEANUP_DISABLED=      # Disable session cleanup and teardown\n320: # SYSTEM_HOOK_INSTALL_DISABLED=         # Disable Codex hook installation and check mode\n321: # SYSTEM_DIST_FRESHNESS_DISABLED=       # Disable dist-freshness checks\n322: # SYSTEM_GIT_WORKTREE_GUARD_DISABLED=   # Disable the worktree warning\n323: # SYSTEM_GIT_HOOKS_CHECK_DISABLED=      # Disable the git-hooks installation warning\n324: # SYSTEM_GIT_COMMIT_HOOKS_DISABLED=     # Emergency-off for the pre-commit chain\n325: \n326: # ── Dotenv guard fingerprint key (unset by default) ──\n327: # The guard compares two dotenv values by an HMAC-SHA256 fingerprint and never shows either one.\n328: # Unset, the fingerprint is refused rather than computed without a key. Generate a key with\n329: # `openssl rand -base64 32` and export it from your shell profile only: never put it in .env, in\n330: # hook-flags.env or in any file inside a repository, because a key the agent can read lets it\n331: # test guesses against a fingerprint.\n332: # ENV_SECRET_GUARD_PEPPER=              # HMAC key for env_secret_fingerprint and `env-secret.cjs fingerprint`\n333: # ENV_SECRET_GUARD_WRITE_CHECK=         # restore (default): undo a dotenv write a shell call made. report: name it and leave it\n334: # ENV_SECRET_GUARD_STATE_DIR=           # Where the guard keeps its record and dotenv backups (default ~/.local/state/env-secret-guard)\n335: \n336: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n337: # 9. HOOK LIFECYCLE\n338: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n339: \n340: # SPECKIT_DIRECTIVE_LIFECYCLE_DEDUP=true # Drop constant policy on a confirmed same-epoch repeat (graduated ON)\n341: # SPECKIT_PI_DIRECTIVE_DEDUP=true       # Pi directive dedup on a proven repeat (graduated ON)\n342: # SPECKIT_DIRECTIVE_LIFECYCLE_STATE_DIR= # Override the directive-lifecycle private state root (temp default)\n343: # SPECKIT_OPENCODE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS=3000 # Timeout for the OpenCode advisor plugin bridge\n344: # SPECKIT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS=       # Timeout for the Claude advisor hook (ms)\n345: # SPECKIT_CLAUDE_CODE_STATE_DIR=        # Override the Claude Code hook state directory\n346: # SPECKIT_OPENCODE_STATE_DIR=           # Override the OpenCode hook state directory\n347: \n348: # --- Session cleanup & orphan sweeper ---\n349: # SESSION_CLEANUP_LOG_PATH=~/.local/share/session-cleanup.log # Session cleanup log (older name CLAUDE_SESSION_CLEANUP_LOG_PATH)\n350: # SESSION_CLEANUP_LOG_MAX_BYTES=10485760 # Size at which the cleanup log rotates (older name CLAUDE_SESSION_CLEANUP_LOG_MAX_BYTES)\n351: # SPECKIT_SESSION_START_ORPHAN_SWEEP=   # Sweep orphaned MCP processes at OpenCode session start (opt-in, set 1)\n352: # SPECKIT_ORPHAN_SWEEPER_BIN=           # Override the orphan sweeper script path\n353: # ORPHAN_AGE_MIN_SEC=300                # Min age before an orphaned MCP helper is swept\n354: # ORPHAN_TMP_AGE_HOURS=24               # Min age before a temporary dispatch artifact is swept\n355: # ORPHAN_TEMP_PROCESS_AGE_HOURS=6       # Min age before a parentless process from a temp or scratch folder is swept\n356: # ORPHAN_SWEEPER_LOG_PATH=~/.local/share/orphan-sweeper.log # Orphan sweeper log\n357: # ORPHAN_SWEEPER_LOG_MAX_BYTES=10485760 # Size at which the sweeper log rotates\n358: \n359: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n360: # 10. SKILL ADVISOR\n361: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n362: \n363: # Threshold / calibration overrides for the 5-lane scorer and prompt-policy.\n364: \n365: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD=0.8 # Confidence threshold for the fusion scorer (0..1)\n366: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_UNCERTAINTY_THRESHOLD=0.35 # Uncertainty ceiling for the fusion scorer (0..1)\n367: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_CALIBRATION_OVERRIDE_JSON= # Partial override for routing calibration bonuses (JSON)\n368: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_PROMPT_POLICY_PATH=   # Override the prompt-policy linguistic-sets JSON (bundled default)\n369: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_PROMPT_POLICY_MIN_VISIBLE_CHARS=15 # Min visible chars for the short-casual skip path\n370: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_PROMPT_POLICY_MEANINGFUL_TOKEN_FLOOR=3 # Min meaningful tokens for the work-intent fire rule\n371: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_PROMPT_POLICY_LENGTH_AND_TOKEN_VISIBLE_CHARS=20 # Visible-char threshold, length+token rule\n372: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_PROMPT_POLICY_LENGTH_AND_TOKEN_MEANINGFUL_FLOOR=4 # Meaningful-token threshold, length+token rule\n373: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_PROMPT_POLICY_LONG_NON_CASUAL_CHARS=50 # Visible-char threshold for the long-prompt fire rule\n374: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_WEIGHTS_JSON=    # Override live-lane weights for the 5-lane scorer (JSON partial)\n375: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_SHADOW_WEIGHTS_JSON= # Override shadow-mode lane weights (JSON partial)\n376: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_DOC_TRIGGERS=         # Opt-in doc-frontmatter trigger harvest (set true)\n377: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_WORKSPACE_ALLOWLIST=  # Extra allowed workspaceRoot prefixes (colon-separated)\n378: # SPECKIT_PRIVATE_SKILL_ROOTS=          # Trusted roots a private local-* skill link may point into (colon-separated absolute paths)\n379: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_RRF_FUSION=false      # Route the scorer through RRF instead of the weighted blend (opt-in)\n380: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_SHADOW_DELTA_ENABLED= # Enable shadow-delta collection (set 1/true)\n381: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_SHADOW_DELTA_PATH=    # Shadow-delta sink path (setting it also enables collection)\n382: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_HOOK_CACHE_HIT_P95_WARN_MS=75 # Warn threshold for advisor cache-hit p95 latency (ms)\n383: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_HOOK_CACHE_HIT_P95_PAGE_MS=150 # Page threshold for advisor cache-hit p95 latency (ms)\n384: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_HOOK_FAILOPEN_WARN_RATE=0.02 # Fail-open rate that raises a warning\n385: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_HOOK_FAILOPEN_PAGE_RATE=0.05 # Fail-open rate that raises a page\n386: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_BM25_LEXICAL_SHADOW=  # Score a BM25 lexical lane in shadow mode (opt-in)\n387: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_FEEDBACK_CALIBRATION_SHADOW= # Record feedback calibration in shadow mode (opt-in)\n388: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_FEEDBACK_CALIBRATION_PATH= # Override the feedback calibration records path\n389: # SPECKIT_ADVISOR_ROUTE_EXCLUSIONS_DIR= # Override the route-exclusions directory\n390: # SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_FALLBACK_TIMEOUT_MS=250 # Budget for the hooks' CLI fallback call\n391: # SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL=    # 1 = the Python advisor scores locally instead of calling the native runtime\n392: \n393: # --- OpenCode advisor plugin limits ---\n394: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_BRIDGE_TIMEOUT_MS=2500 # Timeout for one plugin bridge call\n395: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CACHE_TTL_MS=300000 # How long a cached brief is reused\n396: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_CACHE_ENTRIES=1000 # Max cached briefs\n397: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_TOKENS=80    # Token cap for one brief\n398: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_PROMPT_BYTES=65536 # Longest prompt the plugin sends to the advisor\n399: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_BRIEF_CHARS=2048 # Longest brief the plugin injects\n400: \n401: # --- Skill Advisor daemon: disable / trust / debug ---\n402: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=   # Disable the skill-advisor hook (alias of the kill-switch)\n403: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=           # Enable skill-advisor debug logging\n404: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR=          # Override the skill-advisor DB directory (auto)\n405: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_NODE_BINARY=     # Node binary for the skill-advisor daemon (auto)\n406: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_TRUST_DEFAULT=   # Daemon-side trust default (set \"trusted\" for no-_meta clients)\n407: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_STRICT_SINGLE_WRITER= # Strict single-writer enforcement for the advisor DB\n408: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_THRESHOLD_CONFIDENCE=0.8 # Advisor recommend confidence threshold\n409: # SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=                  # Enable debug output in the skill_advisor.py CLI\n410: # SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLE_BUILTIN_SEMANTIC= # Disable built-in semantic matching in the advisor script\n411: # SKILL_ADVISOR_FRESH_PROMPTS_PATH=    # Test-only path of the fresh behaviour rows the command transcript scorer labels (default: its own behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl)\n412: # (Aliases that route to the SYSTEM_* names above: SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED,\n413: #  SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED, SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_TRUSTED,\n414: #  SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_DEV_ALLOW_STALE.)\n415: \n416: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n417: # 11. OPENCODE GOAL PLUGIN\n418: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n419: \n420: # Plugin-level controls (restart OpenCode after changing).\n421: \n422: # OPENCODE_GOAL_DISABLED=               # Disable goal injection and plugin behavior (set 1) — canonical\n423: # OPENCODE_GOAL_PLUGIN_DISABLED=        # Accepted alias for the line above\n424: # OPENCODE_GOAL_AUTONOMY=               # Continuation mode: active / smoke / passive (unset=disabled)\n425: # OPENCODE_GOAL_DEBUG=                  # Write bounded debug events to the goal-events log (set 1)\n426: # OPENCODE_GOAL_VERIFIER=heuristic      # Completion verifier: heuristic (deterministic) or llm\n427: # OPENCODE_GOAL_MAX_OBJECTIVE_CHARS=4000 # Max stored raw objective length\n428: # OPENCODE_GOAL_MAX_GOAL_PROMPT_CHARS=4000 # Max generated goalPrompt length (clamped to 4000)\n429: # OPENCODE_GOAL_MAX_INJECTION_CHARS=4800 # Max [active_goal] injection block length\n430: # OPENCODE_GOAL_MAX_EVIDENCE_CHARS=1200 # Max verifier evidence retained in goal state\n431: # OPENCODE_GOAL_STATE_ARCHIVE_RETENTION_DAYS=90 # Retention before an archived goal-state file is pruned\n432: # OPENCODE_GOAL_STATE_ACTIVE_RETENTION_DAYS=2 # Age before an orphaned active-state file is swept\n433: # OPENCODE_GOAL_STATE_SWEEP_INTERVAL_MS=3600000 # Min interval between orphaned-active-state sweeps\n434: # OPENCODE_GOAL_VERIFIER_TIMEOUT_MS=30000 # Ceiling on one verifier run (ms)\n435: # OPENCODE_GOAL_CONTINUATION_TIMEOUT_MS=30000 # Ceiling on one guarded continuation turn (ms)\n436: # OPENCODE_GOAL_JSONL_MAX_BYTES=5242880 # Size at which a goal event log rotates\n437: # OPENCODE_GOAL_STATE_DIR=              # Override the goal-state directory\n438: # OPENCODE_GOAL_RUNTIME_LABEL=          # Runtime label recorded in goal state\n439: # OPENCODE_SPECS_ROOT=                  # Specs root the goal plugin resolves against\n440: \n441: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n442: # 12. CLI FRONT DOOR (DUAL-STACK)\n443: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n444: \n445: # Warm-only / prompt-time markers for the daemon-backed CLIs. Truthy = warm-only.\n446: \n447: # SPECKIT_CLI_PROMPT_TIME=              # Cross-CLI prompt-time marker (implies warm-only)\n448: # OPENCODE_PROMPT_TIME=                 # Runtime prompt-time marker (implies warm-only)\n449: # CLAUDE_CODE_PROMPT_TIME=              # Runtime prompt-time marker (implies warm-only)\n450: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_WARM_ONLY=   # Default the skill-advisor CLI to warm-only\n451: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_PROMPT_TIME= # Mark the skill-advisor CLI call as prompt-time\n452: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_DEV_ALLOW_STALE= # Dev override for the skill-advisor shim dist-freshness guard\n453: # SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_TRUSTED=     # Send skill-advisor CLI calls as trusted (needed for mutations)\n454: \n455: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n456: # 13. DEEP-LOOP RUNTIME & GUARD\n457: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n458: \n459: # SPECKIT_FANOUT_NEAR_DUP_DEDUP=false   # Collapse near-duplicate findings in the fan-out merge (opt-in)\n460: # DEEP_LOOP_EVIDENCE_ENFORCEMENT=       # Enforce evidence requirements in the deep loop (opt-in)\n461: # DEEP_LOOP_MIN_OBSERVATIONS=           # Min confirming observations a finding needs before convergence counts it; setting it enables the guard\n462: # SYSTEM_DEEP_LOOP_GUARD_REJECT=        # Hard-block a Deep Route mode-mismatch dispatch (set 1)\n463: # SYSTEM_DEEP_LOOP_GUARD_REJECT_LOOP=   # Hard-block repeated hand-offs to the same loop executor (set 1)\n464: # SYSTEM_DEEP_LOOP_GUARD_ACTIVE_RETENTION_DAYS=2 # Age before an untouched loop-guard state file is swept\n465: # SYSTEM_DEEP_LOOP_GUARD_ARCHIVE_RETENTION_DAYS=90 # Retention before an archived loop-guard file is pruned\n466: # SYSTEM_DEEP_LOOP_GUARD_SWEEP_INTERVAL_MS=3600000 # Min interval between loop-guard state sweeps\n467: \n468: # --- Paths, gates and review enforcement ---\n469: # DEEP_LOOP_REPO_ROOT=                  # Pin the repository root the deep-loop scripts resolve against\n470: # DEEP_LOOP_AUTHORITY_ROOT=             # Override the authority root (relative values resolve against the repo)\n471: # DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR=            # Override the coverage graph database directory\n472: # DEEP_LOOP_LEDGER_BACKING_GATE=        # Set 0 as an emergency off for the ledger-backing gate (on by default)\n473: # DEEP_LOOP_MIN_OBSERVATIONS_GUARD=     # Turn on the min-observations guard at its default count (set 1)\n474: # DEEP_LOOP_VERIFY_GATEWAY_RECEIPT=     # Verify the gateway receipt on each iteration (set 1)\n475: # DEEP_REVIEW_V2_ENFORCEMENT=warn       # Deep-review v2 contract enforcement: warn / strict / off\n476: # SPECKIT_PROVENANCE_CHECK=             # Check executor build provenance (opt-in, set 1)\n477: \n478: # --- Codex dispatch defaults for skill benchmarks ---\n479: # SKILL_BENCH_CODEX_MODEL=gpt-6-luna    # Codex model for benchmark dispatches\n480: # SKILL_BENCH_CODEX_EFFORT=xhigh        # Reasoning effort for benchmark dispatches\n481: # SKILL_BENCH_CODEX_TIER=fast           # Service tier for benchmark dispatches\n482: # SKILL_BENCH_CODEX_SANDBOX=read-only   # Sandbox for benchmark dispatches\n483: # SKILL_BENCH_CODEX_TIMEOUT_MS=480000   # Timeout for one benchmark dispatch\n484: \n485: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n486: # 14. CROSS-AI CLI DISPATCH  (external CLI orchestration)\n487: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n488: \n489: # Overrides for delegating to external coding CLIs. Most CLIs use OAuth; the\n490: # credential vars below are optional headless/API overrides.\n491: # For a dispatched child that must not inherit an enforced spec gate, pair\n492: # SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_ENFORCE=0 with AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 (see Section 5).\n493: \n494: # --- Pi ---\n495: # PI_BIN=pi                             # Pi CLI binary path override\n496: # PI_CACHE_RETENTION=                   # Pi cache retention setting (unset by default)\n497: \n498: # --- Claude Code ---\n499: # CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR=                   # Claude Code project root; Claude Code sets it for hooks, which fall back to the payload cwd\n500: \n501: # --- OpenCode CLI ---\n502: # OPENCODE_BIN=                         # OpenCode CLI binary path override\n503: # OPENCODE_DIR=                         # OpenCode config/project directory override\n504: # OPENCODE_API_KEY=                     # Optional OpenCode headless API key (unset by default)\n505: \n506: # --- Devin CLI ---\n507: # DEVIN_PROJECT_DIR=                    # Devin project root directory override\n508: # DEVIN_API_KEY=                        # Optional Devin headless API key (unset by default)\n509: \n510: # --- Cursor CLI ---\n511: # CURSOR_AUTH_TOKEN=                    # Cursor headless auth token (unset by default)\n512: # CURSOR_API_ENDPOINT=                  # Override the Cursor API endpoint (default api2.cursor.sh)\n513: \n514: # --- Codex CLI ---\n515: # CODEX_PROJECT_DIR=                    # Codex project root directory override\n516: \n517: # --- DeepSeek Harness (dsh) dispatch ---\n518: # LLMGATEWAY_API_KEY=                   # Key the dsh LLM Gateway route patch names (export it, never commit a value)\n519: # DSH_HOME=                             # Set per dispatch to a fresh mktemp -d folder, never shared and never set here\n520: \n521: # --- Mistral Vibe dispatch ---\n522: # MISTRAL_API_KEY=                      # Prefer the Vibe sign-in key from the keychain, which bills the Vibe budget (export it, never commit a value)\n523: # VIBE_HOME=                            # Vibe home override; fan-out lineages set their own, so never set it here\n524: # VIBE_SKILLS_SOURCE_DIR=               # Skills the Vibe skill sync links (.skilled/skills)\n525: # VIBE_SKILLS_OUTPUT_DIR=               # Where the Vibe skill links go (.vibe/skills)\n526: # VIBE_COMMANDS_SOURCE_DIR=             # Commands the Vibe prompt sync reads (.skilled/commands)\n527: # VIBE_PROMPTS_OUTPUT_DIR=              # Where the Vibe prompt stubs go (.vibe/prompts)\n528: # VIBE_AGENTS_SOURCE_DIR=               # Agents the Vibe profile sync reads (.skilled/agents)\n529: # VIBE_AGENTS_OUTPUT_DIR=               # Where the Vibe agent profiles go (.vibe/agents)\n530: \n531: # --- DeepSeek Harness (dsh) mirror sync ---\n532: # DSH_SKILLS_SOURCE_DIR=                # Skills the dsh skill sync links (.skilled/skills)\n533: # DSH_SKILLS_OUTPUT_DIR=                # Where the dsh skill links go (.dsh/skills)\n534: # DSH_COMMANDS_SOURCE_DIR=              # Commands the dsh prompt sync reads (.skilled/commands)\n535: # DSH_PROMPTS_OUTPUT_DIR=               # Where the dsh prompt stubs go (.dsh/prompts)\n536: # DSH_AGENTS_SOURCE_DIR=                # Agents the dsh persona sync reads (.skilled/agents)\n537: # DSH_AGENTS_OUTPUT_DIR=                # Where the dsh persona patches go (.dsh/agents)\n538: \n539: # --- Other skills ---\n540: # SK_CODE_DIR=                          # Override the sk-code skill directory\n541: # SK_DESIGN_STYLE_DB_MODE=              # sk-design style-DB backend mode (e.g. legacy)\n542: \n543: # --- Manual testing playbook conversation runner ---\n544: # CONVERSATION_WATCH=decision-capture   # Comma list of .skilled/skills/.state subfolders the repository snapshot watches\n545: # CONVERSATION_CHECK_TIMEOUT_MS=60000   # Time limit for each turn's check command\n546: # CODEX_HOME=                           # Codex home (~/.codex): the runner's hook-trust step reads and restores its config.toml, and the decision-capture Codex sweep finds session files under its sessions/\n547: # TMUX_TMPDIR=                          # Parent of the tmux-<uid> folder where the runner looks for its private sockets (/tmp)\n548: \n549: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n550: # 16. SK-GIT & LIVE-SYNC\n551: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n552: \n553: # Preflight advisories, git-hook bypasses, and the continuous-integration loop.\n554: \n555: # --- Preflight advisory suppression ---\n556: # SKGIT_ADVISORY=                       # Set 0 to disable all sk-git preflight advisories\n557: # SKGIT_ADVISORY_SKIP=                  # Suppress one rule id, or a family prefix (e.g. commit)\n558: \n559: # --- Git-hook bypasses (use only when a hook is genuinely wrong) ---\n560: # Each one lasts one command and is read from the environment only. Every block\n561: # message names its own. SYSTEM_GIT_COMMIT_HOOKS_DISABLED (Section 8) turns off\n562: # every pre-commit gate, the agent mirror gate included, which has no switch of its own.\n563: # SPECKIT_SKIP_COMMENT_HYGIENE=         # Skip the pre-commit comment-hygiene gate (set 1)\n564: # SPECKIT_SKIP_PHRASE_LINT=             # Skip the pre-commit template phrase lint gate (set 1)\n565: # SPECKIT_SKIP_MIRROR_PARITY=           # Skip the pre-commit mirror-parity gate (set 1)\n566: # SPECKIT_SKIP_CARD_SYNC=               # Skip the pre-commit prompt-card sync gate (set 1)\n567: # SPECKIT_SKIP_MCP_MUTATION_CLASS=      # Skip the pre-commit MCP mutation-class gate (set 1)\n568: # SPECKIT_SKIP_ROUTE_REMINT=            # Skip the pre-commit compiled-routing re-mint (set 1)\n569: # SPECKIT_SKIP_CONTRACT_RECOMPILE=      # Skip the pre-commit deep command contract recompile (set 1)\n570: # SPECKIT_SKIP_SPEC_REMINT=             # Skip the pre-commit spec metadata re-mint (set 1)\n571: # SPECKIT_SKIP_PREPARE_COMMIT_MSG=      # Skip the Commit-Id and Spec: stamper, which never blocks (set 1)\n572: # SPECKIT_COMMIT_SPEC=                  # Packet the stamper writes as the Spec: trailer of a single commit (<track>/<packet>[/<phase>])\n573: # SPECKIT_ALLOW_REMOTE_PUSH=            # Allow ONE push to a non-allowlisted branch (1 updates it, the branch name creates it)\n574: # SPECKIT_SKIP_PREPUSH_SKILL_GATE=      # Skip the pre-push skill-root-metadata gate (set 1)\n575: # SPECKIT_SKIP_PREPUSH_ROUTE_GATE=      # Skip the pre-push compiled-routing gate (set 1)\n576: # SPECKIT_SKIP_PREPUSH_TRACK_GATE=      # Skip the pre-push track-root children_ids gate (set 1)\n577: # SPECKIT_ALLOW_MASS_DELETION=          # Allow a push past the mass-deletion ceiling (set 1)\n578: # SPECKIT_MASS_DELETION_THRESHOLD=100   # Tracked files a push may delete before the ceiling blocks it\n579: \n580: # --- Worktrees ---\n581: # SPECKIT_WORKTREE_BASE=                # Relocate worktrees out of the checkout (default .worktrees)\n582: # SPECKIT_WORKTREE_SHARED_PATHS=        # Extra relative paths symlinked into each wrapper worktree\n583: # SPECKIT_WORKTREE_GUARD=               # Set off to silence the shared-checkout worktree warning\n584: # SPECKIT_GIT_TIMEOUT=20                # Seconds one index-reading git call may take in the git hooks, the launcher and the worktree reaper\n585: # SPECKIT_WORKTREE_ADD_TIMEOUT=60        # Seconds the launcher gives git worktree add before it fails the launch\n586: # SPECKIT_FSMON_REAPER=                 # Override the fsmonitor daemon reaper script path\n587: # SPECKIT_WORKTREE_AUTOREAP=1            # Set 0 to stop the session-start sweep that removes merged, idle numbered worktrees (once per 6 hours)\n588: # SPECKIT_WORKTREE_REAPER=              # Override the worktree reaper script path the session-start sweep runs\n589: # FSMON_PROBE_TIMEOUT=15                # Seconds the reaper waits on one git or lsof call\n590: # FSMON_STOP_TIMEOUT=5                  # Seconds the reaper gives git's own daemon stop\n591: # FSMON_TERM_WAIT=5                     # Seconds the reaper waits after SIGTERM before SIGKILL\n592: # FSMON_KILL_WAIT=3                     # Seconds the reaper waits for a daemon to exit after SIGKILL\n593: # SPECKIT_GIT_HOOKS_GUARD=on            # Git-hooks install warning + self-heal (set off to silence)\n594: \n595: # --- Continuous-integration live sync ---\n596: # SYSTEM_LIVE_SYNC_DISABLED=            # Master switch for the whole live-sync loop\n597: # SYSTEM_PRIMARY_RECONCILE_DISABLED=    # Disable SessionStart reconcile of the primary checkout\n598: # SYSTEM_LIVE_FOLLOW_DISABLED=          # Disable the IDE checkout follower auto-start\n599: # SPECKIT_AUTOSYNC=                     # Per-launch publish opt-out (wrapper sessions export 1)\n600: # SPECKIT_LIVE_BRANCH=                  # The live branch a wrapper session publishes to\n601: # SPECKIT_LIVE_REMOTE=origin            # Remote used by the live-sync scripts\n602: # SPECKIT_SYNC_RETRIES=3                # Push-race retries in the publish loop\n603: # SPECKIT_PRIMARY_RECONCILE_TIMEOUT=12  # Network timeout (s) for the SessionStart reconcile\n604: # SPECKIT_PRIMARY_RECONCILE_LOCK_TTL=45 # Stale-lock TTL (s) for the reconcile single-flight\n605: # SPECKIT_DIST_AUTO_REBUILD=            # Controls dist rebuild after a freshness check (NOT a disable flag)\n606: # LIVE_FOLLOW_MANAGED_LOG=0             # 1 = the IDE follower rotates its own log (the auto-start sets it)\n607: # LIVE_FOLLOW_LOG_MAX_BYTES=262144      # Size at which a managed follower log rotates\n608: # GATE_REGISTRY=                        # Override the git-hook gate registry path\n609: \n610: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n611: # 17. JEV CLASSIFIER FEATURES  (on when a Jev credential is stored)\n612: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n613: \n614: # Each feature below asks Typesafe's Jev classifier one measured question and\n615: # runs on its own once `jev` is on PATH and `jev auth status --provider official`\n616: # passes (store the key once with `jev auth set --provider official`). No key,\n617: # no call: without a credential every path behaves as if these lines were absent.\n618: # Set a switch to 0/false/no/off to turn it off. Read from the environment, then\n619: # from .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env, so a saved switch holds across sessions.\n620: # JEV_FEATURES=                         # Master switch: 0 turns every Jev feature off\n621: # JEV_FEATURE_CITE_DRIFT=               # Citation drift advisory in validate_document.py (older name: SKDOC_CITE_DRIFT_CHECK)\n622: # JEV_FEATURE_INJECTION_SCREEN=         # fetched-text screen for instructions aimed at an AI agent (Claude Code, Devin, OpenCode, Pi)\n623: # JEV_PROVIDER=official                 # Jev provider every feature asks (official or openrouter)\n624: # JEV_TRANSPORT=                        # Set jev to skip Pi's classifier and always use the jev CLI\n625: \n626: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n627: # 18. SESSION HANDOVER  (session handover under skilled-loop)\n628: # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n629: \n630: # The threshold and window apply to every session; outside skilled-loop the nudge asks\n631: # only for a note. The hop and age limits apply inside the loop. The loop ships on for Claude Code\n632: # and off on every other runtime. SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED (Section 8, also read from\n633: # hook-flags.env) set to 1 turns it on everywhere and set to 0 turns it off everywhere, and a\n634: # non-empty SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_<RUNTIME>_ENABLED (Section 8) overrides it for one runtime, so\n635: # ENABLED=1 with CLAUDE_ENABLED=0 is on everywhere except Claude Code. SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_DISABLED=1\n636: # turns it off and wins over every enable flag. While it is off, /speckit:handoff refuses and\n637: # auto-compaction stays the fallback. The loop itself sets SKILLED_LOOP_* for each session, so never set those. The one exception is SKILLED_LOOP_TRUSTED_CHECKOUTS below, which only an operator sets.\n638: # SESSION_HANDOVER_THRESHOLD=0.80       # Context fill that triggers the handoff nudge\n639: # SESSION_HANDOVER_WINDOW_TOKENS=       # Context window to measure against (autoCompactWindow, then 1M for a [1m] model, else unknown and no nudge)\n640: # SESSION_HANDOVER_MAX_HOPS=10          # Max hops in one loop before relaunch stops\n641: # SESSION_HANDOVER_MAX_AGE_MIN=10       # Max age of an armed record the wrapper still relaunches\n642: # SESSION_HANDOVER_NOTIFY_HOPS=         # macOS notice on each hand-over (off; also read from hook-flags.env)\n643: # SKILLED_LOOP_TRUSTED_CHECKOUTS=       # Extra checkouts whose wrapper the shell shim may run (colon-separated absolute paths)\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 644]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".env.example\"}"},"time":{"start":1794848338403,"end":1794848339047}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794848341051,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"id":"prt_1e54c3c3b001yOCMOqDtV26FbV","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e54c0de7001YutKnTnGrw6MO2","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"87dc23a9d825a9ec8aedeca73bd0ce96fbfb3879","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":2838,"output":212,"reasoning":506,"cache":{"read":199296,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794848404044,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"id":"prt_1e54d324c001ucIvfaeXXF1Jt6","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e54c3c4a001Xa2Vev6UKd1iA9","type":"step-start","snapshot":"87dc23a9d825a9ec8aedeca73bd0ce96fbfb3879"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794848404923,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e54d33ba001D1XJ4BjOVnYxRm","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e54c3c4a001Xa2Vev6UKd1iA9","type":"tool","id":"call_588dfe8ed3f741f9a9d1182a","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md, lines 1-208\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Create Skill Router\"\n3: description: \"Sibling router for sk-create-skill: the intent signals, the resource map and the no-match checklist a reader parses first.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"sk-create-skill router\"\n6:   - \"sk-create-skill routing\"\n7: importance_tier: normal\n8: contextType: general\n9: version: 1.0.5.0\n10: router_state: active\n11: skill_pointer: SKILL.md\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # Create Skill Router\n15: \n16: The machine router for [`SKILL.md`](./SKILL.md). `SKILL.md` keeps the short routing prose and the\n17: link that points here; this file holds the declaration a reader parses to decide what loads.\n18: \n19: ---\n20: \n21: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n22: \n23: The router answers one question: given a request, which skill-local resources load, in what order, and\n24: what happens when nothing matches. Every path below stays inside this skill folder, and no resource other than `DEFAULT_RESOURCE`\n25: loads before an intent selects it.\n26: \n27: Requests reach this packet when they ask to create or rebuild an OpenCode skill under `.skilled/skills/`, to run `/create:sk-skill` for a standalone skill or `/create:skill-parent` for a parent hub, to author or repair a skill package's `SKILL.md`, `README.md`, `references/`, `assets/`, `scripts/` or `changelog/`, or to validate and package a skill with `scripts/package_skill.py`. Its vocabulary is `create skill`, `new skill`, `skill scaffold`, `SKILL.md scaffold`, `OpenCode skill`, `parent hub`, `mode packet`, `nested workflow packet` and `package skill`. It routes to two resource families: the `references/shared/` doctrine and its root-metadata contract, which both modes load first, and the mode's own `references/<key>/` plus `assets/<key>/` trees, where `create-skill` resolves the `skill` key and `create-skill-parent` resolves `parent-skill`.\n28: \n29: ---\n30: \n31: ## 2. INTENT MODEL\n32: \n33: - **`SKILL_PACKAGE`** fires on `create skill`, `/create:sk-skill`, `new skill`, `skill scaffold`, `SKILL.md scaffold`, `OpenCode skill`, `sk-skill`, `create sk-`, `reusable capability`, `reusable helper`, `starter reference docs`, `package skill`, `doc rewrite guard`, `doc-rewrite-guard.py`, `render ledger`, `render-known-debt.json`, `exempt from the render checks`, `render exempt map`, `kept every claim` and `kept every original claim` at weight 4. It loads the five shared docs — `references/shared/overview.md`, `references/shared/common-pitfalls.md`, `references/shared/validation-and-packaging.md`, `references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md`, `references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md` — then `references/skill/creation-workflow.md`, `references/skill/examples-and-maintenance.md`, `references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md`, and the eight `assets/skill/` templates: `assets/skill/skill-md-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-asset-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-procedure-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-scaffold-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-smart-router.md`, `assets/skill/skill-router-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-sync-manifest-template.md`. The skill README template is not in this set: the `sk-create-readme` mode owns it and writes the README step.\n34: - **`PARENT_HUB`** fires on `/create:skill-parent`, `parent skill`, `parent hub`, `mode packet`, `nested workflow packet`, `mode-registry.json` and `hub-router.json` at weight 4. It loads the same five shared docs, then `references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md`, `references/parent-skill/parent-hub-router-schema.md`, `references/parent-skill/compiled-routing-architecture.md`, and the five `assets/parent-skill/` templates: `assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-template.md`, `assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-readme-template.md`, `assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-root-router-template.md`, `assets/parent-skill/scaffold/hub-skill-scaffold.md`, `assets/parent-skill/scaffold/packet-skill-scaffold.md`.\n35: \n36: ---\n37: \n38: ## 3. MACHINE ROUTER\n39: \n40: The one machine-readable projection of the intent model above, written as `## MACHINE ROUTER` so every\n41: reader finds it. This section is the last in the file, and it holds the only pseudocode.\n42: \n43: This section holds the packet's mode tree, its route selection, the resource domains it loads and the smart-router pseudocode that reads them.\n44: \n45: ### Primary Detection Signal\n46: \n47: ```text\n48: SKILL AUTHORING REQUEST\n49:     |\n50:     +- Standalone skill -> workflowMode: sk-create-skill\n51:     |   +- scripts/init_skill.py\n52:     |   +- assets/skill/skill-md-template.md\n53:     |   +- README.md step -> the sk-create-readme mode\n54:     |   +- assets/skill/skill-sync-manifest-template.md\n55:     |\n56:     +- Parent hub -> workflowMode: sk-create-skill-parent\n57:         +- assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-template.md\n58:         +- assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-registry-template.json\n59:         +- assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-router-template.json\n60: ```\n61: \n62: ### Route Selection\n63: \n64: Choose `create-skill` when the artifact is one skill with one advisor identity and one runtime contract.\n65: \n66: Choose `create-skill-parent` when the artifact is one advisor-routable hub that dispatches to nested workflow packets or read-only surface packets.\n67: \n68: Ask one focused clarification before authoring if it is unclear whether the user wants a standalone skill or a parent hub.\n69: \n70: ### Resource Domains\n71: \n72: | Domain | Core Resources | Use |\n73: | --- | --- | --- |\n74: | Scaffolding | `scripts/init_skill.py`, `assets/skill/skill-md-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-router-template.md` | Create or normalize standalone skill files. The README step goes to the `sk-create-readme` mode. |\n75: | Resource templates | `assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-asset-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-smart-router.md` | Create routed references, assets, and resilient smart-router pseudocode. |\n76: | Runtime sync manifests | `assets/skill/skill-sync-manifest-template.md` | Document how a runtime config dir derives from the canonical `.skilled` tree (SYNC manifest). |\n77: | Procedure cards | `assets/skill/skill-procedure-template.md` | Add a private, triggerable internal procedure to a skill or mode without a new public identity. |\n78: | Parent hubs | `assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-*` | Create hub SKILL, registry, router, description, and graph metadata files. |\n79: | Validation | `scripts/package_skill.py`, `../shared/scripts/extract_structure.py` | Check completion, package distribution zips, and inspect structure. |\n80: | Leaf-route replay | `scripts/leaf-route-replay.cjs` | Replay the committed stage-two keyword block of each hub's `ROUTER.md` against its gold scenarios with zero model calls. `--transcripts` recounts `ROUTER.md` reads and `--prose` compares the prose arm. |\n81: | Overflow detail | `references/README.md`, `references/{shared,skill,parent-skill}/`, `../shared/` | Load only for edge cases, exhaustive examples, or schema details beyond this SKILL.md. |\n82: \n83: ### Smart Router Pseudocode\n84: \n85: ```python\n86: from pathlib import Path\n87: \n88: SKILL_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n89: RESOURCE_BASES = (SKILL_ROOT / \"references\", SKILL_ROOT / \"assets\")\n90: DEFAULT_RESOURCE = \"references/README.md\"\n91: RESOURCE_KEY_BY_MODE = {\n92:     \"sk-create-skill\": \"skill\",\n93:     \"sk-create-skill-parent\": \"parent-skill\",\n94: }\n95: \n96: INTENT_MODEL = {\n97:     \"SKILL_PACKAGE\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create skill\", \"/create:sk-skill\", \"new skill\", \"skill scaffold\", \"skill.md scaffold\", \"opencode skill\", \"sk-skill\", \"create sk-\", \"reusable capability\", \"reusable helper\", \"starter reference docs\", \"package skill\", \"doc rewrite guard\", \"doc-rewrite-guard.py\", \"render ledger\", \"render-known-debt.json\", \"exempt from the render checks\", \"render exempt map\", \"kept every claim\", \"kept every original claim\"]},\n98:     \"PARENT_HUB\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"/create:skill-parent\", \"parent skill\", \"parent hub\", \"mode packet\", \"nested workflow packet\", \"mode-registry.json\", \"hub-router.json\"]},\n99: }\n100: \n101: # The keyed selection below resolves to exactly these sets. Enumerating them keeps\n102: # the routed inventory legible to a reader and to the connectivity scan, which is\n103: # what catches a new reference that the keyed load silently picks up but no\n104: # documented route names.\n105: RESOURCE_MAP = {\n106:     \"SKILL_PACKAGE\": [\n107:         \"references/shared/overview.md\",\n108:         \"references/shared/common-pitfalls.md\",\n109:         \"references/shared/validation-and-packaging.md\",\n110:         \"references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md\",\n111:         \"references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md\",\n112:         \"references/skill/creation-workflow.md\",\n113:         \"references/skill/examples-and-maintenance.md\",\n114:         \"references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md\",\n115:         \"assets/skill/skill-md-template.md\",\n116:         \"assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md\",\n117:         \"assets/skill/skill-asset-template.md\",\n118:         \"assets/skill/skill-procedure-template.md\",\n119:         \"assets/skill/skill-scaffold-template.md\",\n120:         \"assets/skill/skill-smart-router.md\",\n121:         \"assets/skill/skill-router-template.md\",\n122:         \"assets/skill/skill-sync-manifest-template.md\",\n123:     ],\n124:     \"PARENT_HUB\": [\n125:         \"references/shared/overview.md\",\n126:         \"references/shared/common-pitfalls.md\",\n127:         \"references/shared/validation-and-packaging.md\",\n128:         \"references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md\",\n129:         \"references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md\",\n130:         \"references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md\",\n131:         \"references/parent-skill/parent-hub-router-schema.md\",\n132:         \"references/parent-skill/compiled-routing-architecture.md\",\n133:         \"assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-template.md\",\n134:         \"assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-readme-template.md\",\n135:         \"assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-root-router-template.md\",\n136:         \"assets/parent-skill/scaffold/hub-skill-scaffold.md\",\n137:         \"assets/parent-skill/scaffold/packet-skill-scaffold.md\",\n138:     ],\n139: }\n140: UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST = [\n141:     \"Confirm whether the artifact is a standalone skill or parent hub\",\n142:     \"Confirm the target skill folder and intended advisor identity\",\n143:     \"Provide one concrete trigger, output contract, or resource example\",\n144:     \"Confirm the validation command before completion\",\n145: ]\n146: \n147: def discover_markdown_resources() -> set[str]:\n148:     docs = []\n149:     for base in RESOURCE_BASES:\n150:         if base.exists():\n151:             docs.extend(path for path in base.rglob(\"*.md\") if path.is_file())\n152:     return {doc.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT).as_posix() for doc in docs}\n153: \n154: def _guard_in_skill(relative_path: str) -> str:\n155:     resolved = (SKILL_ROOT / relative_path).resolve()\n156:     resolved.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT)\n157:     if resolved.suffix.lower() != \".md\":\n158:         raise ValueError(f\"Only markdown resources are routable: {relative_path}\")\n159:     return resolved.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT).as_posix()\n160: \n161: def load_if_available(relative_path: str, inventory: set[str], loaded: list[str], seen: set[str]) -> None:\n162:     guarded = _guard_in_skill(relative_path)\n163:     if guarded in inventory and guarded not in seen:\n164:         load(guarded)\n165:         loaded.append(guarded)\n166:         seen.add(guarded)\n167: \n168: def route_skill_authoring_request(request):\n169:     inventory = discover_markdown_resources()\n170:     loaded, seen = [], set()\n171: \n172:     if asks_for_parent_hub_or_mode_registry(request):\n173:         workflow_mode = \"sk-create-skill-parent\"\n174:     elif asks_for_nested_workflow_or_surface_packets(request):\n175:         workflow_mode = \"sk-create-skill-parent\"\n176:     elif asks_for_one_skill_package(request):\n177:         workflow_mode = \"sk-create-skill\"\n178:     elif unclear_standalone_vs_parent(request):\n179:         load_if_available(DEFAULT_RESOURCE, inventory, loaded, seen)\n180:         return {\n181:             \"load_level\": \"UNKNOWN_FALLBACK\",\n182:             \"needs_disambiguation\": True,\n183:             \"disambiguation_checklist\": UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST,\n184:             \"resources\": loaded,\n185:         }\n186:     else:\n187:         load_if_available(DEFAULT_RESOURCE, inventory, loaded, seen)\n188:         return {\"load_level\": \"DEFER\", \"next\": \"matching sk-doc packet\", \"resources\": loaded}\n189: \n190:     routing_key = RESOURCE_KEY_BY_MODE[workflow_mode]\n191:     shared_refs = sorted(path for path in inventory if path.startswith(\"references/shared/\"))\n192:     keyed_refs = sorted(path for path in inventory if path.startswith(f\"references/{routing_key}/\"))\n193:     keyed_assets = sorted(path for path in inventory if path.startswith(f\"assets/{routing_key}/\"))\n194: \n195:     if not keyed_refs and not keyed_assets:\n196:         load_if_available(DEFAULT_RESOURCE, inventory, loaded, seen)\n197:         return {\n198:             \"workflowMode\": workflow_mode,\n199:             \"routing_key\": routing_key,\n200:             \"notice\": f\"No create-skill resources found for routing key '{routing_key}'\",\n201:             \"resources\": loaded,\n202:         }\n203: \n204:     for path in shared_refs + keyed_refs + keyed_assets:\n205:         load_if_available(path, inventory, loaded, seen)\n206: \n207:     return {\"workflowMode\": workflow_mode, \"routing_key\": routing_key, \"resources\": loaded}\n208: ```","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md, lines 1-208\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Create Skill Router\"\n3: description: \"Sibling router for sk-create-skill: the intent signals, the resource map and the no-match checklist a reader parses first.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"sk-create-skill router\"\n6:   - \"sk-create-skill routing\"\n7: importance_tier: normal\n8: contextType: general\n9: version: 1.0.5.0\n10: router_state: active\n11: skill_pointer: SKILL.md\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # Create Skill Router\n15: \n16: The machine router for [`SKILL.md`](./SKILL.md). `SKILL.md` keeps the short routing prose and the\n17: link that points here; this file holds the declaration a reader parses to decide what loads.\n18: \n19: ---\n20: \n21: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n22: \n23: The router answers one question: given a request, which skill-local resources load, in what order, and\n24: what happens when nothing matches. Every path below stays inside this skill folder, and no resource other than `DEFAULT_RESOURCE`\n25: loads before an intent selects it.\n26: \n27: Requests reach this packet when they ask to create or rebuild an OpenCode skill under `.skilled/skills/`, to run `/create:sk-skill` for a standalone skill or `/create:skill-parent` for a parent hub, to author or repair a skill package's `SKILL.md`, `README.md`, `references/`, `assets/`, `scripts/` or `changelog/`, or to validate and package a skill with `scripts/package_skill.py`. Its vocabulary is `create skill`, `new skill`, `skill scaffold`, `SKILL.md scaffold`, `OpenCode skill`, `parent hub`, `mode packet`, `nested workflow packet` and `package skill`. It routes to two resource families: the `references/shared/` doctrine and its root-metadata contract, which both modes load first, and the mode's own `references/<key>/` plus `assets/<key>/` trees, where `create-skill` resolves the `skill` key and `create-skill-parent` resolves `parent-skill`.\n28: \n29: ---\n30: \n31: ## 2. INTENT MODEL\n32: \n33: - **`SKILL_PACKAGE`** fires on `create skill`, `/create:sk-skill`, `new skill`, `skill scaffold`, `SKILL.md scaffold`, `OpenCode skill`, `sk-skill`, `create sk-`, `reusable capability`, `reusable helper`, `starter reference docs`, `package skill`, `doc rewrite guard`, `doc-rewrite-guard.py`, `render ledger`, `render-known-debt.json`, `exempt from the render checks`, `render exempt map`, `kept every claim` and `kept every original claim` at weight 4. It loads the five shared docs — `references/shared/overview.md`, `references/shared/common-pitfalls.md`, `references/shared/validation-and-packaging.md`, `references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md`, `references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md` — then `references/skill/creation-workflow.md`, `references/skill/examples-and-maintenance.md`, `references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md`, and the eight `assets/skill/` templates: `assets/skill/skill-md-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-asset-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-procedure-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-scaffold-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-smart-router.md`, `assets/skill/skill-router-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-sync-manifest-template.md`. The skill README template is not in this set: the `sk-create-readme` mode owns it and writes the README step.\n34: - **`PARENT_HUB`** fires on `/create:skill-parent`, `parent skill`, `parent hub`, `mode packet`, `nested workflow packet`, `mode-registry.json` and `hub-router.json` at weight 4. It loads the same five shared docs, then `references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md`, `references/parent-skill/parent-hub-router-schema.md`, `references/parent-skill/compiled-routing-architecture.md`, and the five `assets/parent-skill/` templates: `assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-template.md`, `assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-readme-template.md`, `assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-root-router-template.md`, `assets/parent-skill/scaffold/hub-skill-scaffold.md`, `assets/parent-skill/scaffold/packet-skill-scaffold.md`.\n35: \n36: ---\n37: \n38: ## 3. MACHINE ROUTER\n39: \n40: The one machine-readable projection of the intent model above, written as `## MACHINE ROUTER` so every\n41: reader finds it. This section is the last in the file, and it holds the only pseudocode.\n42: \n43: This section holds the packet's mode tree, its route selection, the resource domains it loads and the smart-router pseudocode that reads them.\n44: \n45: ### Primary Detection Signal\n46: \n47: ```text\n48: SKILL AUTHORING REQUEST\n49:     |\n50:     +- Standalone skill -> workflowMode: sk-create-skill\n51:     |   +- scripts/init_skill.py\n52:     |   +- assets/skill/skill-md-template.md\n53:     |   +- README.md step -> the sk-create-readme mode\n54:     |   +- assets/skill/skill-sync-manifest-template.md\n55:     |\n56:     +- Parent hub -> workflowMode: sk-create-skill-parent\n57:         +- assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-template.md\n58:         +- assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-registry-template.json\n59:         +- assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-router-template.json\n60: ```\n61: \n62: ### Route Selection\n63: \n64: Choose `create-skill` when the artifact is one skill with one advisor identity and one runtime contract.\n65: \n66: Choose `create-skill-parent` when the artifact is one advisor-routable hub that dispatches to nested workflow packets or read-only surface packets.\n67: \n68: Ask one focused clarification before authoring if it is unclear whether the user wants a standalone skill or a parent hub.\n69: \n70: ### Resource Domains\n71: \n72: | Domain | Core Resources | Use |\n73: | --- | --- | --- |\n74: | Scaffolding | `scripts/init_skill.py`, `assets/skill/skill-md-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-router-template.md` | Create or normalize standalone skill files. The README step goes to the `sk-create-readme` mode. |\n75: | Resource templates | `assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-asset-template.md`, `assets/skill/skill-smart-router.md` | Create routed references, assets, and resilient smart-router pseudocode. |\n76: | Runtime sync manifests | `assets/skill/skill-sync-manifest-template.md` | Document how a runtime config dir derives from the canonical `.skilled` tree (SYNC manifest). |\n77: | Procedure cards | `assets/skill/skill-procedure-template.md` | Add a private, triggerable internal procedure to a skill or mode without a new public identity. |\n78: | Parent hubs | `assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-*` | Create hub SKILL, registry, router, description, and graph metadata files. |\n79: | Validation | `scripts/package_skill.py`, `../shared/scripts/extract_structure.py` | Check completion, package distribution zips, and inspect structure. |\n80: | Leaf-route replay | `scripts/leaf-route-replay.cjs` | Replay the committed stage-two keyword block of each hub's `ROUTER.md` against its gold scenarios with zero model calls. `--transcripts` recounts `ROUTER.md` reads and `--prose` compares the prose arm. |\n81: | Overflow detail | `references/README.md`, `references/{shared,skill,parent-skill}/`, `../shared/` | Load only for edge cases, exhaustive examples, or schema details beyond this SKILL.md. |\n82: \n83: ### Smart Router Pseudocode\n84: \n85: ```python\n86: from pathlib import Path\n87: \n88: SKILL_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n89: RESOURCE_BASES = (SKILL_ROOT / \"references\", SKILL_ROOT / \"assets\")\n90: DEFAULT_RESOURCE = \"references/README.md\"\n91: RESOURCE_KEY_BY_MODE = {\n92:     \"sk-create-skill\": \"skill\",\n93:     \"sk-create-skill-parent\": \"parent-skill\",\n94: }\n95: \n96: INTENT_MODEL = {\n97:     \"SKILL_PACKAGE\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create skill\", \"/create:sk-skill\", \"new skill\", \"skill scaffold\", \"skill.md scaffold\", \"opencode skill\", \"sk-skill\", \"create sk-\", \"reusable capability\", \"reusable helper\", \"starter reference docs\", \"package skill\", \"doc rewrite guard\", \"doc-rewrite-guard.py\", \"render ledger\", \"render-known-debt.json\", \"exempt from the render checks\", \"render exempt map\", \"kept every claim\", \"kept every original claim\"]},\n98:     \"PARENT_HUB\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"/create:skill-parent\", \"parent skill\", \"parent hub\", \"mode packet\", \"nested workflow packet\", \"mode-registry.json\", \"hub-router.json\"]},\n99: }\n100: \n101: # The keyed selection below resolves to exactly these sets. Enumerating them keeps\n102: # the routed inventory legible to a reader and to the connectivity scan, which is\n103: # what catches a new reference that the keyed load silently picks up but no\n104: # documented route names.\n105: RESOURCE_MAP = {\n106:     \"SKILL_PACKAGE\": [\n107:         \"references/shared/overview.md\",\n108:         \"references/shared/common-pitfalls.md\",\n109:         \"references/shared/validation-and-packaging.md\",\n110:         \"references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md\",\n111:         \"references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md\",\n112:         \"references/skill/creation-workflow.md\",\n113:         \"references/skill/examples-and-maintenance.md\",\n114:         \"references/skill/upgrading-a-skill-to-v4.md\",\n115:         \"assets/skill/skill-md-template.md\",\n116:         \"assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md\",\n117:         \"assets/skill/skill-asset-template.md\",\n118:         \"assets/skill/skill-procedure-template.md\",\n119:         \"assets/skill/skill-scaffold-template.md\",\n120:         \"assets/skill/skill-smart-router.md\",\n121:         \"assets/skill/skill-router-template.md\",\n122:         \"assets/skill/skill-sync-manifest-template.md\",\n123:     ],\n124:     \"PARENT_HUB\": [\n125:         \"references/shared/overview.md\",\n126:         \"references/shared/common-pitfalls.md\",\n127:         \"references/shared/validation-and-packaging.md\",\n128:         \"references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md\",\n129:         \"references/shared/skill-root-metadata-contract.md\",\n130:         \"references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md\",\n131:         \"references/parent-skill/parent-hub-router-schema.md\",\n132:         \"references/parent-skill/compiled-routing-architecture.md\",\n133:         \"assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-template.md\",\n134:         \"assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-readme-template.md\",\n135:         \"assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-root-router-template.md\",\n136:         \"assets/parent-skill/scaffold/hub-skill-scaffold.md\",\n137:         \"assets/parent-skill/scaffold/packet-skill-scaffold.md\",\n138:     ],\n139: }\n140: UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST = [\n141:     \"Confirm whether the artifact is a standalone skill or parent hub\",\n142:     \"Confirm the target skill folder and intended advisor identity\",\n143:     \"Provide one concrete trigger, output contract, or resource example\",\n144:     \"Confirm the validation command before completion\",\n145: ]\n146: \n147: def discover_markdown_resources() -> set[str]:\n148:     docs = []\n149:     for base in RESOURCE_BASES:\n150:         if base.exists():\n151:             docs.extend(path for path in base.rglob(\"*.md\") if path.is_file())\n152:     return {doc.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT).as_posix() for doc in docs}\n153: \n154: def _guard_in_skill(relative_path: str) -> str:\n155:     resolved = (SKILL_ROOT / relative_path).resolve()\n156:     resolved.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT)\n157:     if resolved.suffix.lower() != \".md\":\n158:         raise ValueError(f\"Only markdown resources are routable: {relative_path}\")\n159:     return resolved.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT).as_posix()\n160: \n161: def load_if_available(relative_path: str, inventory: set[str], loaded: list[str], seen: set[str]) -> None:\n162:     guarded = _guard_in_skill(relative_path)\n163:     if guarded in inventory and guarded not in seen:\n164:         load(guarded)\n165:         loaded.append(guarded)\n166:         seen.add(guarded)\n167: \n168: def route_skill_authoring_request(request):\n169:     inventory = discover_markdown_resources()\n170:     loaded, seen = [], set()\n171: \n172:     if asks_for_parent_hub_or_mode_registry(request):\n173:         workflow_mode = \"sk-create-skill-parent\"\n174:     elif asks_for_nested_workflow_or_surface_packets(request):\n175:         workflow_mode = \"sk-create-skill-parent\"\n176:     elif asks_for_one_skill_package(request):\n177:         workflow_mode = \"sk-create-skill\"\n178:     elif unclear_standalone_vs_parent(request):\n179:         load_if_available(DEFAULT_RESOURCE, inventory, loaded, seen)\n180:         return {\n181:             \"load_level\": \"UNKNOWN_FALLBACK\",\n182:             \"needs_disambiguation\": True,\n183:             \"disambiguation_checklist\": UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST,\n184:             \"resources\": loaded,\n185:         }\n186:     else:\n187:         load_if_available(DEFAULT_RESOURCE, inventory, loaded, seen)\n188:         return {\"load_level\": \"DEFER\", \"next\": \"matching sk-doc packet\", \"resources\": loaded}\n189: \n190:     routing_key = RESOURCE_KEY_BY_MODE[workflow_mode]\n191:     shared_refs = sorted(path for path in inventory if path.startswith(\"references/shared/\"))\n192:     keyed_refs = sorted(path for path in inventory if path.startswith(f\"references/{routing_key}/\"))\n193:     keyed_assets = sorted(path for path in inventory if path.startswith(f\"assets/{routing_key}/\"))\n194: \n195:     if not keyed_refs and not keyed_assets:\n196:         load_if_available(DEFAULT_RESOURCE, inventory, loaded, seen)\n197:         return {\n198:             \"workflowMode\": workflow_mode,\n199:             \"routing_key\": routing_key,\n200:             \"notice\": f\"No create-skill resources found for routing key '{routing_key}'\",\n201:             \"resources\": loaded,\n202:         }\n203: \n204:     for path in shared_refs + keyed_refs + keyed_assets:\n205:         load_if_available(path, inventory, loaded, seen)\n206: \n207:     return {\"workflowMode\": workflow_mode, \"routing_key\": routing_key, \"resources\": loaded}\n208: ```"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794848404410,"end":1794848404923}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794848404928,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e54d34c8001zwfK6Ku20mleem","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e54c3c4a001Xa2Vev6UKd1iA9","type":"tool","id":"call_c19abf26db0c47db8b97b4d4","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt, lines 1-204\n1: # /doctor:install Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/doctor:install`: the argument failure, the build check, the install prompt, the symlink check, the ordered steps, the caveat line, result templates and next-step text. The command router owns flag binding and asset loading. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n4: \n5: This command only reads. Every step that writes is printed with its exact command, and the operator runs it.\n6: \n7: Write for someone who has just cloned Skilled and wants it in their own project: plain words, short sentences, one thing at a time.\n8: \n9: ## 1. Argument Failure\n10: \n11: An unknown argument fails before any workflow YAML loads and prints the wording below with the bracketed parts filled in, then ends with the status line. Nothing is read and nothing is changed.\n12: \n13: | Situation | Wording |\n14: |-----------|---------|\n15: | A flag other than `--root <dir>`, `--runtimes <list>` and `--json` | `Unknown argument: [argument]` then `/doctor:install takes --root <dir>, --runtimes <list> and --json, or list and ?.` then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"` |\n16: | `--root` or `--runtimes` with no value after it | The same two lines, then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"` |\n17: | A second positional token | The same two lines, then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"` |\n18: \n19: `list`, `?` and `menu` as the whole argument print the steps in section 6, with `<dir>`, `<list>` and `<shape>` left as they stand, then stop. They load no workflow and inspect nothing.\n20: \n21: ## 2. The Build Check\n22: \n23: The Skilled checkout is the repository this command runs in. The runtimes load two builds from it, so check both before anything is planned.\n24: \n25: | Build | Check, run from the checkout root | Built when |\n26: |-------|-----------------------------------|------------|\n27: | Spec Kit | `test -d .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist && test -f .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js` | exit 0 |\n28: | Skill Advisor | `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs list-tools --format json` | exit 0 |\n29: \n30: Render both lines, then carry on either way: a missing build never stops the guide.\n31: \n32: ```text\n33: DOCTOR INSTALL — BUILDS\n34: Source: [the Skilled checkout]\n35: Spec Kit build: [found at .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist and runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js | missing]\n36: Advisor CLI: [answers list-tools | missing or not built]\n37: ```\n38: \n39: A missing build becomes step 0 of the checklist. Step 0 carries the README's build commands word for word:\n40: \n41: ```bash\n42: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit install\n43: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit run build\n44: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime install\n45: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build\n46: ```\n47: \n48: Step 0 runs from the Skilled checkout. Its why line is: `Why: the session hooks and the advisor read these builds, so nothing else works until they are there.` It has no mutation class because no doctor route owns it.\n49: \n50: ## 3. The Install Prompt\n51: \n52: Ask every answer that is still missing in one prompt, then wait. This follows the consolidated question protocol. Questions 1 and 2 are dropped when `--root` and `--runtimes` were passed. The link shape and the instruction choice have no flag, so they are always in the prompt.\n53: \n54: ```text\n55: Where should Skilled go? Answer any or all in one reply, for example \"/Users/me/code/my-app, claude and codex, auto, embed\".\n56: \n57: 1) Target repo: the absolute path, for example /Users/me/code/my-app\n58: 2) Runtimes: claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin, pi, vibe, dsh, or \"the ones already there\"\n59: 3) Link shape: auto / whole / merge   (auto unless a real folder already sits where a link would go)\n60: 4) Instruction file: embed / link   (embed keeps the repo's own AGENTS.md; link points AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and REPO RULES.md at the checkout's copies)\n61: ```\n62: \n63: The example carries all four answers so the shape of a full reply is visible. Never print a question the flags already answered.\n64: \n65: ## 4. Accepted Answers\n66: \n67: | Answer | Binds | Meaning |\n68: |--------|-------|---------|\n69: | An absolute path | `--root <dir>` | The project repo that receives the links. The path must exist and be a directory; the engine exits 2 and names it otherwise |\n70: | `claude`, `claude and codex`, `claude,opencode` | `--runtimes <list>` | The runtime folders to link, as a comma list |\n71: | `the ones already there`, empty, `any` | no `--runtimes` | The engine keeps the runtimes its own detection finds in the root, and always links `.skilled` |\n72: | `auto` | `--mode auto` | Whole link where the path is free, merge where a real folder is in the way. The one to pick |\n73: | `whole` | `--mode whole` | One link per entry, refused where a real folder exists |\n74: | `merge` | `--mode merge` | A real folder whose children are links. A local file already in the folder is kept and reported, never overwritten |\n75: | `embed` | step 2 stays | The repo keeps its own `AGENTS.md` and the shipped sections are refreshed into it |\n76: | `link` | step 1 gains `--link-instructions`, step 2 is dropped | `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `REPO RULES.md` become links into the checkout |\n77: \n78: A runtime name outside the nine, a shape outside the three, or an instruction word outside the two is not guessed. Ask that one question again with the accepted values. When the engine refuses a root, show its `ERROR:` line as it printed and ask question 1 again.\n79: \n80: ## 5. The Symlink Check\n81: \n82: Run `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root <dir> [--runtimes <list>] [--link-instructions]` once, in place and read-only, then render its entry lines as they print:\n83: \n84: ```text\n85: DOCTOR INSTALL — WHAT IS ALREADY THERE\n86: Root: [the target repo]\n87: [the engine's entry lines, verbatim, with its indented detail lines and its repo-level warnings]\n88: ```\n89: \n90: Do not re-sort the lines, re-word a status or sum them into a verdict. A `missing` line is work for step 1, not a failure, and the check still exits 0 for it. The check exits 1 only on drift: a broken or foreign link, including a broken link inside a merged folder, a missing source or a tracked absolute link. Missing children in a partial merge do not count as drift. Add `--link-instructions` when the instruction choice is `link`.\n91: \n92: | Status | What it means for this install |\n93: |--------|-------------------------------|\n94: | `linked-whole` | Already a link into the checkout. Step 1 has nothing to do for it |\n95: | `linked-merge` | A real folder whose children are links. Nothing to do |\n96: | `partial-merge` | A real folder missing some links. Step 1 fills the gaps and never deletes a local file |\n97: | `missing` | Not there yet. Step 1 creates it |\n98: | `broken` | A link whose target is gone. Step 1 replaces it |\n99: | `foreign-link` | A link that points somewhere else. Left alone, and the engine refuses to touch it |\n100: | `local` | A real file or folder of the repo's own. Left alone |\n101: | `source-missing` | The checkout has no such path. Nothing is planned |\n102: \n103: ## 6. The Ordered Steps\n104: \n105: This is the checklist, and it is also what `list`, `?` and `menu` print. Each step carries its exact command, its class and one line of why.\n106: \n107: The class column is the manifest's `mutating` value for the route that owns the printed command, verbatim, so it is read from the route table and never guessed. A command with no route of its own prints `n/a`.\n108: \n109: ```text\n110: 1) /doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode <shape>   [class]\n111:    Why: creates the links. It shows a plan first and asks before it writes.\n112: \n113: 2) /doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>   [class]\n114:    Why: keeps the repo's own AGENTS.md and refreshes the shipped sections into it. Dropped when the instruction choice is link.\n115: \n116: 3) /doctor:mcp install   [class]\n117:    Why: builds and registers Code Mode. Run it from the Skilled checkout.\n118: \n119: 4) /doctor:git setup   [class]\n120:    Why: checks the git hooks and sk-git settings, and names the repair for each one that is off. Run it from the target repo.\n121: \n122: 5) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder   [class]\n123:    Why: sets up meaning matching for commands. It shows the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server. Run it from the target repo.\n124: \n125: 6) /doctor:setup   [class]\n126:    Why: confirms the result. Run it from the target repo.\n127: ```\n128: \n129: Run them in this order. Step 1 takes `--link-instructions` when the instruction choice is `link`.\n130: \n131: When the workflow renders the checklist after the check, print this header above the steps:\n132: \n133: ```text\n134: DOCTOR INSTALL — [the target repo]\n135: Source: [the Skilled checkout]\n136: Runtimes: [the runtime list]   Link shape: [auto|whole|merge]   Instruction file: [embed|link]\n137: ```\n138: \n139: A printed step is handed back, never run: each writing command shows its own plan, asks its own yes and writes under its own gate. This command adds no argument to a printed command beyond the values the operator gave.\n140: \n141: ## 7. The Caveat Line\n142: \n143: Print this one line word for word after the steps, on every run, before the result. It is fixed: do not shorten it and do not rewrite it in the operator's words.\n144: \n145: ```text\n146: context saves land in the target repo's own specs/ when they run from inside it, so run /doctor:setup and later saves from inside the target repo, not from the Skilled checkout.\n147: ```\n148: \n149: ## 8. Result Templates\n150: \n151: ### Summary\n152: \n153: ```text\n154: DOCTOR INSTALL RESULT\n155: Source: [the Skilled checkout]\n156: Root: [the target repo]\n157: Runtimes: [the runtime list]\n158: Link shape: [auto|whole|merge]\n159: Instruction file: [embed|link]\n160: Builds: [both found | missing: <which>, printed as step 0]\n161: Already there: [n] linked, [n] missing, [n] to repair\n162: Steps: [n] printed, [n] of them write\n163: Next: run step 1 from the Skilled checkout, then the rest in order\n164: STATUS=OK STEPS=[n]\n165: ```\n166: \n167: ### JSON\n168: \n169: `--json` prints one JSON object and nothing else: no build lines, no steps, no caveat, no header.\n170: \n171: | Key | Value |\n172: |-----|-------|\n173: | `source` | The Skilled checkout's absolute path |\n174: | `root` | The target repo's absolute path |\n175: | `runtimes` | The runtime names, as strings |\n176: | `builds` | One entry per probe in section 2, true or false |\n177: | `symlink_check` | The engine's `check --json` object, unchanged |\n178: | `steps` | One object per printed step: `order`, `command`, `mutating`, `why` |\n179: \n180: ### Failure Summary\n181: \n182: ```text\n183: DOCTOR TARGET FAILED\n184: Target: guide\n185: Step: [the step that failed]\n186: Error: [message]\n187: Next: [the accepted invocation, or the command to rerun]\n188: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[message]\"\n189: ```\n190: \n191: ## 9. Troubleshooting Display\n192: \n193: | Situation | Suggested Action |\n194: |-----------|------------------|\n195: | The engine exits 2 | Bad invocation or a refused root. Its first line names the flag or the path. Fix that one thing and rerun the same command |\n196: | The root is the checkout, sits inside it, or holds it | The engine refuses it, because linking a checkout into itself would loop. Name the project repo that should receive the links |\n197: | A build is missing | Run the four `npm` commands in section 2 from the checkout, then rerun this guide. They also print as step 0 |\n198: | A step prints `n/a` as its class | That printed command has no route in the manifest yet. The command still works; only its class is unknown |\n199: | A line reads `local` or `foreign-link` | Left alone on purpose. Move that file or link yourself, or bring it under step 1's shape, and rerun the guide |\n200: | Only the steps are wanted | `list` prints them with no build check and no inspection |\n201: | A saved session lands in the checkout's `specs/` | The save ran from the Skilled checkout. Run it again from inside the target repo, as the caveat in section 7 says |\n202: | The project copies Skilled in instead of linking it | This guide covers linking only. A copy that keeps its own changes keeps them as overlays: run `/doctor:overlay status --root <copy>`, and see the overlays reference in `system-skilled-doctor` for adopting the engine when the project already has its own overlay folder |\n203: \n204: End interactive presentations with: `What would you like to do next?`","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt, lines 1-204\n1: # /doctor:install Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/doctor:install`: the argument failure, the build check, the install prompt, the symlink check, the ordered steps, the caveat line, result templates and next-step text. The command router owns flag binding and asset loading. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n4: \n5: This command only reads. Every step that writes is printed with its exact command, and the operator runs it.\n6: \n7: Write for someone who has just cloned Skilled and wants it in their own project: plain words, short sentences, one thing at a time.\n8: \n9: ## 1. Argument Failure\n10: \n11: An unknown argument fails before any workflow YAML loads and prints the wording below with the bracketed parts filled in, then ends with the status line. Nothing is read and nothing is changed.\n12: \n13: | Situation | Wording |\n14: |-----------|---------|\n15: | A flag other than `--root <dir>`, `--runtimes <list>` and `--json` | `Unknown argument: [argument]` then `/doctor:install takes --root <dir>, --runtimes <list> and --json, or list and ?.` then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"` |\n16: | `--root` or `--runtimes` with no value after it | The same two lines, then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"` |\n17: | A second positional token | The same two lines, then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"` |\n18: \n19: `list`, `?` and `menu` as the whole argument print the steps in section 6, with `<dir>`, `<list>` and `<shape>` left as they stand, then stop. They load no workflow and inspect nothing.\n20: \n21: ## 2. The Build Check\n22: \n23: The Skilled checkout is the repository this command runs in. The runtimes load two builds from it, so check both before anything is planned.\n24: \n25: | Build | Check, run from the checkout root | Built when |\n26: |-------|-----------------------------------|------------|\n27: | Spec Kit | `test -d .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist && test -f .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js` | exit 0 |\n28: | Skill Advisor | `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs list-tools --format json` | exit 0 |\n29: \n30: Render both lines, then carry on either way: a missing build never stops the guide.\n31: \n32: ```text\n33: DOCTOR INSTALL — BUILDS\n34: Source: [the Skilled checkout]\n35: Spec Kit build: [found at .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist and runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js | missing]\n36: Advisor CLI: [answers list-tools | missing or not built]\n37: ```\n38: \n39: A missing build becomes step 0 of the checklist. Step 0 carries the README's build commands word for word:\n40: \n41: ```bash\n42: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit install\n43: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit run build\n44: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime install\n45: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build\n46: ```\n47: \n48: Step 0 runs from the Skilled checkout. Its why line is: `Why: the session hooks and the advisor read these builds, so nothing else works until they are there.` It has no mutation class because no doctor route owns it.\n49: \n50: ## 3. The Install Prompt\n51: \n52: Ask every answer that is still missing in one prompt, then wait. This follows the consolidated question protocol. Questions 1 and 2 are dropped when `--root` and `--runtimes` were passed. The link shape and the instruction choice have no flag, so they are always in the prompt.\n53: \n54: ```text\n55: Where should Skilled go? Answer any or all in one reply, for example \"/Users/me/code/my-app, claude and codex, auto, embed\".\n56: \n57: 1) Target repo: the absolute path, for example /Users/me/code/my-app\n58: 2) Runtimes: claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin, pi, vibe, dsh, or \"the ones already there\"\n59: 3) Link shape: auto / whole / merge   (auto unless a real folder already sits where a link would go)\n60: 4) Instruction file: embed / link   (embed keeps the repo's own AGENTS.md; link points AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and REPO RULES.md at the checkout's copies)\n61: ```\n62: \n63: The example carries all four answers so the shape of a full reply is visible. Never print a question the flags already answered.\n64: \n65: ## 4. Accepted Answers\n66: \n67: | Answer | Binds | Meaning |\n68: |--------|-------|---------|\n69: | An absolute path | `--root <dir>` | The project repo that receives the links. The path must exist and be a directory; the engine exits 2 and names it otherwise |\n70: | `claude`, `claude and codex`, `claude,opencode` | `--runtimes <list>` | The runtime folders to link, as a comma list |\n71: | `the ones already there`, empty, `any` | no `--runtimes` | The engine keeps the runtimes its own detection finds in the root, and always links `.skilled` |\n72: | `auto` | `--mode auto` | Whole link where the path is free, merge where a real folder is in the way. The one to pick |\n73: | `whole` | `--mode whole` | One link per entry, refused where a real folder exists |\n74: | `merge` | `--mode merge` | A real folder whose children are links. A local file already in the folder is kept and reported, never overwritten |\n75: | `embed` | step 2 stays | The repo keeps its own `AGENTS.md` and the shipped sections are refreshed into it |\n76: | `link` | step 1 gains `--link-instructions`, step 2 is dropped | `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `REPO RULES.md` become links into the checkout |\n77: \n78: A runtime name outside the nine, a shape outside the three, or an instruction word outside the two is not guessed. Ask that one question again with the accepted values. When the engine refuses a root, show its `ERROR:` line as it printed and ask question 1 again.\n79: \n80: ## 5. The Symlink Check\n81: \n82: Run `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root <dir> [--runtimes <list>] [--link-instructions]` once, in place and read-only, then render its entry lines as they print:\n83: \n84: ```text\n85: DOCTOR INSTALL — WHAT IS ALREADY THERE\n86: Root: [the target repo]\n87: [the engine's entry lines, verbatim, with its indented detail lines and its repo-level warnings]\n88: ```\n89: \n90: Do not re-sort the lines, re-word a status or sum them into a verdict. A `missing` line is work for step 1, not a failure, and the check still exits 0 for it. The check exits 1 only on drift: a broken or foreign link, including a broken link inside a merged folder, a missing source or a tracked absolute link. Missing children in a partial merge do not count as drift. Add `--link-instructions` when the instruction choice is `link`.\n91: \n92: | Status | What it means for this install |\n93: |--------|-------------------------------|\n94: | `linked-whole` | Already a link into the checkout. Step 1 has nothing to do for it |\n95: | `linked-merge` | A real folder whose children are links. Nothing to do |\n96: | `partial-merge` | A real folder missing some links. Step 1 fills the gaps and never deletes a local file |\n97: | `missing` | Not there yet. Step 1 creates it |\n98: | `broken` | A link whose target is gone. Step 1 replaces it |\n99: | `foreign-link` | A link that points somewhere else. Left alone, and the engine refuses to touch it |\n100: | `local` | A real file or folder of the repo's own. Left alone |\n101: | `source-missing` | The checkout has no such path. Nothing is planned |\n102: \n103: ## 6. The Ordered Steps\n104: \n105: This is the checklist, and it is also what `list`, `?` and `menu` print. Each step carries its exact command, its class and one line of why.\n106: \n107: The class column is the manifest's `mutating` value for the route that owns the printed command, verbatim, so it is read from the route table and never guessed. A command with no route of its own prints `n/a`.\n108: \n109: ```text\n110: 1) /doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode <shape>   [class]\n111:    Why: creates the links. It shows a plan first and asks before it writes.\n112: \n113: 2) /doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>   [class]\n114:    Why: keeps the repo's own AGENTS.md and refreshes the shipped sections into it. Dropped when the instruction choice is link.\n115: \n116: 3) /doctor:mcp install   [class]\n117:    Why: builds and registers Code Mode. Run it from the Skilled checkout.\n118: \n119: 4) /doctor:git setup   [class]\n120:    Why: checks the git hooks and sk-git settings, and names the repair for each one that is off. Run it from the target repo.\n121: \n122: 5) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder   [class]\n123:    Why: sets up meaning matching for commands. It shows the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server. Run it from the target repo.\n124: \n125: 6) /doctor:setup   [class]\n126:    Why: confirms the result. Run it from the target repo.\n127: ```\n128: \n129: Run them in this order. Step 1 takes `--link-instructions` when the instruction choice is `link`.\n130: \n131: When the workflow renders the checklist after the check, print this header above the steps:\n132: \n133: ```text\n134: DOCTOR INSTALL — [the target repo]\n135: Source: [the Skilled checkout]\n136: Runtimes: [the runtime list]   Link shape: [auto|whole|merge]   Instruction file: [embed|link]\n137: ```\n138: \n139: A printed step is handed back, never run: each writing command shows its own plan, asks its own yes and writes under its own gate. This command adds no argument to a printed command beyond the values the operator gave.\n140: \n141: ## 7. The Caveat Line\n142: \n143: Print this one line word for word after the steps, on every run, before the result. It is fixed: do not shorten it and do not rewrite it in the operator's words.\n144: \n145: ```text\n146: context saves land in the target repo's own specs/ when they run from inside it, so run /doctor:setup and later saves from inside the target repo, not from the Skilled checkout.\n147: ```\n148: \n149: ## 8. Result Templates\n150: \n151: ### Summary\n152: \n153: ```text\n154: DOCTOR INSTALL RESULT\n155: Source: [the Skilled checkout]\n156: Root: [the target repo]\n157: Runtimes: [the runtime list]\n158: Link shape: [auto|whole|merge]\n159: Instruction file: [embed|link]\n160: Builds: [both found | missing: <which>, printed as step 0]\n161: Already there: [n] linked, [n] missing, [n] to repair\n162: Steps: [n] printed, [n] of them write\n163: Next: run step 1 from the Skilled checkout, then the rest in order\n164: STATUS=OK STEPS=[n]\n165: ```\n166: \n167: ### JSON\n168: \n169: `--json` prints one JSON object and nothing else: no build lines, no steps, no caveat, no header.\n170: \n171: | Key | Value |\n172: |-----|-------|\n173: | `source` | The Skilled checkout's absolute path |\n174: | `root` | The target repo's absolute path |\n175: | `runtimes` | The runtime names, as strings |\n176: | `builds` | One entry per probe in section 2, true or false |\n177: | `symlink_check` | The engine's `check --json` object, unchanged |\n178: | `steps` | One object per printed step: `order`, `command`, `mutating`, `why` |\n179: \n180: ### Failure Summary\n181: \n182: ```text\n183: DOCTOR TARGET FAILED\n184: Target: guide\n185: Step: [the step that failed]\n186: Error: [message]\n187: Next: [the accepted invocation, or the command to rerun]\n188: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[message]\"\n189: ```\n190: \n191: ## 9. Troubleshooting Display\n192: \n193: | Situation | Suggested Action |\n194: |-----------|------------------|\n195: | The engine exits 2 | Bad invocation or a refused root. Its first line names the flag or the path. Fix that one thing and rerun the same command |\n196: | The root is the checkout, sits inside it, or holds it | The engine refuses it, because linking a checkout into itself would loop. Name the project repo that should receive the links |\n197: | A build is missing | Run the four `npm` commands in section 2 from the checkout, then rerun this guide. They also print as step 0 |\n198: | A step prints `n/a` as its class | That printed command has no route in the manifest yet. The command still works; only its class is unknown |\n199: | A line reads `local` or `foreign-link` | Left alone on purpose. Move that file or link yourself, or bring it under step 1's shape, and rerun the guide |\n200: | Only the steps are wanted | `list` prints them with no build check and no inspection |\n201: | A saved session lands in the checkout's `specs/` | The save ran from the Skilled checkout. Run it again from inside the target repo, as the caveat in section 7 says |\n202: | The project copies Skilled in instead of linking it | This guide covers linking only. A copy that keeps its own changes keeps them as overlays: run `/doctor:overlay status --root <copy>`, and see the overlays reference in `system-skilled-doctor` for adopting the engine when the project already has its own overlay folder |\n203: \n204: End interactive presentations with: `What would you like to do next?`"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794848404680,"end":1794848404928}}}}
