{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794848641597,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e550c3fa001e8tW0iIkb44ETe","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e550ab33001v6qmeKq3BBjyzA","type":"tool","id":"call_a394e52535f04b75a7d637cf","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Reading both merge directions (`main..merge` and `branch..merge`) for the same path: the doctor-install asset looks clean from main's side and only the branch-to-merge diff shows the branch test that the merge left behind (iteration 1).\n- Counting the generated command rows instead of trusting the prose: `command-bridges.generated.json` reports `typescriptActive: 47`, which closes the README's changed 46-to-47 sentence on evidence (iteration 1).\n- Tracing each changed sentence to its gate: `hookHealth`, the fresh-prompt path and the no-edit summary each had a readable producer, so only the no-edit summary failed (iteration 1).\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- A first read of the doctor presentation treated the `outside the nine` sentence as a simple wording change; the accepted-runtime count only became checkable after reading the symlink manifest and the engine's unknown-name branch (iteration 1).\n- The merge file `doctor-install-presentation.txt` has no `/create:` text, so the brief's \"kept the /create:sk-skill name\" test could not apply there; the merge question had to be reframed as a test/asset pair (iteration 1).","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-merge-10/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-merge-10/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":