{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794849020154,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e556886a001XbMwFcedHNShJf","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e556731f001X1wz8KjaXbtQ8m","type":"tool","id":"call_6a0540db54b349b289800162","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- Tracing each changed sentence to its gate: `hookHealth`, the fresh-prompt path and the no-edit summary each had a readable producer, so only the no-edit summary failed (iteration 1).\n- Reading the persisted hook record's closed schema instead of the prose: `metrics.ts:50-64` and `:451-463` prove the record is prompt-free and is written without the debug flag, so the release's security claim closes on code (iteration 2).\n- Checking the changelog's aggregate numbers against the committed capture: 24 of 44 typed, 0 of 35 false offers, 28 of 45 tuned and 8 of 24 sealed declines all match the baseline fields (iteration 2).\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- A first read of the doctor presentation treated the `outside the nine` sentence as a simple wording change; the accepted-runtime count only became checkable after reading the symlink manifest and the engine's unknown-name branch (iteration 1).\n- The merge file `doctor-install-presentation.txt` has no `/create:` text, so the brief's \"kept the /create:sk-skill name\" test could not apply there; the merge question had to be reframed as a test/asset pair (iteration 1).\n- The sealed-row fixture count of 1 in the changelog could not be tied to one baseline field; `plain.holdout` reports own 2 and combined 2, so the sentence was left unverified rather than turned into a finding (iteration 2).","oldString":"- Tracing each changed sentence to its gate: `hookHealth`, the fresh-prompt path and the no-edit summary each had a readable producer, so only the no-edit summary failed (iteration 1).\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- A first read of the doctor presentation treated the `outside the nine` sentence as a simple wording change; the accepted-runtime count only became checkable after reading the symlink manifest and the engine's unknown-name branch (iteration 1).\n- The merge file `doctor-install-presentation.txt` has no `/create:` text, so the brief's \"kept the /create:sk-skill name\" test could not apply there; the merge question had to be reframed as a test/asset pair (iteration 1).","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-merge-10/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-merge-10/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-merge-10/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-merge-10/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-merge-10/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-merge-10/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -68,13 +68,16 @@\n \n - Reading both merge directions (`main..merge` and `branch..merge`) for the same path: the doctor-install asset looks clean from main's side and only the branch-to-merge diff shows the branch test that the merge left behind (iteration 1).\n - Counting the generated command rows instead of trusting the prose: `command-bridges.generated.json` reports `typescriptActive: 47`, which closes the README's changed 46-to-47 sentence on evidence (iteration 1).\n - Tracing each changed sentence to its gate: `hookHealth`, the fresh-prompt path and the no-edit summary each had a readable producer, so only the no-edit summary failed (iteration 1).\n+- Reading the persisted hook record's closed schema instead of the prose: `metrics.ts:50-64` and `:451-463` prove the record is prompt-free and is written without the debug flag, so the release's security claim closes on code (iteration 2).\n+- Checking the changelog's aggregate numbers against the committed capture: 24 of 44 typed, 0 of 35 false offers, 28 of 45 tuned and 8 of 24 sealed declines all match the baseline fields (iteration 2).\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n - A first read of the doctor presentation treated the `outside the nine` sentence as a simple wording change; the accepted-runtime count only became checkable after reading the symlink manifest and the engine's unknown-name branch (iteration 1).\n - The merge file `doctor-install-presentation.txt` has no `/create:` text, so the brief's \"kept the /create:sk-skill name\" test could not apply there; the merge question had to be reframed as a test/asset pair (iteration 1).\n+- The sealed-row fixture count of 1 in the changelog could not be tied to one baseline field; `plain.holdout` reports own 2 and combined 2, so the sentence was left unverified rather than turned into a finding (iteration 2).\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n","status":"modified","additions":3,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-merge-10/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"- Tracing each changed sentence to its gate: `hookHealth`, the fresh-prompt path and the no-edit summary each had a readable producer, so only the no-edit summary failed (iteration 1).\\n- Reading the persisted hook record's closed schema instead of the prose: `metrics.ts:50-64` and `:451-463` prove the record is prompt-free and is written without the debug flag, so the release's security claim closes on code (iteration 2).\\n- Checking the changelog's aggregate numbers against the committed capture: 24 of 44 typed, 0 of 35 false offers, 28 of 45 tuned and 8 of 24 sealed declines all match the baseline fields (iteration 2).\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- A first read of the doctor presentation treated the `outside the nine` sentence as a simple wording change; the accepted-runtime count only became checkable after reading the symlink manifest and the engine's unknown-name branch (iteration 1).\\n- The merge file `doctor-install-presentation.txt` has no `/create:` text, so the brief's \\\"kept the /create:sk-skill name\\\" test could not apply there; the merge question had to be reframed as a test/asset pair (iteration 1).\\n- The sealed-row fixture count of 1 in the changelog could not be tied to one baseline field; `plain.holdout` reports own 2 and combined 2, so the sentence was left unverified rather than turned into a finding (iteration 2).\",\"oldString\":\"- Tracing each changed sentence to its gate: `hookHealth`, the fresh-prompt path and the no-edit summary each had a readable producer, so only the no-edit summary failed (iteration 1).\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- A first read of the doctor presentation treated the `outside the nine` sentence as a simple wording change; the accepted-runtime count only became checkable after reading the symlink manifest and the engine's unknown-name branch (iteration 1).\\n- The merge file `doctor-install-presentation.txt` has no `/create:` text, so the brief's \\\"kept the /create:sk-skill name\\\" test could not apply there; the merge question had to be reframed as a test/asset pair (iteration 1).\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-merge-10/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794849015914,"end":1794849020154}}}}
