{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794849141770,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e558348700289GbKW4Si030Qk","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e5581f28001EfcQrVSZrVBYav","type":"tool","id":"call_1271d53060d24f3fb3c36839","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 003\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Lineage: `docs-merge-10`, area `docs-merge`.\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\n- Focus: traceability and maintainability, as the closing cross-reference pass. This iteration re-checked the carried findings against HEAD, tied the remaining doc counts to their producers, and tested whether the merged files agree with the surfaces they name. The pass-ten operator focus still binds: docs claims against HEAD code, merge paths against both parents.\n- `steer.md` does not exist in the lineage directory, so no lead ruling applied.\n- The holdout rule and the recorded limits were honoured exactly as in iterations 1 and 2.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n| File | Lines read | What was checked |\n|------|-----------|------------------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md` | 176-193 | The nine-command table against `references/runtime/cli-front-door-contract.md`, and the `vec_cmd_<dim>` table name against `embedders/schema.ts:92` |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md` | 69-88, 205 | The same nine ids and exit codes, and the adapter paragraph that carries F003 |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md` | 36-70 | The at-a-glance bullets against their bodies and the producer code |\n| `.env.example` | 401-414 | The fresh-prompt line and the alias list it sits above |\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md` | 27-42 | The mode table row and command names after the merge |\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md` | 27-34, 96-99 | The three `/create:sk-skill` mentions and the pseudocode keyword list |\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt` | 58, 78 | The eight-name list and the \"nine\" sentence that carry F002 |\n| `.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md` | 43-69, 213-219 | The rename, Vibe and hook-entry claims that the merge brought in |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` | 154-232 | The holdout and fit guards, to confirm the merged test still backs the capture |\n\nContext evidence: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/references/runtime/cli-front-door-contract.md:52-70`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/references/graph/skill-graph-query-cookbook.md:3`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/embedders/schema.ts:92`.\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new. Carried active: F001.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone new. Carried active: F002, F003, F004.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | notApplicable | No spec implementation surface maps to this docs area; the doc-to-code checks are recorded as findings and integration evidence. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | No `checklist.md` at the packet root; the pass-ten brief and scope file remain the checklist. |\n| `skill_agent` | pass | `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md:29` and `ROUTER.md:27,33,97` name `/create:sk-skill` and `/create:skill-parent`, and both command files exist. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | pass | The Vibe adapter proxies the compiled Claude handler; Pi and DSH import the same module; the hook contract document names Vibe. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | notApplicable | No feature-catalog claim is touched. |\n| `playbook_capability` | notApplicable | No playbook claim is touched. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- **Nine command ids:** `cli-front-door-contract.md:52-70` lists exactly the nine ids the README table and SKILL list name, and the mutating flags match (`advisor_rebuild`, `skill_graph_scan`, apply-mode `propagate_enhances`).\n- **Ten query types:** `skill-graph-query-cookbook.md:3` lists the same ten query types as `README.md:158`.\n- **Vector table name:** `embedders/schema.ts:92` returns `vec_cmd_${dim}`, matching the README's `vec_cmd_<dim>` phrase.\n- **Exit taxonomy:** `README.md:86` and `SKILL.md:89-94` give the same five exits (0, 1, 64, 69, 75); the contract keeps the same ids.\n- **Carried F001:** `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:240-241` still asserts text the merged asset no longer carries; re-read at HEAD, unchanged.\n- **Carried F002:** the asset list at `:58` still has eight names and the sentence at `:78` still says \"nine\"; the manifest still has eight runtime keys.\n- **Carried F003:** `README.md:244` and `SKILL.md:205` still omit Vibe while the adapter and hook contract document name it.\n- **Carried F004:** `changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:44` still says no command at all, while the gate keeps read-only commands (`fusion.ts:1227-1229`).\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **Cross-reference scope:** this pass checked claims the changed lines point at, not the whole advisor reference tree. A claim outside the nine files would need its own lineage.\n- **No new finding:** the nine-command table, the ten query types, the vector table name and the exit taxonomy all resolve; the absence of a new finding is recorded as clean evidence, not as skipped coverage.\n- **Carried P1 is not downgraded by a clean iteration:** F001 stays active because the test/asset pair is unchanged; the final line stays CONDITIONAL.\n- **Measurement claims:** the 185-file and 2121-test figures were not re-run and remain unverified; they are not code claims.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- **Nine commands:** README, SKILL and the CLI contract agree.\n- **Ten query types:** README and the query cookbook agree.\n- **Vector table:** the README name matches the embedder schema.\n- **Exit taxonomy:** README and SKILL agree with the contract.\n- **sk-doc rename:** the hub, the ROUTER and the command files agree on `/create:sk-skill`.\n- **Merged routing test:** the holdout and fit guards still read fields the capture emits.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **A wrong command inventory in the README table:** the nine ids and their mutating flags match the contract.\n- **A wrong query-type count:** ten names in both the README and the cookbook.\n- **A wrong vector-table name:** `vec_cmd_${dim}` in the schema.\n- **A contradictory exit taxonomy:** the same five codes in both advisor files and the contract.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: none remaining\n- Focus area: synthesis of the carried F001 P1 and F002-F004 P2 findings\n- Reason: all four dimensions have at least one pass, every carried finding was re-read, and this iteration added no new finding; the stop decision should now converge\n- Rotation status: complete\n- Required evidence: the `convergence.cjs` stop decision for iteration 3\n- Recovery note: none\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-merge-10/iterations/iteration-003.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-merge-10/iterations/iteration-003.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-merge-10/iterations/iteration-003.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 003\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Lineage: `docs-merge-10`, area `docs-merge`.\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\\n- Focus: traceability and maintainability, as the closing cross-reference pass. This iteration re-checked the carried findings against HEAD, tied the remaining doc counts to their producers, and tested whether the merged files agree with the surfaces they name. The pass-ten operator focus still binds: docs claims against HEAD code, merge paths against both parents.\\n- `steer.md` does not exist in the lineage directory, so no lead ruling applied.\\n- The holdout rule and the recorded limits were honoured exactly as in iterations 1 and 2.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n| File | Lines read | What was checked |\\n|------|-----------|------------------|\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md` | 176-193 | The nine-command table against `references/runtime/cli-front-door-contract.md`, and the `vec_cmd_<dim>` table name against `embedders/schema.ts:92` |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md` | 69-88, 205 | The same nine ids and exit codes, and the adapter paragraph that carries F003 |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md` | 36-70 | The at-a-glance bullets against their bodies and the producer code |\\n| `.env.example` | 401-414 | The fresh-prompt line and the alias list it sits above |\\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md` | 27-42 | The mode table row and command names after the merge |\\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/ROUTER.md` | 27-34, 96-99 | The three `/create:sk-skill` mentions and the pseudocode keyword list |\\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt` | 58, 78 | The eight-name list and the \\\"nine\\\" sentence that carry F002 |\\n| `.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.2.1.md` | 43-69, 213-219 | The rename, Vibe and hook-entry claims that the merge brought in |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` | 154-232 | The holdout and fit guards, to confirm the merged test still backs the capture |\\n\\nContext evidence: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/references/runtime/cli-front-door-contract.md:52-70`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/references/graph/skill-graph-query-cookbook.md:3`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/embedders/schema.ts:92`.\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone new. Carried active: F001.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone new. Carried active: F002, F003, F004.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | notApplicable | No spec implementation surface maps to this docs area; the doc-to-code checks are recorded as findings and integration evidence. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | No `checklist.md` at the packet root; the pass-ten brief and scope file remain the checklist. |\\n| `skill_agent` | pass | `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md:29` and `ROUTER.md:27,33,97` name `/create:sk-skill` and `/create:skill-parent`, and both command files exist. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | pass | The Vibe adapter proxies the compiled Claude handler; Pi and DSH import the same module; the hook contract document names Vibe. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | notApplicable | No feature-catalog claim is touched. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | notApplicable | No playbook claim is touched. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- **Nine command ids:** `cli-front-door-contract.md:52-70` lists exactly the nine ids the README table and SKILL list name, and the mutating flags match (`advisor_rebuild`, `skill_graph_scan`, apply-mode `propagate_enhances`).\\n- **Ten query types:** `skill-graph-query-cookbook.md:3` lists the same ten query types as `README.md:158`.\\n- **Vector table name:** `embedders/schema.ts:92` returns `vec_cmd_${dim}`, matching the README's `vec_cmd_<dim>` phrase.\\n- **Exit taxonomy:** `README.md:86` and `SKILL.md:89-94` give the same five exits (0, 1, 64, 69, 75); the contract keeps the same ids.\\n- **Carried F001:** `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:240-241` still asserts text the merged asset no longer carries; re-read at HEAD, unchanged.\\n- **Carried F002:** the asset list at `:58` still has eight names and the sentence at `:78` still says \\\"nine\\\"; the manifest still has eight runtime keys.\\n- **Carried F003:** `README.md:244` and `SKILL.md:205` still omit Vibe while the adapter and hook contract document name it.\\n- **Carried F004:** `changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:44` still says no command at all, while the gate keeps read-only commands (`fusion.ts:1227-1229`).\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- **Cross-reference scope:** this pass checked claims the changed lines point at, not the whole advisor reference tree. A claim outside the nine files would need its own lineage.\\n- **No new finding:** the nine-command table, the ten query types, the vector table name and the exit taxonomy all resolve; the absence of a new finding is recorded as clean evidence, not as skipped coverage.\\n- **Carried P1 is not downgraded by a clean iteration:** F001 stays active because the test/asset pair is unchanged; the final line stays CONDITIONAL.\\n- **Measurement claims:** the 185-file and 2121-test figures were not re-run and remain unverified; they are not code claims.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- **Nine commands:** README, SKILL and the CLI contract agree.\\n- **Ten query types:** README and the query cookbook agree.\\n- **Vector table:** the README name matches the embedder schema.\\n- **Exit taxonomy:** README and SKILL agree with the contract.\\n- **sk-doc rename:** the hub, the ROUTER and the command files agree on `/create:sk-skill`.\\n- **Merged routing test:** the holdout and fit guards still read fields the capture emits.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **A wrong command inventory in the README table:** the nine ids and their mutating flags match the contract.\\n- **A wrong query-type count:** ten names in both the README and the cookbook.\\n- **A wrong vector-table name:** `vec_cmd_${dim}` in the schema.\\n- **A contradictory exit taxonomy:** the same five codes in both advisor files and the contract.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: none remaining\\n- Focus area: synthesis of the carried F001 P1 and F002-F004 P2 findings\\n- Reason: all four dimensions have at least one pass, every carried finding was re-read, and this iteration added no new finding; the stop decision should now converge\\n- Rotation status: complete\\n- Required evidence: the `convergence.cjs` stop decision for iteration 3\\n- Recovery note: none\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-merge-10/iterations/iteration-003.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794849125511,"end":1794849141770}}}}
