{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794849408034,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e55c4a02001pVCs8fWTicXxMS","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e55c2fd70015sfYMe6B64VMSJ","type":"tool","id":"call_974e2fa10fe046abb5873ae9","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 004\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Lineage: `docs-merge-10`, area `docs-merge`.\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\n- Focus: correctness and traceability, run as the recovery pass after `convergence.cjs` returned `STUCK_RECOVERY` at iteration 3. The recovery changes the unit of evidence from file-level claim checks to token-level checks of the changelog's suffix rules, because the filenames and counts were already exhausted.\n- `steer.md` does not exist in the lineage directory, so no lead ruling applied.\n- The holdout rule and the recorded limits were honoured exactly as in the earlier iterations.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n| File | Lines read | What was checked |\n|------|-----------|------------------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md` | 92-106 | Every sentence of \"Brief Commands\": deep-loop naming, file-name rule, mode suffix rule, retired name |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | 208-245 | `COMMAND_START_BOUNDARY`, `COMMAND_CONTINUATION`, `MODE_SUFFIX`, `RETIRED_COMMANDS` and `typedCommandIn` |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | 425-495 | The typed-command cases that pin the suffix and retired-name behaviour |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md` | 176 | The 47-row sentence as a carried-clean control |\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new. Carried active: F001.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **The suffix list in the changelog is narrower than the parser** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:102` -- The sentence names `:auto`, `:confirm` and `:autopilot`, then says \"Any other suffix reads as no command.\" `MODE_SUFFIX` at `command-attach.ts:210` also accepts `:unattended` and the chained `:with-context`, `:with-phases` and `:with-research` modifiers, and the guard test asserts both `/speckit:implement:unattended` and `/speckit:complete:with-context` resolve to their commands (`command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:453,458`). The documented rule is therefore false for five accepted suffixes.\nFinding class: doc-claim-accuracy\nScope proof: The changelog sentence, the `MODE_SUFFIX` regex and the two test expectations were read at HEAD; the regex's alternation is `auto|confirm|autopilot|unattended|with-(context|phases|research)`.\nAffected surface hints: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`\nCase: A reader types `/speckit:implement:unattended the login spec`; the advisor attaches `/speckit:implement`, although the changelog says any suffix outside `:auto`, `:confirm` and `:autopilot` reads as no command.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | notApplicable | No spec implementation surface maps to this docs area. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | No `checklist.md`; the brief and scope file are the checklist. |\n| `skill_agent` | pass | The sk-doc hub and router still name `/create:sk-skill`; no change in this iteration. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | pass | The runtime adapter set is unchanged; the Vibe adapter still proxies the shared handler. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- **Suffix parser:** `MODE_SUFFIX` at `command-attach.ts:210` matches `:auto`, `:confirm`, `:autopilot`, `:unattended` and the three `:with-*` words, in any chain, and only when the suffix ends the name.\n- **Suffix tests:** `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:453` expects `/speckit:implement:unattended the login spec` → `/speckit:implement`; `:458` expects `/speckit:complete:with-context the login spec` → `/speckit:complete`.\n- **File-name rule:** `:430` expects `see /create:sk-skill.md for details` → undefined, matching the changelog's file-name sentence.\n- **Retired name:** `RETIRED_COMMANDS` maps only `/create:skill` → `/create:sk-skill`, and `:483-493` cover the live and path cases, matching the changelog.\n- **Recovery event:** `deep_review.recovery_started` was recorded for iteration 3 through the gateway; `convergence.cjs` resets `stuckCount` on that row.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Recovery mode: the unit of evidence changed from files and counts to the parser's token rules; the iteration is a new read, not a repeat of the earlier claim sweep.\n- The suffix sentence is a documentation defect only; the parser's permissiveness is intentional, and the test pins it.\n- The `:with-*` suffix list lives in `MODE_SUFFIX` and in the `command-attach.ts` comment, but not in the changelog; the fix is to widen the sentence, not to narrow the parser.\n- No new security surface; the changed file is prose.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- **File-name rule:** `/create:sk-skill.md` reads as no command.\n- **Retired name:** `/create:skill` reads as `/create:sk-skill`, and a path such as `docs/create:skill.md` does not.\n- **Deep-loop naming:** the changelog's `/deep:review` vs `/deep:research` sentence matches the depth-wording gate.\n- **README row count:** unchanged and exact at 47.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **A wrong file-name rule:** the test and regex agree.\n- **A wrong retired-name mapping:** only the one retired key exists.\n- **A parser that accepts any suffix:** the regex rejects a suffix outside its alternation, so the defect is the doc's narrower list, not an open parser.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: traceability\n- Focus area: the remaining \"Command Fit\" and \"No-Edit Prompts\" sentences as token-level claims\n- Reason: the recovery pass found one doc-claim mismatch in \"Brief Commands\"; the same token-level method has not yet been applied to the neighbouring sections\n- Rotation status: correctness and traceability covered; security and maintainability swept\n- Required evidence: one parser or gate read per sentence, plus a test or concrete input\n- Recovery note: this iteration is itself the recovery pass for the iteration-3 stuck decision\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-merge-10/iterations/iteration-004.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-merge-10/iterations/iteration-004.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-merge-10/iterations/iteration-004.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 004\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Lineage: `docs-merge-10`, area `docs-merge`.\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\\n- Focus: correctness and traceability, run as the recovery pass after `convergence.cjs` returned `STUCK_RECOVERY` at iteration 3. The recovery changes the unit of evidence from file-level claim checks to token-level checks of the changelog's suffix rules, because the filenames and counts were already exhausted.\\n- `steer.md` does not exist in the lineage directory, so no lead ruling applied.\\n- The holdout rule and the recorded limits were honoured exactly as in the earlier iterations.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n| File | Lines read | What was checked |\\n|------|-----------|------------------|\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md` | 92-106 | Every sentence of \\\"Brief Commands\\\": deep-loop naming, file-name rule, mode suffix rule, retired name |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | 208-245 | `COMMAND_START_BOUNDARY`, `COMMAND_CONTINUATION`, `MODE_SUFFIX`, `RETIRED_COMMANDS` and `typedCommandIn` |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | 425-495 | The typed-command cases that pin the suffix and retired-name behaviour |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md` | 176 | The 47-row sentence as a carried-clean control |\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone new. Carried active: F001.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **The suffix list in the changelog is narrower than the parser** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:102` -- The sentence names `:auto`, `:confirm` and `:autopilot`, then says \\\"Any other suffix reads as no command.\\\" `MODE_SUFFIX` at `command-attach.ts:210` also accepts `:unattended` and the chained `:with-context`, `:with-phases` and `:with-research` modifiers, and the guard test asserts both `/speckit:implement:unattended` and `/speckit:complete:with-context` resolve to their commands (`command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:453,458`). The documented rule is therefore false for five accepted suffixes.\\nFinding class: doc-claim-accuracy\\nScope proof: The changelog sentence, the `MODE_SUFFIX` regex and the two test expectations were read at HEAD; the regex's alternation is `auto|confirm|autopilot|unattended|with-(context|phases|research)`.\\nAffected surface hints: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`\\nCase: A reader types `/speckit:implement:unattended the login spec`; the advisor attaches `/speckit:implement`, although the changelog says any suffix outside `:auto`, `:confirm` and `:autopilot` reads as no command.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | notApplicable | No spec implementation surface maps to this docs area. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | No `checklist.md`; the brief and scope file are the checklist. |\\n| `skill_agent` | pass | The sk-doc hub and router still name `/create:sk-skill`; no change in this iteration. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | pass | The runtime adapter set is unchanged; the Vibe adapter still proxies the shared handler. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- **Suffix parser:** `MODE_SUFFIX` at `command-attach.ts:210` matches `:auto`, `:confirm`, `:autopilot`, `:unattended` and the three `:with-*` words, in any chain, and only when the suffix ends the name.\\n- **Suffix tests:** `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:453` expects `/speckit:implement:unattended the login spec` → `/speckit:implement`; `:458` expects `/speckit:complete:with-context the login spec` → `/speckit:complete`.\\n- **File-name rule:** `:430` expects `see /create:sk-skill.md for details` → undefined, matching the changelog's file-name sentence.\\n- **Retired name:** `RETIRED_COMMANDS` maps only `/create:skill` → `/create:sk-skill`, and `:483-493` cover the live and path cases, matching the changelog.\\n- **Recovery event:** `deep_review.recovery_started` was recorded for iteration 3 through the gateway; `convergence.cjs` resets `stuckCount` on that row.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Recovery mode: the unit of evidence changed from files and counts to the parser's token rules; the iteration is a new read, not a repeat of the earlier claim sweep.\\n- The suffix sentence is a documentation defect only; the parser's permissiveness is intentional, and the test pins it.\\n- The `:with-*` suffix list lives in `MODE_SUFFIX` and in the `command-attach.ts` comment, but not in the changelog; the fix is to widen the sentence, not to narrow the parser.\\n- No new security surface; the changed file is prose.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- **File-name rule:** `/create:sk-skill.md` reads as no command.\\n- **Retired name:** `/create:skill` reads as `/create:sk-skill`, and a path such as `docs/create:skill.md` does not.\\n- **Deep-loop naming:** the changelog's `/deep:review` vs `/deep:research` sentence matches the depth-wording gate.\\n- **README row count:** unchanged and exact at 47.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **A wrong file-name rule:** the test and regex agree.\\n- **A wrong retired-name mapping:** only the one retired key exists.\\n- **A parser that accepts any suffix:** the regex rejects a suffix outside its alternation, so the defect is the doc's narrower list, not an open parser.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: traceability\\n- Focus area: the remaining \\\"Command Fit\\\" and \\\"No-Edit Prompts\\\" sentences as token-level claims\\n- Reason: the recovery pass found one doc-claim mismatch in \\\"Brief Commands\\\"; the same token-level method has not yet been applied to the neighbouring sections\\n- Rotation status: correctness and traceability covered; security and maintainability swept\\n- Required evidence: one parser or gate read per sentence, plus a test or concrete input\\n- Recovery note: this iteration is itself the recovery pass for the iteration-3 stuck decision\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-merge-10/iterations/iteration-004.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794849393155,"end":1794849408034}}}}
