{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794849523683,"sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","part":{"partID":"prt_1e55e1b8c001pBD98fZutXFae4","sessionID":"ses_e1abf3e70ffe7efVZgFVdgfHx6","messageID":"msg_1e55e074f001L39mF0gSFd3qg6","type":"tool","id":"call_1bc97a372b204032a7edda27","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 005\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Lineage: `docs-merge-10`, area `docs-merge`.\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\n- Focus: traceability and correctness, applying the iteration-4 token-level method to the \"Command Fit\" and \"No-Edit Prompts\" sections of the changelog. The pass-ten operator focus still binds.\n- `steer.md` does not exist in the lineage directory, so no lead ruling applied.\n- The holdout rule and the recorded limits were honoured.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n| File | Lines read | What was checked |\n|------|-----------|------------------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md` | 118-152 | Every sentence of \"No-Edit Prompts\" and \"Command Fit\" against the gate code and its tests |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | 340-470 | `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, the decline leads, the or-list, the question lead and the small-edit constants |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts` | 1160-1235 | The weak-cue gate, the words-only override and the no-edit withholding |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts` | 40-56 | The two score thresholds |\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new. Carried active: F001.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone new. Carried active: F002, F003, F004, F005.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | notApplicable | No spec implementation surface maps to this docs area. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | No `checklist.md`; the brief and scope file are the checklist. |\n| `skill_agent` | pass | The sk-doc rename remains coherent. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | pass | The adapter set is unchanged. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- **No-edit wording:** `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` at `command-attach.ts:351` matches `no edits?`, `make no changes`, `no changes yet`, `don't/dont make any changes`, `don't create it`, `just show` and `just list`; `isNoEditRequest` folds curly apostrophes. The changelog's wording list and its \"Don't add tools\" counterexample both hold, because `tools` is not in the pronoun-or-nothing object list.\n- **No-edit gap:** the changelog's documented gap, \"make no changes to the public API\" reads as no-edit, is the same pattern's scope limit, not a contradiction.\n- **Decline leads:** `COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS` includes `no need to` and `stop/stop using`, and the or-list join is handled by the shared lead pattern; the changelog's two examples hold.\n- **Question leads:** the question-mark and `is the` handling is documented in the parser comments and exercised by the guard tests; no sentence in the changelog contradicts it.\n- **Small edit:** `SMALL_EDIT_GATED_COMMANDS` is exactly `/create:readme`, `/create:feature-catalog` and `/create:manual-testing-playbook`, matching \"readme, catalog or playbook\".\n- **Weak cue:** `DOCTOR_HELPER_WEAK_CUE_MIN_SCORE` is 9 and `DOCTOR_HELPER_UNCUED_MIN_SCORE` is 10, matching both changelog sentences when read in their separate cases.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The \"any other suffix\" defect found in iteration 4 is not repeated here; this pass covers the neighbouring sections and closes clean.\n- The deep-loop depth sentence (\"typing another `/deep:` command no longer does\") relies on route selection, which the `attach-scorer-10` area owns; this iteration checked only the depth-wording list and did not re-report that area.\n- No new security surface; the reviewed files are prose plus gate constants.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- **No-edit gate:** the changelog's examples and counterexample match the pattern.\n- **Decline leads:** the two named leads and the or-list behaviour are present.\n- **Small-edit gate:** the three commands are the three the changelog names.\n- **Weak-cue thresholds:** 9 for a weak cue, 10 for the words-only override.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **A wrong no-edit list:** every example and the counterexample resolve against the pattern.\n- **A missing or-list refusal:** the shared lead covers the list, and the changelog's example holds.\n- **A wrong small-edit command set:** exactly three commands, matching the three document families.\n- **A wrong weak-cue threshold:** both constants match the two sentences when read in their own cases.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: traceability\n- Focus area: the changelog's measurement claims against the committed baseline aggregates\n- Reason: the prose rules are now checked; the remaining unverified claims are the counts in \"The Counts on Sealed Rows\" and \"Tests and Scenarios\"\n- Rotation status: correctness, security, traceability and maintainability have at least one pass each\n- Required evidence: aggregate-only reads of the baseline; no prompt text\n- Recovery note: none\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-merge-10/iterations/iteration-005.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-merge-10/iterations/iteration-005.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-merge-10/iterations/iteration-005.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 005\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Lineage: `docs-merge-10`, area `docs-merge`.\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\\n- Focus: traceability and correctness, applying the iteration-4 token-level method to the \\\"Command Fit\\\" and \\\"No-Edit Prompts\\\" sections of the changelog. The pass-ten operator focus still binds.\\n- `steer.md` does not exist in the lineage directory, so no lead ruling applied.\\n- The holdout rule and the recorded limits were honoured.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n| File | Lines read | What was checked |\\n|------|-----------|------------------|\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md` | 118-152 | Every sentence of \\\"No-Edit Prompts\\\" and \\\"Command Fit\\\" against the gate code and its tests |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | 340-470 | `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, the decline leads, the or-list, the question lead and the small-edit constants |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts` | 1160-1235 | The weak-cue gate, the words-only override and the no-edit withholding |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts` | 40-56 | The two score thresholds |\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone new. Carried active: F001.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone new. Carried active: F002, F003, F004, F005.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | notApplicable | No spec implementation surface maps to this docs area. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | No `checklist.md`; the brief and scope file are the checklist. |\\n| `skill_agent` | pass | The sk-doc rename remains coherent. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | pass | The adapter set is unchanged. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- **No-edit wording:** `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` at `command-attach.ts:351` matches `no edits?`, `make no changes`, `no changes yet`, `don't/dont make any changes`, `don't create it`, `just show` and `just list`; `isNoEditRequest` folds curly apostrophes. The changelog's wording list and its \\\"Don't add tools\\\" counterexample both hold, because `tools` is not in the pronoun-or-nothing object list.\\n- **No-edit gap:** the changelog's documented gap, \\\"make no changes to the public API\\\" reads as no-edit, is the same pattern's scope limit, not a contradiction.\\n- **Decline leads:** `COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS` includes `no need to` and `stop/stop using`, and the or-list join is handled by the shared lead pattern; the changelog's two examples hold.\\n- **Question leads:** the question-mark and `is the` handling is documented in the parser comments and exercised by the guard tests; no sentence in the changelog contradicts it.\\n- **Small edit:** `SMALL_EDIT_GATED_COMMANDS` is exactly `/create:readme`, `/create:feature-catalog` and `/create:manual-testing-playbook`, matching \\\"readme, catalog or playbook\\\".\\n- **Weak cue:** `DOCTOR_HELPER_WEAK_CUE_MIN_SCORE` is 9 and `DOCTOR_HELPER_UNCUED_MIN_SCORE` is 10, matching both changelog sentences when read in their separate cases.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- The \\\"any other suffix\\\" defect found in iteration 4 is not repeated here; this pass covers the neighbouring sections and closes clean.\\n- The deep-loop depth sentence (\\\"typing another `/deep:` command no longer does\\\") relies on route selection, which the `attach-scorer-10` area owns; this iteration checked only the depth-wording list and did not re-report that area.\\n- No new security surface; the reviewed files are prose plus gate constants.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- **No-edit gate:** the changelog's examples and counterexample match the pattern.\\n- **Decline leads:** the two named leads and the or-list behaviour are present.\\n- **Small-edit gate:** the three commands are the three the changelog names.\\n- **Weak-cue thresholds:** 9 for a weak cue, 10 for the words-only override.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **A wrong no-edit list:** every example and the counterexample resolve against the pattern.\\n- **A missing or-list refusal:** the shared lead covers the list, and the changelog's example holds.\\n- **A wrong small-edit command set:** exactly three commands, matching the three document families.\\n- **A wrong weak-cue threshold:** both constants match the two sentences when read in their own cases.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: traceability\\n- Focus area: the changelog's measurement claims against the committed baseline aggregates\\n- Reason: the prose rules are now checked; the remaining unverified claims are the counts in \\\"The Counts on Sealed Rows\\\" and \\\"Tests and Scenarios\\\"\\n- Rotation status: correctness, security, traceability and maintainability have at least one pass each\\n- Required evidence: aggregate-only reads of the baseline; no prompt text\\n- Recovery note: none\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-merge-10/iterations/iteration-005.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794849512332,"end":1794849523683}}}}
